const STUDY_BOOK = [{"id":1,"startPage":7,"endPage":14,"topics":"Meeting people Introduce yourself","strategy":"Set a Goal","goals":"Grammar: Verb BE (I am) in introductions; BE + location Speaking: Meeting people; Ask question and answer “Are you (name)?” Review alphabet and numbers 1-20 Pronunciation: Pronouncing linked sounds","conversation":[{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Hi! Are you Anna?","ko":"안녕하세요! 안나 씨 맞나요?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes! Hi there! Are you Pete?","ko":"네! 안녕하세요! 피트 씨인가요?"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"I am Pete.","ko":"저는 피트예요."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Nice to meet you.","ko":"만나서 반가워요."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Let’s try that again. I’m Anna.","ko":"다시 해 봐요. 저는 안나예요."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"I’m Pete. “Anna” Is that A-N-A?","ko":"저는 피트예요. 'Anna'는 A-N-A인가요?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No. A-N-N-A.","ko":"아니요. A-N-N-A예요."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Well, Anna with two “n’s” … Welcome to … 1400 Irving Street!","ko":"그렇군요, n이 두 개인 안나! 어빙 스트리트 1400번지에 오신 것을 환영해요!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"My new apartment! Yes!","ko":"제 새 아파트군요! 맞아요!"}],"words":[{"en":"apartment","definition":"a usually rented room or set of rooms that is part of a building and is used as a place to live","ko":"아파트"},{"en":"meet","definition":"to see and speak to someone for the first time","ko":"만나다"},{"en":"new","definition":"not known before; recently bought or rented","ko":"새로운"},{"en":"nice","definition":"good and enjoyable","ko":"좋은·친절한"},{"en":"street","definition":"a road in a city, town, or village","ko":"거리"},{"en":"try","definition":"to make an effort to do something","ko":"시도하다"},{"en":"welcome","definition":"used as a friendly greeting to someone who has arrived at a place","ko":"환영합니다"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 1: Welcome\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. Who is she? \na.\t\nMelissa\nb.\t\nMary\nc.\t\nMaurice\nd.\t\nMeghan\t\n4. What does the person say? \na.\t Hi. I am Ross. Are you Jill’s friend?\nb.\t Hello. I am Pete. Are you Anna?\nc.\t Hi. I am Russell. Are you Anna’s friend?\nd.\t Hello. I am John. Are you Mary?\n2. Who is he? \na.\t\nJoseph\nb.\t\nShawn\nc.\t\nJohn\nd.\t\nJosh\n5. What does Anna say?\na.\t Yes, Sam.\nb.\t Yes ma’am.\nc.\t Yes. I am.\n3. What does the person say?\na.\t\nHello. My name is Russell. \n       Are you Sarah?\nb.\t\nWhat is your name?\nc.\t\nHello. What is your name? \n        My name is John.\nd.\t\nHi. I am Jill. Are you John?\n6. What does Anna say?\na.\t Ice cream, please!\nb.\t Nice to meet you!\nc.\t Nice to chew food!\nd.\t Have a nice weekend!","guide":{"id":1,"focus":"인사하고 자신의 이름을 소개해요.","grammar":"I am은 ‘저는 ~입니다’라는 뜻이에요. 대화에서는 I’m으로 줄여 말해요.","mission":"자기 이름을 말하고 철자까지 천천히 소개해 보세요.","example":"I’m Anna.","exampleKo":"저는 안나예요."}},{"id":2,"startPage":15,"endPage":24,"topics":"Welcoming Saying goodbye","strategy":"Preview","goals":"Grammar: BE + noun; BE + location; Subject pronouns: I, you, he, she, we, they Pronunciation: Contractions with BE Speaking: Asking for names; saying your address","conversation":[{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Hey, Pete! Who’s your friend? Pete She is Anna. She is new to D.C.","ko":"안녕, 피트! 네 친구는 누구야? 피트: 안나야. 안나는 워싱턴 D.C.에 새로 왔어."},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Where are you from?","ko":"어디에서 왔어요?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I am from a small town.","ko":"저는 작은 마을에서 왔어요."},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Well, welcome to D.C.","ko":"워싱턴 D.C.에 오신 걸 환영해요."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thank you.","ko":"고마워요."},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"I am Jonathan. I am in apartment B4.","ko":"저는 조너선이에요. B4호에 살아요."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I am in apartment C2. Marsha is my roommate.","ko":"저는 C2호에 살아요. 마샤가 제 룸메이트예요."},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"I know Marsha. She is nice.","ko":"마샤를 알아요. 친절한 사람이죠."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"And I am in Apartment D7. I have to go now.","ko":"저는 D7호에 살아요. 이제 가 봐야 해요."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh!","ko":"아!"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Remember to call Marsha at work. Tell her you’re here.","ko":"직장에 있는 마샤에게 전화하세요. 도착했다고 말해요."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Right, thanks, Pete. Nice to meet you!","ko":"알겠어요. 고마워요, 피트. 만나서 반가웠어요!"},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"You too, Bye.","ko":"저도요. 안녕히 가세요."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Apartment C2, here I come!","ko":"C2호, 제가 갑니다!"}],"words":[{"en":"know","definition":"to have met and talked to (someone)","ko":"알다"},{"en":"meet","definition":"to see and speak to (someone) for the first time.","ko":"만나다"},{"en":"call","definition":"to make a telephone call.","ko":"전화하다"},{"en":"friend","definition":"a person who you like and enjoy being with.","ko":"친구"},{"en":"remember","definition":"to have or keep an image or idea in your mind of (something or someone from the past) or to think of (something or someone from the past) again.","ko":"기억하다"},{"en":"roommate","definition":"a person who shares a room, apartment, or house with someone else.","ko":"룸메이트"},{"en":"work","definition":"the place where you do your job.","ko":"일·직장"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 2: Hello, I’m Anna\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Anna say?\na.\t Where do you work?\nb.\t What do you think?\nc.\t Where are you from?\nd.\t Where are you now?\t\n4. What is her apartment number? \na.\t I am in apartment C2.\nb.\t I am in apartment S2.\nc.\t I am in apartment C4.\nd.\t I am in apartment D4.\n2. Where is she from?\na.\t I am from Austin.\nb.\t I am from a small town.\nc.\t I am from a big city.\nd.\t I am from Somalia.\n5. What does Anna say?\na.\t My department is new. \nb.\t My apartment is number D7.\nc.\t My apartment is number D9.\nd.\t My department is in room D7.\n3. What is her apartment number?\na.\t I live in apartment D4.\nb.\t I am in apartment E4.\nc.\t I live in apartment G4.\nd.\t I am in apartment B4.","guide":{"id":2,"focus":"처음 만난 친구의 이름과 출신을 물어요.","grammar":"I / you / he / she는 사람을 가리키는 말이에요. be동사는 주어에 맞게 바뀌어요.","mission":"친구에게 이름과 사는 곳을 묻고 답해 보세요.","example":"Where are you from?","exampleKo":"어디에서 오셨어요?"}},{"id":3,"startPage":25,"endPage":36,"topics":"Apologizing: I’m sorry; excuse me","strategy":"Look for ways to practice","goals":"Grammar: Place pronouns: here; there Pronunciation: Contractions with BE; polite telephone expressions Speaking: Giving addresses; telephone numbers; making a telephone call","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I am in my new apartment! Great! I live with Marsha. We’re roommates. I want to cook dinner. Hum. Is there a supermarket near here? Marsha knows. Marsha’s work number is 555-8986.","ko":"나는 내 새로운 아파트에 있습니다! 훌륭한! 나는 Marsha와 함께 살고 있습니다. 우리는 룸메이트입니다. 나는 저녁 식사를 요리하고 싶습니다. Hum. 여기에 슈퍼마켓이 있습니까? Marsha는 알고 있습니다. Marsha의 작품 번호는 555-8986입니다."},{"speaker":"Man","en":"Hello.","ko":"안녕하세요."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello. Is this Marsha? It is Anna.","ko":"안녕하세요. 이 마샤인가? 그것은 안나입니다."},{"speaker":"Man","en":"I am sorry. You have the wrong number.","ko":"죄송합니다. 잘못된 번호가 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh. Is this 555-8986?","ko":"오. 이 555-8986?"},{"speaker":"Man","en":"No. This is 555-8689.","ko":"아니오. 이것은 555-8689입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh. Excuse me!","ko":"오. 저를 움직여!"},{"speaker":"Man","en":"Okay. ‘Bye.","ko":"예. 'Bye."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"One more time. 555-8986. Please be Marsha.","ko":"더 많은 시간. 555-8986. 마샤가 되십시오."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Hello. This is Marsha.","ko":"안녕하세요. 이것은 Marsha입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes, Marsha. I want to cook dinner.","ko":"예, Marsha. 저녁 식사를 요리하고 싶습니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Excuse me? Anna? Is that you?","ko":"나를 공격? 안나? 그게 뭐니?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh, yes. I am here!","ko":"오, 예. 나는 여기에 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Good. You are there.","ko":"좋은. 당신은 거기 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I want to find a supermarket.","ko":"슈퍼마켓을 찾고 싶습니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Oh, okay. The supermarket is at 1500 Irving Street. It is near the apartment.","ko":"Oh, 괜찮아. 슈퍼마켓은 1500 Irving Street에 있습니다. 아파트 근처에 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Great! Goodbye!","ko":"큰! 안녕!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Goodbye, Anna.","ko":"안녕, 안나."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"There is a big supermarket on my street. And Marsha says I am a good cook! Until next time … !","ko":"내 거리에 큰 슈퍼마켓이 있습니다. 그리고 Marsha는 내가 좋은 요리라고 말합니다! 다음 시간까지 ... ! 영어 수업을 배우자 3 30"}],"words":[{"en":"cook","definition":"to prepare (food) for eating especially by using heat","ko":"요리하다"},{"en":"dinner","definition":"the main meal of the day","ko":"저녁 식사"},{"en":"excuse","definition":"to forgive someone for making a mistake or doing something wrong","ko":"용서하다·실례"},{"en":"find","definition":"to get or discover something or someone that you are looking for","ko":"찾다"},{"en":"here","definition":"in this place or at this location","ko":"여기"},{"en":"live","definition":"to have a home in a specified place","ko":"살다"},{"en":"near","definition":"close to something or someone","ko":"가까이"},{"en":"number","definition":"a number or a set of numbers and other symbols that is used to identify a person or thing or a telephone number","ko":"숫자·번호"},{"en":"sorry","definition":"feeling sorrow or regret","ko":"미안한"},{"en":"supermarket","definition":"a store where customers can buy a variety of foods and household items","ko":"슈퍼마켓"},{"en":"there","definition":"in that place or at that location","ko":"저기"},{"en":"want","definition":"to desire or wish for something","ko":"원하다"},{"en":"wrong","definition":"not suitable or appropriate for a particular purpose, situation, or person","ko":"잘못된"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 3 - I’m Here!\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Anna say about Marsha?\na.\t Anna says she is in Marsha’s room.\nb.\t She says she wants to meet Marsha.\nc.\t Anna says Marsha is her best friend.\nd.\t She says she and Marsha are\nroommates.\t\n4. Why does the man say he is sorry?\na.\tHe does not know Anna’s number.\nb.\tThe man tells Anna she has the wrong  \nnumber.\nc.\tHe has the wrong phone number.\nd.\tThe man tells Anna that Marsha is not at \nwork.\n2. What does Anna want to do?\na.\t Anna wants to see what is in there.\nb.\t Anna wants to see what is in there.\nc.\t Anna wants to call Marsha.\nd.\t She wants to ask a friend over\n5. What does the man say about his \nphone number?\na.\t He does not know Anna’s number.\nb.\t The man says, his number is 555-8689.\nc.\t He and Marsha have the same    number.\nd.\t His number is 555-8986.\n3. What is Anna asking about?\na.\tAnna wants to find a restaurant near the \napartment.\nb.\tShe asks about the kind of food Marsha \nlikes.\nc.\tAnna wants to buy food at a \nsupermarket.\nd.\tShe asks about where she can park her \ncar. \n6. What does Marsha say to Anna?\na.\t She does not want Anna to go to the \nsupermarket.\nb.\t Marsha says the supermarket is near their \napartment.\nc.\t She says Anna is at 1500 Irving Street.\nd.\t Marsha says the supermarket is on \nanother street.\nConversation Practice Cards - Set 1\nConversation Practice Cards - Set 2","guide":{"id":3,"focus":"전화로 상대방과 위치를 확인해요.","grammar":"here는 ‘여기’, there는 ‘저기’예요. 전화를 잘못 걸었다면 I’m sorry라고 해요.","mission":"가상의 전화번호를 말하고 잘못 걸었을 때 사과해 보세요.","example":"I’m here!","exampleKo":"저 여기 있어요!"}},{"id":4,"startPage":37,"endPage":48,"topics":"Greetings Names of common objects Negation","strategy":"Focus","goals":"Grammar: BE + Noun; Be + Adjective + Noun; BE + Not + Noun; HAVE + Noun Pronunciation: Pronouncing reduced “and​;” BE + noun Speaking: Talking about objects with BE + HAVE","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Pete, hi! Hi, we are here!","ko":"애완 동물, 안녕! 안녕하세요, 우리는 여기!"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Hi, Anna! Hi, Marsha!","ko":"안녕, 안나! 안녕, 마샤!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi!","ko":"안녕하세요!"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"How are you two?","ko":"두 가지 방법은 무엇입니까?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"I am great!","ko":"나는 훌륭합니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"You know, Pete, I am new to D.C. The city is big.","ko":"당신은 알고, Pete, 나는 D.C.에 새로운. 도시는 커다란."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Yeah. But you learn a little more every day. How’s the new apartment?","ko":"그래. 그러나 매일 조금 더 배울 수 있습니다. 새로운 아파트는 어떻습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"The new apartment is great! Let’s get coffee!","ko":"새로운 아파트는 훌륭합니다! 커피를 가져 가자!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Anna, do you have a pen?","ko":"Anna, 펜을 가지고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes. I have a pen in my bag. I have a …","ko":"예. 나는 내 가방에 펜이 있습니다. 나는 ..."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"It is not a pen. It is a book. It is a big book.","ko":"그것은 펜이 아닙니다. 그것은 책입니다. 그것은 큰 책입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes. Yes it is, Pete. I know I have a pen, though… I have a ....","ko":"예. 네, Pete입니다. 나는 펜을 가지고 있지만 ... 나는 ...."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"It is not a pen, Anna ... a toy?","ko":"그것은 펜이 아니, 안나 ... 장난감?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I have a ....","ko":"나는 ....."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"And it is a pillow!","ko":"그리고 그것은 베개입니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Pete, Marsha, I know I have a pen.","ko":"Pete, Marsha, 나는 펜을 가지고 알고있다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Anna, it is a map.","ko":"Anna, 그것은지도입니다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Why do you have a map of the world?","ko":"왜 세계지도가 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Pete, Marsha. Now I know I have a pen.","ko":"Pete, Marsha. 이제 나는 펜을 가지고 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"And now you have a lamp.","ko":"그리고 지금 당신은 램프가 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Anna.","ko":"안나."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I have a pen! Let’s get coffee!","ko":"나는 펜을 가지고! 커피를 얻자! ’ s Learn English Lesson 4 41"}],"words":[{"en":"bag","definition":"a soft container used to hold money and other small things","ko":"가방"},{"en":"big","definition":"large in size","ko":"큰"},{"en":"book","definition":"a set of printed sheets of paper that are held together inside a cover or a long written work","ko":"책"},{"en":"coffee","definition":"a dark brown drink made from ground coffee beans and boiled water","ko":"커피"},{"en":"lamp","definition":"a device that produces light","ko":"램프"},{"en":"little","definition":"small in size","ko":"작은"},{"en":"map","definition":"a picture or chart that shows the rivers, mountains, streets, etc., in a particular area","ko":"지도"},{"en":"pen","definition":"a writing instrument that uses ink","ko":"펜"},{"en":"pillow","definition":"a bag filled with soft material that is used as a cushion usually for the head of a person who is lying down","ko":"베개"},{"en":"toy","definition":"something a child plays with","ko":"장난감"},{"en":"world","definition":"the earth and all the people and things on it","ko":"세계"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 4 - What Is It?\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Anna say about the city?\na.\t She likes the city.\nb.\t Anna says the city is great.\nc.\t She does not like the city.\nd.\t Anna says the city is big.\n4. What does Marsha tell Anna? \na.\t Marsha tells Anna the toy is not a pen.\nb.\t She tells Anna that she has a pen.\nc.\t Marsha says it is a toy.\nd.\t She asks if Anna has another pen.\n2. What does Marsha want?\na.\t She asks Anna where she has been.\nb.\t Marsha asks if Anna is going again.\nc.\t She asks Anna for a pen.\nd.\t Marsha wants to give Anna a pen.\n5. What does Pete say about the map?\na.\t Pete wants to look at the map.\nb.\t He asks why Anna has a map.\nc.\t Pete asks Anna to show him the map.\nd.\t He wants to put the map on the wall.\n3. What does Pete say about the book?\na.\t He thanks her for the book.\nb.\t Pete says it is a big book.\nc.\t He asks why she has a book.\nd.\t Pete wants to look at the book.\n6. What does Pete say to Anna?\na.\t I want to see your lamp.\nb.\t Where is my lamb?\nc.\t Now you have a lamp.\nd.\t Why do you have a lamp?\nMain Video Images – What is it? – Lesson 4\nActivity  – What’s in My Hand?","guide":{"id":4,"focus":"물건의 이름과 모양을 설명해요.","grammar":"What is it?은 ‘그게 뭐예요?’예요. It is a~로 이름을 말하고 big, little 같은 형용사를 붙여요.","mission":"주변 물건 세 개를 골라 영어로 이름과 특징을 설명해 보세요.","example":"What is it?","exampleKo":"그것은 무엇인가요?"}},{"id":5,"startPage":49,"endPage":59,"topics":"Asking about location Naming places and activities Naming rooms in a house","strategy":"Plan to learn","goals":"Grammar: BE + location Speaking: BE + location Pronunciation: Question intonation","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello, everyone! Today my friend Marsha is at her friend’s house. She says it is beautiful. I want to see this house! Here we are!","ko":"안녕하세요, 여러분! 오늘 내 친구 Marsha는 친구의 집에 있습니다. 그녀는 아름답습니다. 나는이 집을보고 싶습니다! 여기 우리는 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Marsha, I am in the kitchen! It is a beautiful kitchen!","ko":"Marsha, 나는 부엌에 있습니다! 아름다운 부엌입니다!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"It is beautiful. We cook in the kitchen.","ko":"그것은 아름답습니다. 우리는 부엌에서 요리합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I eat in the kitchen.","ko":"나는 부엌에서 먹는다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"We relax in the living room.","ko":"우리는 거실에서 휴식합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I relax in the living room. Marsha, let’s go upstairs!","ko":"나는 거실에서 휴식. Marsha, 가자!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Anna? Where are you?","ko":"안나? 어디 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Marsha, I am in the bathroom! I wash in the bathroom.","ko":"Marsha, 나는 욕실에있다! 나는 욕실에 씻어."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"I am in the bedroom. We sleep in the bedroom.","ko":"나는 침실에있다. 우리는 침실에 잠."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I sleep in the bedroom!","ko":"나는 침실에 잠! 영어 수업을 배울하자 5 52"}],"words":[{"en":"bathroom","definition":"a room with a sink and toilet and usually a bathtub or shower","ko":"욕실"},{"en":"beautiful","definition":"very good or pleasing; having beauty","ko":"아름다운"},{"en":"bedroom","definition":"a room used for sleeping","ko":"침실"},{"en":"eat","definition":"to take food into your mouth and swallow it","ko":"먹다"},{"en":"house","definition":"a building in which a family lives","ko":"집"},{"en":"kitchen","definition":"a room in which food is cooked","ko":"부엌"},{"en":"living room","definition":"a room in a house for general family use","ko":"거실"},{"en":"relax","definition":"to spend time resting or doing something enjoyable","ko":"쉬다"},{"en":"sleep","definition":"to rest your mind and body by closing your eyes","ko":"잠자다"},{"en":"upstairs","definition":"on or to a higher floor of a building","ko":"위층에"},{"en":"wash","definition":"to clean (something) with water and usually soap Rooms in a House","ko":"씻다"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 5 - Where Are You?\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. Where is Marsha today?\na.\t Marsha is at the front of the house.\nb.\t Marsha is at her house.\nc.\t Marsha is wearing a blouse.\nd.\t Marsha is at her friend’s house.\t\n4. What does Anna tell Marsha?\na.\t I like chicken.\nb.\t What is in the kitchen?\nc.\t I am in the kitchen.\n2. What does Marsha say?\na.\t Andy wears shoes.\nb.\t Anna, what are you doing?\nc.\t Anna, where are you?\nd.\t Anna, this can’t be true.\n5. Where is Marsha?\na.\t She is in the bathroom.\nb.\t She is in the bedroom.\nc.\t She is in the ballroom.\nd.\t She is in the kitchen.\n3. Where is Anna?\na.\t She is in the ballroom.\nb.\t She is in the bathroom.\nc.\t She is in the restroom.\nd.\t She is in the bedroom. \n6. What does Anna say?\na.\t Let’s go upstairs.\nb.\t Let’s sit on the chairs.\nc.\t Come upstairs.\nd.\t I am on the stairs.\nHow do you learn best? Activity - Lesson 5\nCut out the images above. Place one of each into the three locations around the classroom \nwhich are associated with studying alone, with a friend, or in a group.","guide":{"id":5,"focus":"집 안의 공간과 사람의 위치를 말해요.","grammar":"She is in the kitchen처럼 be동사 뒤에 장소를 붙여요.","mission":"집 안의 방을 떠올리며 가족이 어디 있는지 말해 보세요.","example":"Where are you?","exampleKo":"어디에 계세요?"}},{"id":6,"startPage":60,"endPage":71,"topics":"Informal greetings Asking questions about a location Clarifying information about a location Naming places Rooms and services in an apartment","strategy":"Ask Questions to Clarify","goals":"Grammar: Prepositions: next to, behind, across from Pronunciation: Informal greetings Speaking: Asking about locations","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi there! I’m Anna and I live in Washington, D.C. Every day I learn more about this great city. People in Washington like to work out! Oh, hi, Pete. How’s it going?","ko":"안녕하세요! 저는 Anna이고 저는 워싱턴 D.C.에서 살고 있습니다. 매일 나는이 훌륭한 도시에 대해 더 많은 것을 배웠습니다. 워싱턴의 사람들은 밖으로 일하고 싶습니다! Oh, hi, Pete. 어떻게 가고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Hi, Anna. It’s going great. How’s it going with you?","ko":"안녕, 안나. 그것은 훌륭합니다. 어떻게 너와 함께 갈거야?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Things are awesome! Pete, I want to work out. Where is the gym?","ko":"굉장합니다! Pete, 나는 아웃하고 싶습니다. 체육관은 어디에 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"The gym is across from the lounge. It’s next to the mailroom. Go that way.","ko":"체육관은 라운지에서 있습니다. 그것은 메일룸 옆에 있습니다. 그 길을 이동하십시오."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thanks, Pete! (Anna walks away)","ko":"감사합니다, Pete! (Anna 산책)"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"No, Anna! Not that way! Go that way! (He motions to his left; Anna walks to his right) (In the mailroom)","ko":"아니, 안나! 그건 그렇다! 그 길로 이동! (그 왼쪽으로 그의 움직임; 안나 그의 오른쪽으로 걸어) (우편에)"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh, Pete. This is not the gym.","ko":"Oh, Pete. 이것은 체육관이 아닙니다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"That’s right, Anna. This is the mailroom.","ko":"그건 맞습니다, 안나. 이것은 사서방입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"The gym is across from … what?","ko":"체육관은 ... 무엇을 맞습니까?"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"The gym is across from the lounge.","ko":"체육관은 라운지에서 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Across from the lounge. Right. Thanks! (In the lounge)","ko":"라운지에서. 오른쪽. 감사합니다! (라운지에서)"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Pete! This is not the gym!","ko":"Pete! 이것은 체육관이 아닙니다!"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"The gym is across from the lounge. It is behind the lobby.","ko":"체육관은 라운지에서 있습니다. 로비 뒤에 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Right. Right. See you.","ko":"오른쪽. 오른쪽. 당신을 참조하십시오."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"See you, Anna!","ko":"아, 안나!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"See you.","ko":"더 보기"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"See you, Anna. (In the garage)","ko":"보라, 안나. ( 차고에서)"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This is not the gym. This is a parking garage.","ko":"이것은 체육관이 아닙니다. 이것은 주차장입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello? Pete? (On the rooftop)","ko":"안녕하세요? Pete? ( 옥상에)"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This is not a gym. This is a rooftop. (In the gym)","ko":"이것은 체육관이 아닙니다. 이것은 옥상입니다. ( 체육관에서)"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Pete! Pete?","ko":"페트! 페트?"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"I want to work out too! Join me!","ko":"나는 너무 일하고 싶다! 나를 가입!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I’m good.","ko":"나는 좋다. 영어 수업을 배우자 6 64"}],"words":[{"en":"across from","definition":"on the opposite side from (someone or something)","ko":"맞은편에"},{"en":"behind","definition":"in or to a place at the back of or to the rear of (someone or something)","ko":"뒤에"},{"en":"elevator","definition":"a machine used for carrying people and things to different levels in a building","ko":"엘리베이터"},{"en":"every","definition":"used to describe how often some repeated activity or event happens or is done","ko":"모든"},{"en":"gym","definition":"a room or building that has equipment for sports activities or exercise","ko":"체육관"},{"en":"lobby","definition":"a large open area inside and near the entrance of a public building (such as a hotel or theater)","ko":"로비"},{"en":"lounge","definition":"a room with comfortable furniture for relaxing","ko":"휴게실"},{"en":"mailroom","definition":"a room in which mail is processed and sorted","ko":"우편실"},{"en":"next to","definition":"at the side of (someone or something)","ko":"옆에"},{"en":"parking garage","definition":"a building in which people usually pay to park their cars, trucks, etc.","ko":"주차장"},{"en":"rooftop","definition":"the cover or top of a building or vehicle","ko":"옥상"},{"en":"work out","definition":"to perform athletic exercises in order to improve your health or physical fitness","ko":"운동하다"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 6 - Where Is the Gym?\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Anna say to Pete? \na.\t Where is the gym? \nb.\t Where is Tim? \nc.\t What are you wearing? \nd.\t Where is the lobby? \t\n4. What does Anna ask Pete?\na.\t The gym is across from … what? \nb.\t The gym is near to …. what? \nc.\t Tim lives across from … what? \nd.\t You are the boss? What? \n2. What does Pete say to Anna?\na.\t The gym is across from the lounge.\nb.\t Tim lives across from the lounge. \nc.\t The gym is near to the lounge. \nd.\t The gym is behind the lounge. \n5. What does she say?\na.\t Across from the lounge. \nb.\t Walk across the lounge. \nc.\t A crosswalk is near the lounge. \nd.\t Where are you now? \n3. Where is the gym? \na.\t It’s next to the mailroom. \nb.\t It’s across from the mailroom. \nc.\t It’s behind the mailroom. \nd.\t It’s near the mailroom. \n6. What does Pete say?\na.\t It is behind the lobby. \nb.\t Have you seen Robbie? \nc.\t It is across from the lobby. \nd.\t I live near the lobby.","guide":{"id":6,"focus":"건물 안에서 길을 묻고 안내해요.","grammar":"next to는 ‘옆에’, behind는 ‘뒤에’, across from은 ‘맞은편에’예요.","mission":"집이나 학교에서 두 장소의 위치를 서로 설명해 보세요.","example":"The gym is across from the lounge.","exampleKo":"체육관은 휴게실 맞은편에 있어요."}},{"id":7,"startPage":72,"endPage":81,"topics":"Everyday activities Checking understanding","strategy":"Ask questions to clarify","goals":"Grammar: Present continuous tense; Questions for clarification Pronunciation: Shortened form of Present Continuous verbs; shorter form of the question phrase, “What are you doing?” Speaking: Asking questions to clarify.","conversation":[{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Come in.","ko":"에 있다."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Well, Anna, welcome. Anna: Thank you.","ko":"잘, 안나, 환영. 안나: 감사합니다."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"I am your boss, Caty Weaver. But, please call me Caty.","ko":"나는 당신의 보스, Caty 웨버입니다. 그러나, 저에게 Caty에게 전화하십시오."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thank you, Ms. Weaver.","ko":"감사합니다. Weaver."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Just Caty.","ko":"그냥 Caty."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sure thing, Ms. Weaver. Caty: Okay then. Are you excited?","ko":"물론, Ms. Weaver. Caty : 그럼. 흥분?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes, I am excited!","ko":"예, 나는 흥분!"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"So sorry, but I am busy. Please meet your co-workers. But remember, they are busy working.","ko":"그래서 미안하지만 난 바쁘다. 당신의 동료를 만나십시오. 그러나 기억, 그들은 바쁜 일입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sure. Thanks, Ms. Weaver. Anna: Hi there! I’m Anna.","ko":"확실히. 감사, 미스터. 웨버. 안나: 안녕하세요! 나는 안나."},{"speaker":"Anne","en":"Hi, Anna. I’m Anne.","ko":"안녕, 안나. 나는 Anne입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Nice to meet you. What are you doing?","ko":"당신을 만나는 좋은. 당신은 무엇을 하고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anne","en":"Um, I’m writing.","ko":"움, 나는 쓰고 있다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"You are writing! You are writing a lot!","ko":"너는 쓰고 있다! 너는 많이 쓰고 있다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh! Oh dear.","ko":"오! 오다."},{"speaker":"Anne","en":"No! No! That’s okay. Anna: I am sorry!","ko":"아니! 그건 괜찮아. 안나: 나는 미안 해요!"},{"speaker":"Anne","en":"That’s okay. Really. Anna: I am sorry!","ko":"그건 괜찮아. 정말. 안나 : 나는 미안 해요!"},{"speaker":"Anne","en":"Please. Please. Please stop. Please. Anna: Sorry. Sorry.","ko":"お知らせ Mannam&Daehwa [기능개선] 하나님세상의 주일,수요 말씀 퍼가기 기능 업데이트 2015/11/02"},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"“and people all around the world are waiting to hear news about the next president…”","ko":"“세계의 모든 사람들은 다음 대통령에 대한 뉴스를 듣고 기다리고 있습니다 ...”"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Jonathan, hi! Remember me? I live in your building.","ko":"Jonathan, 안녕하세요! 나를 기억? 나는 건물에 살고있다."},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Oh. Uh. Hi, Anna.","ko":"오. 우. 안녕, 안나."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What are you doing?","ko":"무엇을 하고 있나요?"},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"I am doing my show!","ko":"나는 내 쇼를하고 있어요!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh, sorry. Are you recording?","ko":"오, 죄송합니다. 녹음이 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Yes! And, now I have to record again!","ko":"예! 그리고, 이제 다시 기록해야!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sorry. Have a good show.","ko":"죄송합니다. 좋은 쇼가 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Thank you.","ko":"고마워요."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sorry.","ko":"의논하기"},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"The word of the day is social. Social -","ko":"오늘의 말씀은 사회입니다. 사회 -"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh! Hi!","ko":"오! 안녕!"},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"- is an adjective.","ko":"- 형용사."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi! I’m Anna!","ko":"안녕! 나는 안나 해요!"},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"Hi. I’m Amelia.","ko":"안녕하세요. 나는 Amelia입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Nice to meet you!","ko":"당신을 만나는 좋은!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What are you doing?","ko":"무엇을 하고 있나요?"},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"I’m reading.","ko":"나는 독서입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Are you reading the news? Hi!","ko":"뉴스를 읽으세요? 안녕하세요!"},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"No, I’m reading for my show. (to camera person) Can I read again?","ko":"아니, 나는 내 쇼에 대한 독서입니다. (카메라 사람에게) 나는 다시 읽을 수 있습니까? 영어 수업을 배우자 7 75"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sorry.","ko":"의논하기"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This day is not going well.","ko":"이 날은 잘하지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Anna! Hi! What’re you doing?","ko":"Anna! 안녕하세요! 무엇을하고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I am bothering people, Ms. Weaver.","ko":"나는 두 사람, Ms. 웨버입니다."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Let’s go to my office and talk.","ko":"내 사무실과 대화로 가자."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I like to talk with you, Ms. Weaver.","ko":"나는 당신과 이야기하고 싶습니다, Ms. Weaver."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"It’s Caty.","ko":"그것은 고양이입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Right. Thanks…. Ms. Weaver.","ko":"오른쪽. 감사합니다.... Ms. Weaver. 영어 수업을 배우자 7 76"}],"words":[{"en":"boss","definition":"the person whose job is to tell other workers what to do","ko":"상사"},{"en":"bother","definition":"to annoy someone or to cause someone to feel annoyed","ko":"방해하다"},{"en":"busy","definition":"actively doing something","ko":"바쁜"},{"en":"excited","definition":"very enthusiastic and eager about something","ko":"신난"},{"en":"nervous","definition":"having or showing feelings of being worried and afraid about what might happen","ko":"긴장한"},{"en":"news","definition":"information that is reported in a newspaper, magazine, or a television news program","ko":"뉴스"},{"en":"office","definition":"a building or room in which people work at desks doing business or professional activities","ko":"사무실"},{"en":"read","definition":"to look at and understand the meaning of letters, words, symbols, etc.","ko":"읽다"},{"en":"record","definition":"to store (something, such as sounds, music, images, etc.) on tape or on a disk so that it can be heard or seen later","ko":"녹음하다"},{"en":"show","definition":"a television or radio program","ko":"프로그램·쇼"},{"en":"work","definition":"to do things as part of your job","ko":"일하다"},{"en":"write","definition":"to create (a book, poem, story, etc.) by writing words on paper or on a computer","ko":"쓰다"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 7 - What are you doing?\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n  1. What does Caty say?\na.\t Where are you going?\nb.\t Who are you?\nc.\t What are you doing?\nd.\t What do you want?\n4. What does Anna ask?\na.\t\nAre you reading?\nb.\t\nAre you roaring?\nc.\t\nAre you recording?\n   2. What is Amelia doing?\na.  She doesn’t know.\nb.  She is reading.\nc.  She’s pleading to save her show.\nd.  She is reading for her show.\n5. What is he doing?\na.\t\nHe is doing his shopping.\nb.\t\nHe is reading.\nc.\t\nHe is doing his show.\nd.\t\nHe is writing.\n   3. What does Amelia say?\na.  She is recording.\nb.  She is reading.\nc.  She is bleeding.\nd.  She is feeding.\n6. What does Anna ask?\na.  Water? Are you drinking?\nb.  What are you doing?\nc.  Are you recording?","guide":{"id":7,"focus":"지금 하고 있는 행동을 물어요.","grammar":"be동사 + 동사-ing는 ‘지금 ~하고 있다’라는 현재진행형이에요.","mission":"지금 하는 행동 세 가지를 I’m ~ing으로 말해 보세요.","example":"What are you doing?","exampleKo":"지금 무엇을 하고 있나요?"}},{"id":8,"startPage":82,"endPage":89,"topics":"Times of day: morning, evening, afternoon","strategy":"Use what you know","goals":"Grammar: BE - short answers; simple present tense to describe routine activities Speaking: Times of day; regular activities Pronunciation: Hesitation noise “um;” apologizing with stress or intonation","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello, everyone. Here I am at my new job! Yesterday at my first day of work … Well, let’s not talk about yesterday. Today is a new day! Today I want to apologize to my co-workers.","ko":"안녕하세요, 여러분. 내 새로운 일에 있습니다! 어제 직장에서 ... 잘, 어제에 대해 얘기하지 않습니다. 오늘 새로운 날입니다! 오늘 나는 내 동료들에게 사과하고 싶습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi, Anne. Are you busy?","ko":"안녕, 앤. 당신은 바빴습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anne","en":"Hi, Anna. Yes. At 10 a.m. I am writing. Every day I do my morning show. Sorry!","ko":"안녕하세요, 안나. 예. 오전 10시에서. 나는 쓰기입니다. 매일 나는 내 아침 쇼를합니다. 죄송합니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Okay. See you later, maybe.","ko":"그래. 나중에 봐, 어쩌면."},{"speaker":"Anne","en":"Maybe I’ll see you later.","ko":"어쩌면 나중에 볼 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi, Jonathan. Are you busy?","ko":"안녕하세요, Jonathan. 당신은 바빴습니까?"},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Yes, I’m busy. When the studio light is on, I am recording my evening show.","ko":"예, 난 바쁘다. 스튜디오 조명이 켜지면, 나는 내 저녁 쇼를 기록합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Right. Sorry about yesterday.","ko":"오른쪽. 어제에 대해 죄송합니다."},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"No worries.","ko":"아무 걱정도 없다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"May I see the studio?","ko":"스튜디오를 볼 수 있나요?"},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Um, maybe another time? Right now I am busy.","ko":"우, 어쩌면 또 다른 시간? 지금 나는 바쁘다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sure. Okay, ’bye.","ko":"물론, ’bye."},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"‘Bye.","ko":"‘Bye.’에 대하여"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi, Amelia! Are you busy?","ko":"안녕하세요, 아멜리아! 당신은 바쁜?"},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"I’m a little busy.","ko":"나는 조금 바빠요."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I want to say I’m sorry for yesterday.","ko":"어제 미안 해요."},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"It’s okay, Anna.","ko":"안나는 괜찮습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well, I am sorry.","ko":"잘, 미안 해요."},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"It’s okay, Anna. Come by this afternoon.","ko":"안나. 이 오후에 가자."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Okay.","ko":"이름 *"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Anna.","ko":"안나."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes, Ms. Weaver.","ko":"예, Ms. 웨버."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Are you busy?","ko":"바쁘세요?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes, Ms. Weaver. I am busy.","ko":"예, Ms. 웨버. 나는 바쁘다."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"My office. 5:00 p.m.","ko":"내 사무실. 오후 5시"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"5:00 p.m.","ko":"오후 5시"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Come in.","ko":"에 있다."},{"speaker":"Coworkers","en":"Surprise!","ko":"놀람!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"A party! Awesome! And I still have my job! Phew!* Until next time! * Phew! is a sound used to show that you are relieved, tired or hot.","ko":"파티! 굉장! 그리고 나는 여전히 내 일을 가지고! Phew!* 다음 시간까지! * Phew! 당신이 구호하고 피곤하거나 뜨겁다는 것을 보여주기 위해 사용되는 소리입니다. 영어 수업 8 84을 배우십시오"}],"words":[{"en":"afternoon","definition":"the middle part of the day : the part of the day between noon and evening","ko":"오후"},{"en":"apologize","definition":"to express regret for doing or saying something wrong : to give or make an apology","ko":"사과하다"},{"en":"evening","definition":"the last part of the day and early part of the night","ko":"저녁"},{"en":"job","definition":"the work that a person does regularly in order to earn money","ko":"직업"},{"en":"later","definition":"happening near the end of a process, activity, series, life, etc.","ko":"나중에"},{"en":"light","definition":"a source of light (such as an electric lamp)","ko":"가벼운·빛"},{"en":"maybe","definition":"possibly but not certainly","ko":"아마도"},{"en":"morning","definition":"the early part of the day : the time of day from sunrise until noon","ko":"아침"},{"en":"now","definition":"at the present time","ko":"지금"},{"en":"studio","definition":"the building or room where an artist works","ko":"방송 스튜디오"},{"en":"surprise","definition":"an unexpected event, piece of information, etc.","ko":"놀라움"},{"en":"yesterday","definition":"the day before today Times of Day","ko":"어제"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 8 - Are You Busy?\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Anna say?\na.\t She says that she is busy. \nb.\t She says that she sees bees. \nc.\t She says that she is not busy. \nd.\t  She says that she wants to meet at \n5pm. \t\n4. What does Anne do at 10 am?\na.\t Anne talks about human rights. \nb.\t Anne writes at 10 am. \nc.\t Anne is recording at 10 am. \nd.\t Anne is running at 10 am. \n2. What does Amelia say?\na.\t Amelia says she is busy. \nb.\t Amelia says she is not busy. \nc.\t Amelia says she is a little busy. \n5. What does Anna want to do?\na.\t She wants to see the studio. \nb.\t She wants to record a show. \nc.\t She wants to listen to music. \n3. What is Jonathan doing when he \nturns the studio light on? \na.\t He is calling his friends. \nb.\t He is recording his show. \nc.\t He is watching a show. \nd.\t He is taking a nap.","guide":{"id":8,"focus":"하루 일과와 바쁜 정도를 이야기해요.","grammar":"I work every day처럼 반복되는 습관은 현재형으로 말해요. Are you busy?에는 Yes, I am으로 답해요.","mission":"아침·오후·저녁에 하는 일을 하나씩 말해 보세요.","example":"I’m a little busy.","exampleKo":"저 조금 바빠요."}},{"id":9,"startPage":90,"endPage":99,"topics":"Talk about weather Agree and disagree Use Fahrenheit or Celsius Short answers","strategy":"Look for Ways to Practice","goals":"Grammar: Short answers Pronunciation: Reduced form of short affir­ mative answers (Yessitis) Speaking: Different intonations of ‘oh’","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh, hi, everyone! Here in Washington, DC, the weather changes often. One day is cold and windy. But the next day is warm and sunny! So, every day I check the forecast. Hello, Phone? What is today’s temperature?","ko":"오, 안녕하세요, 여러분! 여기 워싱턴 DC에서, 날씨가 종종 변경됩니다. 하루는 추운 바람입니다. 그러나 다음 날은 따뜻하고 화창합니다! 그래서, 매일 나는 예측을 확인합니다. 안녕하세요, 전화? 오늘의 온도는 무엇입니까?"},{"speaker":"Phone","en":"Today it is 18 degrees ...","ko":"오늘 그것은 18도 ..."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Eighteen degrees! That is cold!","ko":"여덟도! 그것은 추운!"},{"speaker":"Phone","en":"… eighteen degrees Celsius.","ko":"... 8een도 섭씨."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh, Celsius. That is 65 degrees Fahrenheit. That’s warm.","ko":"Oh, Celsius. 그것은 65도 Fahrenheit입니다. 그것은 따뜻합니다."},{"speaker":"Phone","en":"Yes, Anna. It is warm.","ko":"예, 안나. 따뜻합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Excuse me, Phone. Is it windy today?","ko":"죄송합니다, 전화. 오늘 바람이 났습니까?"},{"speaker":"Phone","en":"No, it is not windy today.","ko":"아니, 그것은 오늘 바람이 없습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Is it sunny today?","ko":"오늘도 햇볕이 났습니까?"},{"speaker":"Phone","en":"Yes, Anna. It is sunny.","ko":"예, Anna. 그것은 햇살입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Excuse me, Phone?","ko":", 전화가?"},{"speaker":"Phone","en":"Yes, Anna.","ko":"예, 안나."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Is it snowy today?","ko":"오늘 눈이 났습니까?"},{"speaker":"Phone","en":"No, Anna. It is not snowy.","ko":"아니, 안나. 그것은 눈이 없다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thank you, Phone!","ko":"감사합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Today the weather is warm and sunny -- great for seeing Washington, D.C.","ko":"오늘 날씨는 따뜻하고 화창합니다 -- 워싱턴, D.C.를 참조하십시오."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Phone! It is not warm and sunny! It is cold and windy and snowy!","ko":"전화! 따뜻하고 화창하지 않습니다! 그것은 감기와 바람과 눈입니다!"},{"speaker":"Phone","en":"Anna, it is not cold, windy, or snowy. It is warm and sunny … in Mexico City, Mexico.","ko":"Anna, 그것은 감기, 바람, 또는 눈이 아닙니다. 그것은 따뜻하고 맑은 ... 멕시코 시티에서."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh. I see. Mexico.","ko":"오. 나는. 멕시코."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Washington weather changes often. Remember to check the forecast -- the right forecast.","ko":"워싱턴 날씨가 자주 변경됩니다. 예측을 확인하려면 -- 올바른 예측."},{"speaker":"Phone","en":"Yes, Anna. Next time remember to check the right fore…","ko":"예, Anna. 다음 시간 오른쪽을 확인 기억 ..."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Okay, thank you Phone. Goodbye, Phone. Until next time","ko":"안녕하세요, 전화. Goodbye, 전화. 다음 시간까지 영어 수업 9 94을 배울 수 있습니다"}],"words":[{"en":"Celsius","definition":"relating to or having a scale for measuring temperature on which the boil­ ing point of water is at 100 degrees and the freezing point of water is at 0 degrees","ko":"섭씨"},{"en":"change","definition":"to become different","ko":"변화하다"},{"en":"check","definition":"to get information by looking at something, asking about something, etc.","ko":"확인하다"},{"en":"cold","definition":"having a very low temperature","ko":"추운"},{"en":"degree","definition":"a unit for measuring temperature","ko":"도·온도 단위"},{"en":"Fahrenheit","definition":"relating to or having a scale for measuring temperature on which the boiling point of water is at 212 degrees above zero and the freezing point is at 32 de­ grees above zero","ko":"화씨"},{"en":"forecast","definition":"a statement about what you think is going to happen in the future","ko":"일기예보"},{"en":"phone","definition":"a device that is connected to a telephone system and that you use to listen or speak to someone who is somewhere else","ko":"전화기"},{"en":"snowy","definition":"having falling snow or covered with snow","ko":"눈이 오는"},{"en":"sunny","definition":"having plenty of bright sunlight","ko":"화창한"},{"en":"temperature","definition":"a measurement that indicates how hot or cold something is; a mea­ surement in degrees showing the heat of something (such as air or water)","ko":"기온"},{"en":"warm","definition":"somewhat hot; not cool or cold","ko":"따뜻한"},{"en":"weather","definition":"the temperature and other outside conditions (such as rain, cloudiness, etc.) at a particular time and place","ko":"날씨"},{"en":"windy","definition":"having a lot of wind","ko":"바람 부는"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 9 - Is It Cold?\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Anna want to know?\na.\t Anna wants to know what time it is.\nb.\t Anna wants to learn about today’s \nnews.\nc.\t Anna wants to know the temperature.\nd.\t Anna wants to know how to make tea.\n4. What does she ask?\na.\t She asks if it is sunny.\nb.\t She asks if it is windy.\nc.\t She asks if it is snowy.\nd.\t She asks if it is rainy.\n2. What does the phone say?\na.  “Yes, Anna, it is a farm.”\nb.  “Yes, Anna, it is warm.”\nc.  “Yes, Anna, I have no charm.”\nd.  “Yes, Anna, it smells like a barn.”\n5. What do you learn about the weather \nin Washington, D.C.?\na.\t It is warm today.\nb.\t It is sunny today.\nc.\t It is rainy.\nd.\t It is cold today.\n3. What is the weather like today?\na.  It is windy today.\nb.  It is just like Wednesday.\nc.  It is not windy today.\nd.  It is warm today.","guide":{"id":9,"focus":"날씨를 묻고 예보를 이야기해요.","grammar":"Is it cold?처럼 날씨는 it을 주어로 써요. Yes, it is / No, it isn’t로 답해요.","mission":"오늘의 온도와 날씨를 한 문장씩 말해 보세요.","example":"Is it windy today?","exampleKo":"오늘 바람이 부나요?"}},{"id":10,"startPage":100,"endPage":109,"topics":"Giving directions Sequence of events with “then” Asking questions","strategy":"Use images","goals":"Grammar: Locating places; Imperatives; There is /There are Pronunciation: Using rising intonation to check understanding Speaking: Giving simple directions","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi! Today, my friend Ashley, is coming over. I am showing her my new apartment! Oh! That’s Ashley calling.","ko":"안녕하세요! 오늘, 내 친구 애슐리, 이상 온다. 나는 그녀의 새로운 아파트를 보여! 오! 그건 애슐리 전화입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi Ashley!","ko":"안녕하세요."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Hi Anna! I’m coming to your apartment. Where is your apartment?","ko":"안녕 안나! 나는 아파트에 왔습니다. 아파트는 어디에 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"My apartment is near the Columbia Heights Metro.","ko":"내 아파트는 Columbia Heights Metro 근처에 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"It is near the Columbia Heights Metro?","ko":"Columbia Heights Metro 근처에 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes. Exit the Metro and turn right. Then at the bus station turn left. Then walk straight ahead.","ko":"예. 메트로를 나와 오른쪽으로 켭니다. 그런 다음 버스 정류장에서 좌회전합니다. 그런 다음 곧 걷습니다."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Okay. Exit Metro, turn right, turn left, then go straight ahead?","ko":"괜찮아. 지하철을 종료, 우회전, 왼쪽을 우회전, 그 후 곧 이동?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes. My apartment is near a coffee shop.","ko":"예. 내 아파트는 커피숍 근처에 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Okay. See you soon!","ko":"안녕하세요. 곧 봐!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi, Ashley.","ko":"안녕, 애슐리."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Anna, Which coffee shop? There are three coffee shops.","ko":"안나, 어떤 커피 가게? 3 개의 커피 숍이 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Okay, my apartment is across from a big department store.","ko":"좋은, 내 아파트는 큰 백화점에서 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"A big department store? Ah, I see it!","ko":"큰 백화점? 아, 나는 그것을 본다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Okay! Bye, Ashley. See you soon!","ko":"감사합니다! , 애슐리. 곧 보자!"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Okay. See you soon.","ko":"잘 부탁합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Ashley! Ashley! Ashley! Over here! It’s Anna! It’s Anna! Hi!","ko":"Ashley! Ashley! Ashley! 여기에! 그것은 안나입니다! 그것은 안나입니다! 안녕하세요!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I love having my friends over. Come on!","ko":"나는 내 친구를 사랑합니다. 어서!"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Great!","ko":"위대한! 영어 수업을 배우자 10 103"}],"words":[{"en":"ahead","definition":"to or toward the place where someone is going","ko":"앞으로"},{"en":"bus","definition":"a large vehicle that is used for carrying passengers especially along a particular route at particular times","ko":"버스"},{"en":"coffee shop","definition":"a small restaurant that serves coffee and other drinks as well as simple foods","ko":"커피숍"},{"en":"department store","definition":"a large store that has separate areas in which different kinds of products are sold","ko":"백화점"},{"en":"exit","definition":"to go out of a place","ko":"출구"},{"en":"left","definition":"located on the same side of your body as your heart","ko":"왼쪽"},{"en":"Metro","definition":"an underground railway system in some cities (also called subway)","ko":"지하철"},{"en":"right","definition":"located on the side of your body that is away from your heart","ko":"오른쪽"},{"en":"station","definition":"place where buses, trains, etc., regularly stop so that passengers can get on and off","ko":"역"},{"en":"straight","definition":"in a straight or direct way","ko":"똑바로"},{"en":"then","definition":"used to indicate what happened or happens next","ko":"그다음"},{"en":"turn","definition":"to cause your body or a part of your body to face a different direction","ko":"돌다"},{"en":"walk","definition":"to move with your legs at a speed that is slower than running","ko":"걷다"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 10 - Come Over to My Place\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What do you do after you exit the \nmetro?\na.\t Turn right after you exit.\nb.\t Turn at the light.\nc.\t Turn and exit.\nd.\t Turn into the bus station.\n4. Then where do you go?\na.\t Then you exit the coffee shop.\nb.\t Stay out of the coffee shop.\nc.\t Then you go to the copy shop.\nd.\t You walk to the coffee shop.\n2. Where do you turn?\na.  Turn off the light.\nb.  Make a right turn.\nc.  Turn left at the light.\nd.  After the right.\n5. Where is Anna’s apartment?\na.\t It is next to the department store\nb.\t It is on the corner by the department \nstore.\nc.\t It is across from the department store.\nd.\t It is above the department store.\n3. Where do you turn after the bus \nstation?\na.  Exit the bus station and turn right.\nb.  When you go into the bus station.\nc.  Pass the bus station and turn left.\nd.  Before you get to the bus station.\n6. Where is Anna’s apartment?\na.\t She does not see a coffee shop.\nb.\t Ashley sees three coffee shops.\nc.\t There are no coffee shops on the street.\nd.\t She will meet Anna in the coffee shop.\nMap to Anna’s Place","guide":{"id":10,"focus":"길 찾기와 방향 안내를 연습해요.","grammar":"Go straight는 ‘직진하세요’, turn left는 ‘왼쪽으로 도세요’라는 명령문이에요.","mission":"집에서 가까운 가게까지 가는 길을 영어로 알려 주세요.","example":"Then turn left.","exampleKo":"그다음 왼쪽으로 도세요."}},{"id":11,"startPage":110,"endPage":119,"topics":"Describing neighborhoods Asking for information","strategy":"Ask Questions","goals":"Grammar: Prepositions (across from, behind); cardinal numbers indicating quantity; Singular/Plural introduction Speaking: Expressing gratitude; asking questions to check understanding Pronunciation: Emphasis on words expressing feelings","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello! DC is a city for walking. In our neighborhood, I can do all my errands. Marsha, before we get ice cream, I need to return three books to the library. Where is the library?","ko":"안녕하세요! DC는 걷기위한 도시입니다. 우리 이웃에서 나는 모든 errands를 할 수 있습니다. Marsha, 우리가 아이스크림을 얻기 전에, 나는 도서관에 세 권의 책을 돌려야합니다. 라이브러리는 어디에 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"It is on this street on the corner.","ko":"구석에 이 거리에 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Awesome!","ko":"기본 정보"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Let’s go!","ko":"가자!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Marsha, I can return the books here.","ko":"Marsha, 나는 여기에 책을 반환 할 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Anna, what are those in the books?","ko":"Anna, 그 책은 무엇입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Marsha, these are letters to my family and friends back home … four letters! Is there a post office near here?","ko":"Marsha,이 편지는 내 가족과 친구에 다시 집 ... 네 글자! 여기에 우체국이 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Um, no. The post office is far from here. But there is a mailbox across from the store.","ko":"우우, 아니오. 우체국은 여기에서 멀리 있습니다. 그러나 상점에서 사서함이 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Awesome! Let’s go! (At the mailbox)","ko":"굉장! 가자! (사서함이 아닌)"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Marsha, now I need to buy stamps.","ko":"Marsha, 지금 나는 스탬프를 구입해야합니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Do you have cash?","ko":"현금이 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No. Is there a bank near here?","ko":"아니요. 근처에 은행이 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"There is a bank behind you.","ko":"뒤에 은행이 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thanks, Marsha. You know our neighborhood so well.","ko":"감사합니다, Marsha. 당신은 우리의 이웃을 너무 잘 알고 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Now I have cash. I can buy stamps.","ko":"이제 현금이 있습니다. 나는 스탬프를 살 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"That store sells stamps.","ko":"그 가게는 스탬프를 판매합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Wait here. Anna: I have stamps.","ko":"여기. Anna : 나는 스탬프가 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Wow, you’re fast.","ko":"와우, 당신은 빠릅니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thank you, thank you letters, for sending my words… my love … to my family and friends -","ko":"감사합니다, 내 단어를 보내 주셔서 감사합니다. 내 사랑 ... 내 가족과 친구에게 -"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Do you have more cash?","ko":"더 많은 현금이 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I do! Marsha & Anna: Ice cream!!","ko":"나는! 마샤 & 안나 : 아이스크림!!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I love my new neighborhood! Everything is near our apartment! Even hair salons*, and ice cream!","ko":"나는 내 새로운 이웃을 사랑! 모든 것은 우리의 아파트 근처에 있습니다! 심지어 헤어 살롱 *, 아이스크림!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Until next time! * a business that gives customers beauty treatments (such as haircuts)","ko":"다음 시간까지! * 고객 미용 치료 (예 : 헤어 컷)을 제공하는 사업은 영어 수업 11 113을 배우십시오."}],"words":[{"en":"bank","definition":"a business where people keep their money, borrow money, etc., or the building where such a business operates","ko":"은행"},{"en":"buy","definition":"to get (something) by paying money for it","ko":"사다"},{"en":"cash","definition":"money in the form of coins and bills","ko":"현금"},{"en":"corner","definition":"the place where two streets or roads meet","ko":"모퉁이"},{"en":"errand","definition":"a short journey that you take to do or get something","ko":"볼일"},{"en":"fast","definition":"moving or able to move quickly","ko":"빠른"},{"en":"get","definition":"to obtain (something)","ko":"얻다"},{"en":"ice cream","definition":"a frozen food containing sweetened and flavored cream","ko":"아이스크림"},{"en":"library","definition":"place where books, magazines, and other materials (such as videos and musical recordings) are available for people to use or borrow","ko":"도서관"},{"en":"mailbox","definition":"a public box in which letters and packages are placed to be collected and sent out","ko":"우편함"},{"en":"post office","definition":"a building where the mail for a local area is sent and received","ko":"우체국"},{"en":"return","definition":"to bring, give, send, or take (something) to the place that it came from or the place where it should go","ko":"돌아오다"},{"en":"sell","definition":"to exchange (something) for money","ko":"팔다"},{"en":"send","definition":"to cause (a letter, an e-mail, a package, etc.) to go or to be carried from one place or person to another","ko":"보내다"},{"en":"stamp","definition":"a small piece of paper that you buy and then stick to an envelope or package to pay the cost of mailing it","ko":"우표"},{"en":"store","definition":"a building or room where things are sold Cut out to use in the “Thankful Tree” activity","ko":"상점"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 11 - This is My Neighborhood\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1.Is there a post office near here?\na.\t The post office is near here.\nb.\t There is not a post office near here.\nc.\t The post office is next to a farm.\nd.\t The post office is on the corner.\n4. What is Anna doing with the three \nbooks?\na.\t Anna is sending the three books to her \nfamily.\nb.\t Anna needs to return the books to a \ndepartment store.\nc.\t Anna needs to return three books to the \nlibrary.\nd.\t Anna is taking the books home from the \nlibrary.\n2. Where is a mailbox?\na.\t There is a mailbox far from the store.\nb.\t There is a mailbox behind the store.\nc.\t There is a mailbox across from the store.\nd.\t There is a mailbox inside the store.\n5. Where is the bank?\na.\t The bank is behind Marsha.\nb.\t The bank is far from here.\nc.\t The bank is next to the library.\nd.\t The bank is behind Anna.\n3. How many letters does Anna have?\na.\t Anna has four letters.\nb.\t Anna has forty letters.\nc.\t Anna has one letter.\nd.\t Anna has fourteen letters.","guide":{"id":11,"focus":"동네 가게와 시설의 위치를 알려요.","grammar":"There is는 ‘~이 하나 있어요’, There are는 ‘~들이 있어요’라는 뜻이에요.","mission":"우리 동네의 도서관·은행·우체국을 영어로 소개해 보세요.","example":"Where is the library?","exampleKo":"도서관은 어디에 있나요?"}},{"id":12,"startPage":120,"endPage":129,"topics":"Family members Family relationships","strategy":"Find and Apply Patterns","goals":"Grammar: Auxiliary ‘do’ and the verb ‘make’ Pronunciation: Different ways to pronounce ‘aunt’ Speaking: Asking about a problem","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello! Washington, D.C. has many beautiful parks. In fact, this park reminds me of my home very far away.","ko":"안녕하세요! 워싱턴 D.C.는 많은 아름다운 공원을 가지고 있습니다. 사실,이 공원은 내 집의 저를 멀리 생각한다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Anna, here’s your coffee.","ko":"Anna, 여기 커피입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thanks, Marsha.","ko":"감사합니다, Marsha."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"What’s wrong?","ko":"무엇이 잘못되었습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I’m thinking about my family. I’m feeling homesick.","ko":"나는 내 가족에 대해 생각하고 있습니다. 나는 homeick 느낌입니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Do you want to talk about it?","ko":"그것에 대해 이야기하고 싶습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sure! I have some photos.","ko":"확실히! 나는 몇 가지 사진이 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Yes. Yes, you do!","ko":"예. 네, 넌!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Photos really help.","ko":"사진은 정말 도움이됩니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This is my mother and this is my father. They are rodeo clowns.","ko":"이것은 나의 어머니이고 이것은 나의 아버지입니다. 그들은 rodeo clowns입니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"What do rodeo clowns do?","ko":"rodeo clowns는 무엇을합니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"They make jokes at a rodeo. They make people laugh.","ko":"그들은 로데오에서 농담을합니다. 그들은 사람들이 웃음을합니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"That-That’;s very different.","ko":"그게 다야; 매우 다른."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Who is that woman in the picture?","ko":"사진에 여자는 누구입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"That is my Aunt Lavender. She is my mom’s sister. She loves gardening and makes spoons.","ko":"그건 내 이모 라벤더입니다. 그녀는 나의 엄마의 자매입니다. 그녀는 원예를 사랑하고 숟가락을 만듭니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"She makes spoons?","ko":"그녀는 숟가락을 만든다?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Of course.","ko":"물론."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"That, too, is very different.","ko":"그것은, 너무, 아주 다릅니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh! This is my Uncle John. He is my father’s brother.","ko":"오! 이것은 내 삼촌 존입니다. 그는 아버지의 형제입니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"What does Uncle John do?","ko":"삼촌 존은 무엇을합니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"He’s a chicken farmer. And makes guitars. He’s awesome, and I’m his favorite niece.","ko":"그는 닭 농부입니다. 그리고 기타를 만든다. 그는 최고이며, 나는 그의 마음에 드는 niece입니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Who are they?","ko":"그들은 누구인가?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"They are my cousins. They are my Uncle John’s daughter and son.","ko":"그들은 내 사촌입니다. 그들은 내 삼촌 존의 딸과 아들입니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"What do they do?","ko":"그들은 무엇을합니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"They raise sheep and make sweaters.","ko":"그들은 양을 올리고 스웨터를 만듭니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Yeah, that’s not a surprise.","ko":"그래, 그건 놀라지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Thanks for showing me your family photos. Your family is very different.","ko":"당신의 가족 사진을 보여주는 감사합니다. 당신의 가족은 아주 다릅니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I do feel better. Thanks for listening. I have many more photos!","ko":"나는 더 나은 느낌. 청취 주셔서 감사합니다. 나는 더 많은 사진을 가지고!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Yeah. Yeah, you do.","ko":"그래. 그래, 당신은 할."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Washington, DC is my new home. But I like remembering my old home, too.","ko":"워싱턴 DC는 내 새로운 가정입니다. 그러나 나는 내 오래된 집을 기억하고 싶습니다. 12 123을 배우십시오."}],"words":[{"en":"clown","definition":"someone who often does funny things to make people laugh","ko":"광대"},{"en":"different","definition":"not ordinary or common; unusual","ko":"다른"},{"en":"feel","definition":"used to describe or ask about someone’s physical or mental state","ko":"느끼다"},{"en":"garden","definition":"to work in a garden; to take care of the plants in a garden","ko":"정원"},{"en":"guitar","definition":"a musical instrument that is held against the front of your body and that has usually six strings which are played with your fingers or with a pick","ko":"기타"},{"en":"homesick","definition":"sad because you are away from your family and home","ko":"고향이 그리운"},{"en":"joke","definition":"something said or done to cause laughter","ko":"농담"},{"en":"laugh","definition":"to show that you are happy or that you think something is funny by smiling and making a sound from your throat","ko":"웃다"},{"en":"make","definition":"to build, create, or produce (something) by work or effort","ko":"만들다"},{"en":"park","definition":"piece of public land in or near a city that is kept free of houses and other buildings and can be used for pleasure and exercise","ko":"공원"},{"en":"photo (photograph)","definition":"a picture made by a camera","ko":"사진"},{"en":"raise","definition":"to keep and take care of (animals or crops)","ko":"키우다"},{"en":"remind","definition":"to cause (someone) to remember something","ko":"떠올리게 하다"},{"en":"rodeo","definition":"an event in which people compete at riding horses and bulls, catching animals with ropes, etc.","ko":"로데오"},{"en":"sheep","definition":"an animal with a thick woolly coat that is often raised for meat or for its wool and skin","ko":"양"},{"en":"spoon","definition":"an eating or cooking tool that has a small shallow bowl attached to a handle","ko":"숟가락"},{"en":"sweater","definition":"a warm usually knitted piece of clothing for the upper part of your body","ko":"스웨터"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 12 - Meet My Family\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. Who is Aunt Lavender?\na.\t\t She is Anna’s sister.\nb.\t\t She is Anna’s mother.\nc.\t\t She is the sister of Anna’s mom.\nd.\t\t She is Anna’s niece.\n4.  What do Anna’s cousins do?\na.\t\nThey like to sleep. \nb.\t\nThey collect feathers.\nc.\t\nThey raise sheep.\nd.\t\nThey wear sweatpants.\n2.  Who is Uncle John?\na.\t\t Uncle John is the father of Anna’s \nbrother.\nb.\t\t Uncle John is the brother of Anna’s \nfather.\nc.\t\t Uncle John is Anna’s father.\nd.\t\t Uncle John is Anna’s brother.\n5. What do Anna’s mother and father \ndo?\na.\t\nThey make jokes at rodeos.\nb.\t\nThey own a rodeo.\nc.\t\nThey love to laugh.\nd.\t\nThey ride horses in a rodeo.\n3.  Who are they? (The two young \n     people in a photo)\na.\t\t They are Uncle John’s mother and father.\nb.\t\t They are Uncle John’s brother and sister.\nc.\t\t They are Anna’s friends.\nd.\t\t They are Anna’s cousins.","guide":{"id":12,"focus":"가족을 소개하고 기분을 표현해요.","grammar":"Do you~?는 행동이나 상태를 물을 때 자주 써요. make는 ‘만들다’예요.","mission":"가족 사진 한 장을 보고 관계를 영어로 소개해 보세요.","example":"This is my mother.","exampleKo":"이분은 저희 어머니세요."}},{"id":13,"startPage":130,"endPage":138,"topics":"Usual and unusual activities","strategy":"Make an Inference","goals":"Grammar: Frequency adverbs; cause and effect phrases Pronunciation: Blended sounds Speaking: Using frequency adverbs to talk about cause and effect","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello! In Washington D.C. there are many things to do on a Sunday afternoon. I like to exercise. I like to shop. I like to garden. But today I feel bored. When I feel bored, I always look for something unusual to do! I hear music. Let’s go see! What is going on here?","ko":"안녕하세요! 워싱턴 D.C.에는 일요일 오후에 할 수있는 많은 것들이 있습니다. 나는 운동하고 싶습니다. 나는 가게를 좋아합니다. 나는 정원과 같습니다. 그러나 오늘 나는 지루하게 느낍니다. 지루한 느낌이있을 때, 나는 항상 뭔가 특별한 것을 봅니다! 나는 음악을 듣습니다. 봅시다! 여기에서가는 것은 무엇입니까?"},{"speaker":"Rebecca","en":"It’s a big birthday party for the writer William Shakespeare.","ko":"윌리엄 셰익스피어 작가를위한 큰 생일 파티입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This is a party for William Shakespeare?","ko":"윌리엄 셰익스피어의 파티는?"},{"speaker":"Rebecca","en":"Yes!","ko":"네!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Awesome!","ko":"기본 정보"},{"speaker":"Rebecca","en":"Awesome!","ko":"기본 정보"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This is a drum band. I never listen to a drum band. But today I am listening to a drum band because it’s Shakespeare’s birthday!","ko":"이것은 드럼 밴드입니다. 나는 드럼 밴드를 듣지 않습니다. 그러나 오늘 나는 Shakespeare의 생일이기 때문에 드럼 밴드에 듣습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This is a puppet show. I never watch puppet shows. But today I am watching a puppet show because it’s Shakespeare’s birthday!","ko":"이것은 인형 쇼입니다. 나는 인형 쇼를 볼 수 없습니다. 그러나 오늘 나는 Shakespeare의 생일이기 때문에 인형 쇼를보고 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"My clothes are usual. His clothes are unusual. In Washington, D.C. seeing a politician or even the President is usual. Seeing the Queen of England is very unusual! Your majesty!","ko":"내 옷은 평소입니다. 그의 옷은 특이합니다. 워싱턴에서 D.C.는 정치인 또는 대통령조차 평소입니다. 영국의 여왕을 보는 것은 매우 특이합니다! 당신의 majesty!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This is sword fighting. I never sword fight. But today I am sword fighting because it’s Shakespeare’s birthday!","ko":"이것은 칼 싸움입니다. 나는 결코 칼 싸움을하지 않습니다. 그러나 오늘 나는 Shakespeare의 생일이기 때문에 칼 싸움입니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"There are many things to do on a Sunday in Washington, D.C. -- some usual, some unusual.","ko":"워싱턴 D.C.에서 일요일에 할 수있는 많은 것들이 있습니다. -- 일부 보통, 약간 특이한."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Today, I am not bored because … it is William Shakespeare’s birthday!","ko":"오늘 저는 윌리엄 셰익스피어의 생일이기 때문에 지루하지 않습니다! 영어 레슨 13 133을 알아봅시다"}],"words":[{"en":"band","definition":"a usually small group of musicians who play popular music together","ko":"악단"},{"en":"because","definition":"for the reason that","ko":"왜냐하면"},{"en":"birthday","definition":"the day when someone was born or the anniversary of that day","ko":"생일"},{"en":"bored","definition":"tired and annoyed by too much of the same thing; not interested","ko":"지루한"},{"en":"drum","definition":"a musical instrument that is made with a thin layer of skin or plastic stretched over the end of a round frame and that is played by hitting the skin or plastic with sticks or with your hands","ko":"드럼"},{"en":"exercise","definition":"physical activity that is done in order to become stronger and healthier","ko":"운동"},{"en":"fight","definition":"to use weapons or physical force to try to hurt someone, to defeat an enemy, etc. or to struggle in battle or physical combat","ko":"싸우다"},{"en":"party","definition":"a social event in which entertainment, food, and drinks are provided","ko":"파티"},{"en":"politician","definition":"someone who is active in government usually as an elected official","ko":"정치인"},{"en":"President","definition":"the head of the government in some countries","ko":"대통령"},{"en":"puppet","definition":"a doll that is moved by putting your hand inside it or by pulling strings or wires that are attached to it","ko":"인형극 인형"},{"en":"Queen","definition":"a woman who rules a country and who usually inherits her position and rules for life","ko":"여왕"},{"en":"shop","definition":"to visit places where goods are sold in order to look at and buy things","ko":"가게"},{"en":"show","definition":"a performance in a theater that usually includes singing and dancing","ko":"보여주다"},{"en":"sword","definition":"a weapon with a long metal blade that has a sharp point and edge","ko":"검"},{"en":"unusual","definition":"different or strange in a way that attracts attention","ko":"특이한"},{"en":"usual","definition":"done, found, or used most of the time or in most cases, or normal or regular","ko":"보통의"},{"en":"watch","definition":"to look at (someone or something) for an amount of time and pay attention to what is happening","ko":"지켜보다"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 13 - Happy Birthday, William \nShakespeare!\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Anna like to do on \nSunday?\na.\t She likes to talk and she likes to mop.\nb.\t She likes to eat and she likes to walk.\nc.\t She likes to exercise and she likes to \nshop.\nd.\t She likes to cook and she likes to read.\n3. What does Anna do when she is \nbored?\na.\t Anna always looks for something usual.\nb.\t Anna looks for something unusual.\nc.\t Anna never looks for something unusual \nto do.\n2. How does Anna feel today?\na.\t Anna feels remorse.\nb.\t Anna feels mad..\nc.\t Anna feels happy.\nd.\t Anna feels bored.\n4. What does Anna say about puppet \nshows?\na.\t She never watches puppet shows.\nb.\t She always watches puppet shows.\nc.\t She does not like puppet shows.\nd.\t She likes puppet shows","guide":{"id":13,"focus":"행사와 생일을 이야기해요.","grammar":"always, sometimes, never는 얼마나 자주 하는지 표현해요. because는 ‘왜냐하면’이에요.","mission":"최근 축하했던 일을 한 가지 이야기해 보세요.","example":"It’s a birthday party.","exampleKo":"생일 파티예요."}},{"id":14,"startPage":139,"endPage":149,"topics":"Describing clothing colors and sizes Making suggestions; giving compliments","strategy":"Personalize","goals":"Grammar: Position of adjectives before nouns; use of two phrasal verbs ‘put on’ and ‘take off’ Speaking: Making a suggestion Pronunciation: Using color adjectives with nouns","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi, there! In Washington, D.C. people do many things in the evening. They go listen to music. They eat at a restaurant. They go to the theater.","ko":"안녕하세요, 거기! 워싱턴에서, D.C. 사람들은 저녁에 많은 것들을합니다. 그들은 음악을 듣고. 그들은 레스토랑에 먹는다. 그들은 극장으로 이동합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Tonight I am going to the theater with my friends. But I don’t know what clothes to wear. Maybe this magazine can help.","ko":"밤 나는 친구와 극장에 가고있다. 그러나 나는 옷을 입는 것을 모른다. 어쩌면이 잡지는 도움이 될 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Her clothes are beautiful! I really want a friend like her to help me.","ko":"그녀의 옷은 아름답습니다! 나는 정말 저를 돕기 위해 친구를 원합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Who are you?","ko":"당신은 누구입니까?"},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"I am Genie! You want help. I am here to help you find the right clothes!","ko":"나는 Genie입니다! 당신은 도움을 원합니다. 나는 당신이 올바른 옷을 찾을 수 있도록 여기에 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Awesome! How about jeans and a t-shirt?","ko":"굉장! 청바지와 티셔츠는 어떻습니까?"},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"No! Jeans and a t-shirt are too casual. How about something more formal?","ko":"아니요! 청바지와 티셔츠도 캐주얼합니다. 더 많은 공식적인 것은 어떻습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sure! Wow! Genie, this dress is beautiful. But it’s not the right size. It’s too small.","ko":"물론! 와우! Genie,이 드레스는 아름답습니다. 그러나 올바른 크기가 아닙니다. 너무 작습니다."},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"Yes, it is too small. But green looks great on you.","ko":"네, 너무 작습니다. 그러나 녹색은 당신을 멋지게 보입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thanks.","ko":"감사합니다."},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"Take off the green dress. Let’s try a green shirt and a skirt.","ko":"녹색 옷을 벗고. 녹색 셔츠와 스커트를 시도합시다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh, Genie! This green shirt is too large and this orange skirt is too orange.","ko":"Oh, Genie! 이 녹색 셔츠는 너무 크고이 오렌지 스커트는 너무 오렌지입니다."},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"Yes, the right size for you is medium. Let’s try again.","ko":"네, 중간에 적합한 크기입니다. 다시 시도합시다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh, I don’t like this outfit.","ko":"오, 나는이 의상을 좋아하지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"No. That does not match.","ko":"아니. 그것은 일치하지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Nothing. These clothes are formal: a suit jacket, a dress shirt and a tie! They look great!","ko":"아무것도. 이 옷은 공식적입니다 : 한 벌 재킷, 드레스 셔츠 및 타이! 그들은 멋지다!"},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"Those clothes look great … for a man! Something is wrong.","ko":"그 옷은 멋지다 ... 남자를 위해! 뭔가 잘못된다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Let me see.","ko":"나를 볼 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"There. Now try.","ko":"더. 지금 시도합니다."},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"Oh. Thanks! Now these clothes look great on you!","ko":"오. 감사합니다! 이제이 옷은 당신을 멋지다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"They do! Um, Genie, can you put on a gold belt?","ko":"그들은! 움, Genie, 당신은 금 벨트에 넣을 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"Sure!","ko":"견적 요청"},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"That looks great.","ko":"그것은 멋지다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Can you put on a jacket?","ko":"재킷에 넣을 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"Why not?","ko":"왜 아니?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I love the jacket! How about a hat?","ko":"나는 재킷을 사랑한다! 모자에 대해 어떻게?"},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"Why not?","ko":"왜 아니?"},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"Mm, take off the hat. That’s better.","ko":"mm, 모자를 끄십시오. 그것은 더 낫습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Genie, these clothes look and feel great! Let’s go to the theater!","ko":"Genie,이 옷은 멋지다! 극장에 가자!"},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"Sorry, Anna. I have to help other friends. Go to the magazine if you want me to help again.","ko":"죄송합니다. Anna. 다른 친구를 돕기 위해 왔습니다. 다시 도와야 할 경우 잡지로 이동하십시오."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thanks, Genie. Sure thing. Goodbye!","ko":"감사합니다, Genie. 확실한 것. 안녕!"},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"Goodbye!","ko":"안녕!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"There are many places in DC to go for a great evening out! And it’s nice to have a friend to help me look my best. Until next time! Bye!","ko":"DC의 많은 장소가 멋진 저녁에 갈 수 있습니다! 그리고 그것은 친구가 내 최고의 모습을 돕기 위해 좋은 것입니다. 다음 시간까지! Bye! Learn English Lesson 14 143"}],"words":[{"en":"casual","definition":"designed for or permitting ordinary dress, behavior or something else","ko":"편한 차림의"},{"en":"clothes","definition":"the things that people wear to cover their bodies and that are usually made from cloth","ko":"옷"},{"en":"formal","definition":"requiring or using serious and proper clothes and manners","ko":"격식을 차린"},{"en":"large","definition":"great in size or amount","ko":"큰"},{"en":"magazine","definition":"a type of thin book with a paper cover that contains stories, essays, pictures, etc.","ko":"잡지"},{"en":"man","definition":"an adult male human being","ko":"남자"},{"en":"match","definition":"to be suited to (someone or something); to go well with (someone or something)","ko":"어울리다"},{"en":"medium","definition":"something that is sold in a medium size; something that is the middle size when compared with things that are larger and smaller","ko":"중간 크기"},{"en":"music","definition":"sounds that are sung by voices or played on musical instruments","ko":"음악"},{"en":"nothing","definition":"not anything; not a thing","ko":"아무것도 아닌 것"},{"en":"outfit","definition":"a set of clothes that are worn together","ko":"옷차림"},{"en":"put on","definition":"to dress yourself in (clothing)","ko":"입다"},{"en":"restaurant","definition":"a place where you can buy and eat a meal","ko":"식당"},{"en":"size","definition":"one of a series of standard measurements in which clothing, shoes, etc., are made","ko":"크기"},{"en":"take off","definition":"to remove (something)","ko":"벗다"},{"en":"theater","definition":"a building where plays, shows, etc., are performed on a stage","ko":"극장"},{"en":"too","definition":"usually used at the end of a sentence or clause; in addition; also","ko":"너무"},{"en":"wear","definition":"to use or have (something) as clothing; to have (a shirt, pants, etc.) over part of your body","ko":"입고 있다"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 14 - How About This?\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. Which clothes are too casual? \na.\t A hat and skirt are too casual.\nb.\t Jeans and a mini-skirt are too casual.\nc.\t A t-shirt and jeans are too casual.\n3. What does Genie want Anna to try?\na.\t Genie wants Anna to try a green shirt and \na skirt.\nb.\t Genie wants Anna to try and green dress \nand a shirt.\nc.\t Genie wants Anna to try a green hat and \na red dress.\n2. What does Anna say about the dress?\na.\t Anna says that the dress is not beautiful.\nb.\t Anna says that the dress is too small.\nc.\t Anna says that the dress is the right size.\n4. What does Anna put on? \na.\t Anna puts on a jacket and a t-shirt.\nb.\t Anna puts on a skirt and a t-shirt.\nc.\t Anna puts on a tie and a dress shirt.\nd.\t Anna puts on shorts and a shirt.","guide":{"id":14,"focus":"옷을 고르고 제안하는 말을 배워요.","grammar":"How about~?은 ‘~은 어때요?’, put on은 ‘입다’, take off는 ‘벗다’예요.","mission":"오늘 입은 옷을 설명하고 다른 옷을 제안해 보세요.","example":"How about this?","exampleKo":"이건 어때요?"}},{"id":15,"startPage":150,"endPage":160,"topics":"Describing differences and similarities Watching people","strategy":"Find Out","goals":"Grammar: Descriptive adjectives; tag questions Pronunciation: Rising and falling intonation in tag questions Speaking: Non-verbal expressions of happiness","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello! People from all over the world come to Washington, D.C. When I’m at work, I love eating lunch outside. I like to watch people walking by. They all look very different. Today, my friend Ashley is eating lunch with me.","ko":"안녕하세요! 전 세계의 사람들이 워싱턴에 와서 D.C. 내가 직장에서 때, 나는 밖에 점심 식사를 사랑. 나는 사람들이 걷는 것을보고 싶습니다. 그들은 모두 매우 다릅니다. 오늘, 내 친구 애슐리는 나를 가진 점심 식사를 먹는다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Ashley, today the weather is beautiful, isn’t it?","ko":"애슐리, 오늘 날씨가 아름답습니다. 그렇지 않습니까?"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Yes, it is. Ahh. Ooh, we have to return to work!","ko":"예, 그것은입니다. Ahh. Ooh, 우리는 일에 돌아 왔습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No, we have time! Let’s people-watch a little more.","ko":"아니요, 우리는 시간이 있습니다! 사람들이 좀 더 볼 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Okay.","ko":"이름 *"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh, I know her. She works in my office! Keyana, hi! Come and join us!","ko":"오, 나는 그녀를 알고있다. 그녀는 내 사무실에서 작동합니다! Keyana, 안녕하세요! 와서 우리를 가입!"},{"speaker":"Keyana","en":"Hi Anna, how are you?","ko":"안녕 안나, 당신은 어떻게?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I’m doing great! Keyana, this is my friend Ashley.","ko":"나는 훌륭합니다! Keyana, 이것은 내 친구 Ashley입니다."},{"speaker":"Keyana","en":"Hi, Ashley!","ko":"안녕, 애슐리!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"We need to return to work. But the weather is beautiful and people-watching is fun!","ko":"우리는 일로 돌아 가야합니다. 그러나 날씨는 아름답고 사람의 시계는 재미입니다!"},{"speaker":"Keyana","en":"I love people-watching too!","ko":"나는 사람들도 보고 싶다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well, have a seat! It is fun to see how people are different or the same.","ko":"글쎄, 좌석이 있습니다! 사람들이 다르거나 같은 방법을 볼 수있는 재미입니다."},{"speaker":"Keyana","en":"It is. For example, Anna, you are tall. But Ashley and I are short.","ko":"그것은이다. 예를 들어, 안나, 당신은 키가 큰. 그러나 애슐리와 나는 짧은."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"And Keyana, you and Ashley have brown eyes; I have blue eyes.","ko":"그리고 Keyana, 당신 및 Ashley에는 갈색 눈이 있습니다; 나는 파란 눈이 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Keyana","en":"You two have light skin and I have dark skin.","ko":"당신은 두 가지 빛 피부와 나는 어두운 피부가 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Ashley, you have straight hair. Keyana and I have curly hair.","ko":"Ashley, 당신은 똑바른 머리가 있습니다. Keyana와 나는 curly 머리가 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"You have very curly hair, Anna.","ko":"당신은 아주 곱슬한 머리, Anna가 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Keyana","en":"I need to return to work. See you, Anna! Nice to meet you Ashley!","ko":"나는 일로 돌아가야한다. 너를 참조하십시오, 안나! 애슐리를 만나는 좋은!"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Bye, Keyana!","ko":"으로, 키아나!"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Anna, I have to go, too. Are you returning to work?","ko":"Anna, 나는 갈 필요가있다, 너무. 당신은 작업에 반환?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I still have time. And this sun feels so good!","ko":"나는 여전히 시간이 있습니다. 그리고이 태양은 너무 좋은 느낌!"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Um, Anna, what does your boss look like?","ko":"Um, Anna, 당신의 보스는 무엇을 좋아합니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"She is short. She has straight, light hair.","ko":"그녀는 짧습니다. 그녀는 똑 바른, 가벼운 머리가 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Does she wear glasses?","ko":"그녀는 안경을 착용합니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes. Yes, she does.","ko":"예. 예, 그녀는."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Is she wearing a blue sweater today?","ko":"그녀는 오늘 푸른 스웨터를 착용하고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"How do you know that?","ko":"어떻게 알 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"She’s coming this way.","ko":"그녀는이 길을 왔습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh no! Hide me!","ko":"오 아니! 나를 숨기기!"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Um, bye, Anna. Call me later.","ko":"Um, bye, Anna. 나중에 전화하십시오."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Bye, Ashley! Talk to you later!","ko":"Bye, Ashley! 나중에 이야기하십시오!"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Anna? Is that you?","ko":"안나? 그게 뭐니?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Ms. Weaver! Hi!","ko":"Ms. 웨버! 안녕하세요!"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"What are you doing behind that bench?","ko":"벤치 뒤에 무엇을하고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I am looking for my, my … stick. Here it is.","ko":"나는 내, 내 ... 스틱을 찾고 있습니다. 여기에 있습니다. 영어 수업을 배우자 15 154"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I am people-watching. Oh! But it’s time to return to work!","ko":"나는 사람들이보고있다. Oh! 그러나 그것은 일로 돌아가는 시간입니다!"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"No need to hurry. I love people-watching too! Let’s sit!","ko":"서둘러 할 필요가 없습니다. 나는 사람들이보고 싶다! 앉아하자!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sure! Ahh.","ko":"아, 아,"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"It’s a beautiful day, isn’t it?","ko":"그것은 아름 다운 날, 하지 않습니다?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes. Yes, it is, Ms. Weaver.","ko":"예. 예, 그것은, Ms. 웨버입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"People-watching in D.C. is fun. It makes me forget the time!","ko":"D.C.에서 사람들은 재미있다. 그것은 나를 잊을 시간!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Until next time! Ahh.","ko":"다음 시간까지! Ahh. 영어 수업을 배우자 15 155"}],"words":[{"en":"bench","definition":"a long and usually hard seat for two or more people","ko":"벤치"},{"en":"blue","definition":"having the color of the clear sky","ko":"파란색"},{"en":"brown","definition":"having a color like coffee or chocolate","ko":"갈색"},{"en":"curly","definition":"formed into a round shape","ko":"곱슬곱슬한"},{"en":"dark","definition":"of a person’s hair, eyes, skin, etc.: black or brown in color","ko":"어두운"},{"en":"eyes","definition":"the part of the body that you see with","ko":"눈"},{"en":"forget","definition":"to be unable to think of or remember (something)","ko":"잊다"},{"en":"glasses","definition":"a pair of glass or plastic lenses set into a frame and worn over the eyes to help a person see","ko":"안경"},{"en":"hair","definition":"a thin threadlike growth from the skin of a person or animal","ko":"머리카락"},{"en":"hide","definition":"to put (something) in a place where it cannot be seen or found","ko":"숨다"},{"en":"join","definition":"to come together with (something or someone)","ko":"합류하다"},{"en":"light","definition":"not dark or deep in color; pale","ko":"밝은"},{"en":"like","definition":"similar to look like - to have an appearance that is very similar to (someone or something)","ko":"좋아하다"},{"en":"people-watch","definition":"to spend time idly observing people in a public place.","ko":"사람 구경하다"},{"en":"seat","definition":"something (such as a chair) that you sit on; a place for sitting have a seat - a polite invitation to sit down.","ko":"좌석"},{"en":"short","definition":"having little height; not tall","ko":"키가 작은"},{"en":"skin","definition":"the natural outer layer of tissue that covers the body of a person or animal","ko":"피부"},{"en":"stick","definition":"a cut or broken branch or twig","ko":"붙다"},{"en":"straight","definition":"not having curves, bends, or angles","ko":"곧은"},{"en":"tall","definition":"greater in height than the average person","ko":"키가 큰"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 15 - I Love People Watching!\nCircle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. Choose the correct tag question: \n“The weather is beautiful, ______?”\na.\t isn’t it?\nb.\t is it?\nc.\t it isn’t?\nd.\t it is?\n3. What does Anna look like?\na.\t Anna is short.\nb.\t Anna has straight hair.\nc.\t Anna has dark skin.\nd.\t Anna is tall.\n2. Which of these describes Ms. Weaver?\na.  She has dark, curly hair.\nb.  She is wearing a blue sweater.\nc.  She is wearing glasses.\n4. How are Anna and Keyana \ndifferent than Ashley?\na.\t Ashley has curly hair, but Anna and \nKeyana have straight hair.\nb.\t Anna and Keyana have dark skin, but \nAshley has light skin.\nc.\t Anna and Keyana have curly hair, but \nAshley has straight hair.\na.\t Ashley is tall, but Anna and Keyana are \nshort.","guide":{"id":15,"focus":"사람의 외모와 특징을 설명해요.","grammar":"tall, short, curly 같은 형용사로 사람을 묘사해요. 질문 끝에 right?를 붙여 확인할 수 있어요.","mission":"친구를 떠올리며 머리 모양이나 키를 설명해 보세요.","example":"She has curly hair.","exampleKo":"그녀는 곱슬머리예요."}},{"id":16,"startPage":161,"endPage":173,"topics":"Countries and nationalities Tourism activities","strategy":"Monitor","goals":"Grammar: Nationality and language names used as nouns and adjectives Pronunciation: Saying ‘a couple of’ quickly Speaking: Talking about countries, languages and nationalities","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello! Washington, D.C. has many tourists! People from different countries come here. Today, my job is to interview tourists. I have to learn why they come here. This is very exciting! Excuse me. I’m Anna Matteo from The News. Do you have time for an interview?","ko":"안녕하세요! 워싱턴 D.C.는 많은 관광객을 가지고 있습니다! 다른 나라의 사람들은 여기에 왔습니다. 오늘, 내 직업은 관광객을 인터뷰하는 것입니다. 나는 그들이 여기에 오는 이유를 배울 필요가 있습니다. 이것은 매우 흥미 롭습니다! 뉴스에서 Anna Matteo입니다. 인터뷰를 할 시간이 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Sabrina","en":"Sure, I have time.","ko":"물론, 나는 시간이 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What is your name?","ko":"이름은 무엇인가요?"},{"speaker":"Sabrina","en":"My name is Sabrina.","ko":"내 이름은 Sabrina입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What country are you from?","ko":"어떤 나라에서?"},{"speaker":"Sabrina","en":"I’m from Bangladesh.","ko":"나는 방글라데시 출신이다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"So, you are Bangladeshi.","ko":"그래서, 당신은 방글라데시입니다."},{"speaker":"Sabrina","en":"That’s right! My nationality is Bangladeshi.","ko":"그건 맞습니다! 내 국적은 방글라데시입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Do you like Washington, D.C.?","ko":"워싱턴 D.C.를 좋아 합니까?"},{"speaker":"Sabrina","en":"Yes! The city is very beautiful!","ko":"예! 도시는 매우 아름답습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What do you like to do in Washington D.C.?","ko":"워싱턴 D.C.에서 무엇을하고 싶습니까?"},{"speaker":"Sabrina","en":"I like history. So, I like walking around and looking at all the monuments and memorials. They make history come alive!","ko":"역사처럼. 그래서, 나는 주변에 산책하고 모든 기념물과 추억을 찾고 싶습니다. 그들은 역사가 살아 왔습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Washington has many monuments and memorials. The Washington Monument is behind us! Which is your favorite?","ko":"워싱턴에는 많은 기념물과 기념비가 있습니다. 워싱턴 기념물은 우리 뒤에 있습니다! 좋아하는 것은?"},{"speaker":"Sabrina","en":"I really like Lincoln Memorial. It is very beautiful. And it feels like Abraham Lincoln is still alive.","ko":"나는 정말로 링컨 기념처럼. 그것은 매우 아름답다. 그리고 그것은 아브라함 링컨과 같은 느낌은 여전히 살아있다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Awesome. Thank you for your time, Sabrina!","ko":"굉장합니다. 당신의 시간을 감사합니다, Sabrina!"},{"speaker":"Sabrina","en":"You’re welcome.","ko":"천만에요."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Let’s find another tourist.","ko":"또 다른 관광을 해보자."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh! Excuse me. I am Anna Matteo from The News. Do you have time for a couple of questions?","ko":"오! 나에게 변명. 나는 뉴스에서 Anna Matteo입니다. 당신은 몇 가지 질문을 할 시간이 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Louis","en":"Sure!","ko":"견적 요청"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Are you from Washington, D.C.?","ko":"워싱턴 D.C.에서?"},{"speaker":"Louis","en":"No, I’m not.","ko":"아니, 나는 아니에요."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What is your name and where are you from?","ko":"당신의 이름과 어디에서?"},{"speaker":"Louis","en":"My name is Louis. And I’m from China.","ko":"나의 이름은 루이입니다. 그리고 나는 중국에서 입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What languages do you speak?","ko":"어떤 언어가 말합니까?"},{"speaker":"Louis","en":"I speak Chinese and English.","ko":"나는 중국어와 영어를 말한다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What do you like about Washington DC?","ko":"Washington DC에 대해 무엇을 좋아하나요?"},{"speaker":"Louis","en":"I like the museums. I really like the art museums.","ko":"나는 박물관처럼. 나는 미술관처럼 정말 좋아합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Many of the museums are free.","ko":"박물관의 많은 것은 무료입니다."},{"speaker":"Louis","en":"I like that too!","ko":"나는 그것을 좋아한다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Awesome! Thanks for your time, Louis.","ko":"굉장합니다! 당신의 시간, 루이에 감사드립니다. 영어 수업을 배우자 16 165"},{"speaker":"Louis","en":"You’re very welcome. Bye!","ko":"당신은 아주 환영입니다. Bye!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Now, let’s find another tourist!","ko":"이제 또 다른 관광을 찾았습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello! I am Anna Matteo from The News. Do you have time to answer a couple of questions?","ko":"안녕하세요! 나는 뉴스에서 Anna Matteo입니다. 몇 가지 질문에 대답 할 시간이 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Mehrnoush","en":"Sure!","ko":"견적 요청"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What is your name and where’re you from?","ko":"당신의 이름과 어디에서?"},{"speaker":"Mehrnoush","en":"My name is Mehrnoush. I am from Iran. I’m Iranian.","ko":"내 이름은 Mehrnoush입니다. 나는 이란 출신입니다. 나는 이란입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What language do they speak in Iran? Is it Persian?","ko":"어떤 언어는 이란에서 말합니까? 그것은 페르시아입니까?"},{"speaker":"Mehrnoush","en":"They speak Farsi.","ko":"그들은 Farsi를 말합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What do you like to do in Washington DC?","ko":"워싱턴 DC에서 무엇을하고 싶습니까?"},{"speaker":"Mehrnoush","en":"Well, I like learning about government and politics.","ko":"잘, 나는 정부와 정치에 대해 학습하고 싶습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Washington has many politicians!","ko":"워싱턴에는 많은 정치가가가 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Mehrnoush","en":"It does! I want to see the U.S. Capitol.","ko":"그것은! 나는 미국 국회 의사당을보고 싶습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Look, you are very near.","ko":"봐, 당신은 매우 가까이 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Mehrnoush","en":"I am!","ko":"₢ 킹"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Have fun!","ko":"재미있게!"},{"speaker":"Mehrnoush","en":"Thanks!","ko":"감사합니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"There you have it. Tourists from all over the world come to Washington, D.C. They all like doing and seeing different things in the city. This is Anna Matteo reporting for The News. Until next time!","ko":"거기있다. 전 세계의 관광객은 워싱턴에 와서, D.C. 그들은 모두 같은 일을하고 도시에 다른 것들을보고. 이것은 Anna Matteo 뉴스에 대한보고입니다. 다음 시간까지!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Is that okay? Awesome! Now, I want to do my favorite thing in the city … ride the carousel!","ko":"그게 괜찮아? 굉장! 지금, 나는 도시에서 내 마음에 드는 일을하고 싶습니다 ... 캐러멜을 타고! 영어 수업을 배우자 16 166"}],"words":[{"en":"Abraham Lincoln","definition":"the 16th President of the United States","ko":"에이브러햄 링컨"},{"en":"alive","definition":"living; not dead","ko":"살아 있는"},{"en":"art","definition":"something that is created with imagination and skill and that is beautiful or that expresses important ideas or feelings","ko":"미술"},{"en":"carousel","definition":"a machine or device with a moving belt or part that carries things around in a circle","ko":"회전목마"},{"en":"country","definition":"an area of land that is controlled by its own government","ko":"나라"},{"en":"couple","definition":"two (things) or a few (things)","ko":"한 쌍"},{"en":"favorite","definition":"a person or a thing that is liked more than others","ko":"가장 좋아하는"},{"en":"free","definition":"not costing any money","ko":"자유로운·무료의"},{"en":"government","definition":"the group of people who control and make decisions for a country, state, etc.","ko":"정부"},{"en":"history","definition":"the study of past events","ko":"역사"},{"en":"memorial","definition":"something (such as a monument or ceremony) that honors a person who has died or serves as a reminder of an event in which many people died","ko":"기념물"},{"en":"monument","definition":"a building, statue, etc., that honors a person or event","ko":"기념비"},{"en":"museum","definition":"a building in which interesting and valuable things (such as paintings and sculptures or scientific or historical objects) are collected and shown to the public","ko":"박물관"},{"en":"nationality","definition":"the fact or status of being a member or citizen of a particular nation","ko":"국적"},{"en":"question","definition":"a sentence, phrase, or word that asks for information or is used to test someone’s knowledge","ko":"질문"},{"en":"politics","definition":"activities that relate to influencing the actions and policies of a government or getting and keeping power in a government","ko":"정치"},{"en":"ride","definition":"to sit on and control the movements of (a horse, motorcycle, bicycle, etc.)","ko":"타다"},{"en":"tourist","definition":"a person who travels to a place for pleasure","ko":"관광객"},{"en":"U.S. Capitol","definition":"the building in which the U.S. Congress meets in Washington, D.C. Countries / Nationalities / Languages","ko":"미국 국회의사당"},{"en":"Bangladesh","definition":"a country in Asia","ko":"방글라데시"},{"en":"Bangladeshi","definition":"a native or inhabitant of Bangladesh. adj. of, relating to, or characteristic of Bangladesh or its people.","ko":"방글라데시의·방글라데시 사람"},{"en":"China","definition":"People’s Republic of, a country in East Asia.","ko":"중국"},{"en":"Chinese","definition":"the standard language of China, based on the speech of Beijing; Mandarin; a native or descendant of a native of China","ko":"중국의·중국 사람"},{"en":"Chinese","definition":"of or relating to China, its inhabitants, or one of their languages","ko":"중국어"},{"en":"Iran","definition":"a republic in the Middle East.","ko":"이란"},{"en":"Iranian","definition":"of or relating to Iran, its inhabitants, or their language; of or relating to the Iranian languages.","ko":"이란의·이란 사람"},{"en":"Iranian","definition":"a subbranch of the Indo-European family of languages, an inhabitant of Iran; Persian.","ko":"이란의"},{"en":"Farsi","definition":"the modern language spoken in Iran and western Afghanistan, written in the Arabic alphabet; modern Persian.","ko":"페르시아어"},{"en":"Persian","definition":"of or relating to ancient and recent Persia (now Iran), its people, or their language.","ko":"페르시아의"},{"en":"Persian","definition":"a member of the native peoples of Iran; the principal language of Iran and western Afghanistan, in its historical and modern forms.","ko":"페르시아어"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 16 - Where Are You From?\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. Anna wants to know about Louis’s \ncountry. Pick the right question:\na.\t What is your country?\nb.\t Where is your family?\nc.\t Where are you from?\nd.\t What is your name?\n3. How does Anna politely ask \nSabrina to talk with her?\na.\t Excuse me for asking you a question.\nb.\t Thank you for answering my questions.\nc.\t Excuse me. Do you have time for an \t\n\t\ninterview?\nd.\t You are welcome to interview me.\n2. Anna wants to know about \nSabrina’s interests. What does she \nask?\na.\t What are you doing today?\nb.\t What do you like to do?\nc.\t Where are you from?\nd.\t What language do you speak?\n4. What does Mehrnoush like to do in \nWashington, DC?\na.\t Mehrnoush wants to go into \n\t\ngovernment.\nb.\t She wants to be a politician.\nc.\t Mehrnoush is looking for the Lincoln \n\t\nMemorial.\nd.\t She likes to learn about politics and \n\t\ngovernment.","guide":{"id":16,"focus":"나라와 언어, 출신지를 소개해요.","grammar":"나라 이름과 사람·언어 이름이 다를 수 있어요. from 뒤에 출신 국가를 써요.","mission":"출신 국가와 사용 언어를 한 문장으로 말해 보세요.","example":"Where are you from?","exampleKo":"어느 나라에서 오셨어요?"}},{"id":17,"startPage":174,"endPage":183,"topics":"Talking about schedules and leisure time activities","strategy":"Evaluate","goals":"Grammar: Simple Future tense with ‘will’ and ‘going to’ Pronunciation: Shortened forms of future verbs and invitations Speaking: Future verb forms","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This city is very interesting, I really like my job, and I have some good friends! Speaking of friends … I see one now! Marsha! Hi!","ko":"이 도시는 매우 흥미로운, 나는 정말 내 일을 좋아하고, 나는 몇 가지 좋은 친구가 있습니다! 친구의 말하기 ... 나는 지금 하나를 참조하십시오! 마샤! 안녕하세요!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Hi, Anna. What’s going on?","ko":"안녕, 안나. 무슨 일이 일어나고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Not much. How about you?","ko":"아니. 어때요?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Busy as usual. Hey, do you wanna see a movie with me?","ko":"평소처럼 Busy. 이봐, 당신은 나를 가진 영화를보고 싶습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sure! I never have time to see a movie. When?","ko":"물론! 영화를 볼 시간이 없습니다. 언제?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Are you busy this Thursday at 6pm?","ko":"이 목요일 오후 6 시까 지 바빴습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Let’s see …. I’m busy. I am going to tap dance with my friends Thursday night.","ko":"봅시다 .... 난 바쁘다. 나는 내 친구 목요일 밤과 춤을 탭하려고합니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Tap dancing? That sounds fun!","ko":"타 춤? 그건 재미!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I’m still learning. But it is fun!","ko":"나는 아직도 학습이다. 그러나 그것은 재미있다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Are you busy on Friday night?","ko":"금요일 밤에는 바쁜가요?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Yes. Friday nights are when I visit my parents.","ko":"예. 금요일 밤은 내 부모를 방문 할 때입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What do you and your family do together?","ko":"당신과 당신의 가족은 함께합니까?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"We always eat dinner together and sometimes we play board games.","ko":"우리는 항상 저녁 식사를 함께 먹고 때로는 우리는 보드 게임을합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Playing board games is fun, too! The word game Scrabble is my favorite.","ko":"플레이 보드 게임은 재미, 너무! 단어 게임 Scrabble은 내 마음에 드는."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"I like Connect Four!","ko":"4를 연결하고 싶습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I’m not busy Monday night. Are you?","ko":"나는 월요일 밤을 바쁘지 않습니다. 당신은?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"I am busy on Monday night. I’m going to jog in the park with my friend. Do you jog?","ko":"나는 월요일 밤에 바빴다. 나는 내 친구와 공원에서 조그를하려고합니다. 당신은 조그를합니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh! I always jog. Well, sometimes I jog. Okay, I never jog. But I will try because it is good for you.","ko":"오! 나는 항상 jog. 잘, 때때로 나는 jog. 괜찮아, 나는 결코 jog. 그러나 나는 당신을 위해 좋은 때문에 시도 할 것이다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"I always feel great after I jog.","ko":"나는 항상 좋은 느낌 후 나는 jog."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"How about on Wednesday night?","ko":"수요일 밤은 어떻습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Wednesday night I am not busy. Oh, no, wait. This Wednesday night I will be busy.","ko":"수요일 밤 나는 바쁘지 않습니다. Oh, no, wait. 이 수요일 밤 나는 바쁠 것입니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"What are you doing?","ko":"무엇을 하고 있나요?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I’m going to teach children how to play the ukulele.","ko":"아이들을 가르치는 것은 ukulelele을 어떻게 연주하는지."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Now, children, play “C.” Good. I like your “C.”","ko":"지금, 아이들, 놀이 “C.” 좋은. 나는 당신의 “C”를 좋아합니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"The world does need more ukulele players.","ko":"세계는 더 많은 ukulele 선수를 필요로 합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Marsha, it looks like we’ll never have time to see a movie.","ko":"Marsha, 그것은 우리가 영화를 볼 때 시간이 없을 것 같다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Wait a minute. Are you busy now?","ko":"1 분을 기다립니다. 당신은 지금 바빴습니까?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"It’s Saturday afternoon. This is always when I do my errands.","ko":"그것은 토요일 오후입니다. 이것은 항상 내 errands를 할 때입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Okay, but the new Star Wars movie is gonna start in 30 minutes.","ko":"괜찮아,하지만 새로운 스타 워즈 영화는 30 분에서 시작 될 것입니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"I’ll do my errands on Sunday. Let’s go!","ko":"저는 일요일에 errands를 할 것입니다. 가자!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Most days of the week, people are really busy. But it’s important to find time to be with your friends!","ko":"대부분의 주일, 사람들은 정말 바쁜. 그러나 그것은 당신의 친구와 함께 할 시간을 찾는 것이 중요합니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Until next time! * Connect Four is a two-player connection game using colored discs.","ko":"다음 시간까지! * 커넥트 4는 착색 된 디스크를 사용하여 두 플레이어 연결 게임입니다. 영어 수업을 배우자 17 178"}],"words":[{"en":"always","definition":"at all times; on every occasion; in a way that does not change board games - a game (such as chess) that is played by moving pieces on a special board","ko":"항상"},{"en":"important","definition":"having serious meaning or worth","ko":"중요한"},{"en":"jog","definition":"to run slowly especially for exercise","ko":"조깅하다"},{"en":"movie","definition":"a recording of moving images that tells a story and that people watch on a screen or television","ko":"영화"},{"en":"night","definition":"the time of darkness between one day and the next","ko":"밤"},{"en":"play","definition":"to do activities for fun or enjoyment Scrabble - trademark. a board game in which players use lettered tiles to create words in a crossword fashion.","ko":"놀다·연주하다"},{"en":"sing","definition":"to use your voice to make musical sounds in the form of a song or tune","ko":"노래하다"},{"en":"sometimes","definition":"at certain times; occasionally","ko":"가끔"},{"en":"Star Wars","definition":"an epic film series chronicling the rise, fall, and redemption of Anakin Skywalker","ko":"스타워즈"},{"en":"start","definition":"to do the first part of something : to begin doing something","ko":"시작하다"},{"en":"tap dance","definition":"a kind of dance in which you wear special shoes with metal plates on the heels and toes and make tapping sounds with your feet","ko":"탭댄스"},{"en":"teaching","definition":"to cause or help (someone) to learn about a subject by giving lessons","ko":"가르치는 일"},{"en":"ukulele","definition":"a musical instrument that is like a small guitar with four strings","ko":"우쿨렐레"},{"en":"week","definition":"a period of seven days - in the U.S., a week is usually considered to start on Sunday and end on Saturday, while in the U.K. a week is usually considered to start on Monday and end on Sunday.","ko":"주"},{"en":"will","definition":"verb. used to say that something is expected to happen in the future Days of the Week: In the U.S., the week starts on Sunday and ends on Saturday. Sunday / Monday / Tuesday / Wednesday / Thursday / Friday / Saturday","ko":"미래를 나타내는 will"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 17 - Are You Free on Friday?\nCircle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. Marsha asks Anna, “What’s going \non?” What  is another way to ask this \nquestion?\na.\t What do you do?\nb.\t How are you?\nc.\t Where are you going?\nd.\t Please say it again.\n3. What does Anna do with children on \nWednesday night?\na.\t Anna teaches the children to play \n\t\nukulele.\nb.\t The children teach Anna about ukulele.\nc.\t She studies ukulele. \nd.\t She plays ukulele for money.\n2. What question is Anna answering \nin the photo? (Her answer is, “I’m \nbusy.”)\na.\t What time are you free?\nb.\t What game do you like?\nc.\t What do you do on Friday?\nd.\t Are you busy this Thursday? \n4. What does Marsha sometimes do \nwith her parents on Friday nights?\na.\t They sometimes make dinner.\nb.\t Marsha and her parents always go to a \n\t\nmovie.\nc.\t They sometimes play board games.\nd.\t Marsha and her parents always play \n\t\nukulele music.","guide":{"id":17,"focus":"약속과 미래 일정을 정해요.","grammar":"will과 be going to 모두 미래를 이야기해요. 계획을 말할 때는 going to를 자주 써요.","mission":"이번 주말 계획을 세 문장으로 만들어 보세요.","example":"Are you free on Friday?","exampleKo":"금요일에 시간 있어요?"}},{"id":18,"startPage":184,"endPage":197,"topics":"Reacting to information Facts or feelings","strategy":"Grouping","goals":"Grammar: Describing frequency of actions; object pronouns; ordinal numbers Speaking: Using the phrase ‘get it’ Pronunciation: Object pronouns with /h/ sound deleted (‘em; ‘im); two ways to pronounce -s at the end of words","conversation":[{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Now, Anna, remember. When we read the news we are always reading facts. We never show our feelings.","ko":"이제 Anna, 기억하십시오. 우리는 뉴스를 읽을 때 우리는 항상 사실을 읽습니다. 우리는 우리의 감각을 결코 보여주지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sure thing, Ms. Weaver.","ko":"물론, Ms. 웨버."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Great. Are you ready?","ko":"좋은. 준비가 되셨습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes.","ko":"예."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Okay, let’s try the first story!","ko":"감사합니다, 첫 번째 이야기를 시도하자!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello, and welcome to The News.","ko":"안녕하세요, 뉴스에 오신 것을 환영합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"A new book is very popular with children and families. This is it.","ko":"새로운 책은 아이들과 가족과 아주 대중적입니다. 이것은 그것입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"It is about a lost duckling. The duck’s mother cannot find him.","ko":"그것은 잃어버린 오리에 관한 것입니다. 오리의 어머니는 그를 찾을 수 없습니다."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Stop! Anna, when you say the words “duck” and “duckling” you look really sad.","ko":"중지! 안나, 당신은 단어를 말할 때 “duck” 과 “duckling” 당신은 정말 슬픈."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I do?","ko":"나는?"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Yes. Sad is a feeling.","ko":"예. Sad는 느낌입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sad is not a fact. Sorry. Let me try again.","ko":"Sad는 사실이 아닙니다. 죄송합니다. 다시 시도하십시오."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Okay, she’s trying again! And go.","ko":"괜찮아, 그녀는 다시 시도 해요! 그리고 가자."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello, and welcome to The News. A new book is very popular with children and families. This is it.","ko":"안녕하세요, 그리고 뉴스에 오신 것을 환영합니다. 새로운 책은 아이들과 가족과 매우 인기가 있습니다. 이것은 그것입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"It is about a lost duckling. The duck’s mother cannot find ‘im. But a family gives him a home.","ko":"그것은 잃어버린 오리에 관한 것입니다. 오리의 어머니는 'im을 찾을 수 없습니다. 그러나 가족은 그를 집에 제공합니다."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Stop! Anna, you are doing it again.","ko":"중지! 안나, 당신은 다시하고 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This story is very sad.","ko":"이 이야기는 매우 슬픈."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"I have an idea. Let’s read the second story. She’s reading the second story. And … go!","ko":"나는 아이디어가 있습니다. 두 번째 이야기를 읽으십시오. 그녀는 두 번째 이야기를 읽습니다. 그리고 ... 가자!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello , and welcome to The News. In Indiana, a grandmother is the first 80-year- old woman to win The Race Car 500.","ko":"안녕하세요, 그리고 뉴스에 오신 것을 환영합니다. 인디애나에서, 할머니는 레이스 자동차 500 승리 최초의 80 살 여성입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"That is awesome!","ko":"그것은 굉장하다!"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Stop! Stop! Anna, please -- no feelings.","ko":"중지! 안나, 제발 -- 아무 느낌."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Right. But it is awesome that an 80-year-old grandmother wins a car race.","ko":"오른쪽. 그러나 80 세의 할머니가 자동차 경주를 승리하는 것이 굉장합니다."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Just the facts, Anna.","ko":"그냥 사실, 안나."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Right.","ko":"견적 요청"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello, and welcome to The News. In Indiana, a grandmother is the first 80-year-old woman to win The Race Car 500.","ko":"안녕하세요, 그리고 뉴스에 오신 것을 환영합니다. 인디애나에서, 할머니는 레이스 자동차 500 승리 최초의 80 살 여성입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"She rarely talks to reporters. But when she does, she often says, “Nothing can stop me now!”","ko":"그녀는 거의 기자 회견. 그러나 그녀가 할 때, 그녀는 종종 말한다, \"그들은 지금 나를 중지 할 수 없습니다!\""},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I am very happy for her!","ko":"나는 그녀를 위해 아주 행복합니다!"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Stop, stop, stop!! Anna, you cannot say you are happy.","ko":"중지, 중지, 중지!! 안나, 당신은 당신이 행복 할 수 없습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"But I am happy.","ko":"그러나 나는 행복합니다."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"But you can’t say it.","ko":"그러나 당신은 그것을 말할 수 없습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Why?","ko":"왜?"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"This is the News. Happy and sad are feelings. You can’t have them in The News.","ko":"이것은 뉴스입니다. 행복하고 슬픈 느낌입니다. 당신은 뉴스에서 그들을 가질 수 없습니다. 영어 수업을 배우자 18 188"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Okay. I got it.","ko":"그래. 나는 그것을 가지고."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Okay. Let’s try the third story. She’s reading the third story!","ko":"괜찮아. 세 번째 이야기를 시도하자. 그녀는 세 번째 이야기를 읽었다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello and welcome to The News. City politicians in Big Town are using city money to have a big party on a cruise ship. They are taking the money for the party from the children’s library.","ko":"안녕하세요, 뉴스에 오신 것을 환영합니다. 빅 타운의 도시 정치인은 크루즈 배에 큰 파티를 가지고 도시 돈을 사용하고 있습니다. 그들은 아이들의 도서관에서 파티에 돈을 복용하고 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What?! That makes me very angry.","ko":"무엇?! 그것은 나에게 매우 화가를 만든다."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"No, no, no! Anna, you cannot say you are angry! This is The News!!!","ko":"아니, 아니! 안나, 당신은 당신이 화가라고 말할 수 없습니다! 이것은 뉴스입니다!!!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What can I do, Ms. Weaver? Take out my feelings and put them here … on the news desk?","ko":"나는 무엇을 할 수, Ms. 웨버? 내 감정을 꺼내 여기에 넣어 ... 뉴스 데스크에?"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Yes. Yes. That’s right! Now you’ve got it!","ko":"예. 그렇습니다. 그게 맞습니다! 이제 당신은 그것을 얻었다!"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Let’s repeat the first story.","ko":"첫 번째 이야기를 반복하자."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This is going to be a very long day.","ko":"이것은 매우 긴 날이 될 것입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Until next time!","ko":"다음 시간까지! 영어 수업을 배우자 18 189"}],"words":[{"en":"angry","definition":"having a strong feeling of being upset or annoyed","ko":"화가 난"},{"en":"cruise ship","definition":"a large ship that stops at different ports and carries passengers who are traveling for pleasure","ko":"유람선"},{"en":"desk","definition":"a piece of furniture that is like a table and often has drawers","ko":"책상"},{"en":"duck","definition":"a bird that swims and has a flat beak, a short neck, a heavy body, short legs, and webbed feet","ko":"오리"},{"en":"duckling","definition":"a young duck","ko":"아기 오리"},{"en":"fact","definition":"a true piece of information","ko":"사실"},{"en":"feeling","definition":"an emotional state or reaction","ko":"감정"},{"en":"get","definition":"to understand (something or someone)","ko":"얻다"},{"en":"Indiana","definition":"state of the U.S.","ko":"인디애나주"},{"en":"long","definition":"lasting or continuing for a great amount of time","ko":"긴"},{"en":"lost","definition":"not knowing where you are or how to get to where you want to go","ko":"잃어버린"},{"en":"popular","definition":"liked or enjoyed by many people","ko":"인기 있는"},{"en":"race car","definition":"a very fast car that is used in professional auto racing","ko":"경주용 자동차"},{"en":"rarely","definition":"not very often","ko":"드물게"},{"en":"repeat","definition":"to say (something) again","ko":"반복하다"},{"en":"sad","definition":"not happy","ko":"슬픈"},{"en":"story","definition":"a description of how something happened","ko":"이야기"},{"en":"win","definition":"to achieve victory in a fight, contest, game, etc.","ko":"이기다"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 18 - She Always Does That\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Caty tell Anna to do?\na.\t She tells Anna to read only the facts.\nb.\t Caty wants Anna to read fast.\nc.\t She wants Anna to read with more \nfeeling.\nd.\t Caty tells Anna to read louder.\n3. What happens when Anna says “duck” \nand “duckling”?\na.\t Anna is happy because she is telling the \nfacts.\nb.\t She looks at the book.\nc.\t Anna looks sad because she is showing \nher feelings.\nd.\t She starts to read to Caty.\n2. Why is Anna talking about the book?\na.\t The book is about a boy who is lost.\nb.\t It is a book for lost children.\nc.\t The book is the first one about a \nduckling.\nd.\t Many children and families are reading \nthe book.\n4. Why does Caty stop Anna?\na.\t Anna made a mistake - it is a 70-year-old \ngrandmother.\nb.\t Caty wants Anna to stop showing her \nfeelings.\nc.\t Anna is reading the story too fast.\nd.\t Caty does not think the grandmother is \nawesome.\nFruits and Vegetables\nFirst\nSecond\nThird\nFourth\nFifth\nSixth\nSeventh\nEighth\nNinth\nTenth\nOrdinal Number Cards\nActions and Adverbs","guide":{"id":18,"focus":"평소 습관과 빈도를 말해요.","grammar":"always는 ‘항상’, sometimes는 ‘가끔’, rarely는 ‘드물게’예요.","mission":"자주 하는 일과 가끔 하는 일을 비교해 보세요.","example":"She always does that.","exampleKo":"그녀는 항상 그렇게 해요."}},{"id":19,"startPage":198,"endPage":212,"topics":"Saying the months of the year Talking about seasons and activities","strategy":"Summarize","goals":"Grammar: ‘Which’ as an adjective alone and with pronouns; adjectives ‘next’ and ‘every’ Speaking: Using ‘which’ and ‘which one’ to offer a choice; using ‘every’ and ‘next’ with time expressions Pronunciation: The month of February","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi there! Summer in Washington, D.C. is hot and sunny. I always ride the Metro to work. Riding the Metro is cool and fast. But today it’s closed. So, I am walking to work. (On the phone) Ms. Weaver, I am late this morning. The Metro is closed. So, I am walking to work.","ko":"안녕하세요! 워싱턴의 여름, D.C.는 뜨겁고 화창합니다. 나는 항상 메트로를 타고 일합니다. 메트로를 타고 차갑고 빠릅니다. 그러나 오늘 그것은 닫힙니다. 그래서, 나는 일하는 것을 걷습니다. (전화) Ms. Weaver, 나는 아침 늦게입니다. 메트로가 닫힙니다. 그래서, 나는 일을 걷고 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"That’s too bad. It’s really hot today.","ko":"그것은 너무 나쁘다. 그것은 정말 뜨거운 오늘입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes it is.","ko":"예."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"When you arrive, please come to my office. I have important news to tell you.","ko":"도착하면 사무실에 오십시오. 나는 당신에게 중요한 뉴스가 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Of course. Good-bye. My boss has news for me. The question is: Is it good news or bad news? (At work)","ko":"물론입니다. 안녕. 내 보스는 나를 위해 뉴스가 있습니다. 질문은: 그것은 좋은 뉴스 또는 나쁜 뉴스입니까? (작동)"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello, Ms. Weaver.","ko":"안녕하세요, Ms. 웨버."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Anna, I have good news and I have bad news. Which do you want to hear first?","ko":"Anna, 나는 좋은 소식을 가지고 나는 나쁜 소식이 있습니다. 당신이 먼저 듣고 싶은 것은?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"The good news. No … okay, the bad news.","ko":"좋은 소식. 아니 ... 괜찮아, 나쁜 소식."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"The bad news is you are not good at reading the news.","ko":"나쁜 소식은 뉴스를 읽는 것은 좋지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh. I am very sorry to hear that.","ko":"오. 나는 그것을 듣고 매우 미안 해요."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"So, starting next month you will not read the news.","ko":"그래서, 다음 달을 시작 당신은 뉴스를 읽지 않을 것입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Next month is July. You are firing me in July.","ko":"다음 달은 7 월입니다. 당신은 7 월에 나를 치르고 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"No. I am not firing you in July … or in August or in September. That is the good news.","ko":"아니요. 7 월에 당신을 치지 않습니다 ... 또는 8 월 또는 9 월에. 그것은 좋은 소식입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Okay. You are not firing me. I am not reading the news. What will I be doing?","ko":"괜찮아. 저를 치지 않습니다. 나는 뉴스를 읽지 않습니다. 나는 무엇을 할 것인가?"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Well, you are good at asking questions. You are good at talking to people. You are good at showing your feelings. And you are great at being silly.","ko":"잘, 당신은 질문에 좋은. 당신은 사람들에게 얘기에 좋은. 당신은 당신의 감각을 보여주는 좋은. 그리고 당신은 silly에 중대합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thank you, Ms. Weaver. But what does all that mean?","ko":"감사합니다, Ms. 웨버. 그러나 그게 무슨 뜻이야?"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"I have a new assignment for you! Your skills are perfect for a new show … a children’s show.","ko":"나는 당신을 위한 새로운 할당이 있습니다! 당신의 기술은 새로운 쇼를 위해 완벽합니다 ... 아이들의 쇼."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"A children’s show ... That is awesome! When do I start?","ko":"아이들의 쇼 ... 그것은 굉장합니다! 내가 시작할 때?"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"You start next month. Start thinking of ideas for the show.","ko":"다음 달을 시작합니다. 쇼에 대한 아이디어의 시작."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I have tons of ideas! I can show children what it’s like in outer space ...","ko":"나는 아이디어의 톤이 있습니다! 나는 외부 공간에서 좋아하는 아이들을 보여줄 수 ..."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Great …","ko":"큰 ..."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"… or in the deep, dark ocean …","ko":"... 또는 깊은 곳에서, 어두운 바다 ..."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Those are great ideas, Anna. Please go think of more … at your desk.","ko":"그들은 훌륭한 아이디어, 안나입니다. 더 많은 것을 생각하십시오 ... 책상에."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes. What other things can I show them? Mt. Everest! Everyone has different skills. You have skills. I have skills. The important thing is to know what you are good at. Until next time!","ko":"예. 다른 것들이 어떻게 보여 줄 수 있습니까? Mt. Everest! 모두가 다른 기술을 가지고 있습니다. 당신은 기술이 있습니다. 중요한 것은 당신이 좋은 것을 알고있는 것입니다. 다음 시간까지!"}],"words":[{"en":"arrive","definition":"to come to or reach a place after traveling","ko":"도착하다"},{"en":"assignment","definition":"a job or duty that is given to someone","ko":"과제"},{"en":"child","definition":"a young person (plural: children)","ko":"아이"},{"en":"closed","definition":"not operating or open to the public","ko":"닫힌"},{"en":"deep","definition":"having a large distance to the bottom from the surface or highest point","ko":"깊은"},{"en":"everyone","definition":"every person; everybody","ko":"모든 사람"},{"en":"fire","definition":"to dismiss (someone) from a job","ko":"불"},{"en":"idea","definition":"a thought, plan, or suggestion about what to do mean - v.. to cause or result in (something)","ko":"생각"},{"en":"month","definition":"any one of the 12 parts into which the year is divided","ko":"달"},{"en":"Mt. Everest","definition":"a mountain in Asia; it is the highest mountain in the world","ko":"에베레스트산"},{"en":"ocean","definition":"the salt water that covers much of the Earth’s surface","ko":"바다"},{"en":"other","definition":"used to refer to the one person or thing that remains or that has not been mentioned","ko":"다른"},{"en":"outer space","definition":"the region beyond the Earth’s atmosphere in which there are stars and planets","ko":"우주 공간"},{"en":"perfect","definition":"having all the qualities you want in that kind of person or situation","ko":"완벽한"},{"en":"silly","definition":"playful or funny","ko":"우스운"},{"en":"skill","definition":"an ability to do something that comes from training, experience, or practice","ko":"기술"},{"en":"ton","definition":"informal: a large amount; in the US, a ton is a unit for measuring weight that equals 2,000 pounds (907 kilograms)","ko":"톤"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 19 - When Do I Start?\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. Why does Anna say, “Oh. I am very \nsorry to hear that?”\na.\t She is apologizing for being late.\nb.\t She does not want to work.\nc.\t She hears bad news.\nd.\t She wants to tell some good news.\n4. When does Anna ride the metro?\na.\t Anna always rides the metro to work.\nb.\t Anna rides the metro when the weather \nis bad.\nc.\t Anna rides the metro when it is cold.\nd.\t Anna usually rides the metro when she \nis late. \n2. What will happen in July?\na.\t Anna will lose her job in July.\nb.\t In July, Anna will stop reading the news.\nc.\t Anna will go to a new city in July.\nd.\t In July, Anna will start writing the news.\n5. Why does Ms. Weaver say, “That’s \ntoo bad!”?\na.\t Ms. Weaver learns that the metro is slow \nwhen it is hot and sunny.\nb.\t She does not want Anna to come to work \nwhen it is hot.\nc.\t Ms. Weaver wants Anna to tell a story \nabout the metro.\nd.\t She learns that Anna has to walk to work \nwhen it is hot.\n3. Why does Anna say, “That is \nawesome!”?\na.\t She wants to write more news stories.\nb.\t She wants to read the news.\nc.\t She does not want to work with children.\nd.\t She hears good news.","guide":{"id":19,"focus":"새 일을 시작할 때 필요한 질문을 해요.","grammar":"Which는 ‘어느 것’인지 선택할 때 써요. next는 ‘다음’이에요.","mission":"새 학원이나 직장에서 첫날 물을 질문을 만들어 보세요.","example":"When do I start?","exampleKo":"언제 시작하나요?"}},{"id":20,"startPage":213,"endPage":225,"topics":"Saying the months of the year Talking about seasons and activities","strategy":"Identify Problems","goals":"","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi, there! Washington, D.C. is a great place to work. Many people here work in government and politics. But there are many other jobs. You can work at a hospital; a university. You can work in a coffee shop. Wait a minute, I think I see a friend of mine. Pete? Is that you?","ko":"안녕하세요, 거기! 워싱턴, D.C.는 직장에 좋은 곳입니다. 많은 사람들이 여기에 정부와 정치에서 일하고 있습니다. 그러나 다른 많은 일자리가 있습니다. 당신은 병원에서 일할 수 있습니다. 당신은 커피 숍에서 일할 수 있습니다. 분을 기다립니다, 나는 내 친구를보고 생각합니다. Pete? 그게?"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Hi, Anna.","ko":"안녕, 안나."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"You look different. Your beard … is really big.","ko":"당신은 다른 모습. 당신의 수염 ... 정말 큰입니다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"You don’t like it, do you?","ko":"당신은 그것을 좋아하지 않습니다, 당신은?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No, no. You just look … different. (To server) Thank you. So, what’s wrong? You look sad.","ko":"아니요, 아니오. ... 다른 것 같습니다. (서버) 고맙습니다. 그래서, 무엇이 잘못되었습니까? 슬픔을보십시오."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"I don’t have a job.","ko":"나는 일을하지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sorry, I can’t hear you.","ko":"죄송합니다, 나는 당신을 듣지 못합니다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"I do not have a job!","ko":"나는 직업이 없다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh. I’m sorry to hear that, Pete.","ko":"오. 나는 그것을 듣고 미안 해요, Pete."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"I don’t have a skill.","ko":"나는 기술이 없습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Everyone has a skill. You need to find yours.","ko":"모두가 기술이 있습니다. 당신은 당신의 것을 찾을 필요가 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"I don’t know, Anna.","ko":"나는 안나를 모른다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Pete, I am good at asking questions. Let me ask you some.","ko":"Pete, 나는 질문을하는 것이 좋습니다. 나를 물어 보자."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Really, Anna? Can you help me?","ko":"정말, Anna? 당신은 나를 도울 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes, I can. Let me help.","ko":"예, 나는 할 수 있습니다. 나를 도와주세요."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Sure, Anna. Maybe you can help.","ko":"물론, Anna. 어쩌면 당신은 도움이 될 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Can you write code?","ko":"코드를 작성할 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Sure, c-o-l-d. How is this going to help?","ko":"물론 c-o-l-d. 어떻게 도움이 될 것인가?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No, not “cold.” Code; you know, for making phone apps, or websites. You can make tons of money writing code.","ko":"No, not “cold.” Code; 당신은 알고, 전화 응용 프로그램, 또는 웹 사이트를 만들기. 당신은 돈 작성 코드의 톤을 만들 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Tons of money? But I can’t code.","ko":"돈의 톤? 그러나 나는 코드를 할 수 없습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Next question. Can you drive?","ko":"다음 질문. 운전할 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Do you mean drive a race car? It’s really hard to be a race car driver.","ko":"당신은 경주 차를 운전 의미합니까? 그것은 경주 자동차 드라이버가되기 위해 정말 어렵습니다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"First, you need a race car ...","ko":"먼저, 당신은 레이스 자동차가 필요합니다 ..."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No, I mean drive a taxi or drive a bus.","ko":"아니요, 택시를 운전하거나 버스를 운전합니다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"No, I always fall asleep when I drive.","ko":"아니, 나는 항상 잠들 때 나는 드라이브."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh, that’s not good. Next question. Can you teach? You can be a teacher in a school.","ko":"오, 그건 좋지 않습니다. 다음 질문. 가르치실 수 있습니까? 당신은 학교에 교사가 될 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"No, I cannot teach.","ko":"아니, 나는 가르쳐 할 수 없습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Can you cook? You can be a chef in a restaurant.","ko":"요리 할 수 있습니까? 레스토랑에서 요리사가 될 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"No, I can’t code! I can’t teach! I can’t cook! Anna, I can’t do anything. This is sad. I’m gonna write about my feelings in my blog.","ko":"아니, 나는 코드를 할 수 없습니다! 나는 가르치지 않습니다! 나는 요리 할 수 없습니다! 안나, 나는 아무것도 할 수 없습니다. 이것은 슬픈입니다. 나는 내 블로그에서 내 감정에 대해 쓸 것입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"You write a blog?","ko":"당신은 블로그를 작성?"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Yeah, I write a blog.","ko":"그래, 블로그를 작성합니다."}],"words":[{"en":"app","definition":"a computer program that performs a particular task (such as word processing)","ko":"앱"},{"en":"beard","definition":"the hair that grows on a man’s cheeks and chin","ko":"수염"},{"en":"blog","definition":"a Web site on which someone writes about personal opinions, activities, and experiences","ko":"블로그"},{"en":"chef","definition":"a professional cook who usually is in charge of a kitchen in a restaurant","ko":"요리사"},{"en":"code","definition":"- a set of instructions for a computer","ko":"코드"},{"en":"code","definition":"to change (information) into a set of letters, numbers, or symbols that can be read by a computer","ko":"코딩하다"},{"en":"drive","definition":"to direct the movement of a vehicle such as a car, truck, or bus","ko":"운전하다"},{"en":"easy","definition":"not hard to do","ko":"쉬운"},{"en":"follower","definition":"a person who likes and admires (someone or something) very much good luck - expression. used to say that you hope someone will succeed","ko":"팔로어"},{"en":"hard","definition":"physically or mentally difficult","ko":"어려운"},{"en":"lot(s) or a lot (informal)","definition":"a large amount","ko":"많은 양"},{"en":"hospital","definition":"a place where sick or injured people are given care or treatment and where children are often born","ko":"병원"},{"en":"school","definition":"a place where children go to learn","ko":"학교"},{"en":"taxi","definition":"a car that carries passengers to a place for an amount of money","ko":"택시"},{"en":"teacher","definition":"a person or thing that teaches something","ko":"선생님"},{"en":"university","definition":"a school that offers courses leading to a degree and where research is done","ko":"대학교"},{"en":"website","definition":"a place on the World Wide Web that contains information about a person, organization, etc., and that usually consists of many Web pages joined by hyperlinks","ko":"웹사이트"},{"en":"well","definition":"in a skillful way","ko":"잘"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 20 - What Can You Do?\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Anna say to make \nPete say his sentence again?\na.\t “Sorry, I can’t bear you.”\nb.\t “Sorry, I can’t hear you.”\nc.\t “So, I can hear you.”\nd.\t “So what did you say?”\n4. What does Pete say to show he \ndoes not understand?\na.\t\nDo I need a race car?\nb.\t\nCan you teach me how to drive?\nc.\t\nDo you mean drive a race car?\nd.\t\nDo you want me to drive a race car?\n2. Why is Pete sad?\na.\t Pete is sad because he does not have \na skill.\nb.\t He is sad because he lost all of his \nmoney.\nc.\t Pete is sad because he does not have \nfriends.\nd.\t He is sad because he failed at school.\n5. Why can’t Pete be a bus driver?\na.\t\nHe falls asleep when he drives.\nb.\t\nHe does not have a driver’s license.\nc.\t\nHe does not know how to drive.\nd.\t\nHe is not a good driver.\n3. Why does Anna say “No, I mean \ncode.”?\na.\t Anna wants to say she is cold.\nb.\t She does not understand Pete.\nc.\t Anna said the wrong word.\nd.\t She sees that Pete does not   \nunderstand.\n6. How many followers does Pete \nhave?\na.\t\nPete has 59,538 followers.\nb.\t\nHe has 52,958 followers.\nc.\t\nPete has 55,538 followers.\nd.\t\nHe has 69,538 followers.","guide":{"id":20,"focus":"할 수 있는 일과 능력을 소개해요.","grammar":"can + 동사원형은 ‘~할 수 있다’라는 뜻이에요. can’t는 ‘못한다’예요.","mission":"잘하는 일 두 가지, 연습 중인 일 한 가지를 말해 보세요.","example":"What can you do?","exampleKo":"무엇을 할 수 있나요?"}},{"id":21,"startPage":226,"endPage":238,"topics":"Invitations Apologizing Hobbies & Personal Skills Expressing obligation","strategy":"Cooperate","goals":"","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi there! Washington, D.C. has some great coffee shops. My favorite is this one -- Busboys & Poets.","ko":"안녕하세요! 워싱턴 D.C.에는 훌륭한 커피 가게가 있습니다. 내 마음에 드는 것은이 것입니다 -- Busboys & Poets."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Actually it’s more than a coffee shop. It’s also a bookstore, a restaurant and a theater!","ko":"실제로 커피 숍보다 더 많은 것입니다. 또한 책방, 레스토랑 및 극장입니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Marsha and I love coming here.","ko":"Marsha 과 나는 사랑 coming 여기에."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Hey, Anna, my friend is having a party on Saturday. Can you come with me?","ko":"안녕하세요, Anna, 내 친구는 토요일에 파티를하고 있습니다. 나를 함께 올 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sorry, I can’t come with you. I have to get my driver’s license.","ko":"죄송합니다, 나는 당신과 함께 올 수 없습니다. 나는 내 드라이버의 라이센스를 얻을 필요가있다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Will you be busy all day?","ko":"매일 바쁘게 될까요?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I don’t know. First, I have to take a test on the computer. Then I have to take a test in the car.","ko":"나는 모른다. 첫째, 나는 컴퓨터에서 시험을해야합니다. 그런 다음 나는 자동차에서 시험을해야합니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"But you have to take the test during the day, don’t you?","ko":"그러나 당신은 하루 동안 시험을 취해야, 당신을하지?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes.","ko":"예."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"The party is at night.","ko":"파티는 밤에 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh. Then I can come with you to the party on Saturday night.","ko":"오. 그런 다음 토요일 밤에 파티에 올 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Great! I have to help my friend with the party. Can you help me?","ko":"좋은! 나는 파티와 내 친구를 돕고있다. 당신은 나를 도울 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sure. That sounds like fun.","ko":"확실히. 그것은 재미처럼 들린다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Everyone has to bring something or do something. You can bring food, or you can perform.","ko":"누구나 무언가를 가져 와서 무언가를 할 수 있습니다. 음식을 가져갈 수 있습니다. 또는 수행 할 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Really, I can perform?","ko":"정말, 나는 수행 할 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"You can! Can you?","ko":"할 수 있습니다! 당신은 할 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes! I can recite poetry. (Anna is in a club reciting a poem) - A poem - Light dark Light dark Darkness Dark","ko":"예! 나는 poetry를 회견 할 수 있습니다. (Anna는 클럽에서 시를 인용) - A시 - 밝은 어두운 어둠 어둠 어둠 다크"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"In this country, nobody recites poetry at parties. Um … can you do anything else?","ko":"이 나라에서는 아무도 당사자에 시인을 구합니다. 우 ... 다른 것을 할 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hmm, yes. I can do a card trick. (Anna is doing a card trick) Your card is the 10 of diamonds! No? Pick a card. Any card. Here, just pick this one. Great!","ko":"Hmm, 예. 카드 트릭을 할 수 있습니다. (Anna는 카드 트릭을하고 있습니다) 귀하의 카드는 다이아몬드의 10입니다! 아니? 카드를 선택. 모든 카드. 여기, 그냥이 하나를 선택. 큰!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Anna, maybe you can just bring food.","ko":"Anna, 어쩌면 당신은 단지 음식을 가져올 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No, I can’t cook. And I really want to perform. You know, there is one thing I can do. (Anna plays a song on the ukulele and sings) Trouble in mind. I’m blue...","ko":"아니, 나는 요리 할 수 없습니다. 그리고 난 정말 수행하고 싶습니다. 당신은 알고, 내가 할 수있는 한 가지가 있습니다. (Anna는 ukulele과 sings) Trouble에 노래를합니다. 나는 푸른 ..."}],"words":[{"en":"bookstore","definition":"a store that sells books","ko":"서점"},{"en":"card","definition":"a small piece of stiff paper that is used for playing games","ko":"카드"},{"en":"day","definition":"the part of the day when light from the sun can be seen","ko":"낮·하루"},{"en":"driver’s license","definition":"an official document or card which shows that you have the legal right to drive a vehicle","ko":"운전면허증"},{"en":"else","definition":"used to refer to a different or additional person or thing","ko":"그 밖의"},{"en":"night","definition":"the time of darkness between one day and the next","ko":"밤"},{"en":"perform","definition":"to entertain an audience by singing or acting","ko":"공연하다"},{"en":"poetry","definition":"the writings of a poet","ko":"시"},{"en":"recite","definition":"to read (something) out loud or say (something) from memory","ko":"낭송하다"},{"en":"test","definition":"a set of questions or problems that are designed to measure a person’s knowledge, skills, or abilities","ko":"시험"},{"en":"trick","definition":"a clever and skillful action that someone performs to entertain or amuse people","ko":"속임수·묘기"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 21 - Can You Come to the Party?\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Marsha want Anna to \ndo? \na.\t Marsha wants Anna to have a party on \nSaturday.\nb.\t She wants Anna to get a driver’s license.\nc.\t Marsha wants Anna to go to a party with \nher.\nd.\t She wants Anna to leave the party now.\n4. Why does Anna say “Can I help? \nI’m not busy right now.” \na.\t She wants to spend more time with \nMarsha.\nb.\t Anna wants to leave the coffee shop.\nc.\t She wants to go home and sleep.\nd.\t Anna needs to take food to the party.\n2. Why can’t Anna go to the party on \nSaturday? \na.\t She does not like going to parties.\nb.\t Anna has to get her driver’s license.\nc.\t She has to learn how to drive.\nd.\t Anna has to do work on her computer.\n5. What is one thing Anna says that \nshe has to do? \na.\t Anna needs to study for the driving test.\nb.\t She has to help Marsha shop for the \nparty.\nc.\t Anna has to cook something for the \nparty.\nd.\t She has to bring food to the party.\n3. What does Anna have to do when \nshe goes to the party? \na.\t She has to perform something at the \nparty.\nb.\t Anna has to bring food and drinks to the \nparty.\nc.\t She has to welcome the guests at the \nparty.\nd.\t Anna has to do something or bring some­\nthing.","guide":{"id":21,"focus":"초대하고 함께할 일을 제안해요.","grammar":"Can you~?는 부탁이나 초대에 사용해요. Sure!는 기꺼이 좋다는 응답이에요.","mission":"친구를 파티에 초대하고 참석 여부를 물어보세요.","example":"Can you come to the party?","exampleKo":"파티에 올 수 있나요?"}},{"id":22,"startPage":239,"endPage":252,"topics":"Vacations Seasons","strategy":"Plan","goals":"Grammar: Future events and intentions using going to Speaking: “My favorite season is…” and “When I go on vacation, I like ____.” Pronunciation: Shadowing","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Washington, D.C. has four seasons: winter, spring, summer and autumn or fall. My favorite season is summer because of summer vacation! Hey, that will be a great subject for my new work assignment -- the children’s show. I can teach what families in the U.S. do during summer vacation. Today, I’m planning the show with Amelia. This is the first time we are working together. I hope we can work well together. Hi, Amelia!","ko":"워싱턴 D.C.에는 4 시즌이 있습니다 : 겨울, 봄, 여름 및 가을 또는 가을. 내 좋아하는 계절은 여름 휴가 때문에 여름입니다! Hey, 그것은 내 새로운 작업 할당을위한 훌륭한 주제가 될 것입니다 -- 아이들의 쇼. 나는 여름 휴가 동안 미국에 어떤 가족을 가르치는 수 있습니다. 오늘, 나는 Amelia와 함께 쇼를 계획하고 있습니다. 이것은 우리가 함께 일하는 첫 번째 시간입니다. 나는 우리가 함께 일할 수 있기를 희망합니다. 안녕하세요, Amelia!"},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"Hi, Anna! So, what are we going to talk about on the first show?","ko":"안녕, 안나! 그래서, 우리는 첫 번째 쇼에 대해 이야기 할 것입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I want to talk about summer vacation.","ko":"여름 휴가에 대해 이야기하고 싶습니다."},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"That will be fun! Are you going on vacation this summer?","ko":"그것은 재미있을 것입니다! 당신은 여름 휴가에 가고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No. This summer I am too busy.","ko":"아니. 이 여름 나는 너무 바빴다."},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"That’s too bad.","ko":"그것은 너무 나쁘다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"It’s okay. I can go on vacation next summer. This show will be a lot of fun too!","ko":"괜찮습니다. 나는 다음 여름 휴가에 갈 수 있습니다. 이 쇼는 너무 재미있게 될 것입니다!"},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"So, Anna, what’s the plan for the show?","ko":"그래서, Anna, 쇼를위한 계획은 무엇입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"First, we’re going to introduce the subject. Then we can show pictures and video.","ko":"첫째, 우리는 주제를 소개하려고합니다. 그런 다음 그림과 비디오를 보여줄 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"We can show tons of video!","ko":"우리는 영상의 톤을 보여줄 수 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Right! We can interview children and have guests, too.","ko":"오른쪽! 우리는 아이들과 손님도 인터뷰 할 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"Kids can ask us questions.","ko":"아이들은 저희에게 질문을 할 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Great idea! Finally, we can read the questions and tell them where to learn more.","ko":"좋은 아이디어! 마지막으로, 우리는 질문을 읽고 더 많은 것을 배우는 그들을 말할 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"Okay, let’s try it!","ko":"괜찮아, 그것을 시도하자!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Let’s do it!","ko":"그것을하자!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi there! And welcome to … Amelia, we don’t have a name for the show.","ko":"안녕하세요! 그리고 환영합니다 ... Amelia, 우리는 쇼의 이름을 가지고 있지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"We’ll think of a name later. For now, we’ll call it “The Show.”","ko":"우리는 나중에 이름을 생각할 것입니다. 지금, 우리는 \"The Show\"라고 부를 것입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Great. Hi there! And welcome to “The Show.”","ko":"훌륭합니다. 안녕! 그리고 \"The Show\"에 오신 것을 환영합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Today we are going to take you on a summer vacation! You will see popular things to do on vacation!","ko":"오늘 우리는 여름 휴가에 당신을 데려 갈 것입니다! 당신은 휴가에 할 인기있는 것들을 볼 것입니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"One is camping. When you go camping, you cook, sleep and play outdoors!","ko":"하나는 캠핑입니다. 당신이 캠핑을 갈 때, 당신은 요리, 수면과 야외를 재생!"},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"When I go camping, Anna, I like to go hiking and fishing.","ko":"내가 캠핑을 갈 때, Anna, 나는 하이킹과 낚시를하고 싶습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Me, too. Those are fun things to do when you go camping!","ko":"나를, 너무. 그들은 당신이 캠핑을 갈 때 할 수있는 재미있는 것들입니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"These people are hiking.","ko":"이 사람들은 하이킹입니다."},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"Okay, let’s talk about the next vacation.","ko":"그럼, 다음 휴가에 대해 이야기합시다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Another popular summer vacation is going to an amusement park. At an amusement park, you go on rides and eat lots of fun food!","ko":"또 다른 인기있는 여름 휴가는 놀이 공원에 가고있다. 놀이 공원에서, 당신은 타고 가서 재미 음식의 제비를 먹고!"},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"I love cotton candy … ! Anna & Amelia: and roller coasters!","ko":"나는 코튼 캔디 사랑 ... ! Anna & Amelia : 및 롤러 코스터! 영어 수업을 배우자 22 244"},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"This show is going to be a lot of fun.","ko":"이 쇼는 많은 재미가 될 것입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I know!","ko":"나는 알고있다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This is riding a roller coaster!","ko":"롤러 코스터를 타고 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"Whoooo! What is the last vacation?","ko":"누가! 마지막 휴가는 무엇입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"One of the most popular vacations is … going to the beach! Anna & Amelia: I love the beach!","ko":"가장 인기있는 휴가 중 하나 ... 해변에 가고! Anna & Amelia : 나는 해변을 사랑!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"When I see that blue ocean, I want to leave Washington, D.C. immediately and go to the beach!","ko":"푸른 바다가 보일 때, 나는 워싱턴, D.C.를 즉시 떠나 해변에 가자!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Maybe next summer.","ko":"다음 여름."},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"But right now, it’s time to work!","ko":"그러나 지금, 그것은 일하는 시간입니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Right. Until next time ...","ko":"오른쪽. 다음 시간까지 ... 영어 수업을 배우자 22 245"}],"words":[{"en":"amusement park","definition":"a place that has many games and rides (such as roller coasters and merry-go-rounds) for entertainment","ko":"놀이공원"},{"en":"beach","definition":"an area covered with sand or small rocks that is next to an ocean or lake","ko":"해변"},{"en":"camping","definition":"the activity of sleeping outdoors in a tent usually for enjoyment","ko":"캠핑"},{"en":"cotton candy","definition":"candy made from sugar that is boiled, spun into a soft material using a special machine, and then wound around a stick","ko":"솜사탕"},{"en":"fishing","definition":"the sport or business of catching fish","ko":"낚시"},{"en":"guest","definition":"a usually well-known person who is invited to appear or perform on a program","ko":"손님"},{"en":"hike","definition":"to walk a long distance especially for pleasure or exercise","ko":"하이킹하다"},{"en":"immediately","definition":"without any delay","ko":"즉시"},{"en":"introduce","definition":"to speak briefly to an audience about something that is about to begin","ko":"소개하다"},{"en":"kid","definition":"a young person","ko":"아이"},{"en":"outdoors","definition":"outside a building or not inside a building","ko":"야외"},{"en":"plan","definition":"a set of actions that have been thought of as a way to do or achieve something","ko":"계획"},{"en":"plan","definition":"to think about and arrange the parts or details of (something) before it happens or is made","ko":"계획하다"},{"en":"right","definition":"in a direct course or manner right now = immediately","ko":"맞는"},{"en":"roller coaster","definition":"a ride at an amusement park which is like a small, open train with tracks that are high off the ground and that have sharp curves and steep hills","ko":"롤러코스터"},{"en":"season","definition":"one of the four periods into which the year is commonly divided","ko":"계절"},{"en":"subject","definition":"the person or thing that is being discussed or described","ko":"과목"},{"en":"swimming","definition":"the sport or activity of moving through water by moving your arms and legs","ko":"수영"},{"en":"vacation","definition":"a period of time that a person spends away from home, school, or business usually in order to relax or travel The Four Seasons","ko":"휴가"},{"en":"spring","definition":"the season when plants and trees begin to grow","ko":"봄"},{"en":"summer","definition":"the warmest season of the year","ko":"여름"},{"en":"autumn","definition":"the third season of the year, when crops and fruits are gathered and leaves fall","ko":"가을"},{"en":"winter","definition":"the coldest season of the year","ko":"겨울"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 22 - Next Summer\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. Why does Anna say summer is her \nfavorite season?\na.\t\nShe likes summer vacation.\nb.\t\nAnna likes the temperature.\nc.\t\nShe does not like autumn.\nd.\t\nAnna says she likes the rain.\n4. What does Anna say about the \nbeach?\na.\t\nAnna likes the beach in Washington, \nD.C.\nb.\t\nShe wants to go to the beach \nimmediately.\nc.\t\nAnna does not want to go to the beach.\nd.\t\nShe likes the blue water, but does not \nlike the beach.\n2. What does Anna want to do after \nthey introduce the subject?\na.\t\nShe wants to talk to adults.\nb.\t\nAnna wants to end the show.\nc.\t\nShe wants to ask kids questions.\nd.\t\nAnna wants to show videos.\n5. Why does Anna say “Maybe next \nsummer?”\na.\t\nAnna does not really want to go to the \nbeach.\nb.\t\nShe does not know where she will live \nnext summer.\nc.\t\nAnna wants Amelia to go on a vacation \nnext summer.\nd.\t\nShe is sad she cannot take vacation \nthis summer.\n3. What do Anna and Amelia like to do \nwhen they go camping?\na.\t\nThey like to cook and sleep.\nb.\t\nThey sleep in a warm, comfortable bed.\nc.\t\nThey like to go hiking and fishing.\nd.\t\nThey cook, sleep, and play indoors.","guide":{"id":22,"focus":"휴가와 미래 계획을 이야기해요.","grammar":"I’m going to~는 ‘~할 계획이에요’예요. 계절과 활동을 함께 말해 보세요.","mission":"다음 여름에 하고 싶은 일 두 가지를 영어로 적어 보세요.","example":"I’m going to the beach.","exampleKo":"저는 해변에 갈 거예요."}},{"id":23,"startPage":253,"endPage":263,"topics":"Asking the time Counting change","strategy":"Respond","goals":"Grammar: Using want to express desires Speaking: Counting Change Pronunciation: Informal expressions - outta, yep, and whaddaya.","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Washington, D.C. has great food from all over the world.","ko":"워싱턴 D.C.는 전세계에서 훌륭한 음식이 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Today I’m having lunch with my boss. Ms. Weaver says we’re going on a trip around the world. But she knows I only have an hour for lunch! Silly woman.","ko":"오늘 나는 내 보스와 점심을 가지고있다. Ms. 웨버는 우리가 전 세계 여행에 가고 말한다. 그러나 그녀는 나는 점심에 대한 시간 만 알고! 실리 여성."},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Hi, Anna!","ko":"안녕, 안나!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi Jonathan! Hey, we are meeting Ms. Weaver for lunch at noon, aren’t we?","ko":"Hi Jonathan! Hey, 우리는 Ms 회의입니다. 노온에서 점심을 위해 웨버, 우리는하지 않습니다?"},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Yes.","ko":"예."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What time is it now?","ko":"지금 몇시입니까?"},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"11:50.","ko":"11:50."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"11:50! We have to go!","ko":"11:50! 우리는 가자!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"So, where is this world food restaurant?","ko":"그래서,이 세계 음식 레스토랑은 어디에 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"We’re not eating at a restaurant.","ko":"레스토랑에서 식사를하지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Where are we eating?","ko":"우리가 먹는 곳?"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"We are eating at ... food trucks!","ko":"우리는 ... 식품 트럭에서 먹는다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Food trucks … awesome! What’s a food truck?","ko":"식품 트럭 ... 멋진! 식품 트럭은 무엇입니까?"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"These are food trucks!","ko":"이 음식 트럭입니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Wow!","ko":"와우!"},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Whoa!","ko":"이름 *"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Okay, Jonathan, you will buy the first dish. Here is $10. Surprise us!","ko":"괜찮아, Jonathan, 당신은 첫 번째 접시를 살 것이다. 여기에는 $ 10. 우리를 놀라게!"},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Okay, I’ll be back in 15 minutes.","ko":"괜찮아, 나는 15 분 후에 돌아올 것입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What country do I want to visit?","ko":"어떤 국가가 방문하고 싶습니까?"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Anna, you pick the second country. Here is $10.","ko":"Anna, 당신은 두 번째 국가를 선택합니다. 여기에는 $ 10입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I want chicken.","ko":"닭고기를 원한다."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"The food truck, over there, has great chicken.","ko":"음식 트럭, 거기에, 중대한 닭이 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Awesome!","ko":"기본 정보"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"After you buy your food, meet me here.","ko":"당신이 당신의 음식을 사는 후에, 여기 만나십시오."},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Excuse me, I’ll have the shrimp.","ko":"내가 새우를 갖게 될 것입니다."},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Oh, you’re out of shrimp. Okay, I’ll have the beef then.","ko":"오, 새우가 있습니다. 괜찮아, 나는 쇠고기를 가지고있을거야."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello. I want the chicken dish.","ko":"안녕하세요. 닭고기를 원합니다."},{"speaker":"Worker","en":"We’re out of chicken.","ko":"닭고기입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"You’re out of chicken.","ko":"닭고기 밖으로."},{"speaker":"Worker","en":"Yep.","ko":"뚱 베어"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I’ll try another food truck. Thanks!","ko":"나는 다른 음식 트럭을 시도 할 것이다. 감사합니다!"},{"speaker":"Worker","en":"You’re welcome.","ko":"천만에요."},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Okay, here is your change. The dish is $7. So, here is 1, 2, 3 dollars back from your 10.","ko":"괜찮아, 여기에 당신의 변경입니다. 접시는 $7. 그래서, 여기에 1, 2, 3 달러에서 다시 10."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Great.","ko":"큰."},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Where’s Anna? Is she dancing by that food truck?","ko":"어디 안나? 그녀는 그 음식 트럭에 의해 춤?"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Yes. Yes, she is.","ko":"예. 예, 그녀는. 영어 수업을 배울하자 23 257"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Ms. Weaver, here is your change. The dish costs $5. So - $5 back.","ko":"Ms. Weaver, 여기에 당신의 변경입니다. 요리 비용 $5. 그래서 - $5 다시."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Thanks, Anna. But where is the food?","ko":"감사, 안나. 그러나 어디 음식?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I’m eating it. The Peruvian chicken is delicious! Try some! (Caty and Jonathan shake their heads “no”)","ko":"나는 그것을 먹고있다. 페루 닭은 맛있다! 약간 시도! (Caty and Jonathan은 머리 \"no\")"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Well, we still have $8! What do you want now?","ko":"글쎄, 우리는 여전히 $ 8을 가지고 있습니다! 지금 무엇을 원하십니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"We can buy dessert!","ko":"디저트를 구입할 수 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"I’ll buy dessert.","ko":"나는 디저트를 살거야."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"In Washington, D.C., you can travel around the world … with food trucks! And it does not cost a lot.","ko":"워싱턴에서, D.C., 당신은 세계를 여행 할 수 있습니다 ... 식품 트럭! 그리고 그것은 많은 비용을 지불하지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Until next time!","ko":"다음 시간까지! 영어 수업을 배우자 23 258"}],"words":[{"en":"after","definition":"following in time or at a later time","ko":"~후에"},{"en":"beef","definition":"meat from a cow or the meat of the cow used as food","ko":"소고기"},{"en":"chicken","definition":"a bird that is raised by people for its eggs and meat or the meat of the chicken used as food","ko":"닭고기"},{"en":"cost","definition":"to have (an amount of money) as a price","ko":"비용이 들다"},{"en":"delicious","definition":"very pleasant to taste","ko":"맛있는"},{"en":"dessert","definition":"sweet food eaten after the main part of a meal","ko":"디저트"},{"en":"dish","definition":"food that is prepared in a particular way","ko":"요리"},{"en":"hour","definition":"one of the 24 equal parts of a day; 60 minutes","ko":"시간"},{"en":"minute","definition":"a unit of time equal to 60 seconds; one 60th of an hour","ko":"분"},{"en":"noon","definition":"the middle of the day;12 o’clock in the daytime","ko":"정오"},{"en":"only","definition":"no more than","ko":"오직"},{"en":"pick","definition":"to choose or select (someone or something) from a group","ko":"고르다"},{"en":"shrimp -","definition":"small shellfish that has a long body and legs and that is eaten as food","ko":"새우"},{"en":"trip","definition":"a journey to a place","ko":"여행"},{"en":"truck","definition":"a very large, heavy vehicle that is used to move large or numerous objects","ko":"트럭"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 23 - What Do You Want?\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What time is it now?\na.\t\nIt is eleven-fifteen.\nb.\t\nIt is twelve-fifteen. \nc.\t\nIt is eleven-fifty. I want shrimp.\nd.\t\nIt is twelve-fifty.\n4. What does Jonathan say to ask for \nfood?\na.\t\nI want shrimp.\nb.\t\nGive me beef.\nc.\t\nI have some shrimp.\nd.\t\nI’ll have the beef.\n2. Why does Anna say “We have to go?”\na.\t\nAnna does not want to be late.\nb.\t\nShe wants to take Jonathan to lunch.\nc.\t\nAnna sees a person who she knows.\nd.\t\nShe does not want to see Ms. Weaver.\n5. How does Anna respond to what the \nwoman says?\na.\t\nShe says “I want the chicken dish.”\nb.\t\nAnna says “Thanks.”\nc.\t\nShe repeats what the woman says.\nd.\t\nAnna asks for a different dish.\n3. How much does the dish cost?\na.\t\nThe dish is $3.\nb.\t\nJonathan says the dish is $7.\nc.\t\nThe dish is $10.\nd.\t\nJonathan says the dish is $5.","guide":{"id":23,"focus":"가게에서 원하는 음식과 가격을 말해요.","grammar":"I want~는 ‘~을 원해요’, How much~?는 ‘얼마예요?’라는 뜻이에요.","mission":"가게 손님이 되어 원하는 상품과 가격을 묻고 답해 보세요.","example":"What do you want?","exampleKo":"무엇을 원하세요?"}},{"id":24,"startPage":264,"endPage":275,"topics":"Festivals Cultural traditions","strategy":"Substitute","goals":"Grammar: Regular Past Tense Verbs Speaking: Voiced and voiceless past tense pronunciations Pronunciation: Substituting one word for another","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yesterday was the most amazing day. I want to tell my friend back home about it. So, I am writing her a letter!","ko":"어제는 가장 놀라운 일이었습니다. 나는 그것에 대해 내 친구를 다시 집에 알리고 싶습니다. 그래서, 나는 그녀의 편지를 쓰고 있어요!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Dear Penelope, Life in Washington, D.C. is interesting. I see something new every day -- like yesterday. Yesterday started like a usual work day","ko":"친애하는 Penelope, 워싱턴의 생활, D.C. 흥미로운. 나는 어제처럼 새로운 것을 볼. 어제 평소처럼 시작"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I said, “Yesterday started like a usual work day.” Anna’s voice: I was at work. And I wanted a break. So, I walked and walked … and walked. Then, I saw something! It was a festival -- a big festival!","ko":"나는 말했다, “어제 일은 평소처럼 시작.” 안나의 목소리: 나는 일에 있었다. 그리고 나는 휴식하고 싶었다. 그래서, 나는 걸어 ... 그리고 걸어. 그런 다음, 나는 무언가를 보았다! 그것은 축제였다 -- 큰 축제!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"It is the Smithsonian Folklife Festival. Anna’s voice: Yes. It was the Smithsonian Folklife Festival. Every year the festival shows different cultures. This year one of the cultures was the Basque culture. There was dancing and food and games!”","ko":"Smithsonian Folklife Festival입니다. Anna의 목소리 : 예. Smithsonian Folklife Festival이었습니다. 매년 축제는 다양한 문화를 보여줍니다. 올해 문화 중 하나는 바스크 문화였습니다. 춤과 음식과 게임이있었습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I am dancing a traditional Basque dance. Anna’s voice: At the festival, I danced a traditional Basque dance!","ko":"나는 전통적인 바스크 춤을 춤. 안나의 목소리 : 축제에서 나는 전통 바스크 댄스를 춤 췄다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"They are cooking traditional Basque food. Anna’s voice: They cooked a lot of traditional Basque food.","ko":"그들은 전통 바스크 음식을 요리하고 있습니다. Anna의 목소리 : 그들은 많은 전통적인 바스크 음식을 요리했습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"They are playing a game. It’s a kind of handball. What do they call it? They call it pilota! Anna’s voice: They played a game with their hands and a small ball. It’s a kind of handball. But this game is called pilota.","ko":"그들은 게임을하고 있습니다. 그것은 핸드볼의 일종입니다. 그들은 그것을 호출하는 것은 무엇입니까? 그들은 파일럿에게 전화! Anna의 목소리 : 그들은 자신의 손으로 게임을 연주하고 작은 공. 그것은 핸드볼의 일종입니다. 그러나이 게임은 파일럿이라고합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This is beautiful! This is traditional Basque art.","ko":"이것은 아름답습니다! 이것은 전통적인 바스크 예술입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"They are making a traditional Basque ship. This festival is a lot of fun! Anna’s voice: The whole day was a lot of fun!","ko":"그들은 전통적인 바스크 배를 만들고있다. 이 축제는 재미의 많은! 안나의 목소리 : 하루는 재미의 많은이었다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Who said that? I want to write my friends and tell them about my day!","ko":"누가 말했다? 나는 내 친구를 쓰고 내 날에 그들에게 말씀하고 싶습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"… So, I wanted to tell you about my day! Please, my friend, come visit Washington, D.C. soon. There is a lot to do! Until next time … Anna.","ko":"... 그래서, 나는 내 날에 대해 말해 원! 제발, 내 친구, 방문 워싱턴, D.C. 곧. 할 많이있다! 다음 시간까지 ... 안나. 영어 수업을 배울하자 24 267"}],"words":[{"en":"was","definition":"past tense of the verb “be” in first or third person (I was; he/she/it was)","ko":"~였다"},{"en":"Basque Country","definition":"region of Spain","ko":"바스크 지방"},{"en":"culture","definition":"the beliefs, customs, or arts of a particular society","ko":"문화"},{"en":"festival","definition":"an organized series of performances","ko":"축제"},{"en":"handball","definition":"a game for two or four players who use their hands to hit a ball against a wall","ko":"핸드볼"},{"en":"interesting","definition":"attracting your attention and making you want to learn more about something or to be involved in something","ko":"흥미로운"},{"en":"said","definition":"past tense of the verb “say”","ko":"말했다"},{"en":"traditional","definition":"following the tradition of a certain group or culture Past tense verbs start - started want - wanted walk - walked dance - danced play - played call - called","ko":"전통적인"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 24 - Yesterday Was Amazing!\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What happened yesterday?\na.\t\nYesterday, Anna worked all day.\nb.\t\nAnna did not have to work.\nc.\t\nAnna saw something new.\nd.\t\nYesterday ended like a usual day.\n4. What does Anna say about the \nfestival?\na.\t\nShe liked the food and dancing at the\n festival.\nb.\t\nThe festival shows many cultures.\nc.\t\nAnna says the festival was long.\nd.\t\nThe Smithsonian Folklife festival is\nnew.\n2. What did they do?\na.\t\nThe men cooked Basque chicken.\nb.\t\nThey cooked traditional food.\nc.\t\nThe men looked at traditional Basque\nfood.\nd.\t\nThey ate traditional Basque food.\n5. Anna is using a machine in this\nvideo. You may not know the name of \nthe machine. What learning strategy \ncan you use to talk about it?\na.\t\nPlan\nb.\t\nMonitor\nc.\t\nSubstitute\nd.\t\nSummarize\n3. How does Anna describe the game?\na.\t\nAnna says the game is for small people.\nb.\t\nShe says they call it Dakota.\nc.\t\nAnna says pilota is a slow game.\nd.\t\nShe says it is a kind of handball.\n6. What does Anna say about the \npottery?\na.\t\nI want to learn to make beautiful \nBasque art.\nb.\t\nWhat do you call this Basque art?\nc.\t\nThese are Basque artists at work.\nd.\t\n...beautiful! This is traditional Basque\nart.\nPhotos for Practicing Substituting\n“Anna is helping make a ship. What is she using?”\n“What is the thing under the clay pot?”","guide":{"id":24,"focus":"어제 있었던 일을 이야기해요.","grammar":"과거 일을 말할 때 동사 뒤에 -ed를 붙이기도 해요. was는 am/is의 과거형이에요.","mission":"어제 즐거웠던 순간을 영어 두 문장으로 소개해 보세요.","example":"Yesterday was amazing!","exampleKo":"어제는 정말 멋졌어요!"}},{"id":25,"startPage":276,"endPage":286,"topics":"Playing games Warnings Recommending products, giving advice","strategy":"Make associations","goals":"","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello from Washington, DC! This city has many monuments and memorials.","ko":"워싱턴 DC에서 안녕하세요! 이 도시에는 많은 기념물과 기념비가 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Today I am visiting the ones built in memory of our Presidents: Washington, Jefferson, Lincoln and Roosevelt.","ko":"오늘 나는 우리의 대통령의 기억에 내장 된 것들을 방문 : 워싱턴, 제퍼슨, 링컨 및 로시벨트."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I want to learn more about them.","ko":"나는 그들에게 대해 더 많은 것을 배우고 싶다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hey! Watch out!","ko":"안녕하세요! 조심해!"},{"speaker":"Dan","en":"Sorry! I didn’t see you.","ko":"죄송합니다! 나는 당신을 볼 수 없었다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"You were not looking. You should be more careful.","ko":"너는 보고하지 않았다. 너는 더 조심해야 한다."},{"speaker":"Dan","en":"I know I should be more careful. But this game is really fun.","ko":"나는 더 조심해야합니다. 그러나이 게임은 정말 재미 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What kind of game?","ko":"어떤 종류의 게임?"},{"speaker":"Dan","en":"You have to find things that aren’t really there.","ko":"당신은 정말 거기 있지 않는 것들을 찾을 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"How can you find things that aren’t really there?","ko":"당신은 정말 거기 있지 않는 것들을 찾을 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Dan","en":"They’re in your phone. See?","ko":"그들은 휴대 전화에 있습니다. 참조?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I see. It’s like a scavenger hunt.","ko":"내가 본다. 그것은 사기꾼 사냥 처럼."},{"speaker":"Dan","en":"That’s right!","ko":"그게 바로!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I don’t have time for games. I want to learn about U.S. presidents.","ko":"나는 게임을 할 시간이 없습니다. 나는 미국 대통령에 대해 배우고 싶습니다."},{"speaker":"Dan","en":"Then you should play this game! When you find an American symbol, you win points and a Fun Fact about a U.S. President.","ko":"그런 다음이 게임을해야합니다! 당신은 미국 기호를 찾을 때, 당신은 포인트와 미국 대통령에 대한 재미있는 사실 승리."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I have time for this game!","ko":"나는이 게임에 대한 시간을 가지고!"},{"speaker":"Dan","en":"Here are the symbols that I caught: the Statue of Liberty for 20 points, Uncle Sam for 40 points and the American flag for 60 points.","ko":"여기에 내가 잡은 상징입니다: 자유의 동상 20 포인트, 삼촌 샘 40 포인트와 60 포인트에 대한 미국 국기."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What symbol are you looking for now?","ko":"지금 어떤 기호를 찾고 계십니까?"},{"speaker":"Dan","en":"I am looking for the bald eagle. That is 100 points! It should be near the Washington Monument.","ko":"나는 소설을 찾고 있습니다. 즉 100 점입니다! 그것은 워싱턴 기념물 근처에 있어야합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This game is awesome.","ko":"이 게임은 굉장합니다."},{"speaker":"Dan","en":"You ought to buy the app right now. It’s called “Catch Americana.”","ko":"지금 앱을 구입하는 것이 좋습니다. \"Catch Americana\"라고 불립니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Got it. Catch Americana.","ko":"그것을 얻었습니다. 캐치 Americana."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thanks! Good luck!","ko":"감사합니다! 행운을 빌어 요!"},{"speaker":"Dan","en":"Good luck to you too!","ko":"행운을 빌어요!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This is the Jefferson Memorial. I know that Thomas Jefferson signed the Declaration of Independence! Now, where is that symbol?","ko":"이 제퍼슨 기념입니다. 나는 토마스 제퍼슨이 독립 선언을 체결했다고 알고 있습니다! 지금, 그 기호는 어디에 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Here it is! My first one. It’s an American flag! I won 60 points!","ko":"여기! 내 첫 번째. 그것은 미국 국기입니다! 나는 60 포인트를 원!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"An American flag works well for Thomas Jefferson*. I see lots of American flags on Independence Day!","ko":"미국 플래그는 Thomas Jefferson*에서 잘 작동합니다. 나는 Independence Day에서 미국 플래그를 많이 볼 수 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Where is my Jefferson Fun Fact?","ko":"제퍼슨 펀팩트는 어디에 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Voice","en":"In his lifetime, Thomas Jefferson wrote about 19,000 letters!","ko":"그의 일생에서 Thomas Jefferson은 약 19,000 글자를 썼습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I did not know that. Where is the next symbol? *See an explanation of this sentence in the Learning Strategy section.","ko":"나는 그것을 모른다. 다음 기호는 어디에 있습니까? * 학습 전략 섹션에서이 문장의 설명을 참조하십시오."}],"words":[{"en":"Americana","definition":"things produced in the U.S. and thought to be typical of the U.S. or its culture","ko":"미국 전통문화의"},{"en":"bald eagle","definition":"a very large bird of North America that has a white head and white tail feathers","ko":"흰머리독수리"},{"en":"build / built","definition":"to make (something) by putting together parts or materials be careful! - an instruction to take care in a particular situation","ko":"짓다·지었다"},{"en":"catch/caught","definition":"to capture and not allow (a person, animal, or fish) to escape","ko":"잡다·잡았다"},{"en":"Declaration of Independence","definition":"the statement adopted by the Second Continental Congress meeting at Philadelphia, Pennsylvania on July 4, 1776. It said that the thirteen American colonies would not accept British rule","ko":"미국 독립선언문"},{"en":"find / found","definition":"to get or discover something or someone that you are looking for","ko":"찾다·찾았다"},{"en":"flag","definition":"a piece of cloth with a special design that is used as a symbol of a nation or group","ko":"깃발"},{"en":"Independence Day","definition":"July 4 celebrated as a legal holiday in the U.S. in honor of the day when the Declaration of Independence was signed in 1776","ko":"독립기념일"},{"en":"memory","definition":"the power or process of remembering what has been learned in memory of or in someone’s memory - made or done to honor someone who has died","ko":"기억"},{"en":"ought to","definition":"verb. used to say or suggest that something is the proper, reasonable, or best thing to do. It has the same meaning as should and is used in the same ways, but it is less common and somewhat more formal.","ko":"~해야 한다"},{"en":"point","definition":"a unit that is used to score a game or contest","ko":"가리키다"},{"en":"scavenger hunt","definition":"a game in which players try to find specified items within a particular period of time","ko":"보물찾기"},{"en":"should","definition":"used to say or suggest that something is the proper, reasonable, or best thing to do","ko":"~하는 게 좋다"},{"en":"Statue of Liberty","definition":"A large sculpture given to the United States from the people of France. It is a symbol of freedom and democracy.","ko":"자유의 여신상"},{"en":"symbol","definition":"an action, object, event, etc., that expresses or represents a particular idea or quality","ko":"상징"},{"en":"Uncle Sam","definition":"A common symbol of the government of the United States.","ko":"엉클 샘"},{"en":"Watch out!","definition":"to be aware of something dangerous America’s Presidents Thomas Jefferson - America’s 3rd president, Thomas Jefferson, signed the Declaration of Independence on America’s birthday - the 4th of July. (The symbol for President Jefferson in the Catch Americana game is an American flag.)","ko":"조심해!"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 25 - Watch Out!\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. How does Anna give advice to Dan? \na.\t Anna says “Hey!” To Dan. \nb.\t She tells Dan he was not looking. \nc.\t Anna tells Dan to stay away. \nd.\t She says Dan should be more careful. \n4. Which learning strategy is Anna \nusing? \na.\t Anna is summarizing. \nb.\t Anna is making associations. \nc.\t Anna is asking questions. \nd.\t Anna is predicting. \n2. Why does Dan tell Anna to play the \ngame? \na.\t Anna says she loves to play games on \nher phone. \nb.\t Dan says the game will help Anna meet \nnew friends. \nc.\t Anna says she wants to learn about \nU.S. Presidents. \nd.\t Dan wants to teach Anna about the U.S. \nPresidents. \n5. What does Anna say about the U.S. \nPresidents? \na.\t Hi, want to learn more about them? \nb.\t I want to learn more about Tim. \nc.\t She wants to tell their stories. \nd.\t I want to learn more about them. \n3. How does Dan give advice to Anna? \na.\t Dan says Anna ought to buy the app. \nb.\t He says Anna should play the game \nwith him. \nc.\t Dan says Anna has to buy the app right \nnow. \nd.\t He says everyone is playing the game. \n6. What does Dan say about the \ngame? \na.\t You have to find things that aren’t on \nthe chair. \nb.\t You have to find things that aren’t really \nthere. \nc.\t You have to find rings that are really \nthere. \nd.\t You have to put things in places here \nand there.\nThomas Jefferson Memorial\n(for a video introduction, see https://www.nps.gov/thje/index.htm)","guide":{"id":25,"focus":"위험을 경고하고 조언해요.","grammar":"Watch out!은 ‘조심해!’예요. should는 ‘~하는 게 좋다’, ought to도 조언이에요.","mission":"위험한 상황 두 가지를 떠올려 주의 문장을 만들어 보세요.","example":"Watch out!","exampleKo":"조심하세요!"}},{"id":26,"startPage":287,"endPage":296,"topics":"Warning of danger U.S. Presidents Symbols of the United States","strategy":"Make associations","goals":"","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This is the Roosevelt Memorial. Where is the symbol? (Anna remembers that Dan said: You have to find things that aren’t really there. ... When you find an American symbol, you win points and a Fun Fact about a U.S. President.)","ko":"이것은 Roosevelt 기념입니다. 기호는 어디에 있습니까? (Anna는 Dan이 말한 것을 기억합니다. 당신은 정말 거기 있지 않는 것들을 찾을 필요가 있습니다. ... 당신이 미국 기호를 찾을 때, 당신은 포인트와 미국 대통령에 대한 재미있는 사실.)"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yay! I found Uncle Sam and I won another 40 points! What is the Fun Fact?","ko":"Yay! 나는 삼촌 Sam을 발견하고 나는 또 다른 40 포인트를 받았다! 재미 사실은 무엇입니까?"},{"speaker":"Voice","en":"Franklin Roosevelt was the first to fly in a plane as president!","ko":"프랭클린 Roosevelt는 대통령으로 비행기에서 비행 한 최초의이었다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I didn’t know that. This is a really beautiful memorial.","ko":"나는 그것을 몰랐다. 이것은 정말 아름다운 기념입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This is the Lincoln Memorial! Where is the symbol?","ko":"링컨 기념! 상징은 어디입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I found it! The Statue of Liberty! Please give me my Fun Fact.","ko":"나는 그것을 발견! 자유의 동상! 내 재미 사실을주십시오."},{"speaker":"Voice","en":"Abraham Lincoln was a great wrestler!","ko":"아브라함 링컨은 훌륭한 레슬링자였습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I didn’t know that. Lincoln wanted freedom for all people. So, the Statue of Liberty works well.","ko":"나는 그것을 몰랐다. 링컨은 모든 사람들을 위해 자유를 원했다. 그래서, 자유의 동상은 잘 작동합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"And I won 20 points! Time to find the next symbol.","ko":"그리고 나는 20 포인트를 수상! 다음 기호를 찾을 시간."},{"speaker":"Dan","en":"Hey! Look out!","ko":"안녕하세요! 봐!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sorry. Hey, it’s you! Now, I should be more careful.","ko":"죄송합니다. 여러분! 이제 더 조심해야 합니다."},{"speaker":"Dan","en":"That’s okay.","ko":"그게 괜찮아."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This game is a lot of fun. Hey, what’s your name?","ko":"이 게임은 많은 재미입니다. 이봐, 당신의 이름은 무엇입니까?"},{"speaker":"Dan","en":"Dan. What’s yours?","ko":"댄. 너의 것은 무엇입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Anna.","ko":"안나."},{"speaker":"Dan","en":"Like Americana!","ko":"미국인처럼!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yeah, I guess so.","ko":"그래, 나는 그렇게 추측한다."},{"speaker":"Dan","en":"Did you find any symbols?","ko":"어떤 기호를 발견 했습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes, I found three and won 120 points!","ko":"네, 세 번을 찾았고 120 포인트를 획득했습니다!"},{"speaker":"Dan","en":"Me too. But, did you find the bald eagle?","ko":"나를 너무. 그러나, 당신은 bald 독을 발견 했습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No. Did you?","ko":"아니. 너?"},{"speaker":"Dan","en":"No.","ko":"아니요."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"First one to find it wins?","ko":"먼저 승리를 찾을 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Dan","en":"Anna, look out for that tree!","ko":"Anna, 그 나무를 조심!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I learned a lot about presidents with this game. But I ought to be more careful. Until next time …!","ko":"나는이 게임과 함께 대통령에 대해 많이 배웠다. 그러나 나는 더 조심해야합니다. 다음 시간까지 ...!"}],"words":[{"en":"(air)plane","definition":"a vehicle that has wings and an engine and can carry people or things in the air","ko":"비행기"},{"en":"fly","definition":"to travel in an aircraft or spacecraft","ko":"날다"},{"en":"freedom","definition":"the power to do what you want to do or the ability to move or act freely","ko":"자유"},{"en":"Look out","definition":"used to tell someone to be aware of something dangerous","ko":"조심해!"},{"en":"wrestler","definition":"someone who competes in the sport of wrestling","ko":"레슬링 선수"},{"en":"yay","definition":"used to express joy, approval, or excitement American Presidents and Symbols (Part Two) Abraham Lincoln America’s 16th President, Abraham Lincoln signed the Emancipation Proclamation. It said the 3 million enslaved people in the South were free. They could enjoy some kinds of freedom after the end of the American Civil War. (President Lincoln’s symbol in the Catch Americana game is the Statue of Liberty.) Franklin Delano Roosevelt America’s 32nd president, Franklin Delano Roosevelt, was president from March 4, 1933 – April 12, 1945. He was the only President elected to four terms, and the only paralyzed President. FDR led the United States through World War Two. (President Roosevelt’s symbol in the Catch Americana game is Uncle Sam. The Uncle Sam symbol called many American men to join the U.S. Army to fight in the World Wars.) George Washington George Washington was the first President of the United States, from 1789 to 1797. He was a strong leader for America. The bald eagle is the national bird of the United States. People think of the eagle as strong and powerful.","ko":"야호!"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 26 - This Game is Fun!\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Dan say about the \ngame? \na.\t You have to find things that aren’t really\n there. \nb.\t You have to find things then run from a\n bear. \nc.\t True, you can find things that are near \nthe chair. \n4. Why does Dan say “like \nAmericana?”\na.\t Dan is making associations. \nb.\t He is showing he does not understand.\nc.\t Dan is trying to be polite. \nd.\t He is asking Anna if she likes Catch\nAmericana. \n2. What is the fun fact about Franklin \nRoosevelt?\n  a.  He was the first President to pilot a \nplane\n  b.  Roosevelt was the first to use planes in \nwar.\n  c.  He was the first President to own an \nairplane. \n5. What does Anna say when she \nwalks into the tree?\na.\t I ought to be more careful. \nb.\t I have got to be more careful. \nc.\t But I have to call my friend Carol. \nd.\t The butter in my hair smells terrible. \n3. What is the fun fact about \nAbraham Lincoln?\na.\t Abraham Lincoln was a game player. \nb.\t The game says he built the Statue of \nLiberty. \nc.\t Abraham Lincoln was a great wrestler. \nd.\t The game says Lincoln freed the \nslaves.","guide":{"id":26,"focus":"게임을 하며 주의 사항을 알려요.","grammar":"Look out!도 ‘조심해!’라는 뜻이에요. ought to는 빠르게 연결해서 발음해요.","mission":"게임할 때 필요한 규칙과 주의 사항을 말해 보세요.","example":"This game is fun!","exampleKo":"이 게임은 재미있어요!"}},{"id":27,"startPage":297,"endPage":308,"topics":"Asking about health problems Giving advice for health problems","strategy":"Analyze information","goals":"Grammar: Irregular past tense verbs Speaking: Health problems and excuses Pronunciation: Wh-questions and Yes/No question intonation","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello! I am sure that today, in Washington, D.C,. there are a lot of great things to do. But I am not doing any of them. I am sick. Right now, I’m going to call my boss and tell her I cannot come in to work.","ko":"안녕하세요! 저는 오늘, 워싱턴 DC에서,. 할 수있는 많은 좋은 것들이 있습니다. 그러나 나는 그들 중 하나를하지 않습니다. 나는 아픈. 지금, 나는 내 보스를 호출하고 내가 작업 할 수 없다는 것을 말해."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Hello?","ko":"안녕하세요?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Ms. Weaver, Hi. I can’t come to work today.","ko":"Ms. Weaver, 안녕하세요. 오늘 일할 수 없습니다."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Why not? What is wrong?","ko":"왜 잘못되었습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well, yesterday I felt fine.","ko":"잘, 어제 나는 벌금을 느꼈다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"In the morning, I painted for hours. In the afternoon, I cut wood. Then, I built a fire.","ko":"아침에, 나는 시간을 위해 그려. 오후에, 나는 나무를 잘라. 그런 다음, 나는 불을 만들었습니다."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"Anna, what do you mean? Why can’t you come to work today?","ko":"Anna, 무엇을 의미합니까? 왜 오늘 일할 수 없습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I do not feel well. I think I’m sick.","ko":"나는 잘 느끼지 않는다. 나는 아픈 생각한다."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"I’m sorry to hear that. I was sick last week, too. I had the flu.","ko":"나는 그것을 듣고 미안 해요. 나는 지난 주에 아픈, 너무. 나는 독감했다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"(sneezes) What did you do?","ko":"(sneezes) 당신은 무엇을 했습니까?"},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"I slept a lot and I drank a lot of water. Do you have a doctor?","ko":"나는 많은 물을 붓고 난 많은 물을 붓는다. 당신은 의사가 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes, I do.","ko":"예, 나는."},{"speaker":"Caty","en":"You should call your doctor. And get lots of rest!","ko":"당신은 당신의 의사에게 전화해야합니다. 그리고 나머지를 많이 얻을!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thanks, Ms. Weaver. I’ll call right now. I’m calling my doctor. Dr. Bennett: (to herself) Now, where does this thing go? Dr. Bennett: Hello. This is Dr. Bennett. How can I help you?","ko":"감사합니다, Ms. 웨버. 나는 지금 바로 전화 할 것입니다. 나는 내 의사를 호출합니다. 벤넷 박사 : (자신) 지금,이 일을하는 곳? 박사 Bennett : 안녕하세요. 이것은 벤넷 박사입니다. 어떻게 도와 드릴 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello, Dr. Bennett. This is Anna. Dr. Bennett: Oh, Hi, Anna. How can I help you?","ko":"안녕하세요, 벤넷 박사. 이것은 안나입니다. 벤넷 박사 : 오, 안녕, 안나. 어떻게 도와 드릴 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I think I’m sick. Dr. Bennett: Let me ask you a couple of questions. Do you have a sore throat?","ko":"나는 아픈 생각. 박사. Bennett : 나는 당신에게 몇 가지 질문을하자. 당신은 아픈 목이 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes. I have a sore throat. Dr. Bennett: Do you have a cough?","ko":"예. 나는 목이 있습니다. 박사. Bennett : 당신은 기침이 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes. I have a cough. Dr. Bennett: When did you start feeling sick?","ko":"예. 나는 기침이 있습니다. 벤넷 박사 : 당신은 아픈 느낌을 시작했을 때?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This morning. Yesterday I felt great. In the morning I painted, for hours - in the afternoon I cut wood - Dr. Bennett: Excuse me, Anna. But I don’t need to know all that. Do you have a fever?","ko":"이 아침. 어제 나는 큰 느낌. 아침에 나는 페인트, 시간 - 오후에 나는 나무를 잘라 - 박사. 베네넷 : 나에게 변태, 안나. 그러나 나는 그 모든 것을 알 필요가 없습니다. 당신은 발열이 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh. My thermometer says 125 degrees?! What?? Dr. Bennett: Yeah, that’s not right.","ko":"오. 내 온도계는 125도라고 말합니까?! 무엇? 박사. Bennett : 그래, 그게 맞지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh. Wait. The thermometer was in my hot cup of coffee. Dr. Bennett: Please take it again, Anna.","ko":"오. 대기. 온도계는 커피의 나의 뜨거운 컵에 있었습니다. Bennett 박사: anna를 다시 가지고 가십시오."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Okay, the thermometer says 100.5 degrees. Dr. Bennett: 100.5 degrees is not too high. I want you to drink lots of water. Rest in bed and get lots of sleep.","ko":"잘, 온도계는 말한다 100.5 도. 박사 Bennett: 100.5 도 너무 높지 않습니다. 나는 많은 물을 마시고 싶습니다. 침대에서 휴식과 수면을 많이 얻을 수 있습니다. 영어 수업 27 301"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"That is what my boss said to do. Um, Dr. Bennett, when can I go to work? Dr. Bennett: Don’t go to work for a couple of days.","ko":"그게 내 보스가 할 것이라고 말했다. 우우, 박사 Bennett, 내가 일할 때? 박사. Bennett : 며칠 동안 일하지 마십시오."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes! I mean, I don’t want to make my co-workers sick. Dr. Bennett: That’s right. Call me back in a couple of days.","ko":"예! 나는 의미, 나는 내 협동자 병을 만들기 원하지 않는다. 벤넷 박사 : 그게 맞습니다. 몇 일 안에 다시 전화하십시오."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I will, Dr. Bennett. And thanks.","ko":"나는 Bennett 박사. 그리고 감사."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well, you heard the doctor – no work for a couple of days. I need water, sleep and um … lots of movies! Well, the doctor didn’t say anything about movies. But it can’t hurt! Until next time!","ko":"잘, 당신은 의사를 들었다 - 몇 일 동안 작동하지 않습니다. 나는 물, 수면 및 um을 필요로 ... 영화의 제비! 글쎄, 의사는 영화에 대해 아무것도 말하지 않았다. 그러나 그것은 상처를 입을 수 없습니다! 다음 시간까지! 영어 수업을 배우자 27 302"}],"words":[{"en":"cough","definition":"the act of forcing air through your throat with a short, loud noise often because you are sick","ko":"기침하다"},{"en":"doctor","definition":"a person who is skilled in the science of medicine","ko":"의사"},{"en":"fever","definition":"a body temperature that is higher than normal","ko":"열"},{"en":"fire","definition":"the light and heat and especially the flame produced by burning","ko":"불"},{"en":"flu","definition":"a common disease that is caused by a virus and that causes fever, weakness, body aches, and breathing problems; also called influenza","ko":"독감"},{"en":"rest","definition":"to stop doing work or an activity","ko":"쉬다"},{"en":"sick","definition":"affected with a disease or illness; ill","ko":"아픈"},{"en":"sneeze","definition":"to suddenly force air out through your nose and mouth with a usually loud noise because your body is reacting to dust or a sickness","ko":"재채기하다"},{"en":"sore","definition":"feeling or affected by pain","ko":"쓰라린"},{"en":"thermometer","definition":"an instrument used for measuring temperature","ko":"체온계"},{"en":"throat","definition":"the tube inside the neck that leads to the stomach and lungs","ko":"목구멍"},{"en":"wood","definition":"the hard substance that makes up the stems and branches of trees and shrubs Past Tense Verbs","ko":"나무"},{"en":"cut / cut","definition":"to use a sharp tool (such as a knife) to open or divide (something, such as paper or wood)","ko":"자르다·잘랐다"},{"en":"do / did","definition":"to perform an action or activity","ko":"하다·했다"},{"en":"drink / drank","definition":"to take a liquid into your mouth and swallow it","ko":"마시다·마셨다"},{"en":"feel / felt","definition":"used to describe someone’s physical or mental state","ko":"느끼다·느꼈다"},{"en":"hear / heard","definition":"to be aware of (sound) through the ear","ko":"듣다·들었다"},{"en":"hurt / hurt","definition":"to be a source or cause of pain","ko":"다치다·다쳤다"},{"en":"paint / painted","definition":"to cover (something) with paint or to put paint on (something)","ko":"칠하다·칠했다"},{"en":"say / said","definition":"to use your voice to express (something) with words","ko":"말하다·말했다"},{"en":"sleep / slept","definition":"to rest your mind and body by closing your eyes and becoming unconscious","ko":"잠자다·잤다"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 27 - I Can’t Come In\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. How do you know that Ms. Weaver is \ntalking about the past?\na.\t\nShe uses past tense verbs.\nb.\t\nMs. Weaver says the word “before.”\nc.\t\nShe says the words “last year.”\nd.\t\nMs. Weaver uses the present \ncontinuous.\n4. What strategy is Dr. Bennett using?\na.\t Dr. Bennett is predicting.\nb.\t She is rehearsing a conversation.\nc.\t Dr. Bennett is analyzing information.\nd.\t She is summarizing.\n2. Why does Dr. Bennett say, “This is Dr. \nBennett. How can I help you?”\na.\t\nShe does not want to talk to anyone.\nb.\t\nDr. Bennett knows that Anna is sick.\nc.\t\nShe does not know who is calling.\nd.\t\nDr. Bennett is asking Anna for help.\n5. Why does Dr. Bennett say, “Excuse \nme”?\na.\t\nDr. Bennett cannot hear Anna.\nb.\t\nShe has another patient.\nc.\t\nDr. Bennett does not like Anna.\nd.\t\nShe wants a chance to speak.\n3. What does Anna say?\na.\t\nAnna waited in the morning.\nb.\t\nShe painted for hours.\nc.\t\nAnna picked wildflowers.\nd.\t\nShe painted some flowers.","guide":{"id":27,"focus":"몸 상태가 안 좋을 때 설명해요.","grammar":"I have a fever는 ‘열이 나요’예요. did, drank처럼 형태가 달라지는 불규칙 과거형도 나와요.","mission":"병원에서 증상을 설명하고 휴식이 필요하다고 말해 보세요.","example":"I have a fever.","exampleKo":"저 열이 나요."}},{"id":28,"startPage":309,"endPage":320,"topics":"Apologizing Giving reasons or excuses","strategy":"Self talk","goals":"Grammar: Imperative (command) verb forms; BE verb in the past tense Speaking: How to apologize Pronunciation: Saying “well” when giving an unexpected answer","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello! Guess what this is? This is my driver’s license! I passed my driving test! Today, I rented a car so I can drive around Washington, D.C. You can see more of the city this way. Marsha!","ko":"안녕하세요! 이것이 무엇입니까? 이것은 내 드라이버의 라이센스입니다! 나는 내 운전 테스트를 통과했습니다! 오늘, 나는 워싱턴, D.C. 주위에 운전 할 수 있도록 차를 빌려. 당신은이 방법의 더 많은 도시를 볼 수 있습니다. 마샤!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Anna, did you get your driver’s license?","ko":"Anna, 당신은 당신의 드라이버의 라이센스를 얻을?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I did! But it was not easy.","ko":"나는 않았다! 그러나 그것은 쉽지 않았습니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Why? What happened?","ko":"왜? 무슨 일이 있었습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well, you know, I can drive farm equipment really well. But I was really nervous driving in Washington, D.C. traffic!","ko":"글쎄, 나는 농장 장비를 정말 잘 구동 할 수 있습니다. 그러나 나는 워싱턴, D.C. 트래픽에서 정말 긴장했다!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Did you pass the test the first time?","ko":"테스트를 처음 통과 했습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well…no. But I did pass the second time.","ko":"글쎄...아니. 그러나 나는 두 번째 시간을 통과했다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"What happened during the first test?","ko":"첫 번째 테스트 중에 무슨 일이 있었습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"It started fine.","ko":"그것은 잘 시작."},{"speaker":"John","en":"Okay … Anna. Is your seatbelt buckled?","ko":"좋아 ... Anna. 당신의 seatbelt 버클?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes, sir!","ko":"예, 사이!"},{"speaker":"John","en":"Great. Please start the car.","ko":"좋은. 차를 시작하십시오."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"(to herself) Okay, Anna, start the car. Started the car. Good job, Anna.","ko":"(자신) 잘, 안나, 차를 시작. 차를 시작. 좋은 일, 안나."},{"speaker":"John","en":"Why are you talking to yourself?","ko":"왜 너 자신에 대해 얘기하나요?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I am a little nervous. When I’m nervous, I talk to myself.","ko":"나는 조금 신경입니다. 나는 신경이있을 때, 나는 자신에게 이야기합니다."},{"speaker":"John","en":"You don’t need to be nervous.","ko":"당신은 신경이 없어."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Listen to that engine!","ko":"그 엔진을 듣다!"},{"speaker":"John","en":"Please, stop pushing the gas pedal!","ko":"가스 페달을 밀어주십시오!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sorry.","ko":"의논하기"},{"speaker":"John","en":"Okay, when you are ready, turn.","ko":"그래, 준비가 될 때, 턴."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Great!","ko":"큰!"},{"speaker":"John","en":"Not now! You almost hit that car!","ko":"이제까지! 당신은 거의 자동차에 충돌!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"You said “turn!”","ko":"당신은 말했다 “턴!”"},{"speaker":"John","en":"Look first! There were cars in the street.","ko":"먼저 봐! 거리에서 자동차가있었습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Please don’t yell at me!","ko":"너를 저에 넣지 말라!"},{"speaker":"John","en":"I’m sorry! I was afraid.","ko":"나는 미안 해요! 나는 두려워했다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"You were yelling.","ko":"너희는 너희가 거역하였노라"},{"speaker":"John","en":"Look out for that car! Brake! Brake!! Anna & John: Ahhh!","ko":"그 차를 찾아 봐! 브레이크! 브레이크! Anna & John : Ahhh!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Why is everyone honking at us?","ko":"왜 우리 모두에 혼동입니까?"},{"speaker":"John","en":"You were driving too slow! Anna, stay on the street!","ko":"당신은 너무 느리게 운전했다! 안나, 거리에 머물!"},{"speaker":"John","en":"Hands on the wheel, Anna.","ko":"바퀴에 손을, Anna."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What’s that sound?","ko":"그 소리는 무엇입니까? 영어 수업을 배우자 28 314"},{"speaker":"John","en":"That, Anna, is the police.","ko":"그, 안나, 경찰이다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"That sounds awful.","ko":"그 소리가 울렸다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes, it did not go well. But, I practiced and passed the second time!","ko":"예, 잘하지 않았다. 그러나, 나는 연습하고 두 번째 시간을 통과!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Do you know where you want to take your first drive in Washington, D.C.?","ko":"워싱턴 D.C.에서 첫 번째 드라이브를 찍고 싶으신가요?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes! Let’s go!","ko":"예! 가자!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"There it is … the White House!","ko":"그것은 ... 화이트 하우스!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Anna, you do know you can’t drive up to the White House, don’t you?","ko":"Anna, White House까지 운전할 수 없습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes. No. I didn’t know. I guess we walk from here!","ko":"예. 아니오. 나는 몰랐다. 나는 우리가 여기에서 걸어 봅시다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sometimes you can see more of Washington, D.C. in a car. If you want to see the White House, you need to walk. Until next time … !","ko":"때로는 더 많은 것을 볼 수 있습니다 워싱턴, D.C. 차. 당신은 화이트 하우스를보고 싶다면, 당신은 걸어해야합니다. 다음 시간까지 ... ! 영어 수업을 배우자 28 315"}],"words":[{"en":"afraid","definition":"feeling fear","ko":"두려운"},{"en":"brake","definition":"to use the brake on a vehicle - n. a device for slowing or stopping something (such as a wheel or vehicle)","ko":"브레이크"},{"en":"buckle","definition":"to fasten (something, such as a belt) with a buckle","ko":"버클·잠그다"},{"en":"equipment","definition":"supplies or tools needed for a special purpose","ko":"장비"},{"en":"gas pedal","definition":"a pedal in a vehicle that is pressed down to make the vehicle go faster Guess what? - expression. a phrase used to build anticipation","ko":"가속 페달"},{"en":"pass / passed","definition":"to complete a test or a class successfully","ko":"통과하다·합격했다"},{"en":"police","definition":"the people or the department of people who enforce laws, investigate crimes, and make arrests","ko":"경찰"},{"en":"seat belt","definition":"a strap on a vehicle’s seat that holds a person in the seat if there is an accident","ko":"안전벨트"},{"en":"tractor","definition":"a short, heavy truck that is designed to pull a large trailer","ko":"트랙터"},{"en":"traffic","definition":"all the vehicles driving along a certain road or in a certain area","ko":"교통"},{"en":"turn","definition":"to move in a particular direction and especially toward the left or right","ko":"방향을 틀다"},{"en":"turn signal","definition":"one of the lights on a vehicle that flash to indicate that the vehicle is turning left or right","ko":"방향지시등"},{"en":"White House","definition":"the place in Washington, D.C., where the U.S. President lives","ko":"백악관"},{"en":"yell","definition":"to say (something) very loudly especially because you are angry, surprised, or are trying to get someone’s attention","ko":"소리치다"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 28 - I Passed It!\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Anna plan to do today?\na.\t\nTake a driving test\nb.\t\nLook for a new car\nc.\t\nGo to another city\nd.\t\nDrive around the city\n5. Which learning strategy is Anna \nusing?\na.\t\nAnna is using Visualization.\nb.\t\nShe is Analyzing Information.\nc.\t\nAnna is using Self-Talk.\nd.\t\nShe is using Movements.\n2. What does Marsha want to know?\na.\t\nDoes Anna have her driver’s license?\nb.\t\nWill Anna go driving today?\nc.\t\nIs it hard to pass the driving test?\nd.\t\nDoes Anna have a new car? \n6. Which are the imperative verbs in \nthis video?\na.\t\nplease, sorry, ready\nb.\t\nturn, look, yell\nc.\t\nalmost, first, now\nd.\t\nokay, great, don’t\n3. Why didn’t Anna pass the test?\na.\t\nAnna drove farm equipment.\nb.\t\nShe drove too fast in traffic.\nc.\t\nAnna was too nervous.\nd.\t\nShe had an accident. \n7. What does John Russell tell \nAnna?\na.\t Watch out for other cars.\nb.\t Stop yelling.\nc.\t You failed your test.\nd.\t Drive fast.  \n4. Why does Anna say the word “Well” \nslowly?\na.\t She does not know the answer to the \nquestion.\nb.\t She does not want to tell Marsha the \nstory.\nc.\t Anna wants to make Marsha laugh.\nd.\t Anna is happy about her driving test. \n8. What does Anna do wrong?\na.\t She drives off of the street.\nb.\t She drives too slowly. \nc.\t She takes her hand off of the wheel.\nd.\t She does all of these things.","guide":{"id":28,"focus":"실수를 사과하고 도움을 구해요.","grammar":"명령문은 동사로 시작해요. I was~는 ‘저는 ~였어요’라는 과거 표현이에요.","mission":"길에서 실수했을 때 정중하게 사과하는 연습을 해 보세요.","example":"I’m sorry.","exampleKo":"죄송합니다."}},{"id":29,"startPage":321,"endPage":332,"topics":"Active listening Childhood dreams","strategy":"Personalize","goals":"Grammar: Review simple past and irregular past tense verbs; Using adjectives with correct adjective placement; Infinitives: to read, to be; to work Speaking: Using adjectives Pronunciation: Active listening using uh-huh and um-hum","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello! In Washington, D.C., there are many places that bring history to life. But people who live here often do not have time to see them. They are too busy with work -- like me. Hi, Marsha!","ko":"안녕하세요! 워싱턴에서 D.C., 삶에 역사를 가지고 많은 장소가 있습니다. 그러나 여기에 살고있는 사람들은 수시로 그들을 볼 시간이 없습니다. 그들은 너무 바쁘다 -- 나처럼. 안녕, 마샤!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Hi, Anna! Have a seat.","ko":"안녕, 안나! 좌석이 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thanks. This was a good idea. Working outdoors is nice.","ko":"감사합니다. 이것은 좋은 아이디어였습니다. 일하는 옥외는 좋습니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Um-hum, it is.","ko":"움푹, 그것은입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I am tired. Today was a busy day at work. And I still have work to do!","ko":"나는 피곤했습니다. 오늘은 직장에서 바쁜 일이었습니다. 그리고 나는 여전히 일을했습니다!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Hmm, that’s too bad.","ko":"Hmm, 그것은 너무 나쁘다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"How are you these days?","ko":"이 날은 어떻습니까?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"I’m really busy too, Anna. Let’s get to work.","ko":"나는 정말 바쁘다, 안나. 일을 하자."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Marsha, look! That bus has a photo of Abraham Lincoln!","ko":"Marsha, 봐! 그 버스는 아브라함 링컨의 사진을 가지고!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"That’s an advertisement for Ford’s Theatre. They have a new show.","ko":"그것은 포드 극장을위한 광고입니다. 그들은 새로운 쇼가 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"They have shows where Abraham Lincoln died?","ko":"그들은 아브라함 링컨이 죽었는지 보여줍니다?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Yeah, it’s a working theater and a museum.","ko":"그래, 작업 극장과 박물관입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I love Lincoln. You know, Marsha, that advertisement reminds me of something.","ko":"나는 링컨을 사랑한다. 당신은 알고, Marsha, 그 광고는 무언가의 나를 상기."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Um-hum. What’s that?","ko":"Um-hum. 그게 뭐니?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"When I was a little girl … When I was a little girl … I was not like other children.","ko":"언제 나는 작은 소녀 ... 때 나는 작은 소녀였다 ... 나는 다른 아이들과 같은하지 않았다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Um-hum, I can believe that. Anna’s voice: I was a tall, serious child. At the playground the other children played silly games. They played with dart guns. They played on the swings, the slide and the teeter-totter. They also played ball But not me. I loved to read serious books about U.S. presidents.","ko":"U.S. 대통령에 대한 심각한 책을 읽을 수 있습니다. 그는이 기사에 대해 이야기 할 수 있습니다. 그는이 기사에 대해 이야기 할 수 있습니다. 그는이 기사에 대해 이야기 할 수 있습니다. 그는이 기사에 대해 이야기 할 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"In fact, I wanted to be … don’t laugh … President of the United States.","ko":"사실, 나는 ... 웃지 않는다 ... 미국의 대통령."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"(laughs)","ko":"(웃음)"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Stop! I know it’s a silly childhood dream.","ko":"중지! 나는 그것이 실리 어린 시절 꿈이다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"I’m sorry. It’s not silly. Guess what I wanted to be?","ko":"나는 미안 해요. 그것은 실로 아니에요. 나는 무엇을 원 했는가?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What?","ko":"? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"I wanted to be... an astronaut.","ko":"나는... astronaut."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Really? Marsha’s Voice: When I was a kid, I studied the stars and planets. I wanted to fly into outer space!","ko":"정말? Marsha의 목소리 : 아이가있을 때, 나는 별과 행성을 공부했습니다. 나는 외부 공간으로 비행하고 싶었다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"You know, Marsha, childhood dreams are really important.","ko":"Marsha, 어린 시절의 꿈은 정말 중요합니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"They are. And it’s good to remember them.","ko":"그들은. 그리고 그것은 그들을 기억하는 것이 좋습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hey! I have an idea. Let’s go.","ko":"안녕하세요! 나는 아이디어가 있습니다. 가자."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Go where?","ko":"오시는 길"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Let’s go make our childhood dreams come true.","ko":"우리의 어린 시절의 꿈을 실현합시다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"We’re going to the Air & Space Museum! Yes!","ko":"에어 & 우주 박물관에 가고 있습니다! 예!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No. We’re going to see a show at Ford’s Theatre just like Abraham Lincoln did  when he died! It’s not far from here.","ko":"아니. 우리는 아브라함 링컨과 같은 포드 극장에서 쇼를 볼 예정은 그가 죽었을 때 영어 수업 29 325을 배울 것입니다! 그것은 여기에서 멀지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Uh huh. That is your childhood dream.","ko":"Uhh. 그것은 당신의 어린 시절 꿈입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Good point. Okay, next week, we’ll come here and be astronauts.","ko":"좋은 점. , 다음 주, 우리는 여기 와서 astronauts."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Honestly?","ko":"정직하게?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Honestly.","ko":"흠."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Tonight we are seeing a show at Ford’s Theatre, where a man shot President Abraham Lincoln. This is history come to life … and a childhood dream come true! Until next time ...","ko":"오늘 우리는 포드 극장에서 쇼를보고있다, 남자 샷 대통령 아브라함 링컨. 이 역사는 삶에 온다 ... 그리고 어린 시절의 꿈이 실현! 다음 시간까지 ... 의 Learn English Lesson 29 326"}],"words":[{"en":"advertisement (ad)","definition":"something (such as a short film or a written notice) that is shown or presented to the public to help sell a product or to make an announcement","ko":"광고"},{"en":"astronaut","definition":"a person who travels in a spacecraft into outer space","ko":"우주비행사"},{"en":"ball","definition":"a usually round object that is used in a game or sport or as a toy","ko":"공"},{"en":"believe","definition":"to accept or regard (something) as true childhood - n.the period of time when a person is a child come true - expression. to materialize, to become a reality, or become fulfilled","ko":"믿다"},{"en":"dart gun","definition":"a small toy weapon that throws out small objects with a sharp point at one end","ko":"장난감 총"},{"en":"die","definition":"to stop living","ko":"죽다"},{"en":"dream","definition":"something that you have wanted very much to do, be, or have for a long time","ko":"꿈"},{"en":"Ford’s Theatre","definition":"Ford’s Theatre is a historic theatre in Washington, D.C., used for various stage performances beginning in the 1860s. It is also the site of the shooting of U.S. President Abraham Lincoln on April 14, 1865.","ko":"포드 극장"},{"en":"planet","definition":"a large, round object in space (such as the Earth) that travels around a star (such as the sun)","ko":"행성"},{"en":"really","definition":"without question or doubt—used to make a statement more definite or forceful","ko":"정말로"},{"en":"serious","definition":"thoughtful or quiet in appearance or manner","ko":"심각한"},{"en":"shoot","definition":"to fire a weapon such as a gun (the past tense is shot)","ko":"쏘다"},{"en":"slide","definition":"a structure with a slippery surface that children slide down","ko":"미끄럼틀"},{"en":"star","definition":"any one of the objects in space that are made of burning gas and that look like points of light in the night sky","ko":"별"},{"en":"swing","definition":"a seat that hangs from ropes or chains and that moves back and forth","ko":"그네"},{"en":"teeter-totter","definition":"a long, flat board that is balanced in the middle so that when one end goes up the other end goes down","ko":"시소"},{"en":"tired","definition":"feeling a need to rest or sleep","ko":"피곤한"},{"en":"true","definition":"agreeing with the facts or not false","ko":"사실인"},{"en":"um–hum / uh-huh","definition":"— used to express affirmation, agreement, comprehension, or interest","ko":"응·그래"},{"en":"working","definition":"doing work or in operation","ko":"일하는 중"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 29 - A Long Time Ago\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. How does Marsha react after Anna \nasks, “How are you these days?”\na.\t\nMarsha is very tired.\nb.\t\nShe helps Anna with her work.\nc.\t\nMarsha stops talking.\nd.\t\nShe wants to begin working.\n5. What was Anna’s “childhood dream?”\na.\t\nTo become a U.S. President\nb.\t\nTo teach people how to enjoy books\nc.\t\nTo tell stories to big crowds\nd.\t\nTo act in a play about President Lincoln\n2. What does Marsha say about \nFord’s Theatre?\na.\t\nShe hates going to the theater.\nb.\t\nThere is a new show happening there.\nc.\t\nThe theater is closed this week.\nd.\t\nShe wants to see a show with Anna.\n6. What does Anna say about \nMarsha’s “childhood dream?”\na.\t\nShe remembers Marsha from school.\nb.\t\nChildhood dreams are important.\nc.\t\nMarsha should follow her dreams.\nd.\t\nMarsha’s dream is sillier than Anna’s.\n3. What does “I was not like the other \nchildren” mean?\na.\t\nAnna wore colorful clothes.\nb.\t\nShe was the newest child at her school.\nc.\t\nAnna wanted to be popular.\nd.\t\nShe was more serious than other \nchildren.\n7. How do Anna and Marsha make \ntheir childhood dreams “come true?” \na.\t\nThey go to Ford’s Theatre.\nb.\t\nThey go to the Air and Space Museum.\nc.\t\nThey go to the White House.\nd.\t\nThey go to the Lincoln Memorial.\n4. What does Anna say about books?\na.\t\nThe other children at school laughed at \nher books.\nb.\t\nShe wanted to write stories about \npresidents.\nc.\t\nAnna liked reading books about \npresidents.\nd.\t\nHer friends did not have good reading\nskills.\n8.  Why does Marsha want to go to \nthe National Air and Space Museum?\na.\t\nShe wants to teach Anna about    \nastronauts.\nb.\t\nMarsha works at the museum.\nc.\t\nShe dreamed of being an \nastronaut as a child.\nd.\t\nMarsha is really an astronaut.","guide":{"id":29,"focus":"옛날 이야기와 추억을 들려줘요.","grammar":"과거형을 사용해 예전에 했던 일을 말해요. to + 동사원형은 목적을 나타낼 수 있어요.","mission":"어린 시절 기억나는 일을 두 문장으로 말해 보세요.","example":"A long time ago...","exampleKo":"아주 오래전에…"}},{"id":30,"startPage":333,"endPage":344,"topics":"Asking for and making food recommendations Units of measure & their abbreviations Dollar amounts expressed in numerals","strategy":"Make inferences (guess)","goals":"Grammar: Comparative and superlative adjectives; quantitatives (much/many); count/ non-count nouns Speaking: Using count and non-count nouns Pronunciation: Abbreviations for amounts","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello! Washington, D.C. sits on the Potomac River. This river is important to the history and culture of the city. Today, I am at an outdoor seafood market near the Potomac River. Some say it is the oldest outdoor seafood market in the United States! I am here to buy seafood. Let’s see what they have!","ko":"안녕하세요! 워싱턴, D.C.는 포로마 강에 앉아. 이 강은 도시의 역사와 문화에 중요. 오늘, 나는 포로마 강 근처의 야외 해산물 시장에서입니다. 일부는 미국에서 가장 오래된 야외 해산물 시장이라고 말했습니다! 나는 해산물을 구입하기 위해 여기 있습니다. 그들은 무엇을 볼 수 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Excuse me. Can you help me?","ko":"나를 돕는다. 나를 도울 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Sure! What do you need?","ko":"확실히! 당신은 무엇을 필요로 합니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Pete!","ko":"팟캐스트"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Anna!","ko":"안나!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What are you doing here?","ko":"여기에 무엇을하고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"I work here. You know, it’s not easy to be a writer.","ko":"나는 여기에 일한다. 당신은 알고, 그것은 작가가 될 쉽지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yeah, I heard that. Sorry.","ko":"그래, 나는 그것을 들었다. 미안 해요."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"But this job is great. I work outside by the river. And I can eat all the free seafood I want!","ko":"그러나이 직업은 훌륭합니다. 나는 강에 의해 밖에 일합니다. 그리고 나는 내가 원하는 모든 무료 해산물을 먹을 수 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"That is great, Pete. In fact, I am here to buy some seafood for my dinner party.","ko":"그건 훌륭합니다. 사실, 나는 저녁 파티에 대한 몇 가지 해산물을 구입하는 것이 여기에 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"You came to the right place. They have the freshest seafood in town. How much money can you spend?","ko":"오른쪽에 왔습니다. 그들은 도시에서 가장 신선한 해산물을 가지고 있습니다. 얼마나 많은 돈을 소비 할 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I can only spend $50.","ko":"$ 50 만 지출 할 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Okay. What do you want?","ko":"그래. 무엇을 원하십니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"First, I want to buy some shrimp.","ko":"첫째, 나는 약간 새우를 구입하고 싶습니다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Sure thing. Follow me. How much shrimp do you want?","ko":"확실한 것. 나를 따르라. 얼마나 새우를 원합니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"How much do I need for five people?","ko":"5 명에 대해 얼마나 필요합니까?"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"(yells to co-worker) Give her a pound of shrimp!","ko":"(공 노동자에 게) 새우의 두 파운드를 제공!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Ok, now I want to buy some crabs.","ko":"Ok, 지금 나는 약간 게를 사고 싶어."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"The crabs here are delicious! They are the best because they come from the nearby Chesapeake Bay! Walk this way.","ko":"여기 게는 맛있다! 그들은 인근 Chesapeake Bay에서 온 것이 가장 좋습니다! 이 길을 걸어."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"How many crabs do you want?","ko":"얼마나 많은 게를 원합니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I want a dozen crabs.","ko":"나는 수십 개의 게를 원한다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"You should get the larger crabs. They have the most meat.","ko":"더 큰 게를 얻고 있어야 합니다. 그들은 가장 고기가 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Then I want a dozen large crabs, please!","ko":"그런 다음 다 큰 게를 원합니다!"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Is that everything you need?","ko":"당신이 필요로하는 모든 것입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Let’s see … I have shrimp and crabs. And a friend is bringing a salad and many e ears of corn-on-the-cob.","ko":"봅시다 ... 나는 새우와 게가 있습니다. 그리고 친구는 옥수수 - 온 - 옥수수의 샐러드와 많은 전자 귀를 가져다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Is that all the seafood that you need?","ko":"필요한 모든 해산물은?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes.","ko":"예."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"That’ll be $49.95. Cash or credit?","ko":"즉 $ 49.95입니다. 현금 또는 신용?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Credit, please.","ko":"결제 정보"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Anna, you love to eat seafood. Did you grow up on the water?","ko":"Anna, 당신은 해산물을 먹는 것을 좋아합니다. 물에 자랐습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No, I didn’t. But I love the water. And I love being on the water.","ko":"아니, 나는하지 않았다. 그러나 나는 물을 사랑한다. 그리고 나는 물에 사랑한다. 영어 수업을 배울하자 30 336"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"You know how to sail?","ko":"당신은 항해하는 방법을 알고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well … this afternoon I am going on a boat.","ko":"잘 ...이 오후 나는 보트에 가고있다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"You are full of surprises. What kind of boat? Is it a motorboat or a sailboat?","ko":"놀라움이 가득합니다. 어떤 종류의 보트입니까? 모터 보트 또는 보트입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"It’s a special boat, Pete. Well, thanks for your help. See you later!","ko":"특별한 보트, Pete입니다. 잘, 당신의 도움을 주셔서 감사합니다. 나중에보십시오!"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"See you, Anna! Wow, Anna’s a sailor! Who knew?","ko":"너, 안나! 와우, 안나의 항해자! 누가 알 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes, rivers are important to the history and culture of Washington, D.C. And now I am part of this city’s interesting waterfront culture. Until next time! corn on the cob blue crabs Chesapeake Bay","ko":"예, 강은 워싱턴의 역사와 문화에 중요, D.C. 그리고 지금 나는이 도시의 흥미로운 워터 프론트 문화의 일부입니다. 다음 시간까지! 옥수수는 코브 블루 게스 체사크 베이를 배울 수 있습니다 영어 수업 30 337"}],"words":[{"en":"best","definition":"better than all others in quality or value","ko":"최고의"},{"en":"Chesapeake Bay","definition":"an inlet of the Atlantic, in Maryland and Virginia. It is 200 miles (or 320 km) long; and from 4–40 miles (or 6–64 km) wide.","ko":"체서피크 만"},{"en":"corn-on-the-cob","definition":"corn when cooked and eaten straight from the cob - the part of corn that the kernels grow on; an ear of corn","ko":"옥수수 통째 요리"},{"en":"crab","definition":"a sea animal that has a hard shell, eight legs, and two large claws","ko":"게"},{"en":"credit","definition":"money that a bank or business will allow a person to use and then pay back in the future","ko":"신용"},{"en":"dozen","definition":"a group of 12 people or things","ko":"12개"},{"en":"ear","definition":"the part of a corn plant on which the seeds grow","ko":"옥수수 한 자루"},{"en":"freshest","definition":"the most fresh","ko":"가장 신선한"},{"en":"many","definition":"used to refer to a large number of things or people","ko":"많은·셀 수 있는"},{"en":"much","definition":"large in amount or extent","ko":"많은 양"},{"en":"larger","definition":"greater in size or amount","ko":"더 큰"},{"en":"market","definition":"a place where products are bought and sold","ko":"시장"},{"en":"money","definition":"something (such as coins or bills) used as a way to pay for goods and services and to pay people for their work","ko":"돈"},{"en":"most","definition":"almost all or the majority of","ko":"가장 많은"},{"en":"motorboat","definition":"a boat with a motor","ko":"모터보트"},{"en":"oldest","definition":"having the highest age of a group Potomac River - proper noun. a river flowing from West Virginia to the Chesapeake Bay. It flows between Maryland and Virginia.","ko":"가장 오래된"},{"en":"pound","definition":"a unit of weight that is equal to 16 ounces or about a half of a kilogram","ko":"파운드"},{"en":"river","definition":"a large natural flow of water that crosses an area of land and goes into an ocean or a lake","ko":"강"},{"en":"sail","definition":"to travel on water in a ship or boat","ko":"항해하다"},{"en":"sail","definition":"large piece of strong cloth that is connected to a ship or boat and that is used to catch the wind that moves the ship or boat through the water","ko":"돛"},{"en":"sailboat","definition":"a boat that has a sail","ko":"범선"},{"en":"sailor","definition":"a person who works on a boat or ship as part of the crew","ko":"선원"},{"en":"salad","definition":"a mixture of raw green vegetables, such as different types of lettuce, usually combined with other raw vegetables","ko":"샐러드"},{"en":"seafood","definition":"fish and shellfish that live in the ocean and are used for food","ko":"해산물"},{"en":"some","definition":"refers to an unspecified amount or number","ko":"약간의"},{"en":"spend","definition":"to use money to pay for something","ko":"쓰다·소비하다"},{"en":"water","definition":"an area of water such as a lake, river, or ocean","ko":"물"},{"en":"waterfront","definition":"the land or the part of a town next to the water of an ocean, river or lake.","ko":"해안가"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 30 - Rolling on the River\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Anna say she is doing\ntoday?\na.\t\nShe is fishing in the Potomac River. \nb.\t\nAnna is selling seafood on the river. \nc.\t\nShe is visiting an old friend. \nd.\t\nAnna is going to buy seafood\n5. What does Anna want to know?\na.\t\nHow many people work with Pete \nb.\t\nWhere to buy five pounds of shrimp \nc.\t\nHow much shrimp to buy for five \npeople \nd.\t\nWhere Pete is going after work \n2. What is Pete doing at the market?\na.\t\nPete is writing about the market. \nb.\t\nHe is looking for a job. \nc.\t\nPete is working at the market. \nd.\t\nHe is looking for Anna. \n6. What advice does Pete give to \nAnna?\na.\t\nHe says Anna should buy Chesapeake \nBay crabs here. \nb.\t\nPete tells Anna there are no \nChesapeake Bay crabs here. \nc.\t\nHe says to go to the Chesapeake Bay \nto buy crabs. \nd.\t\nPete says he likes going to the \nChesapeake Bay. \n3.  What are the good things about \nPete’s job?\na.\t\nThe job gives him sailing and fishing \nlessons. \nb.\t\nHe gets to see food and the river. \nc.\t\nThe job lets him learn about seafood \nand corn. \nd.\t\nHe can work by the river and eat free \nfood. \n7. What does Pete tell Anna to buy?\na.\t\nPete says she should buy the larger \ncrabs, with the most meat. \nb.\t\nHe says she should go to the meat \nmarket. \nc.\t\nPete tells her to try to find the crab \nboat. \nd.\t\nHe tells Anna to look for a larger \nmarket. \n4.  What is Anna doing at the river?\na.\t\nAnna is looking for a party by the river. \nb.\t\nShe wants to buy seafood for a party. \nc.\t\nAnna wants Pete to give her $50 for a \nparty. \nd.\t\nShe is looking for a fishing boat.\n8. What strategy does Pete use in \nthis clip?\na.\t\nMaking inferences, or Guessing \nb.\t\nMaking associations \nc.\t\nParaphrasing or Substituting \nd.\t\nSelf Talk\nBlue Crab\nCoconut Crab\nJapanese Spider Crab","guide":{"id":30,"focus":"시장과 여행에서 비교 표현을 써요.","grammar":"bigger는 ‘더 큰’, biggest는 ‘가장 큰’이에요. many는 셀 수 있는 것, much는 양을 말할 때 써요.","mission":"두 물건의 가격이나 크기를 비교해 보세요.","example":"This is the freshest.","exampleKo":"이게 가장 신선해요."}},{"id":31,"startPage":345,"endPage":356,"topics":"Making comparisons Asking for and giving advice","strategy":"Visualize","goals":"Grammar: Comparatives: faster, earlier Speaking: Using comparative and superlative adjectives Pronunciation: Pronouncing reduced “than” in comparative sentences","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi, there, sports fans! Baseball is America’s sport. Today, I am going to Nationals Park. It is home to Washington, D.C.’s baseball team -- the Washington Nationals!","ko":"안녕하세요, 거기, 스포츠 팬! 야구는 미국의 스포츠입니다. 오늘, 나는 국립 공원에 가고있다. 그것은 워싱턴에 집, D.C.의 야구 팀 -- 워싱턴 국립!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi, Jonathan!","ko":"안녕, Jonathan!"},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Hi, Anna! Where are you going?","ko":"안녕, 안나! 어디 가고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I am taking a bus to a Nationals baseball game!","ko":"나는 국립 야구 게임에 버스를 타고!"},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Don’t take the bus. A taxi is faster than a bus.","ko":"버스를 타지 마십시오. 택시는 버스보다 빠릅니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh, good idea. You know I love baseball.","ko":"Oh, 좋은 생각. 당신은 내가 야구를 사랑 알고."},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"That’s great. Have fun.","ko":"그게 훌륭합니다. 재미있어."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"In fact, I wanted to be a baseball player.","ko":"실제로 야구 선수가되기를 원했습니다."},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Is this one of your memories? I’m really busy.","ko":"기억의 이 것입니까? 나는 정말 바쁘다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This won’t take long. I can see it now... I am at home plate. I wait for the pitch. The ball comes. I swing. It’s a hit! I run to first base, second base, third base, then home plate. It’s a home run! The crowd cheers! Woo hoo!","ko":"이것은 오래 걸리지 않습니다. 나는 지금 그것을 볼 수 있습니다 ... 나는 집 판에 있습니다. 나는 피치를 기다립니다. 공이 온다. 나는 스윙입니다. 그것은 히트! 나는 처음 기지, 두 번째베이스, 세 번째베이스, 그 다음 홈 플레이트로 실행됩니다. 그것은 홈 실행입니다! 군중 응원! Woo hoo!"},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"You really love baseball. Have fun at the game, Anna.","ko":"당신은 정말 야구를 좋아합니다. 게임, 안나에서 재미있다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thanks, Jonathan.Taxi!","ko":"감사합니다, Jonathan.Taxi!"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Hi, Anna. Where are you going?","ko":"안녕, 안나. 어디 가고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi, Ashley. I am going to see a Nationals baseball game!","ko":"안녕, 애슐리. 나는 Nationals 야구 게임을 볼거야!"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"What time is the game?","ko":"어떤 시간은 게임입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"7 o’clock.","ko":"7시."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Do you have a ticket?","ko":"티켓이 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No, not yet.","ko":"아니, 아직."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Anna, you should go a lot earlier than 7 o’clock.","ko":"안나, 7 시부 터 이전까지 갈 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"That is why I’m taking a taxi. Taxi!","ko":"택시를 복용하는 이유입니다. 택시!"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Anna, Anna, that’s not a good idea. A bicycle is faster than a taxi.","ko":"Anna, Anna, 그게 좋은 아이디어가 아닙니다. 자전거는 택시보다 빠릅니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh, Ashley. Ashley, Ashley, Ashley. A car is faster than your bicycle.","ko":"Oh, Ashley. Ashley, Ashley, Ashley. 자동차는 자전거보다 빠릅니다."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"In D.C. traffic sometimes a bicycle is faster than a car. And right now, there is a lot of traffic.","ko":"D.C. 트래픽은 때때로 자전거는 자동차보다 빠릅니다. 그리고 지금, 교통이 많이 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Good point. But I don’t have a bicycle.","ko":"좋은 점. 그러나 나는 자전거를 가지고 있지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Okay, Anna, you can use my bicycle.","ko":", Anna, 당신은 내 자전거를 사용할 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thanks! I really want to learn how to ride one.","ko":"감사합니다! 나는 정말로 한 번 타고가는 방법을 배우고 싶습니다."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"What do you mean, learn how to ride a bike? Oh, Anna! Anna, Anna!","ko":"무엇을 의미, 자전거를 타고하는 방법을 배우십니까? 오, 안나! 안나, 안나!"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"You know, Anna, the Metro is faster than a taxi and a bicycle. You ought to take the Metro. It’s that way.","ko":"당신은 알고, 안나, 메트로 택시와 자전거보다 더 빠릅니다. 당신은 메트로를 취할 수있을 것입니다. 그것은 그 방법입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Good idea.","ko":"좋은 아이디어."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"OK.","ko":"확인."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"See you later!","ko":"나중에 보자! 영어 수업을 배우자 31 349"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Bye, Anna!","ko":"으로, 안나!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Bye!","ko":"이름 *"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"The Metro was a lot faster than a bus, taxi or bike. And now I’m at Nationals Park! Look at all these fans! So many people like to watch baseball. There’s the ticket window. What? The tickets are sold out? Nooooooo!Nooooooo! But I really want to watch a baseball game. Does anyone have an extra ticket?","ko":"메트로는 버스, 택시 또는 자전거보다 훨씬 빠릅니다. 그리고 이제는 국립 공원에 있습니다! 이 모든 팬을 봐! 그래서 야구를보고 싶은 많은 사람들. 티켓 창이 있습니다. 무엇? 티켓은 판매됩니까? Nooooooo!Nooooooo! 그러나 나는 정말 야구 게임을보고 싶어합니다. 누구든지 추가 티켓을 가지고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Fan","en":"Next time, you should buy your ticket online.","ko":"다음 시간, 당신은 온라인 티켓을 구입해야합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thanks. Thanks a lot. It is good advice. Being early is better than being late. Until next time …","ko":"감사합니다. 고마워요. 그것은 좋은 조언입니다. 일찍이 늦은 것보다 낫습니다. 다음 시간까지 ... Learn English Lesson 31 350"}],"words":[{"en":"base","definition":"any one of the four places a runner must touch in order to score in baseball","ko":"바닥·베이스"},{"en":"baseball","definition":"a game played on a large field by two teams of nine players who try to score runs by hitting a small ball with a long rounded stick and then running to each of the four places a runner must touch in order to score without being put out","ko":"야구"},{"en":"better","definition":"more attractive, appealing, effective or useful","ko":"더 좋은"},{"en":"bicycle/bike","definition":"a 2-wheeled vehicle that a person rides by pushing on foot pedals","ko":"자전거"},{"en":"cheer(s)","definition":"to shout with joy, approval, or enthusiasm","ko":"응원·환호"},{"en":"crowd","definition":"a large group of people who are together in one place","ko":"군중"},{"en":"earlier","definition":"before the usual or expected time","ko":"더 이른"},{"en":"extra","definition":"more than is usual or necessary","ko":"추가의"},{"en":"fan(s)","definition":"a person who likes and admires someone, such as a famous person, or something, such as a sport or a sports team, in a very enthusiastic way","ko":"팬들"},{"en":"faster","definition":"with great speed","ko":"더 빠른"},{"en":"hit","definition":"to cause a ball to move by hitting it forcefully with a bat in baseball;","ko":"치다"},{"en":"hit","definition":"when a baseball player is able to successfully swing the bat and connect it with the ball","ko":"안타"},{"en":"home plate","definition":"the base that a runner must touch in order to score in baseball","ko":"홈 플레이트"},{"en":"home run","definition":"a hit that allows the batter to go around all the bases and score a run in baseball","ko":"홈런"},{"en":"Nationals Park","definition":"a baseball park located in Washington, D.C. that is the home ballpark for the Washington Nationals baseball team","ko":"내셔널스 파크"},{"en":"online","definition":"done over the Internet","ko":"온라인"},{"en":"pitch","definition":"to throw a ball to the player who is trying to hit the ball in baseball","ko":"공을 던지다"},{"en":"sell out","definition":"to be bought until no more are available","ko":"매진되다"},{"en":"swing","definition":"to move your arms while holding the long rounded stick that is used to hit the ball in baseball with a quick, curving motion","ko":"휘두르다"},{"en":"team","definition":"a group of people who compete in a sport or game against another group","ko":"팀"},{"en":"than","definition":"used to introduce the second or last of two or more things or people that are being compared — used with the comparative form of an adjective or adverb","ko":"~보다"},{"en":"ticket","definition":"a piece of paper that allows you to see a show, participate in an event, travel on a vehicle","ko":"표"},{"en":"window","definition":"an opening in a wall or door that usually contains a sheet of glass","ko":"창구"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 31 - Take Me Out to the Ball Game\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What is Anna going to do?\na.\t\nVisit a national park \nb.\t\nPlay on a baseball team \nc.\t\nWatch a baseball game \nd.\t\nLearn a new sport\n4. What does Ashley explain to \nAnna?\na.\t Traffic is often unsafe in Washington,\nDC. \nb.\t A bicycle can sometimes be faster than \na car. \nc.\t Taxis are usually busy because of traffic. \nd.\t She always rides her bicycle to baseball \ngames.\n2. What advice does Jonathan give \nAnna?\na.\t\nTake a taxi to the game. \nb.\t\nA taxi cannot enter the park. \nc.\t\nTake a faster bus. \nd.\t\nThe bus is not coming.\n5. What advice does Ashley give \nAnna?\na.\t The Metro is faster than a taxi but slower \nthan a bicycle. \nb.\t Anna ought to take the Metro because \nit’s the fastest way. \nc.\t The Metro is located near the baseball \nstadium. \nd.\t Anna should take Ashley to the baseball \ngame.\n3. What does Ashley say to Anna?\na.\t\nAnna is always late for events. \nb.\t\nThe ticket sales end at 7:00 pm. \nc.\t\nThe stadium doors open at 7:00 pm. \nd.\t\nAnna must go to the game earlier.\n6. Why is Anna sad when she arrives \nat Nationals Park? \na.\t There are no tickets for the game. \nb.\t The game has already started. \nc.\t There is not a game tonight. \nd.\t Tickets are only available online.","guide":{"id":31,"focus":"야구 경기를 보며 응원해요.","grammar":"faster는 ‘더 빠른’, earlier는 ‘더 이른’이에요. than 뒤에 비교 대상을 붙여요.","mission":"좋아하는 두 스포츠를 비교하는 문장을 써 보세요.","example":"Take me out to the ball game!","exampleKo":"저를 야구장에 데려가 주세요!"}},{"id":32,"startPage":357,"endPage":369,"topics":"Requesting help or information Talking about technology","strategy":"Monitor","goals":"Grammar: Direct and indirect objects; interjections Speaking: Indirect objects Pronunciation: Interjections","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello! Today is a big day. My first children’s show is on television! Woo-hoo! I’m excited and nervous. Ms.","ko":"안녕하세요! 오늘은 큰 날입니다. 내 첫 번째 아이들의 쇼는 텔레비전에 있습니다! Woo-hoo! 나는 흥분과 긴장입니다. Ms."},{"speaker":"Weaver","en":"Hello, Anna.","ko":"안녕하세요, 안나."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello, Ms. Weaver! Ms. Weaver: Some people are going to watch your children’s show. After they watch it, they’ll tell me what they liked, and what they didn’t like.","ko":"안녕하세요, Ms. Weaver! Ms. Weaver : 일부 사람들은 자녀의 쇼를 볼 것입니다. 그들이 그것을보고 한 후, 그들은 내가 좋아하는 것을 말해 줄 것입니다, 그들은 무엇을 좋아하지 않았다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh, dear. Ms. Weaver: They’re in the conference room.","ko":"Oh, dear. Ms. 웨버: 회의실에 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello, everyone. I’m Anna, and thanks for coming! Coworker 2: What is the show about?","ko":"안녕하세요, 여러분. 나는 안나이고, 고마워요! 코워커 2 : 쇼는 어떻습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"It’s a children’s show. Coworker 1: But we are not children!","ko":"그것은 아이들의 쇼입니다. 협동자 1 : 그러나 우리는 아이들이 아닙니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"But this children’s show is different. I hope. Coworker 3: I don’t really like children’s shows.","ko":"그러나이 아이들의 쇼는 다르다. 나는 희망한다. 코워커 3 : 나는 아이들의 쇼처럼 정말하지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Shhh, please. The show is starting!","ko":"Shhh, 제발. 쇼는 시작!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh, hi! Just give me one minute ….oops! Oh well. I can fix that later.","ko":"Oh, hi! 그냥 나를 1 분 ....oops! Oh 잘. 나는 나중에 수정 할 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello, I’m Anna! Welcome to “The Time Traveling Treehouse!” This is not a usual treehouse. It can time travel! That is why it’s called “The Time Traveling Treehouse.”","ko":"안녕하세요, 저는 Anna입니다! \"시간 여행 트리 하우스!\"에 오신 것을 환영합니다. 이것은 평소 트리 하우스가 아닙니다. 그것은 시간 여행 할 수 있습니다! 그것은 \"시간 여행 트리 하우스\"라고 불리는 이유입니다."},{"speaker":"MINDY","en":"Anna, do not forget me.","ko":"Anna, 나를 잊지 말라."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Of course not! This is my partner, MINDY!","ko":"물론 아닙니다! 내 파트너, MINDY입니다!"},{"speaker":"MINDY","en":"My name means Massive Information Navigation Device, for You!","ko":"내 이름은 Massive Information Navigation Device를 의미합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"That means we can travel to many places and learn many things. Kids from all over the world ask us questions. We find them answers!","ko":"즉, 우리는 많은 장소에 여행하고 많은 것을 배울 수 있습니다. 전 세계의 아이들은 우리에게 질문을합니다. 우리는 그들에게 답변을 찾을 수 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"MINDY","en":"Woo-hoo! That is right, Anna.","ko":"Woo-hoo! 그건 맞습니다, 안나."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"MINDY, what is our first question?","ko":"MINDY, 우리의 첫 번째 질문은 무엇입니까?"},{"speaker":"MINDY","en":"Layla asks us this question.","ko":"Layla는이 질문을합니다."},{"speaker":"Layla","en":"Hello, Anna! Hello, MINDY! I’d like to know -- how do you play baseball?","ko":"안녕하세요, 안나! 안녕하세요, MINDY! 나는 알고 싶습니다. -- 당신은 야구를 재생하는 방법?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"That is a great question! MINDY, we need to find her an answer!","ko":"그것은 훌륭한 질문입니다! MINDY, 우리는 그녀의 대답을 찾을 필요가!"},{"speaker":"MINDY","en":"I know that we can find it, Anna!","ko":"나는 우리가 그것을 찾을 수 있다는 것을 알고, 안나!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Where am I now? MINDY, now I am on a snowy mountain!","ko":"지금 어디? MINDY, 지금 나는 눈이 산에있다!"},{"speaker":"MINDY","en":"That is a good place to learn how to ski.","ko":"스키를 배우는 좋은 곳입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes, MINDY, but it cannot teach us about baseball! And I don’t know how to ski!","ko":"예, MINDY,하지만 야구에 대해 가르쳐 할 수 없습니다! 그리고 나는 스키 방법을 모른다!"},{"speaker":"MINDY","en":"Sorry, Anna. Let’s try again.","ko":"죄송합니다. Anna. 다시 시도합시다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Where I am now!? MINDY, I am in the ocean! An ocean cannot teach us about baseball!","ko":"지금 어디!? MINDY, 나는 바다에 있습니다! 바다는 야구에 대해 가르쳐 할 수 없습니다! 영어 수업 32 361을 배울 수 있습니다"},{"speaker":"MINDY","en":"Please don’t yell, Anna. The ocean can teach us about surfing.","ko":"안나. 바다는 서핑에 대해 가르쳐 줄 수 없습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes, MINDY, it can teach us about surfing … and sharks! Ahhh!","ko":"예, MINDY, 그것은 서핑에 대해 우리에게 가르쳐 할 수 ... 그리고 상어! Ahhh!"},{"speaker":"MINDY","en":"Anna, please wait. I need to fix my navigation device","ko":"Anna, 기다렸다. 내 탐색 장치를 해결해야합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"MINDY, please fix it faster. And get me out of here … now!","ko":"MINDY, 그것을 빨리 고칠 수 있습니다. 그리고 여기에서 나를 얻을 ... 지금!"},{"speaker":"Announcer","en":"Whoa! Is Anna going to be lost forever? Next week, you can watch part two of “The Time Traveling Treehouse!” Coworker 1: Aw, man! Will the shark eat her? Coworker 2: Will Anna find the answer? Coworker 3: Please tell me the ending!","ko":"Whoa! Anna는 영원히 잃어 버릴거야? 다음 주, 당신은 \"시간 여행 트리 하우스!\" Coworker 1 : Aw, 남자! 상어가 그녀를 먹을 것입니까? 코워 2 : 윌 안나가 대답을 찾을 수 있습니까? 코워 3 : 내 종료를 알려주세요!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"So, you liked it?","ko":"그래서, 당신은 그것을 좋아?"},{"speaker":"Coworkers","en":"Yes!","ko":"네!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well, you can watch the ending next week!","ko":"잘, 당신은 다음 주 종료 볼 수 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Coworkers","en":"Noooooo!","ko":"노우오!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Don’t forget to watch next week!","ko":"다음 주를 지켜보는 것을 잊지 마세요! 영어 수업 32 362"}],"words":[{"en":"aw","definition":"used to express mild disappointment or sympathy","ko":"어이쿠"},{"en":"man","definition":"used to express frustration","ko":"아이고"},{"en":"oops","definition":"used to express surprise or distress or to say in a mild way that you are sorry about having done or said something wrong","ko":"이런"},{"en":"shhh","definition":"used to tell someone to be quiet","ko":"쉿"},{"en":"whoa","definition":"used to tell someone to slow down or stop and think about something","ko":"와!"},{"en":"woo-hoo","definition":"used to express excitement GENERAL VOCABULARY","ko":"야호!"},{"en":"answer","definition":"something you say or write when someone asks you a question","ko":"대답하다"},{"en":"ask","definition":"to say or write something to someone as a way of gaining information","ko":"질문하다"},{"en":"device","definition":"an object, machine, or piece of equipment that has been made for some special purpose","ko":"장치"},{"en":"ending","definition":"the final part of something","ko":"끝·결말"},{"en":"fix","definition":"to make (something) whole or able to work properly againorto repair (something)","ko":"고치다"},{"en":"information","definition":"knowledge that you get about someone or something such asfacts or details about a subject","ko":"정보"},{"en":"massive","definition":"very large and heavy","ko":"거대한"},{"en":"mountain","definition":"an area of land that rises very high above the land around it and that is higher than a hill","ko":"산"},{"en":"navigation","definition":"the act, activity, or process of finding the way to get to a place when you are traveling in a ship, airplane or car","ko":"길 안내"},{"en":"partner","definition":"one of two or more people or businesses that work together or do business together","ko":"동료"},{"en":"shark","definition":"a large and often dangerous sea fish with very sharp teeth","ko":"상어"},{"en":"ski","definition":"to move or glide on a pair of long narrow pieces of wood over snow or water","ko":"스키 타다"},{"en":"surf","definition":"to ride on ocean waves using a special board (called a surfboard)","ko":"서핑하다"},{"en":"travel","definition":"to go to a place that is far away","ko":"여행하다"},{"en":"treehouse","definition":"a small house that is built among the branches of a tree for children to play in","ko":"나무 위의 집"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 32 - Welcome to the Treehouse!\n1. What does Anna say about today?\na.\t\nShe is sad about a show on television. \nb.\t\nAnna says, “I’m excited and nervous.” \nc.\t\nShe does not want to be on television. \nd.\t\nAnna says, “There will be children at \nwork.” \n6. What is one purpose of the show?\na.\t To travel the world and ask questions\nb.\t To take children to another time \nc.\t To answer questions for children \nd.\t To teach children about computers\n2. What does Ms. Weaver say to Anna?\na.\t Some people will tell their children \nabout Anna’s show. \nb.\t The people will watch the show and tell \nMs. Weaver how they like it. \nc.\t\nSome people will tell Ms. Weaver which \nshows they like to watch. \nd.\t The people will make a new show with \nAnna.\n7. What does Layla want?\na.\t Layla wants to know how to play \nbaseball. \nb.\t She wants to travel with Anna. \nc.\t Layla wants to know how MINDY works. \nd.\t She wants to find the treehouse on a \nmap.\n3. What does Anna’s coworker ask?\na.\t\nWill I like the show? \nb.\t\nWhat is the show about? \nc.\t\nCan we watch the show? \nd.\t\nWhen will the show come out?\n8. What strategy is Anna using in this \nclip?\na.\t Self-talk \nb.\t Monitoring \nc.\t Predicting \nd.\t Summarizing \n4. What does Anna say about the show?\na.\t\nThe show will give them hope. \nb.\t\nThey will like the show. \nc.\t\nThe children like the show. \nd.\t\nThe show is different.\n9. MINDY has a problem. What is it?\na.\t She needs to fix her navigation device. \nb.\t MINDY does not like baseball. \nc.\t She cannot go in the ocean. \nd.\t MINDY is afraid of sharks. \n5. What is different about Anna’s \ntreehouse?\na.\t\nThe treehouse can travel to another \ntime. \nb.\t\nIt is just a usual treehouse. \nc.\t\nThe treehouse is from a long time ago. \nd.\t\nIt is from a different time. \n10. Why does Anna’s coworker say, “Aw, \nman?”\na.\t He did not like the show. \nb.\t The man does not understand the \nshow. \nc.\t He has to wait a week for the next \nshow. \nd.\t The man found a mistake on the show.","guide":{"id":32,"focus":"특별한 장소를 소개하고 정보를 주고받아요.","grammar":"give me, tell you처럼 누구에게 주는지 목적어를 말해요. 감탄사는 감정을 짧게 표현해요.","mission":"내가 좋아하는 장소를 소개하고 친구의 질문에 답해 보세요.","example":"Welcome to the treehouse!","exampleKo":"나무 위의 집에 온 것을 환영해요!"}},{"id":33,"startPage":370,"endPage":378,"topics":"Complimenting someone’s ability Explaining how to play a sport or activity","strategy":"Sequence","goals":"Grammar: Agent nouns Speaking: Agent nouns Pronunciation: American pronunciation of -er endings","conversation":[{"speaker":"대화","en":"Coworker 2: It is time for part two of the children’s show! Coworker 1: It’s time! It’s time! I can’t wait! Coworker 3: Shh! I can’t hear it!","ko":"Coworker 2 : 아이들의 쇼의 두 부분을위한 시간입니다! 코워커 1 : 그것은 시간입니다! 그것은 시간이 없습니다! 나는 기다릴 수 없습니다! 코워커 3 : 슈! 나는 그것을들을 수 없습니다!"},{"speaker":"Announcer","en":"Last time on “The Time Traveling Treehouse,” Anna was lost, really lost. She wants to learn about baseball. But her computer, MINDY, sent her to many wrong places.","ko":"마지막에 “시간 여행 트리 하우스,” 안나 손실, 정말 손실. 그녀는 야구에 대해 배우고 싶어. 그러나 그녀의 컴퓨터, MINDY, 많은 잘못된 장소에 그녀를 보냈습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"MINDY! Help me! I am in the ocean with a shark!","ko":"MINDY! 나를 도와주세요! 상어와 바다에 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"MINDY","en":"I will try one more time, Anna.","ko":"나는 한 번 더 시도합니다, Anna."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Please try harder, MINDY!","ko":"더 열심히 시도해 보세요!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Now, where am I? I am at a playground with a baseball field! Yes! I can teach children about baseball here! MINDY, MINDY, it took you a long time. But you did it!","ko":"지금, 어디 내가? 나는 야구 필드와 놀이터에! 예! 나는 야구에 대해 아이들을 가르치 수 있습니다! MINDY, MINDY, 그것은 당신에게 오랜 시간이 걸렸다. 그러나 당신은 그것을했다!"},{"speaker":"MINDY","en":"Thanks, Anna. Give me a call when you find the answer.","ko":"감사합니다, Anna. 대답을 찾을 때 전화하십시오."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Okay. Come with me. Let’s learn how to play baseball! This is a baseball field. This is a pitcher’s mound. This is first base! This is second base! This is third base! This is home plate!","ko":"괜찮아. 저와 함께 가자. 야구를 재생하는 방법을 배우자! 이것은 야구장입니다. 이것은 투수의 무서운입니다. 이것은 첫 번째 기지입니다! 이것은 두 번째 기지입니다! 이것은 세 번째 기지입니다! 이것은 홈 플레이트입니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"To play baseball, you really only need a bat, a ball and a glove. Each team has many players. Pitchers pitch the ball. Catchers catch the ball. Batters bat the ball. Runners run the bases! Fielders field the ball.","ko":"야구를 연주하기 위해, 당신은 정말 단지 배, 공과 장갑을 필요로. 각 팀은 많은 선수가 있습니다. 투수는 공을 투수합니다. 배터는 공을 전투합니다. 런너는베이스를 실행합니다! Fielders는 공을 필드."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"First, the pitcher pitches the ball to the batter. The batter bats the ball. Then, the runner runs to first base.","ko":"첫째, 투수는 배터에 공을 투구합니다. 배터는 공을 박습니다. 그런 다음 주자는 첫 번째 기지로 실행됩니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Each time a batter bats, the runners run around the bases. Each time a runner runs across home plate, they score a run! There are nine innings in a game. The team with the most runs at the end of nine innings wins the game!","ko":"각 배터 배터, 런너는베이스 주위에 실행됩니다. 각 시간 런너는 홈 플레이트를 통해 실행됩니다, 그들은 런을 점수! 게임에서 9 배닝이 있습니다. 9 배닝의 끝에서 가장 실행되는 팀은 게임을 승리!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"MINDY, MINDY, we found the answer! It’s time to return to the treehouse.","ko":"MINDY, MINDY, 우리는 대답을 발견했습니다! 그것은 트리하우스로 돌아갈 시간입니다."},{"speaker":"MINDY","en":"Good job! That was fast. Coworker 3: Good job Anna. You know, I still don’t like children’s shows, but I like this children’s show. Coworker 2: I liked the time travel. Coworker 1: But time travel is not real. You’re so silly, Anna.","ko":"좋은 일! 그것은 빠른이었다. 코워커 3 : 좋은 일 안나. 당신은 알고, 나는 여전히 아이들의 쇼와 같은하지 않습니다, 그러나 나는이 아이들의 쇼와 같습니다. 코워커 2 : 나는 시간 여행을 좋아했다. 코워커 1 : 그러나 시간 여행은 실제하지 않습니다. 당신은 너무 침묵, 안나."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yeah, time travel is so silly. Thanks, goodbye. Bye, thank you.","ko":"그래, 시간 여행은 너무 실리다. 감사, 안녕. Bye, 감사합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello, MINDY? Are you there?","ko":"안녕하세요, MINDY? 거기에 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"MINDY","en":"Hello, Anna.","ko":"안녕하세요, 안나."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"MINDY, I want to go to China! Until next time …","ko":"MINDY, 나는 중국으로 가고 싶다! 다음 시간까지 ... 영어 수업 33 373을 배우자"}],"words":[{"en":"bat","definition":"to hit (something, such as a ball) with a bat or club","ko":"방망이"},{"en":"batter","definition":"baseball. a player who is trying to hit the ball","ko":"타자"},{"en":"catcher","definition":"baseball. the player who plays behind home plate and catches the pitches thrown by the pitcher","ko":"포수"},{"en":"catch","definition":"to use your hands to stop and hold (an object that is moving through the air)","ko":"잡다"},{"en":"field","definition":"baseball or cricket. to catch or stop and throw a ball","ko":"경기장"},{"en":"fielder","definition":"baseball or cricket. a player who is in the field while the opposing team is batting","ko":"야수"},{"en":"glove","definition":"baseball. a padded leather covering for the hand that is used to catch the ball and that has individual thumb and finger sections","ko":"글러브"},{"en":"harder","definition":"(try harder) working or doing something with more energy","ko":"더 세게"},{"en":"inning","definition":"baseball. one of the usually nine parts of a game in which each team bats until three outs are made","ko":"이닝"},{"en":"mound","definition":"the slightly raised area of ground on which a baseball pitcher stands","ko":"마운드"},{"en":"out*","definition":"baseball. no longer batting or on a base because of a play made by the other team","ko":"아웃"},{"en":"pitch","definition":"baseball. to throw a baseball to a batter","ko":"투구하다"},{"en":"pitcher","definition":"baseball. the player who throws the ball to the batter in baseball","ko":"투수"},{"en":"player","definition":"a person who plays a sport or game","ko":"선수"},{"en":"runner","definition":"baseball. a player who is on base or is trying to reach a base * This word is not in the conversation but may be used for explaining of the game of baseball","ko":"주자"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 33 - Learning America’s Sport\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Anna want?\na.\t\nTo learn to use a computer \nb.\t\nTo learn how to travel \nc.\t\nTo learn about MINDY \nd.\t\nTo learn about baseball  \n4. Which baseball player hits the ball?\na.\t Catchers \nb.\t Runners \nc.\t Pitchers \nd.\t Batters \n2. What did MINDY do?\na.\t\nTaught Anna to ask questions \nb.\t\nMade another mistake \nc.\t\nFound the baseball field \na.\t\nCalled Anna to find the answer\n5. What strategy is Anna using in this \nvideo?\na.\t\nMonitoring \na.\t\nPredicting \na.\t\nSequencing \na.\t\nSelf-talk \n3. What is Anna doing?\na.\t Finding out what you know about \nbaseball \nb.\t Teaching you about the game of \nbaseball \nc.\t Talking about how much she loves \nbaseball \nd.\t Explaining that it is hard to learn \nbaseball \n6. What does the man say to Anna?\na.\t He hates to travel. \nb.\t Time travel is so silly. \nc.\t Her show is really old. \nd.\t Time travel is not real.","guide":{"id":33,"focus":"미국 스포츠의 규칙을 설명해요.","grammar":"play + er처럼 행동하는 사람을 나타내는 단어가 있어요. pitcher는 공을 던지는 선수예요.","mission":"스포츠 규칙 세 가지를 쉬운 영어로 알려 주세요.","example":"The pitcher throws the ball.","exampleKo":"투수가 공을 던져요."}},{"id":34,"startPage":379,"endPage":389,"topics":"Life events American customs","strategy":"Make your best guess (Make an inference)","goals":"Grammar: modals “might” and “will” Speaking: the future; expressing probability & possibility Pronunciation: Stress on the words “might” and “will”","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello! Halloween is very popular in the United States.","ko":"안녕하세요! 할로윈은 미국에서 매우 인기가 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Children trick-or-treat. They ask people for candy. Children and adults wear costumes and go to parties!","ko":"아이들의 속임수. 그들은 사탕을 위해 사람들을 물었다. 어린이와 성인은 의상을 입고 파티에 가자!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"In fact, there is a Halloween party tonight. I need my friend, Genie. Genie!","ko":"사실, 할로윈 파티 밤이 있습니다. 나는 친구, Genie가 필요합니다. Genie!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi!","ko":"안녕하세요!"},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"Hi, Anna! What do you need?","ko":"안녕, 안나! 당신은 무엇을 필요로 합니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Tonight, there is a Halloween party.","ko":"밤에는 할로윈 파티가 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"I love Halloween! Are you going?","ko":"나는 할로윈을 좋아합니다! 당신은 가고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I might go. I might not go. I don’t have a costume. Can you help me?","ko":"나는 갈 수 있습니다. 나는 갈 수 없습니다. 나는 의상을 가지고 있지 않습니다. 나를 도울 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"Dress as a genie!","ko":"genie로 옷을 입는다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Great idea! I can do a genie trick like read minds!","ko":"좋은 아이디어! 나는 읽힌 마음과 같은 genie 트릭을 할 수 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"Anna, be careful. Things might go wrong.","ko":"안나, 조심해. 것들이 잘못 될 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What can go wrong?","ko":"잘못 될 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"Okay.","ko":"이름 *"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hey, look! I’m a genie! This is going to be fun!","ko":"이봐, 봐! 나는 genie입니다! 이것은 재미있게 될 것입니다!"},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"Remember, Anna. Be careful!","ko":"기억하십시오. 안나. 조심하십시오!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Don’t worry, Genie! I will!","ko":"걱정하지 마세요, Genie! 나는!"},{"speaker":"Rebecca","en":"Excuse me, are you really a mind reader?","ko":"나에게는 정말 마음 리더입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I might be.","ko":"나는 할 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Rebecca","en":"Okay, tell me what I am thinking.","ko":"그래, 내가 생각하고있는 것을 말해."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sure! First, what do you do?","ko":"확실히! 먼저, 당신은 무엇을합니까?"},{"speaker":"Rebecca","en":"I study. I’m a junior in college.","ko":"나는 공부합니다. 나는 대학에서 주니어입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What do you study?","ko":"당신은 무엇을 공부하나요?"},{"speaker":"Rebecca","en":"I study journalism.","ko":"나는 저널리즘을 연구한다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Okay. Wait. You are thinking … you will graduate from college in about one year.","ko":"괜찮아. 기대합니다. 당신은 생각하고 있습니다 ... 당신은 약 1 년 동안 대학에서 졸업 할 것입니다."},{"speaker":"Rebecca","en":"Well, yeah. That’s the plan. I told you, I’m a junior in college.","ko":"글쎄, 그래. 그게 계획입니다. 나는 당신에게 말했다, 나는 대학에 주니어입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Right, um, wait. There’s more. You are thinking … you might get a job writing the news.","ko":"오른쪽, um, 기다립니다. 더 많은 것. 당신은 생각 ... 당신은 작업이 뉴스를 작성할 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Rebecca","en":"I MIGHT get a job writing the news? I MIGHT! That means I might not. And I’m studying really hard.","ko":"나는 MIGHT는 뉴스를 쓰는 일을 얻습니까? 나는 MIGHT! 즉, 나는 할 수 없습니다. 그리고 나는 정말로 열심히 공부하고 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No, no, no, no. Uh, no, you will! You WILL get a job writing the news.","ko":"아니, 아니, 아니, 아니. Uh, 아니, 당신은! 당신은 작업을 작성할 것입니다 뉴스."},{"speaker":"Rebecca","en":"I will?","ko":"나는?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"You will.","ko":"당신은 할 것이다."},{"speaker":"Rebecca","en":"I will. I think.","ko":"나는 생각한다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"‘Bye. Happy to help!","ko":"'Bye. 도움이 될 행복!"},{"speaker":"Kaveh","en":"Can you really read minds?","ko":"당신은 정말로 마음을 읽을 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I might.","ko":"나는 할 수 있습니다. 영어 수업을 배우자 34 382"},{"speaker":"Kaveh","en":"Well, today, I will ask my girlfriend to marry me. What am I thinking?","ko":"글쎄, 오늘, 나는 내 여자 친구에게 나를 감사하도록 요청합니다. 나는 무엇을 생각합니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Wait. Wait, you are thinking ... you might have a wedding very soon!","ko":"기대. 기대, 당신은 생각 ... 당신은 곧 결혼식이있을 수 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Kaveh","en":"Might? MIGHT? She won’t say “no,” will she?","ko":"마이트? 미트? 그녀는 \"아니,\"라고 말하지 않겠습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No, no! She WILL say “yes”!","ko":"아니, 아니! 그녀는 \"예\"라고 말할 것이다!"},{"speaker":"Kaveh","en":"I will have a wedding, won’t I?","ko":"나는 결혼식이있어, 나는하지 않을거야?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"You will. You will!","ko":"당신은. 당신은!"},{"speaker":"Kaveh","en":"Thanks. I think.","ko":"감사합니다. 나는 생각한다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Good luck!","ko":"행운을 빌어!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This is hard. Genie! Genie!","ko":"이것은 어렵습니다. Genie! Genie!"},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"Anna, what’s wrong?","ko":"Anna, 무엇이 잘못되었습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I don’t want to be a genie for Halloween. I might not go to the party.","ko":"나는 할로윈을위한 genie가되고 싶지 않습니다. 나는 파티에 갈 수 없습니다."},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"Of course you will go. I have another costume for you!","ko":"물론 갈 것입니다. 나는 당신을 위해 또 다른 의상을 가지고!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I’m a rock star! You read my mind!","ko":"나는 바위 별입니다! 당신은 나의 마음을 읽습니다!"},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"No. You told me you like rock music.","ko":"아니. 당신은 바위 음악처럼 나를 말했다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh, right. Well, I love it!","ko":"오, 맞습니다. 잘, 나는 그것을 사랑한다!"},{"speaker":"Genie","en":"Have fun, Anna!","ko":"재미, 안나!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thanks, Genie!!","ko":"감사합니다, Genie!!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I am ready for the Halloween party! But I am not going to read minds. I might play some rock music! Or I might not. Until next time …","ko":"나는 할로윈 파티를 준비합니다! 그러나 나는 마음을 읽지 않을 것입니다. 나는 약간의 바위 음악을 재생할 수 있습니다! 또는 나는 할 수 없습니다. 다음 시간까지 ... 영어 수업을 배우자 34 383"}],"words":[{"en":"candy","definition":"a sweet food made with sugar or chocolate college - n.. school that offers courses leading to a degree (such as a bachelor’s degree or an associate’s degree) costume - n.the clothes that are worn by someone (such as an actor) who is trying to look like a different person or thing","ko":"사탕"},{"en":"dress","definition":"to put clothes on (yourself or someone else)","ko":"드레스"},{"en":"girlfriend","definition":"a woman with whom someone is having a romantic relationship","ko":"여자친구"},{"en":"graduate","definition":"to earn a degree or diploma from a school, college, or university","ko":"졸업하다"},{"en":"Halloween","definition":"the night of October 31 when children dress up as ghosts, witches or monsters, and go to houses to ask for candy","ko":"핼러윈"},{"en":"journalism","definition":"the activity or job of collecting, writing, and editing news stories for newspapers, magazines, television, or radio","ko":"언론학"},{"en":"junior","definition":"US: a student in the third of four years in a high school or college","ko":"후배·하급생"},{"en":"marry","definition":"to become the husband or wife of (someone)orto become joined with (someone) in marriage","ko":"결혼하다"},{"en":"might","definition":"used to say that something is possible","ko":"~일지도 모른다"},{"en":"mind","definition":"the part of a person that thinks, reasons, feels, and remembers","ko":"신경 쓰다"},{"en":"rock star","definition":"a person who plays a kind of popular music with a strong beat that is played on instruments that are made louder electronically","ko":"록 스타"},{"en":"think","definition":"to form or have (a particular thought) in your mind","ko":"생각하다"},{"en":"trick","definition":"something that causes confusion or that makes something seem different from what it actually is trick-or-treat - expression. a custom on Halloween in which children knock on people’s doors and say “trick or treat” when the doors are opened to ask for candy","ko":"속임수"},{"en":"wedding","definition":"a ceremony at which two people are married to each other","ko":"결혼식"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 34 - What Will I Do?\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Anna say about \nHalloween?\na.\t\nAdults and children wear costumes.\nb.\t\nChildren trick-or-treat: they ask for \ncandy.\nc.\t\nHalloween is very popular in the United \nStates.\nd.\t\nAnna says all of these things about\nHalloween. \n5. What does Anna say to the \nwoman?\na.\t\nThe woman might not get the right job.\nb.\t\nShe might not get a job writing the \nnews.\nc.\t\nThe woman will get a job writing the \nnews.\nd.\t\nShe will study hard for a news job.\n2. What does Anna need for tonight?\na.\t\nA friend to go to the party with.\nb.\t\nA costume to wear to the party.\nc.\t\nA genie to create a party.\nd.\t\nA way to go to the party.\n6. What does the man plan to do \ntoday?\na.\t\nTell Anna when his wedding will \nhappen. \nb.\t\nAsk Anna for help about marriage.\nc.\t\nTell his girlfriend that he will not marry \nher. \nd.\t\nAsk his girlfriend to marry him. \n3. What does Genie say might happen?\na.\t\nAnna’s costume might look wrong.\nb.\t\nGenie might not have special powers.\nc.\t\nThe costume might have bad results.\nd.\t\nGenie might not find the right dress.\n7. What does Anna tell the man?\na.\t\nHe might have a wedding very soon. \nb.\t\nHis girlfriend will probably say no today. \nc.\t\nHe might not ask his girlfriend to marry \nhim. \nd.\t\nHe will have a wedding, but not very \nsoon. \n4. What does Anna say that the woman \nis thinking?\na.\t\nShe will study at a new college in about \none year.\nb.\t\nIn about one year, she will graduate \nfrom college.\nc.\t\nShe will meet a journalist in about one \nyear.\nd.\t\nIn about one year, she will study \njournalism.\n8. What does Anna say to Genie?\na.\t\nGenie loves rock music. \nb.\t\nThis costume is better.\nc.\t\nGenie read Anna’s mind. \nd.\t\nThis costume rocks!","guide":{"id":34,"focus":"미래 직업과 가능성을 이야기해요.","grammar":"will은 미래, might는 ‘~일지도 몰라’라는 불확실한 가능성을 나타내요.","mission":"나중에 하고 싶은 일과 아직 고민 중인 일을 말해 보세요.","example":"I might be a journalist.","exampleKo":"저는 기자가 될지도 몰라요."}},{"id":35,"startPage":390,"endPage":401,"topics":"Foods Shopping Giving reasons for concern","strategy":"Cooperate","goals":"Grammar: partitives (measure words) with count and noncount nouns Speaking: using measure words, like “jar of” and “bag of.” Pronunciation: reduced form of the word “of” before measure words","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi there! Washington, D.C. has many fun places to eat. But, sometimes it’s more fun to cook. In fact, tonight Marsha and I are cooking for friends. Well, she is cooking. I am doing the shopping. (phone rings) It’s Marsha. Hi, Marsha.","ko":"안녕하세요! 워싱턴 D.C.는 많은 재미 장소가 먹을. 그러나 때때로 요리하는 것이 더 재미입니다. 사실, 박 마샤와 나는 친구를 위해 요리하고 있습니다. 글쎄, 그녀는 요리입니다. 나는 쇼핑을하고 있습니다. (전화 링) 그것은 마샤입니다. 안녕, 마샤입니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Hi, Anna. Do you have the shopping list?","ko":"안녕하세요, Anna. 쇼핑 목록이 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes, I told you: I have the shopping list. Can you hear it?","ko":"예, 나는 당신에게 말했다 : 나는 쇼핑 목록이 있습니다. 당신은 그것을들을 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Okay, good. I hear the list. Anna, please buy all the ingredients on the list.","ko":"잘. 나는 목록을 듣는다. 안나, 목록에서 모든 재료를 구입하시기 바랍니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes, Marsha, I will.","ko":"예, 마샤, 나는 것입니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"And do not spend too much time shopping.","ko":"그리고 너무 많은 시간 쇼핑을하지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No, Marsha, I won’t. See you later.","ko":"아니오, Marsha, 나는 원하지 않습니다. 나중에보십시오."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sometimes, Marsha worries too much. I love shopping! And, I did not spend too much money. Oh, no! But I did spend too much time! I have to return home now!","ko":"때로는 Marsha 걱정 너무 많이. 나는 쇼핑을 사랑! 그리고, 나는 너무 많은 돈을 지출하지 않았다. 오, 아니! 그러나 나는 너무 많은 시간을 소비했다! 나는 지금 집에 돌아 왔습니다!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Anna, what took you so long? Our guests will be here soon!","ko":"Anna, 얼마나 오래 걸었습니까? 우리의 손님은 곧 될 것입니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Don’t worry, Marsha. I bought everything on the list.","ko":"걱정하지 마세요, Marsha. 나는 목록에 모든 것을 샀다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Let me see. You bought a bunch of bananas, a box of pancake mix, a bag of coffee … Anna, this is all wrong!","ko":"나를 볼 수 있습니다. 바나나, 팬케이크 믹스 박스, 커피 백 ... 안나, 이것은 모든 잘못입니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What do you mean wrong? I bought a jar of peanut butter and a loaf of bread … no, wait … two loaves of bread.","ko":"당신이 틀린 것을 의미합니까? 나는 땅콩 버터의 단지를 샀고 빵의 loaf ... 아니, 기다리 ... 빵의 두 개의 loaves."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Anna, these are the wrong ingredients!","ko":"Anna, 이것은 잘못된 재료입니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"These ingredients are all on the list! I took this list from the counter.","ko":"이 성분은 모두 목록에 있습니다! 나는 카운터에서이 목록을했다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Anna, this is the shopping list for breakfast. I said, take the shopping list - on the refrigerator - for dinner!","ko":"Anna, 이것은 아침 식사를위한 쇼핑 목록입니다. 나는 말했다, 쇼핑 목록 - 냉장고에 - 저녁 식사!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Marsha, there was no shopping list - on the refrigerator - for dinner!","ko":"Marsha, 쇼핑 목록이 없었다 - 냉장고에 - 저녁 식사!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Oh no! It’s on the floor!! Anna/Marsha: Ahh!!! Ahh!!!","ko":"Oh no! 그것은 바닥에! Anna/Marsha: Ahh!!! Ahh!!!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"What are we going to do?","ko":"우리는 무엇을 할 것인가?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"When do our guests arrive?","ko":"손님이 도착 할 때?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"They arrive in 30 minutes!","ko":"그들은 30 분에 도착!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I can fix this. Do you trust me?","ko":"나는 이것을 해결할 수 있습니다. 당신은 나를 신뢰합니까?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Do I have to?","ko":"나는 가지고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes. (The story continues next week)","ko":"예. (이 이야기는 다음 주 동안 계속됩니다) 영어 수업을 배우자 35 393"}],"words":[{"en":"banana","definition":"a long curved fruit with a thick peel that is yellow when it is ripe","ko":"바나나"},{"en":"bought","definition":"past tense of buy: to get (something) by paying money for it","ko":"샀다"},{"en":"box","definition":"a container that is made of a hard material (such as wood, metal, or cardboard) and that usually has four straight sides","ko":"상자"},{"en":"bread","definition":"a baked food made from a mixture of flour and water","ko":"빵"},{"en":"bunch","definition":"a group of things of the same kind that are held or tied together or that grow together","ko":"한 다발"},{"en":"counter","definition":"a long, flat surface on which food is prepared in a kitchen","ko":"조리대"},{"en":"floor","definition":"the part of a room on which you stand","ko":"바닥"},{"en":"ingredient","definition":"one of the things that are used to make a food or product","ko":"재료"},{"en":"jar","definition":"a glass container that has a wide opening and usually a lid","ko":"병"},{"en":"loaf","definition":"an amount of bread that has been baked in a long, round, or square shape (plural: loaves)","ko":"빵 한 덩이"},{"en":"mix","definition":"a dry mixture of ingredients that is sold in one package and used for making something (such as a type of food)","ko":"섞다"},{"en":"pancake","definition":"a thin, flat, round cake that is made by cooking batter on both sides in a frying pan or on a hot surface","ko":"팬케이크"},{"en":"peanut butter","definition":"a creamy food made from peanuts","ko":"땅콩버터"},{"en":"shopping list","definition":"a list of things to be bought at a shop or store","ko":"쇼핑 목록"},{"en":"told","definition":"past tense of tell: to give information to (someone) by speaking or writing","ko":"말했다"},{"en":"trust","definition":"to believe that someone or something is reliable, good, honest, or effective","ko":"믿다"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 35 - Let’s Make Dinner!\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Anna say about this \nevening?\na.\t\nAnna and her friends will eat dinner in a \nrestaurant.\nb.\t\nMarsha wants to go shopping with \nAnna.\nc.\t\nShe and Marsha are cooking dinner for \nsome friends.\nd.\t\nAnna is cleaning the house with \nMarsha.\n5. What is wrong with the food in the \nbag?\na.\t\nThere are too many loaves of bread.\nb.\t\nThey are the wrong ingredients for \ndinner.\nc.\t\nAnna bought too much peanut butter.\nd.\t\nTheir guests cannot eat these \ningredients.\n2. What does Marsha want Anna to \ndo?\na.\t\nMeet her at the market to go shopping\nb.\t\nTell her what is on the shopping list\nc.\t\nBuy all the ingredients on the shopping \nlist\nd.\t\nSpend lots of time shopping for food\n  6. Where did Marsha put the \nshopping list for dinner?\na.\t\nMarsha put it on the kitchen table.\nb.\t\nShe said it was near the refrigerator.\nc.\t\nMarsha put it on the counter.\nd.\t\nShe said it was on the refrigerator.\n3. What does Anna say about shopping?\na.\t\nShe spent too much time.\nb.\t\nMarsha gave her some money.\nc.\t\nShe did not have enough money.\nd.\t\nMarsha called to change the list.\n7. What does Anna want Marsha to\ntrust her to do?\na.\t\nFind the right shopping list for dinner\nb.\t\nReturn the wrong ingredients to the \nmarket\nc.\t\nTell the guests not to come for dinner\nd.\t\nFix the problem of having the wrong \ningredients\n4. What does Marsha say to Anna?\na.\t\nAnna went to the wrong store.\nb.\t\nThe food will take too long to cook.\nc.\t\nThe food cost too much money.\nd.\t\nAnna bought the wrong foods.","guide":{"id":35,"focus":"음식 만들기와 재료의 양을 배워요.","grammar":"a jar of는 ‘한 병의’, a bunch of는 ‘한 다발의’처럼 수량을 세는 표현이에요.","mission":"좋아하는 요리의 재료 목록을 영어로 적어 보세요.","example":"Let’s make dinner!","exampleKo":"저녁을 만들어 봐요!"}},{"id":36,"startPage":402,"endPage":411,"topics":"Locations Objects in the Kitchen","strategy":"Substitute","goals":"Grammar: Prepositions Speaking: Prepositions of location Pronunciation: Compound nouns","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Last time on Let’s Learn English, Marsha and I invited friends to a dinner party but I shopped with the wrong list. Guests are coming soon. Marsha is worried but I have a plan. Let’s see what it is.","ko":"영어, Marsha 및 나는 저녁 파티에 친구를 초대하지만 난 잘못된 목록으로 쇼핑. 손님이 곧 온다. Marsha는 걱정하지만 나는 계획이 있습니다. 그것이 무엇인지 보자."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I just need a couple of ingredients. Marsha, please hand me the flour.","ko":"나는 단지 몇 가지 성분이 필요합니다. Marsha, 밀가루를 손으로."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Anna, where is the flour? It’s not in the cabinets.","ko":"Anna, 어디 밀가루? 그것은 캐비닛에 있지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I put the flour inside the refrigerator.","ko":"나는 냉장고 안쪽에 밀가루를 넣어."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Why?","ko":"왜?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"It’s cold and dry in the refrigerator. See, it says: “Put in a cold, dry place.” Okay, now, Marsha, please hand me the eggs.","ko":"그것은 냉장고에 감기와 건조. 참조, 그것은 말한다: \"냉각에 넣어, 건조한 장소.\" 그래, 지금, 마샤, 나에게 계란을 손."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Anna, where are the eggs?","ko":"안나, 어디 계란?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"The eggs are inside the cabinet under the sink.","ko":"계란은 싱크대의 밑에 장 안쪽에 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Anna, why are the eggs in here?","ko":"Anna, 왜 계란이 여기에 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"On the farm, we always put the eggs there. How else can the chickens see them? Okay. You clean the living room. I will make dinner.","ko":"농장에서 우리는 항상 계란을 넣어. 다른 닭이 그들을 볼 수 있습니까? 괜찮아. 당신은 거실을 청소합니다. 나는 저녁 식사를 만들 것입니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"What are you going to make with these ingredients?","ko":"이 성분으로 만드는 것은 어떨까요?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I have a plan.","ko":"나는 계획이 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Okay, the apartment is clean. The kitchen is not. What are you cooking?","ko":"괜찮아, 아파트는 깨끗합니다. 주방은 없습니다. 요리하는 것은 무엇입니까?"},{"speaker":"I made my favorite recipe","en":"peanut-butter-banana pancakes!","ko":"땅콩 버터 바나 팬케이크!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"You made breakfast.","ko":"아침 식사."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes! I call it let’s-eat-breakfast-for-dinner dinner!","ko":"예! 나는 그것을 봅시다-eat-breakfast-for-dinner 저녁 식사!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Anna! Mmm! Hey, this tastes good! Anna, you made it work!","ko":"Anna! Mmm! Hey,이 맛 좋은! Anna, 당신은 그것을 작동!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"That’s our guests!","ko":"그것은 우리의 손님입니다!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"I’ll answer the door.","ko":"나는 문에 대답할 것입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I’ll finish here.","ko":"나는 여기에 완료됩니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Like I said, sometimes Marsha worries too much. When something goes wrong with your plan, just change the plan! Till next time!","ko":"내가 말했듯이, 때로는 Marsha 걱정 너무 많이. 뭔가가 계획과 잘못되면, 그냥 계획을 변경! 다음 시간! 영어 학습하자 36 406"}],"words":[{"en":"breakfast","definition":"the first meal of the day","ko":"아침 식사"},{"en":"cabinet","definition":"a piece of furniture that is used for storing things and usually has doors and shelves","ko":"수납장"},{"en":"dry","definition":"having no or very little water or liquid","ko":"마른"},{"en":"egg","definition":"a hard-shelled oval thing from which a young bird is born","ko":"달걀"},{"en":"flour","definition":"powder made from a grain (especially wheat) that is used in cooking for making bread or cakes inside - p. in or into the inner part of (something or someone)","ko":"밀가루"},{"en":"recipe","definition":"a set of instructions for making food","ko":"조리법"},{"en":"refrigerator","definition":"a device or room that is used to keep things (such as food and drinks) cold","ko":"냉장고"},{"en":"sink","definition":"a wide bowl that has a faucet for water and a drain at the bottom and is usually positioned in a counter","ko":"싱크대"},{"en":"taste","definition":"to have a particular flavor under - p. in or to a lower place than (something)","ko":"맛보다"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 36 - I Can Fix This!\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. Why did Anna put the flour in the \nrefrigerator?\na.\t\nThere was no room in the cabinets.\nb.\t\nShe wants to keep it warm.\nc.\t\nThe bag says to keep in a cold, dry \nplace.\nd.\t\nShe thinks the flour is too old.\n4. How does Marsha ask what Anna \nis going to make?\na.\t\nWhere are you planning to do with the \ningredients?\nb.\t\nWhat are you cooking for dinner with \nthese things?\nc.\t\nWhat are you going to make with these \ningredients?\nd.\t\nHow are you going to make something \nfor dinner?\n2. Why did Anna put the eggs under \nthe sink?\na.\t\nThey always did that on the farm.\nb.\t\nSo the chickens can keep them warm.\nc.\t\nThere is no room in the refrigerator.\nd.\t\nSo no one can see them.\n5. What makes Marsha angry?\na.\t\nMarsha thinks Anna is not done.\nb.\t\nAnna made her favorite recipe.\nc.\t\nMarsha cannot clean the kitchen.\nd.\t\nAnna made breakfast, not dinner.\n3. What strategy are Anna and \nMarsha using when Anna offers to \nmake dinner while Marsha cleans \nthe living room?\na.\t\nSummarize\nb.\t\nCooperate\nc.\t\nSelf-Talk\nd.\t\nSubstitution\n6. What strategy did Anna use in this \nlesson?\na.\t\nPredict\nb.\t\nSubstitute\nc.\t\nPersonalize\nd.\t\nSummarize","guide":{"id":36,"focus":"부엌에서 물건 위치와 요리 방법을 말해요.","grammar":"in, on, under 같은 전치사로 위치를 설명해요. 단어를 묶어 새 명사를 만들기도 해요.","mission":"요리 순서를 세 단계로 나누어 영어로 말해 보세요.","example":"I can fix this!","exampleKo":"제가 이걸 해결할 수 있어요!"}},{"id":37,"startPage":412,"endPage":422,"topics":"Exchanging opinions Agreement and disagreement Comparing things, places, & people","strategy":"Personalize","goals":"Grammar: Possessive pronouns Speaking: Giving a reason for your opinion Pronunciation: Pronouncing possessive pronouns","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"You know, I am from the country and sometimes I miss it. But I really like life in the city! I love the city. Oh, look. Someone lost a bag. Maybe it’s theirs. Excuse me. Is this bag yours? Dr. Jill: No. It’s not mine. It might be hers.","ko":"당신이 알고, 나는 나라에서이고 때때로 나는 그것을 놓습니다. 그러나 나는 정말 도시에서 생활을 좋아합니다! 나는 도시를 사랑합니다. Oh, 봐. 누군가 가방을 잃었다. 어쩌면 그것은 그들입니다. 변태 나를. 이 가방은? 박사. Jill: No. 그것은 내지 않습니다. 그것은 그녀의 것일 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Excuse me. Is this bag yours?","ko":"실례 나를. 이 가방은?"},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"No. It’s not mine. It might be his.","ko":"아니. 그것은 내 아니에요. 그것은 그의 될 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thank you. Hello. Is this bag yours?","ko":"감사합니다. 여보세요. 이 부대는 당신입니까?"},{"speaker":"Phil","en":"Yes, that’s mine. These are all my travel things. Thank you, thank you!","ko":"예, 그게 내. 이 모든 여행입니다. 감사합니다, 감사합니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Are you okay? You seem ... nervous.","ko":"당신은 괜찮아? 당신은 ... 긴장 보인다."},{"speaker":"Phil","en":"Well, this is my first visit to Washington, D.C. I’m from a small town in the country. I feel a little lost.","ko":"글쎄, 이것은 워싱턴에 처음 방문, D.C. 나는 나라의 작은 도시에서입니다. 나는 조금 잃어버린 느낌."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I am from the country too! And I understand. When I first came here, I felt lost ... all the time.","ko":"나는 나라에서 너무! 그리고 나는 이해. 내가 처음 왔을 때, 나는 잃어버린 느낌 ... 모든 시간."},{"speaker":"Phil","en":"So, do you like living in the country or in the city?","ko":"그래서, 당신은 나라 또는 도시에서 살고 싶습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I like to live in the city.","ko":"나는 도시에서 살고 싶습니다."},{"speaker":"Phil","en":"Why?","ko":"왜?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"The city is exciting! It has more culture than the country. There are many museums and restaurants. Every night, there is theater and music. And, there are more jobs. That is why I’m here.","ko":"도시는 흥미 진진합니다! 그것은 국가보다 더 문화가있다. 많은 박물관과 레스토랑이 있습니다. 매일 밤, 극장과 음악이 있습니다. 그리고, 더 많은 작업이 있습니다. 그것은 왜 여기에 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Phil","en":"Well, I agree. There is more culture in the city and there might be more jobs. But the country has more nature! It’s peaceful and beautiful. There are more trees and mountains. The air is clean. You can go hiking and camping. The city is not beautiful. It’s noisy and dirty.","ko":"도시에 더 많은 문화가 있고 더 많은 일자리가있을 수 있습니다. 그러나 국가는 더 많은 자연이 있습니다! 그것은 평화롭고 아름답습니다. 더 많은 나무와 산이 있습니다. 공기가 깨끗합니다. 하이킹과 캠핑을 갈 수 있습니다. 도시는 아름답지 않습니다. 그것은 유쾌하고 더러운입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I disagree. I think all the different buildings are beautiful. And I like to watch all the different people.","ko":"나는 동의한다. 나는 다른 모든 건물이 아름다워 생각한다. 그리고 나는 다른 모든 사람들을보고 싶습니다."},{"speaker":"Phil","en":"That’s another thing that is different. People in the country are friendly. They always say “hello!” Here, no one says “hello.” I think city people are rude.","ko":"그것은 다른 일이다. 국가의 사람들은 친절합니다. 그들은 항상 \"안녕하세요!\" 여기, 아무도 \"안녕하세요.\"라고 나는 도시 사람들이 빠졌다고 생각합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well, I agree. Country people are friendly. But I don’t think city people are rude. I think they’re just busy.","ko":"글쎄, 나는 동의한다. 국가 사람들은 친절합니다. 그러나 나는 도시 사람들이 빠지지 않는다고 생각하지 않는다. 나는 단지 바쁘다 생각합니다."},{"speaker":"Phil","en":"That’s a good point.","ko":"그것은 좋은 점입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Look at me. I live in the city and I said “hello” to you.","ko":"나를 봐. 나는 도시에서 살고 나는 \"hello\"라고 말했다."},{"speaker":"Phil","en":"But you are from the country.","ko":"그러나 당신은 나라에서."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I have an idea. Let’s say “hello!” to people -- to many people!","ko":"나는 아이디어가 있습니다. 사람들이 \"안녕!\"라고 말하자 -- 많은 사람들에게!"},{"speaker":"Phil","en":"What? Why?","ko":"왜?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well, if we say “hello,” maybe they will say “hello” to other people ... Hello!","ko":"글쎄, 우리는 \"hello,\"라고 말하면 그들은 다른 사람들에게 \"hello\"라고 말할 것입니다 ... 안녕하세요!"},{"speaker":"Phil","en":"... and they will say “hello” to more people! That’s a great idea! I’m glad you found my bag.","ko":"... 그리고 그들은 더 많은 사람들에게 \"hello\"라고 말할 것입니다! 그것은 훌륭한 아이디어입니다! 나는 당신이 내 가방을 발견하게되어 기쁩니다. 영어 수업을 배우자 37 416"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Come on. Let’s go say “hello” to people.","ko":"에 가자. \"hello\"사람에게 말하자."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"We don’t have to agree with people. They have their opinions. We have ours. And as we like to say, you can always agree to disagree! Until next time...! Hello!","ko":"우리는 사람들과 동의하지 않습니다. 그들은 그들의 의견이 있습니다. 우리는 우리의. 그리고 우리는 말하고 싶습니다, 당신은 항상 동의 할 수 있습니다! 다음 시간까지! 안녕하세요!"}],"words":[{"en":"agree","definition":"to have the same opinion","ko":"동의하다"},{"en":"dirty","definition":"not clean","ko":"더러운"},{"en":"disagree","definition":"to have a different opinion","ko":"의견이 다르다"},{"en":"friendly","definition":"acting like a friend or kind and helpful","ko":"친근한"},{"en":"nature","definition":"the physical world and everything in it that is not made by people","ko":"자연"},{"en":"noisy","definition":"making a lot of loud or unpleasant noise","ko":"시끄러운"},{"en":"opinion","definition":"a belief, judgment, or way of thinking about something","ko":"의견"},{"en":"peaceful","definition":"quiet and calm or without noise","ko":"평화로운"},{"en":"rude","definition":"not polite","ko":"무례한"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 37 - Let’s Agree to Disagree\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1.    What does Anna say about the city \nand country?\na.\t\nAnna is moving to the country. \nb.\t\nShe likes to visit the city. \nc.\t\nAnna wants to go to the city soon. \nd.\t\nShe misses life in the country \n4. What does Anna say about the city?\na.\t  The city is an exciting place to live. \nb.\t There are more theater and music jobs. \nc.\t There is too much excitement in the \ncity. \nd.\t The restaurants and museums are \nbetter.\n2. What does Dr. Jill say to Anna?\na.\t\nI saw her with your bag. \nb.\t\nIt might be hers. \nc.\t\nIt is mine. \nd.\t\nIs this bag yours?\n5. What does Phil say about the \ncountry?\na.\t\nThere is more culture. \nb.\t\nIt has more nature. \nc.\t\nThere are more jobs. \nd.\t\nIt has noise and dirt. \n3. What does Phil say to Anna?\na.\t Please give me my travel things. \nb.\t Where did you find my travel things? \nc.\t These are all my travel things. \nd.\t Are these all my travel things? \n6. What does Phil think about city \npeople?\na.\t He thinks that they are noisy. \nb.\t Phil thinks that they are friendly. \nc.\t Phil thinks that they are rude. \nd.\t He thinks that they are busy.","guide":{"id":37,"focus":"다른 의견을 존중하며 대화해요.","grammar":"mine, yours, hers는 ‘내 것’, ‘네 것’, ‘그녀의 것’처럼 소유를 나타내요.","mission":"좋아하는 것에 관해 찬성·반대 이유를 하나씩 말해 보세요.","example":"Let’s agree to disagree.","exampleKo":"서로 의견이 다르다는 점을 인정해요."}},{"id":38,"startPage":423,"endPage":433,"topics":"Describing people, places, & things Reporting details Identifying positive & negative personal qualities","strategy":"Evaluate","goals":"Grammar and Speaking: Superlative adjectives Speaking: Superlative adjectives Pronunciation: Pronouncing superlative adjectives","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello! I have great news. My best friend from my hometown is coming here -- to Washington, D.C.! I can’t wait to catch up with her! Oh! I gotta go. Her train arrives in 10 minutes!","ko":"안녕하세요! 나는 훌륭한 소식이 있습니다. 내 고향에서 가장 친한 친구는 여기 -- 워싱턴, D.C.! 나는 그녀를 잡아 기다릴 수 없습니다! 오! 나는 간다. 그녀의 기차는 10 분에 도착!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Penelope!","ko":"페넬로프!"},{"speaker":"Penelope","en":"Anna! I am really happy to see you!","ko":"Anna! 나는 정말 당신을보고 행복 해요!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Me too! How was your trip?","ko":"나를 너무! 어떻게 여행 이었습니까?"},{"speaker":"Penelope","en":"It was fine.","ko":"그것은 훌륭했습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Let me help you with your bags.","ko":"가방에 당신을 도와주세요."},{"speaker":"Penelope","en":"I’m really excited to be in Washington, D.C.! I can’t wait to hear about … everything!","ko":"나는 워싱턴 DC에있을 정말 흥분! 나는 ... 모든 것을 듣고 기다릴 수 없다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I have so much to tell you. Let’s go to my apartment. We can talk over a hot cup of tea.","ko":"나는 당신을 말해 너무 많이있다. 내 아파트에 가자. 우리는 차의 뜨거운 컵에 대해 이야기 할 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Penelope","en":"I love your apartment building, Anna. Is your rent expensive?","ko":"나는 아파트 건물을 사랑, Anna. 비싼 임대입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well, I have a roommate. So, we split the rent.","ko":"글쎄, 나는 룸메이트가 있습니다. 그래서, 우리는 임대를 분할합니다."},{"speaker":"Penelope","en":"Oh, that’s right. Is your roommate nice?","ko":"오, 그게 맞습니다. 당신의 roommate는 좋은가요?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Marsha is the nicest person I know in this city. Sometimes she worries too much. And she says I’m the messiest cook she knows. But we are great roommates.","ko":"Marsha는이 도시에서 알고있는 가장 좋은 사람입니다. 때때로 그녀는 너무 많이 걱정합니다. 그리고 그녀는 그녀가 알고있는 가장 쉬운 요리입니다. 그러나 우리는 훌륭한 룸메이트입니다."},{"speaker":"Penelope","en":"So, Anna, is it hard to make friends in D.C.?","ko":"그래서, 안나, 그것은 D.C에서 친구를 만들기 어렵다.?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"At first it was hard. But now, Marsha is a good friend. And there’s Pete. Of all the people I know in D.C., Pete is the most serious and also the silliest.","ko":"처음에는 열심히했다. 그러나 이제 Marsha는 좋은 친구입니다. 그리고 Pete가 있습니다. 모든 사람들이 D.C.에서 알고 있습니다. Pete는 가장 심각하고 침묵합니다."},{"speaker":"Penelope","en":"He sounds … interesting.","ko":"그는 ... 흥미로운."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Jonathan and Ashley are two other good friends of mine. In the city, they are the friendliest people I know. They always help me when I need it.","ko":"Jonathan과 Ashley는 광산의 두 가지 좋은 친구입니다. 도시에서, 그들은 내가 알고있는 친구입니다. 그들은 항상 나를 도울 때 나는 그것을 필요로합니다."},{"speaker":"Penelope","en":"Your friends sound great! So, tell me about your job.","ko":"당신의 친구는 훌륭한 소리! 그래서, 당신의 일에 대해 말해."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I love my work! I make a children’s show called the “Time Traveling Treehouse.”","ko":"나는 나의 일을 사랑한다! 나는 아이들의 쇼가 \"Time Traveling Treehouse\"라고 불렀다."},{"speaker":"Penelope","en":"Anna, that is the best job for you! Do you remember when we were little? We played in that old treehouse behind my family’s house for hours!","ko":"Anna, 그게 당신을 위해 최고의 일입니다! 우리가 조금했을 때 기억하십니까? 우리는 시간 동안 가족의 집 뒤에 오래된 트리 하우스에서 연주!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I forgot about that! We thought it really time traveled! Penelope, it is really good to talk to you. New friends are good. But old friends are the best.","ko":"나는 그것에 대해 잊었다! 우리는 정말 시간을 여행했습니다! Penelope, 그것은 정말 당신에게 이야기하는 것이 좋습니다. 새로운 친구는 좋습니다. 그러나 오래된 친구는 최고입니다."},{"speaker":"Penelope","en":"I know. Our hometown isn’t the same now. You are not there.","ko":"나는 알고있다. 우리의 고향은 지금 동일하지 않습니다. 당신은 거기 없습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No crying. Why don’t you move here and live with me and Marsha?","ko":"울고있다. 왜 당신은 여기 이동하지 않고 나와 마샤와 함께 살 수?"},{"speaker":"Penelope","en":"Anna, I can’t leave our hometown. You forget -- I love my job, too.","ko":"Anna, 나는 우리의 고향을 떠나지 않을 수 있습니다. 잊었다 -- 나는 내 일을 사랑, 너무."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I didn’t forget. You are the most famous turkey farmer I know!","ko":"나는 잊지 않았다. 당신은 내가 알고있는 가장 유명한 turkey 농부입니다!"},{"speaker":"Penelope","en":"Thanks, Anna.","ko":"감사, 안나."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Come on. Let’s go eat dinner at one of D.C.’s most famous restaurants.","ko":"에 가자. D.C.의 가장 유명한 레스토랑 중 하나에서 저녁 식사를 가자."},{"speaker":"Penelope","en":"Awesome!","ko":"굉장! 영어 수업 38 427"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"That’s the restaurant, Penelope. I’ll be right there.","ko":"레스토랑, Penelope입니다. 나는 거기있을거야."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I have a great apartment. I love my work. And I have awesome friends -- both old and new. I am the luckiest woman in Washington, D.C. (sound of thunder) Until next time?","ko":"나는 훌륭한 아파트가 있습니다. 나는 내 일을 좋아합니다. 그리고 나는 멋진 친구가 -- 이전과 새로운 것을 가지고 있습니다. 나는 워싱턴 D.C.에서 가장 운이 좋은 여성입니다. (삼둥의 소리) 다음 시간까지?"}],"words":[{"en":"catch up (with)","definition":"to talk to someone you have not seen for some time and find out what they have been doing","ko":"연락하며 밀린 이야기를 나누다"},{"en":"cry","definition":"to produce tears from your eyes often while making loud sounds because of pain, sorrow, or other strong emotions","ko":"울다"},{"en":"expensive","definition":"costing a lot of money","ko":"비싼"},{"en":"famous","definition":"known or recognized by very many people","ko":"유명한"},{"en":"friendly","definition":"acting like a friend friendliest - superlative adj.","ko":"친절한"},{"en":"lucky","definition":"having good luck luckiest - superlative adj.","ko":"운 좋은"},{"en":"messy","definition":"not clean or tidy messiest superlative adj.","ko":"지저분한"},{"en":"nice","definition":"kind, polite, and friendly nicest - superlative adj.","ko":"좋은"},{"en":"rent","definition":"money that you pay in return for being able to use property and especially to live in an apartment or house that belongs to someone else","ko":"집세"},{"en":"silly","definition":"silliest - superlative adj. playful and funny","ko":"어리석은"},{"en":"split","definition":"to divide (something, such as money or food) among two or more people or things","ko":"나누다"},{"en":"tea","definition":"a drink that is made by soaking the dried leaves of an Asian plant in hot water","ko":"차"},{"en":"train","definition":"a group of vehicles that travel on a track and are connected to each other and usually to an engine","ko":"기차"},{"en":"turkey","definition":"a large American bird that is related to the chicken and that is hunted or raised by people for its meat","ko":"칠면조"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 38 - She’s My Best Friend!\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What is Anna doing today?\na.\t\nA Visiting a friend in her hometown \nb.\t\nGoing to her hometown \nc.\t\nTraveling on a train \nd.\t\nCatching up with a friend\n4. What does Anna say about Jonathan?\na.\t He is her silliest friend. \nb.\t He is friendly and helpful. \nc.\t He is Anna’s serious friend. \nd.\t He is the most interesting.\n2. What does Penelope say to Anna?\na.\t\nShe wants to see the monuments. \nb.\t\nShe wants to have a cup of tea. \nc.\t\nShe can’t wait to hear about everything. \nd.\t\nShe wants to tell Anna everything.\n5. Why does Penelope want to stay in \nher hometown?\na.\t\nT She loves her job as a turkey farmer. \nb.\t\nPenelope is afraid of living in the city. \nc.\t\nShe doesn’t want to leave her family. \nd.\t\nPenelope thinks it will not change.\n3. What does Anna say about Marsha?\na.\t Marsha does not always pay her rent. \nb.\t Marsha is the nicest person in the city. \nc.\t Marsha is a messy cook. \nd.\t Marsha pays all the rent.\nHoliday Sweaters","guide":{"id":38,"focus":"친구를 소개하며 가장 친한 관계를 말해요.","grammar":"best, nicest처럼 ‘가장 ~한’을 나타내는 최상급을 배워요.","mission":"가장 친한 친구의 장점을 영어로 소개해 보세요.","example":"She’s my best friend!","exampleKo":"그녀는 제 가장 친한 친구예요!"}},{"id":39,"startPage":434,"endPage":447,"topics":"Shopping online Interpreting factual statements Critical thinking about advertisements","strategy":"Ask questions to clarify or get more information","goals":"Grammar: Adjectives with negative preﬁxes (in-, un-, dis-, im-) Speaking: Using negative prefixes with adjectives Pronunciation: Pronouncing “comfortable” and “uncomfortable.”","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello! Winter weather in Washington, D.C. can be really windy. And wind messes up my hair. It is really windy today. Look at my hair. Will it be windy this weekend? I’ll listen to the news. I am tired of my untidy hair.","ko":"안녕하세요! 워싱턴의 겨울 날씨, D.C. 정말 바람이 될 수 있습니다. 그리고 바람은 내 머리카락을 엉망. 그것은 정말 바람이 오늘. 내 머리카락을 봐. 이번 주말에 바람이 될 것입니까? 나는 뉴스를 듣게 될 것입니다. 나는 내 비열한 머리카락의 피곤합니다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Are you tired of your untidy hair?","ko":"당신은 당신의 untidy 머리의 피곤?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes. Yes, I am. And it’s … uncomfortable.","ko":"예. 예, 나는. 그리고 그것은 ... 불편."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Is it … uncomfortable?","ko":"그것은 ... 불행히도?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes. Yes, it is! Hey, is that … Pete?","ko":"예. 예, 그것은! 이봐, 그 ... Pete?"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Hi. I’m Pete. And I have the perfect product for you -- Hair Be Good!","ko":"안녕. 나는 Pete입니다. 그리고 나는 당신을 위한 완벽한 제품이 있습니다 -- 머리는 좋습니다!"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Just spray Hair Be Good on your hair … wrap in a towel … and you are done! Hair Be Good works and it’s inexpensive. One can costs only $10! So, go online and order your Hair Be Good today!","ko":"그냥 스프레이 헤어는 당신의 머리에 좋은 ... 수건에 포장 ... 그리고 당신은 완료! 헤어는 좋은 작품이며 그것은 저렴합니다. 하나는 단지 $ 10을 요할 수 있습니다! 그래서, 온라인으로 가서 머리카락을 주문 오늘!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hair Be Good sounds perfect! And I can trust Pete! I am buying some right now. Okay, I will order one can of Hair Be Good for $10. I’ll pay with a credit card. My delivery will arrive in 2 days. Awesome!","ko":"머리는 좋은 소리가 완벽합니다! 그리고 나는 Pete를 신뢰 할 수 있습니다! 나는 지금 바로 구입하고 있습니다. 잘, 나는 머리의 하나가 10 달러를 위해 좋다는 것을 주문할 것입니다. 나는 신용 카드로 지불할 것입니다. 나의 납품은 2 일에 도착할 것입니다. 최고!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"It arrived! I’ll use it before I go to work. Okay, Hair Be Good, make my untidy hair tidy! No, make it … fabulous!","ko":"그것은 도착했습니다! 나는 일하기 전에 그것을 사용할 것입니다. 잘, 머리는 좋, 나의 untidy 머리 tidy를 만드십시오! 아니, 그것을 만드십시오 ... 멋진!"},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"Hi, Anna.","ko":"안녕, 안나."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello, Amelia!","ko":"안녕하세요, 아멜리아!"},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"Anna, you look … different.","ko":"Anna, 당신은 ... 다른."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thanks! I used a new product called Hair Be Good.","ko":"감사합니다! 나는 머리가 좋다라는 새로운 제품을 사용했습니다."},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"Well, it’s not.","ko":"잘, 그것은 아닙니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"It’s not what?","ko":"그것은 무엇일까요?"},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"Good. Your hair does not look good.","ko":"좋은. 당신의 머리는 좋은 보이지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh, no! This is not good.","ko":"오, 아니! 이것은 좋지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"Why don’t you go home and take care of … this.","ko":"왜 집에 가서 걱정하지 마십시오 ... 이것."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Good idea.","ko":"좋은 아이디어."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Hi, Anna!","ko":"안녕, 안나!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello, Pete.","ko":"안녕, Pete."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Is something wrong?","ko":"뭔가 잘못되었습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This is wrong!","ko":"이것은 잘못되었습니다!"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"What did you do to your hair?","ko":"당신은 당신의 머리에 무엇을 했습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hair Be Good did this to my hair.","ko":"머리는 내 머리에 이것을 했습니다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Ah, you bought it!","ko":"아, 당신은 그것을 샀다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes, I bought it. You said in your ad it was a perfect product. This is not perfect. This is imperfect!","ko":"예, 나는 그것을 샀다. 당신은 당신의 광고에 그것을 완벽한 제품이었다고 말했다. 이것은 완벽하지 않습니다. 이것은 불완전합니다!"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"It’s unbelievable!","ko":"믿을 수 없습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I believed your ad, Pete. It was dishonest!","ko":"나는 당신의 광고를 믿고, Pete. 그것은 요리했다! &#8217;s Learn English Lesson 39 438"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Anna, you don’t believe everything you see in ads, do you?","ko":"Anna, 당신은 당신이 광고에서 볼 모든 것을 믿지 않는다, 당신은?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No, Pete. Just the ones with my friends.","ko":"아니, Pete. 그냥 내 친구와 함께."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Your hair will be okay. Just wash it ... a couple of times.","ko":"당신의 머리는 괜찮습니다. 그냥 씻어 ... 몇 번의."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thanks. Thanks a lot, Pete! Here, here’s your product! You should call it “Hair Be Really Bad!” Until next time, Pete! Till next time.","ko":"감사합니다. 많은 감사합니다. Pete! 여기, 여기에 당신의 제품입니다! 당신은 다음에 때까지 \"Hair Be Really Bad!\"라고 부릅니다. Pete! Till 다음 시간."}],"words":[{"en":"can","definition":"a closed metal container that is usually shaped like a cylinder and that holds food, drink, or other liquids","ko":"~할 수 있다"},{"en":"delivery","definition":"something that is taken to a person or place or something that is delivered","ko":"배달"},{"en":"dishonest","definition":"not honest: such as saying or likely to say things that are untrue","ko":"부정직한"},{"en":"imperfect","definition":"having mistakes or problems or not perfect","ko":"불완전한"},{"en":"fabulous","definition":"very good","ko":"멋진"},{"en":"inexpensive","definition":"low in price o rnot expensive","ko":"저렴한"},{"en":"order","definition":"to place an order for (something): such as to request (something) from a company","ko":"주문하다"},{"en":"product","definition":"something that is made or grown to be sold or used","ko":"제품"},{"en":"spray","definition":"to put a stream of small drops of liquid on (someone or something)","ko":"스프레이"},{"en":"tidy","definition":"clean and organized or not messy","ko":"말끔한"},{"en":"towel","definition":"a piece of cloth used for drying things","ko":"수건"},{"en":"unbelievable","definition":"difficult or impossible to believe","ko":"믿을 수 없는"},{"en":"uncomfortable","definition":"causing a feeling of physical or mental discomfort","ko":"불편한"},{"en":"untidy","definition":"not neat or clean","ko":"지저분한"},{"en":"wrap","definition":"to cover (something) by winding or folding a piece of material around it","ko":"포장하다"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 39 - It’s Unbelievable!\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Anna say about the \nweather?\na.\t\nIt’s really windy. \nb.\t\nAnna says it is messy. \nc.\t\nIt is wintery. \nd.\t\nAnna says she loves it.\n5. What is Anna doing on the computer?\na.\t Asking Pete about Hair Be Good \nb.\t Looking for a store that sells the \nproduct \nc.\t Buying Hair Be Good online \nd.\t Reading comments on Hair Be Good\n2. What does Anna want to know \nabout?\na.\t\nHow to change her hair. \nb.\t\nThe latest TV program. \nc.\t\nThe weekend weather. \nd.\t\nHow to listen to the news.\n6. At the office, what does Amelia say to \nAnna?\na.\t\nYour hair does not look good. \nb.\t\nIt’s nice to see you today. \nc.\t\nDid you do that at home? \nd.\t\nWhat did you do to your hair?\n3. Why is Anna talking to Pete?\na.\t He is in Anna’s dream. \nb.\t Pete called on the phone. \nc.\t He is at Anna’s house. \nd.\t Pete is in a TV ad.\n7. What does Anna yell at Pete?\na.\t Pete is an imperfect actor. \nb.\t He was wrong about her hair. \nc.\t Pete should use Hair Be Good. \nd.\t His ad was not true\n4. What is one thing Pete says about the \nproduct?\na.\t He bought it online. \nb.\t It has a low cost. \nc.\t He uses it all of the time. \nd.\t It comes with a free towel.\n8. What advice does Pete give to Anna?\na.\t Trust what your friends tell you. \nb.\t Try using another hair product. \nc.\t You should wash your hair. \nd.\t You should believe what you see in ads.\n1946 cigarette advertisement launched by R.J. Reynolds Tobacco Company.\nFalse claim: Doctors think smoking is healthy\nFalse claim: Donuts are healthy\nFalse claim: Soap can remove fat from inside the body\nFalse claim: Sugar helps you lose weight","guide":{"id":39,"focus":"광고에서 좋고 나쁜 표현을 구분해요.","grammar":"un-, in-, im-, dis-를 붙이면 반대 의미가 될 수 있어요. believable과 unbelievable을 비교해요.","mission":"광고 문장 속 과장된 표현을 찾아 설명해 보세요.","example":"It’s unbelievable!","exampleKo":"정말 믿을 수 없어요!"}},{"id":40,"startPage":448,"endPage":459,"topics":"Describing people’s actions Asking for & giving feedback","strategy":"Self-evaluate","goals":"Grammar: Adverbs (loudly, quietly, slowly); comparatives of adverbs (more seriously) Speaking: Asking for and giving feedback Pronunciation: Projecting when public speaking","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Happy New Year! Some people, at the start of a new year, make a resolution -- a promise to yourself to be better. I thought about my resolution carefully. I want to be an actor on the stage! Today I will audition for a show called “The Woods Are Alive!” Wish me luck!","ko":"새해 복 많이 받으세요! 새로운 해의 시작에서, 해결 -- 자신을 더 나은 약속합니다. 나는 신중하게 내 해결에 대해 생각한다. 나는 무대에 배우가 되기를 원한다! 오늘 나는 \"나무가 살아있다\"라는 쇼에 대한 오디션을 할 것입니다! 나에게 행운을 빌어!"},{"speaker":"Director","en":"Next! What is your name?","ko":"다음! 당신의 이름은 무엇입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"My name is Anna Matteo.","ko":"내 이름은 Anna Matteo입니다."},{"speaker":"Director","en":"Are you ready to audition?","ko":"당신은 오디션을 준비?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"(warms up voice) Yes.","ko":"(음성) 예."},{"speaker":"Director","en":"Great. Let’s begin on page 1. Here is the story. You are lost in the woods. You are searching desperately for a way out. Suddenly, you hear something. Now, say your line.","ko":"좋은. 페이지 1에서 시작합시다. 여기에 이야기입니다. 당신은 나무에서 잃어버린. 당신은 길에 desperately 검색하고 있습니다. 갑자기, 당신은 무언가를들을 수 있습니다. 지금, 당신의 선을 말한다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"‘What was that? Hello. Is someone there?’","ko":"‘무엇이 되었나요? 안녕하세요. 누군가가 있습니까?’"},{"speaker":"Director","en":"Anna, you are speaking too softly. Can you speak more loudly and a little more, um, seriously?","ko":"Anna, 당신은 너무 부드럽게 말하고 있습니다. 더 확고하고 조금 더, um, 심각하게 말할 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes, of course I can. ‘What was that? Hello. Is someone there?’ Is that loud enough?","ko":"예, 물론 나는 할 수 있습니다. '무엇이? 안녕하세요. 누군가가 있습니까?'는 충분히 굉장합니까?"},{"speaker":"Director","en":"Yes, that is loud enough. Let’s turn to page 25. In this scene, you are moving slowly and quietly through the woods.","ko":"예, 그것은 충분히 크다. 을 켭니다 페이지 25. 이 장면에서,당신은 천천히 움직이고 조용히 숲을 통해."},{"speaker":"Director","en":"Anna. Anna! You are walking quickly and loudly. Walk slowly and quietly.","ko":"Anna. Anna! 당신은 신속하고 확고하게 걷고 있습니다. 천천히 그리고 조용히 걸어."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I’m walking slowly and quietly. I am walking…","ko":"나는 천천히 걷고 조용히. 나는 걷는거야 ..."},{"speaker":"Director","en":"Anna. Anna. You don’t need to say “slowly” and “quietly.” Alright, let’s try the last scene. Turn to page 48. I say my line first, then you say your line. ‘You will never get out of these woods alive! Mwa-ha-ha-ha-ha Mwa-ha-ha-ha-ha!’","ko":"안나. 안나. 당신은 \"즐거운\"과 \"quietly\"라고 말할 필요가 없습니다. Alright, 마지막 장면을 시도 할 수 있습니다. 첫 번째 줄을 말한다, 다음 당신은 당신의 선을 말한다. '당신은이 숲에서 살아 결코 얻을 것이다! Mwa-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!'"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"‘Yes, I will.’","ko":"'예, 나.'"},{"speaker":"Director","en":"Okay, Anna, you said that line -- you said that line really late. You need to say it earlier.","ko":"괜찮아, 안나, 당신은 선을 말했다 -- 당신은 정말 늦게 선 말했다. 당신은 그것을 일찍 말해야합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sorry. Sorry. Let me try again.","ko":"죄송합니다. 죄송합니다. 다시 시도하십시오."},{"speaker":"Director","en":"‘You will never …’","ko":"'당신은 결코 ...'"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"‘Yes, I will.’","ko":"'예, 나.'"},{"speaker":"Director","en":"‘… get out of the woods alive.’","ko":"‘... 살아 있는 숲에서 얻다.’"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I was too early, wasn’t I?","ko":"나는 너무 일찍 없었다, 나는하지 않았다?"},{"speaker":"Director","en":"Yes. Yes, you were.","ko":"예. 네, 당신은 있었다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Director, how am I doing?","ko":"이사, 어떻게하고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Director","en":"You know, Anna. I think that I have the perfect part for you. The costume is in the back. Please go try it on.","ko":"당신은 알고, 안나. 나는 당신을 위해 완벽한 부분이 있다고 생각합니다. 의상은 뒷면에 있습니다. 그것을 시도하십시오."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Awesome! (Anna returns as a tree.)","ko":"최고! (Anna는 나무로 반환합니다.)"},{"speaker":"Director","en":"Oh, Anna, that fits you perfectly!","ko":"오, 안나, 완벽하게 맞습니다! English Lesson 40 452를 배우십시오."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I’m a tree. I’m a tree in … “The Woods Are Alive!” Yes!","ko":"나는 나무입니다. 나는 나무입니다 ... \"나무는 살아있다!\" 예!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"My new year is starting awesomely! Excuse me, Director! I have a great idea for my tree. Oh, wait! Until next time!","ko":"내 새 해가 시작 굉장합니다! 예, 이사! 나는 내 나무에 대한 큰 아이디어를 가지고. 오, 기다려! 다음 시간까지! 영어 수업을 배우자 40 453"}],"words":[{"en":"actor","definition":"a person who acts in a play or a movie","ko":"배우"},{"en":"audition","definition":"a short performance to show the talents of someone (such as an actor or a musician) who is being considered for a role in a play or a position in an orchestra","ko":"오디션"},{"en":"desperately","definition":"in a way that is very sad and or upset manner because of having little or no hope","ko":"필사적으로"},{"en":"director","definition":"a person who directs a play or a movie","ko":"감독"},{"en":"enough","definition":"equal to what is needed","ko":"충분한"},{"en":"line","definition":"the words that an actor speaks in a play, movie or TV show","ko":"대사"},{"en":"loudly","definition":"in a manner that makes or causes a lot of noise","ko":"큰 소리로"},{"en":"page","definition":"one side of a sheet of paper","ko":"페이지"},{"en":"quickly","definition":"at a fast speed; rapidly","ko":"빠르게"},{"en":"quietly","definition":"in a manner that makes little noise","ko":"조용히"},{"en":"resolution","definition":"a promise to yourself that you will make a serious effort to do something that you should do","ko":"해결"},{"en":"scene","definition":"a division of an act in a play during which the action takes place in a single place without a break in time","ko":"장면"},{"en":"script","definition":"the written form of a play, movie, or television show","ko":"대본"},{"en":"softly","definition":"in a quiet voice or manner","ko":"부드럽게"},{"en":"stage","definition":"a raised platform in a theater or auditorium where the performers stand","ko":"무대"},{"en":"suddenly","definition":"very quickly in usually an unexpected way","ko":"갑자기"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 40 - The Woods Are Alive\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Anna plan to do in the \nnew year? \na.\t\nWatch a show on the stage \nb.\t\nBecome an actor in a show.  \nc.\t\nFind actors for a show. \nd.\t\nOpen a new theater\n4. What strategy is Anna using when \nshe says, “I was too early, wasn’t I?”\na.\t\nSelf-evaluate \nb.\t\nPlanning \nc.\t\nLooking for patterns \nd.\t\nPersonalize\n2. What does the director want Anna \nto do? \na.\t\nLook more desperate \nb.\t\nBe less serious \nc.\t\nTalk more loudly \nd.\t\nSpeak more quietly\n5. Why is Anna happy?\na.\t\nShe will be lost in the woods. \nb.\t\nAnna will act as a tree. \nc.\t\nShe will play in the trees. \nd.\t\nAnna will help with costumes.\n3. What should Anna do? \na.\t\nWalk more quickly and loudly \nb.\t\nMove loudly \nc.\t\nWalk faster \nd.\t\nMove more slowly and quietly\nBreathing to Speak More Loudly","guide":{"id":40,"focus":"연기와 발표를 하며 말하는 방식을 배워요.","grammar":"slowly, loudly, quietly처럼 -ly로 끝나는 말은 동작하는 방식을 알려줘요.","mission":"같은 문장을 크게·작게·천천히 세 번 읽어 보세요.","example":"Please speak slowly.","exampleKo":"천천히 말해 주세요."}},{"id":41,"startPage":460,"endPage":472,"topics":"Asking for & giving feedback about job performance Identifying ways to improve performance at work or school Interpreting advice","strategy":"Focus","goals":"Grammar: future real conditional (if clauses) Speaking: sentences that include the words “if” and “will.” Pronunciation: pronouncing contrastive stress","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi. I am walking to work. Today my boss will tell me what she thinks of my work. Is it good? Or is it bad? Okay, time for work. I am going right now. Okay, okay, I’m going! Ms. Weaver: Anna, hello.","ko":"안녕. 나는 일을 걷고있다. 오늘 내 보스가 내 작품의 생각을 말해 줄 것입니다. 그것은 좋은가요? 아니면 나쁜가요? 잘, 직장 시간. 나는 지금 바로 갈거야. 괜찮아, 괜찮아, 나는 갈거야! Ms. Weaver : Anna, hello."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello. Ms. Weaver: Sit down. As you know, at the start of a new year we have a work review.","ko":"안녕하세요. Ms. Weaver: Sit down. 아시다시피, 새해 시작부터 우리는 작업 검토가 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes. It’s time for mine. Ms. Weaver: Yes. Anna, this chart shows the audience of The Time Traveling Treehouse. If you look at it, you will see something bad. Your audience is going down, down, DOWN!","ko":"예. 그것은 광산 시간입니다. Ms. Weaver : 예. Anna,이 차트는 The Time Traveling Treehouse의 청중을 보여줍니다. 당신이 그것을 보면, 당신은 나쁜 것을 볼 수 있습니다. 당신의 청중은 아래로, 아래로, DOWN!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Ms. Weaver, I think the chart is upside down.","ko":"Ms. Weaver, 나는 차트가 아래로 올라 있다고 생각합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Here, let’s flip that around. Now, it’s right-side up. Ms. Weaver: Oh. If you look at this chart, you will see something good. Your audience is big.","ko":"여기, 그 주위에 플립 할 수 있습니다. 지금, 그것은 오른쪽입니다. Ms. Weaver: Oh. 이 차트를 보면 좋은 무언가를 볼 수 있습니다. 당신의 청중은 커다란 것입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Good! Ms. Weaver: But not big enough.","ko":"좋은! Ms. 웨버 : 그러나 충분히 크지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Not good. Ms. Weaver: I want to see these numbers go up, and up, and UP!","ko":"좋은. Ms. 웨버: 나는이 숫자가 올라갈 것을보고 싶다, 그리고 위로!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"How? Ms. Weaver: I have something -- idea posters!","ko":"어떻게? Ms. 웨버: 나는 뭔가가 -- 아이디어 포스터!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"(whispers) Idea posters. Ms. Weaver: You really ought to think seriously about them. I like this one. Please read it.","ko":"(whispers) 아이디어 포스터. Ms. 웨버 : 당신은 정말 그들에게 심각한 생각을하지 않습니다. 나는 이것을 좋아한다. 그것을 읽으십시오."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"“If at first you SUCCEED; you will be a success.” Well, it’s a cute cat. Ms. Weaver: Here’s another one. I like it.","ko":"“최초에 당신은 성공할 것입니다..” 글쎄, 그것은 귀여운 고양이입니다. 마법사 : 여기에 또 다른 것. 나는 그것을 좋아한다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"“WORKING HARD looks hard because it really is hard.” I see. It’s another cute cat. Ms. Weaver: This is my favorite.","ko":"“WORKING HARD는 정말 어렵기 때문에 열심히 봅니다.” 나는 볼 수 있습니다. 그것은 또 다른 귀여운 고양이입니다. 마법사 : 이것은 내 마음에 드는 것입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"“TEAMWORK works best with a team.” A team of cats. Look at all those cats! Ms. Weaver: So, Anna, do you understand what I want?","ko":"\"TEAMWORK는 팀과 잘 작동합니다.\" 고양이의 팀. 모든 고양이를 봐! Ms. Weaver : So, Anna, 내가 원하는 것을 이해합니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes, Ms. Weaver. I understand.","ko":"예, Ms. 웨버. 나는 이해."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Okay, team. There is a problem in the Treehouse.","ko":"괜찮아, 팀. 트리 하우스에 문제가 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"Problem? What’s the problem?","ko":"문제? 문제가 무엇입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Our audience is big.","ko":"우리의 청중은 커다란."},{"speaker":"Bryan","en":"But that’s a good thing.","ko":"그러나 그것은 좋은 일입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No, it is not big enough.","ko":"아니, 그것은 충분히 크지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Please don’t worry. I know what Ms. Weaver wants. Here’s the plan. (whispers)","ko":"걱정하지 마세요. Ms. Weaver가 원하는 것을 알고 있습니다. 여기 플랜입니다. (whispers)"},{"speaker":"Bryan","en":"Is that what she wants?","ko":"그녀는 무엇을 원합니까? 영어 수업을 배우자 41 467"},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"Are you sure?","ko":"당신은 확실합니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes. Let’s get to work!","ko":"예. 일할 수 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Good job, team. This is exactly what Ms. Weaver wants!","ko":"좋은 일, 팀. 이것은 정확히 무엇 Ms입니다. 웨버 원!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Welcome to The Time Traveling Treehouse! Today you will learn about a very popular pet … cats!","ko":"The Time Traveling Treehouse에 오신 것을 환영합니다! 오늘 당신은 매우 인기있는 애완 동물에 대해 배울 것입니다 ... 고양이!"},{"speaker":"MINDY","en":"Anna. Did I give you enough cats?","ko":"Anna. 나는 당신에게 충분한 고양이를주었습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I don’t know, MINDY. I think we need more cats!","ko":"나는 몰랐다, MINDY. 나는 더 많은 고양이를 필요로 생각한다!"}],"words":[{"en":"audience","definition":"the people who watch, read, or listen to something","ko":"관객"},{"en":"cat","definition":"a small animal that is related to lions and tigers and that is often kept by people as a pet","ko":"고양이"},{"en":"chart","definition":"information in the form of a table or a diagram","ko":"도표"},{"en":"cute","definition":"having a pleasing and usually youthful appearance","ko":"귀여운"},{"en":"exactly","definition":"used to stress that something is accurate, complete, or correct","ko":"정확히"},{"en":"flip","definition":"to cause (something) to turn or turn over quickly","ko":"뒤집다"},{"en":"meow","definition":"to make a crying sound as cats do","ko":"야옹"},{"en":"pet","definition":"an animal (such as a dog, cat, bird, or fish) that people keep mainly for pleasure","ko":"반려동물"},{"en":"poster","definition":"a usually large picture that is put on walls as a decoration","ko":"포스터"},{"en":"review","definition":"an act of carefully looking at or examining the quality or condition of something or someone right-side up - noun phrase. with the top or correct side facing up","ko":"검토하다"},{"en":"succeed","definition":"to do what you are trying to do or to achieve the correct or desired result","ko":"성공하다"},{"en":"success","definition":"a person or thing that succeeds","ko":"성공"},{"en":"teamwork","definition":"the work done by people who work together as a team to do something","ko":"팀워크"},{"en":"upside down","definition":"in such a way that the upper and the lower parts are reversed in position","ko":"거꾸로"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 41 - Teamwork Works Best With a \nTeam\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. Why is Anna nervous on her way \nto work today?\na.\t\nHer boss is going to talk about her \nwork today.\nb.\t\nAnna is a little late to work today.\nc.\t\nHer boss is angry at her.\nd.\t\nAnna made a mistake at work \nyesterday.\n3. What advice is on Ms. Weaver’s \nposters?\na.\t\nBe a success.\nb.\t\nWork hard.\nc.\t\nWork with a team.\nd.\t\nThe posters say all of these things.\n2. What does Ms. Weaver say \nhappens at the beginning of a new \nyear?\na.\t\nShe gives more work to Anna.\nb.\t\nShe reviews Anna’s work.\nc.\t\nShe changes workers’ desks.\nd.\t\nShe has a change of mind.\n4. What does Anna say about the \ntree house?\na.\t\nThe audience is not big enough.\nb.\t\nThe team doesn’t think.\nc.\t\nThe audience is going down.\nd.\t\nThe team makes problems.\n3. What does Ms. Weaver say about \nAnna’s audience?\na.\t\nAnna is doing something bad.\nb.\t\nHer audience is feeling down.\nc.\t\nHer audience is going down.\nd.\t\nAnna should look at her audience.","guide":{"id":41,"focus":"팀으로 협력하며 조건을 말해요.","grammar":"If it rains, we will stay home처럼 if 뒤에 조건, will 뒤에 결과를 말해요.","mission":"팀 활동에서 맡을 역할을 정하고 조건문을 만들어 보세요.","example":"Teamwork works best with a team.","exampleKo":"팀워크는 함께할 때 가장 잘돼요."}},{"id":42,"startPage":473,"endPage":486,"topics":"Describing ongoing past activities Asking about past events Giving information about past events Describing a sequence of events","strategy":"Read Between the Lines","goals":"Grammar: reﬂexive pronouns; while-clauses; past continuous tense Speaking: reﬂexive pronouns: herself, ourselves, and yourself Pronunciation: pronouncing /didjə/","conversation":[{"speaker":"Guy","en":"Hello. I’m Guy Newsman with News Channel XYZ. I’m here in Washington, D.C. at the scene of a crime. We are talking with this woman. She saw the crime during her lunch break. It looks like she hurt herself while she was trying to stop the crime. Tell us your name.","ko":"안녕하세요. 저는 News Channel XYZ와 함께 Guy Newsman입니다. 저는 워싱턴 D.C.에서 범죄 장면입니다. 우리는이 여자와 이야기하고 있습니다. 그녀는 그녀의 점심 휴식 동안 범죄를 보았습니다. 그녀는 범죄를 중지하려고하면서 그녀와 같이 상처를 입었습니다. 귀하의 이름을 알려줍니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi, Guy. I’m Anna.","ko":"안녕, 얘들 아. 나는 안나."},{"speaker":"Guy","en":"Anna, what did you see and what happened to your arm?","ko":"안나, 당신이 보고 무슨 일이 당신의 팔에 무슨 일이 있었습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Guy, I was minding my own business. See, I work over there.","ko":"얘들 아, 나는 내 자신의 사업을 염두에두고 있었다. 참조, 나는 거기에서 일."},{"speaker":"Guy","en":"Um-hum","ko":"우메후엠"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I left work to get some lunch. Then suddenly, I heard a woman yelling. She was yelling like this ... “Help! Help!”","ko":"나는 약간의 점심을 얻게 작업을 떠났다. 그런 다음 갑자기, 나는 여자를 들었다. 그녀는 이것을 좋아했다. \"도움말! 도와주세요!\""},{"speaker":"Guy","en":"Um-hum","ko":"우메후엠"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Two robbers were grabbing her bag like this. She was hitting them with her umbrella.","ko":"두 robbers was grabbing 그녀의 백 같은 이. 그녀는 그녀의 우산으로 그들을 타격했다."},{"speaker":"Guy","en":"Is that when you hurt your arm?","ko":"당신은 당신의 팔을 아프릴 때?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No. At that time, I was not fighting the robbers.","ko":"아니. 그 시간에, 나는 강도를 싸우지 않았다."},{"speaker":"Guy","en":"Um-hum.","ko":"움푹신한"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"See. I was too far away and I didn’t have my own umbrella.","ko":"참고. 나는 너무 멀리 있었고 나는 내 자신의 우산을 가지고 있지 않았다."},{"speaker":"Guy","en":"So, what happened next?","ko":"그럼, 다음 일이 있었습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"They grabbed her bag and ran away! So, I grabbed her umbrella and ran after the robbers.","ko":"그들은 그녀의 가방을 잡고 멀리 ran! 그래서, 나는 그녀의 우산을 잡고 강도 후 ran을 잡아."},{"speaker":"Guy","en":"Then that is the time that you hurt your arm?","ko":"그런 다음 팔을 아프는 시간입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No. I was yelling, “Stop, robbers! Stop!” She was yelling, “Hey, come back with my umbrella!”","ko":"아니. 나는 너희에게 이르렀다, “정지, 강도! 정지!” 그녀는 너희에게 이르렀다, “그녀, 내 우산으로 돌아가라!”"},{"speaker":"Guy","en":"Were you afraid?","ko":"당신을 두려워?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I had no time to be afraid, Guy. Well, I had time while I was resting on a bench. I had a lot of time.","ko":"나는 두려워 할 시간이 없었다, 남자. 잘, 나는 벤치에 앉아있는 동안 시간을했다. 나는 많은 시간을했다."},{"speaker":"Guy","en":"Then what happened?","ko":"그런 다음 무슨 일이 있었습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"The robbers got on a bus. So, I ran after the bus.","ko":"겉옷은 버스에 도착했습니다. 그래서, 나는 버스 후에 ran."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"While I was running, I tripped and fell.","ko":"내가 달리는 동안, 나는 여행하고 떨어졌다."},{"speaker":"Guy","en":"And that is the time that you hurt your arm?","ko":"그리고 당신은 당신의 팔을 아프는 시간입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No. While I was lying on the ground, someone stepped on my arm!","ko":"아니. 나는 땅에 lying 동안, 내 팔에 걸린 누군가!"},{"speaker":"Guy","en":"Ouch. That’s too bad.","ko":"너무 나쁘다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yeah. And they didn’t apologize. Well, then the robbers got themselves kicked off the bus.","ko":"그래. 그리고 그들은 apologize하지 않았다. 글쎄, 그 후 robbers는 스스로 버스를 쫓았다."},{"speaker":"Guy","en":"Why?","ko":"왜?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"They didn’t pay. You’ve got to pay when you get on a bus. The police came and took them away.","ko":"그들은 지불하지 않았다. 당신은 당신이 버스에 도착했을 때 지불해야합니다. 경찰이 와서 멀리했다."},{"speaker":"Guy","en":"And that’s when you hurt your arm!","ko":"그리고 팔을 마칠 때입니다! 영어 수업 42 477을 배우십시오."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No.","ko":"아니요."},{"speaker":"Guy","en":"Then, when did you hurt yourself?","ko":"그때, 당신은 자신을 아프었을 때?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well, Guy, by this time, I was feeling very hungry. So, I went to my office to get a snack.","ko":"글쎄, 얘들 아, 이 시간, 나는 아주 배고픈 느낌이었다. 그래서, 나는 내 사무실에 가서 간식을 얻을."},{"speaker":"Ms Weaver","en":"Anna, I’m calling for help right now. (on the phone) Hello? Yes, please come right away. My co-worker is stuck in a vending machine.","ko":"Anna, 나는 지금 당장 도움을 요청합니다. (전화) 안녕하세요? 예, 오른쪽으로 오십시오. 내 공동 작업자는 자동 판매기에 갇혀 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Guy","en":"You hurt your arm in a vending machine buying a bag of chips?","ko":"당신은 칩의 부대를 사는 자동 판매기에 있는 당신의 팔을 어둡니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I was really hungry and the bag was stuck. I had to -","ko":"나는 정말 배고픈 가방이 붙어 있었다. 나는 -"},{"speaker":"Guy","en":"That’s all from News Channel XYZ. This is Guy Newsman saying goodbye.","ko":"그것은 뉴스 채널 XYZ에서 모두. 이것은 Guy Newsman 말하는 goodbye입니다."},{"speaker":"Guy","en":"Okay, we have to find ourselves another story, guys.","ko":"그래, 우리는 다른 이야기, 녀석을 찾아야합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Until next time! Hi Mom!!","ko":"다음 시간까지! 안녕 엄마!!"}],"words":[{"en":"arm","definition":"either one of the two long body parts that join the top of your body at the shoulder and that end at the hand or wrist","ko":"팔"},{"en":"chips","definition":"thin, hard, and usually salty pieces of food","ko":"감자칩"},{"en":"crime","definition":"an illegal act for which someone can be punished by the government","ko":"범죄"},{"en":"fall (past tense: fell)","definition":"to come or go down suddenly from a standing position","ko":"넘어지다·넘어졌다"},{"en":"grab","definition":"(past participle: grabbing) to quickly take and hold (someone or something) with your hand or arms","ko":"움켜잡다"},{"en":"ground","definition":"the soil that is on or under the surface of the earth","ko":"땅"},{"en":"kick off","definition":"(past tense: kicked off) force (someone) to leave","ko":"시작되다"},{"en":"lie","definition":"(gerund: lying) to be in a flat position on a surface minding my own business - idiom. doing what you normally do and not bothering anyone","ko":"눕다"},{"en":"robber","definition":"a criminal who steals money or property or a thief who robs people","ko":"강도"},{"en":"snack","definition":"a small amount of food eaten between meals","ko":"간식"},{"en":"step","definition":"to put your foot down — usually + in or on","ko":"발을 내딛다"},{"en":"stuck","definition":"difficult or impossible to move from a position","ko":"꼼짝 못 하는"},{"en":"trip","definition":"(past tense: tripped) to fall or nearly by accidentally hitting your foot on something as you are walking or running","ko":"걸려 넘어지다"},{"en":"umbrella","definition":"a device that is used for protection from the rain and sun","ko":"우산"},{"en":"vending machine","definition":"a machine that you put money into in order to buy food or drinks","ko":"자판기"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 42 - I Was Minding My Own Business\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. Why does the reporter want to talk \nwith Anna?\na.\t\nHe wants to learn about Washington \nDC.\nb.\t\nShe was the victim of a crime.\nc.\t\nHe wants to find out how she hurt her\narm.\nd.\t\nShe was watching the police stop a \ncrime.\n5. What did Anna do?\na.\t\nAnna hit the robbers with an umbrella.\nb.\t\nShe grabbed the robbers and ran with\n them.\nc.\t\nAnna took the woman’s umbrella and \nran.\nd.\t\nShe grabbed the woman’s bag and \nran away.\n2. What was happening to the woman?\na.\t\nShe was taking Anna’s umbrella.\nb.\t\nTwo robbers were taking her bag.\nc.\t\nShe was taking a bag from Anna.\nd.\t\nTwo robbers were hitting her.\n6. When did Anna have time to be\nafraid?\na.\t\nWhen she was running after the \nrobbers.\nb.\t\nAfter the robbers took the bag.\nc.\t\nWhen she was resting on the bench.\nd.\t\nBefore she went back to work.\n3. What strategy is Guy using when he \nasks, “Is that when you hurt your \narm?”\na.\t\nPersonalize\nb.\t\nCooperate\nc.\t\nUse Selective Listening\nd.\t\nRead Between the Lines\n7. Why did Anna fall?\na.\t\nAnna fell off of the bus.\nb.\t\nShe was getting on a bus quickly.\nc.\t\nThe bus ran into Anna.\nd.\t\nShe tripped while she was chasing \nthe robbers.\n4. Why could the robbers run away from \nAnna?\na.\t\nShe was too far away and didn’t have \nher umbrella.\nb.\t\nThe robbers hurt her arm.\nc.\t\nShe was too afraid of them and it was \nraining.\nd.\t\nThe robbers took her umbrella.\n8. How did Anna hurt herself?\na.\t\nAnna tripped and fell on a bag of \nchips.\nb.\t\nShe was trying to get a bag of chips\nfrom a machine.\nc.\t\nAnna fell when she was going back to\nwork.\nd.\t\nShe was helping Ms. Weaver move a \nvending machine.","guide":{"id":42,"focus":"지나가던 상황과 사건을 설명해요.","grammar":"was/were + 동사-ing는 과거에 진행 중이던 행동을 나타내요. while은 ‘~하는 동안’이에요.","mission":"어떤 일이 일어났을 때 무엇을 하고 있었는지 말해 보세요.","example":"I was minding my own business.","exampleKo":"저는 그냥 제 할 일을 하고 있었어요."}},{"id":43,"startPage":487,"endPage":497,"topics":"Polite requests Expressing past and future ability and obligation","strategy":"Use what you know","goals":"Grammar: Modal verbs Speaking: Modal verbs “would” and “could” Pronunciation: Informal pronunciation with “what are you” and “would you”","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hey there! Tonight, I am teaching my ukulele class. It is far away. So, I am going to ride the Metro. Oh, no! I lost my wallet! It has my Metro card, my credit card and my money! Oh, no!","ko":"안녕하세요! 오늘 밤, 나는 ukulele 클래스를 가르치고 있습니다. 그것은 멀리 떨어져 있습니다. 그래서, 나는 메트로를 타고 가고있다. 오, 아니! 나는 내 지갑을 잃었다! 그것은 내 메트로 카드, 내 신용 카드와 내 돈이 있습니다! 오, 아니!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"It’s times like this I remember my father’s important words. He said, “Anna, never … ” No wait, “Always have emergency money.” .” (Anna pulls an envelope out of her bag and looks inside) It’s empty. Time for Plan B. ‘Extra Emergency Money.’ (Anna pulls another envelope out of her bag and looks inside)","ko":"그것은 내가 아버지의 중요한 단어를 기억 같은 시간입니다. 그는 말했다, \"Anna, 결코 ... \" 기다리지 않고, \"Always는 비상 돈을 가지고있다.\" . (Anna는 그녀의 가방에서 봉투를 꺼내 내부에서 볼 수 있습니다) 빈입니다. 계획 B를위한 시간. 'Extra Emergency Money.' (Anna는 가방에서 다른 봉투를 끌어 내고 내부를 볼 수 있습니다)"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No! It’s empty too! Anna, it’s time for Plan C.","ko":"아니! 그것은 너무 비어있다! 안나, 그것은 계획 C에 대한 시간입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi, Marsha!","ko":"안녕, 마샤!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Hi Anna. What’s up?","ko":"안녕 안나. 뭐죠?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I’m stuck downtown without any money. Would you be able to come downtown? Please?","ko":"어떤 돈없이 시내에 갇혀있다. 당신은 시내에 갈 수 있습니까? 제발?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Anna, I can’t. I’m too busy. I have to give a big presentation in one hour. Sorry!","ko":"Anna, 나는 할 수 없습니다. 나는 너무 바빴습니다. 나는 1 시간에서 큰 프리젠 테이션을 제공해야합니다. 죄송합니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"That’s ok. Good luck with your presentation!","ko":"그게 ok입니다. 당신의 프리젠 테이션에 행운을 빌어요!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Thanks!","ko":"감사합니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Time for Plan D.","ko":"계획 D. 시간."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi, Jonathan! How’s it going?","ko":"안녕, Jonathan! 어떻게 가고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Hey, Anna. Things are great. What’s up?","ko":"안녕, 안나. 것들이 훌륭합니다. 무엇일까요?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well, I was wondering if you could give me some money.","ko":"글쎄, 나는 당신이 나에게 돈을 줄 수 있다면 궁금해했다."},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"What?","ko":"이름 *"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"See, I lost my wallet and I’m stuck downtown and I --","ko":"참고, 나는 내 지갑을 잃고 나는 시내를 갇혀있다 --"},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Anna, I wish I could. I’m at the airport with my mother. Her flight leaves in two hours.","ko":"Anna, 나는 할 수 있기를 바랍니다. 나는 나의 어머니와 공항에 있습니다. 그녀의 비행은 2 시간 동안 나뉩니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"That’s okay. Tell your Mom to have a nice trip!","ko":"그게 괜찮아. 좋은 여행을해야 할 엄마를 말하십시오!"},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"I do wish I could help. Thanks.","ko":"나는 도움을 줄 수 있기를 바랍니다. 감사합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"‘Bye.","ko":"‘Bye.’에 대하여"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This is serious. Time for … Plan E.","ko":"이것은 심각합니다. 시간 ... 계획 E."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Hello.","ko":"안녕하세요."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi, Ashley! What are you doing?","ko":"안녕, 애슐리! 당신은 무엇을하고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Oh! Hi Anna!","ko":"오! 안녕 안나!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"(Anna hears a child crying through the phone.) Ashley, I was wondering, uh, would you be able to come downtown? And could you give me $20?","ko":"(안나는 전화를 통해 울고 아이들을 듣습니다.) 애슐리, 나는 경이롭고, 당신은 시내를 갈 수있을 것입니까? 그리고 당신은 저에게 $20를 줄 수 있었습니까?"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Anna, I can’t.","ko":"Anna, 나는 할 수 없습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I’ll pay you back the money. I promise.","ko":"나는 돈을 지불합니다. 나는 약속합니다."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Anna, I’m not worried about the money. I’m babysitting. (off-camera to niece) That was very, very, bad!","ko":"Anna, 나는 돈에 대해 걱정하지 않습니다. 나는 babysitting입니다. (off-camera to niece) 그것은 매우, 나쁜! 영어 수업을 배우자 43 490"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well, losing your wallet is bad, but it’s not the end of the world, Ashley.","ko":"잘, 지갑을 잃는 것은 나쁘다, 하지만 그것은 세계의 끝이 아닙니다, 애슐리."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"I was talking to my niece, Anna.","ko":"나는 내 niece, 안나에 이야기했다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well, thanks anyway, Ashley!","ko":"잘, 어쨌든 감사합니다, 애슐리!"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Good luck getting money.","ko":"좋은 행운을 얻 돈."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Good luck babysitting!","ko":"행운을 빌어 요!"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Thanks.","ko":"감사합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well, Plans A, B, C, D and E did not work. Think, Anna, think. Time for Plan F.","ko":"글쎄, 계획 A, B, C, D 및 E는 작동하지 않았다. 생각, 안나, 생각. 계획 F에 대한 시간."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"(singing) Won’t you give, could -- Thank you very much, sir! -- would you give me money, won’t you give -- Thank you very much! -- could you give, won’t you give me money -- until next time! -- won’t you give me money?","ko":"(singing) 당신이 줄 수 없습니다, 할 수 없습니다 -- 대단히 감사합니다, 사이! -- 당신은 나에게 돈을 주지 않을 것입니다, 당신에게 제공하지 않을 것입니다 -- 대단히 감사합니다! -- 당신이 줄 수, 다음 시간까지 나에게 돈을 주지 않을 것입니다! -- 당신은 나에게 돈을 주지 않을거야? 영어 레슨을하자 43 491"}],"words":[{"en":"airport","definition":"a place where aircraft land and take off and where there are buildings for passengers to wait in and for aircraft to be sheltered","ko":"공항"},{"en":"babysit","definition":"to take care of a child while the child’s parents are away","ko":"아이를 돌보다"},{"en":"could","definition":"verb. used in speech to make a polite request or suggestion","ko":"~할 수 있다"},{"en":"downtown","definition":"to, toward, or in the main or central part of a city or town","ko":"시내"},{"en":"emergency","definition":"an unexpected and usually dangerous situation that calls for immediate action","ko":"긴급상황"},{"en":"empty","definition":"containing nothing","ko":"빈"},{"en":"flight","definition":"a journey on an airplane","ko":"항공편"},{"en":"presentation","definition":"an activity in which someone shows, describes, or explains something to a group of people","ko":"발표"},{"en":"wallet","definition":"a small folding case that holds paper money or credit cards","ko":"지갑"},{"en":"without","definition":"not having or including (something)","ko":"~없이"},{"en":"wonder","definition":"to have interest in knowing or learning something","ko":"궁금해하다"},{"en":"worried","definition":"feeling or showing fear and concern because you think that something bad has happened or could happen","ko":"걱정하는"},{"en":"would","definition":"verb. used to ask a polite question or to make a polite request, offer, or invitation","ko":"~할 것이다"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 43 - Time for Plan B\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Anna remember?\na.\t\nThe words of her father\nb.\t\nTo call her father\nc.\t\nTo bring emergency money\nd.\t\nHer father’s wallet\n4. What does Jonathan have to do? \na.\t\nHelp a friend get to the airport \nb.\t\nWait with his mother at the airport \nc.\t\nGo on a trip with his mother \nd.\t\nTake Anna to the airport \n2. What is Marsha’s answer to Anna’s \nquestion?\na.\t\nShe is not able to give Anna money.\nb.\t\nMarsha must present at work soon.\nc.\t\nShe will go downtown to help Anna.\nd.\t\nMarsha is listening to the television.\n5. What strategy is Anna using when \nshe plays her ukulele?\na.\t\nUse Selective Attention\nb.\t\nSummarize\nc.\t\nUse What You Know\nd.\t\nFocus\n3. What does Ashley tell Anna?\na.\t\nAnna is a very bad friend.\nb.\t\nAshley lost her wallet, too.\nc.\t\nShe is worried about money.\nd.\t\nAshley is watching her niece.","guide":{"id":43,"focus":"문제가 생겼을 때 대안을 찾아요.","grammar":"could, would는 가능성이나 정중한 부탁에 사용해요. Could you~?는 ‘~해 주실 수 있나요?’예요.","mission":"계획이 어긋났을 때 다른 방법을 제안해 보세요.","example":"Could you help me?","exampleKo":"저를 도와주실 수 있나요?"}},{"id":44,"startPage":498,"endPage":507,"topics":"Nutrition Food Choices","strategy":"Classify","goals":"Grammar: Modals Speaking: “Mustn’t” and “don’t have to” Pronunciation: “Mustn’t”","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi there, Ashley!","ko":"안녕하세요, 애슐리!"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Anna! Hi! Where are you going? (Anna’s stomach growls loudly)","ko":"Anna! 안녕하세요! 어디 가고 있습니까? (Anna의 위장은 크게 성장합니다)"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"What was that?","ko":"그 이유는 무엇입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I’m hungry. When I’m hungry, I only want to eat junk food! But I know I should eat healthy food. So, I fight with myself. One side says, ‘You should eat healthy food.’ The other side says, ‘But I want to eat junk food!’","ko":"나는 배고프다. 내가 배고프다 때, 나는 단지 정크 음식을 먹고 싶어! 그러나 나는 건강한 음식을 먹어야한다. 그래서, 나는 나 자신과 싸울. 한쪽은 말한다, '당신은 건강한 음식을 먹어야한다.’ 다른 쪽은 말한다, '그러나 나는 정크 음식을 먹고 싶다!'"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Well, Anna, go to the Giant supermarket. You should be able to find all kinds of food there - for all of you.","ko":"글쎄, Anna, Giant 슈퍼마켓으로 이동합니다. 모든 종류의 음식을 찾을 수 있어야합니다 - 당신을 위해."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Good idea, Ashley. See you later!","ko":"좋은 아이디어, 애슐리. 나중에 보자!"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"‘Bye, Anna.","ko":"'Bye, 안나."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Wow! This supermarket is huge! Look at all of these fruits and vegetables! I should eat more vegetables.","ko":"와우! 이 슈퍼마켓은 거대! 이 과일과 야채 모두 봐! 나는 더 많은 야채를 먹어야한다."},{"speaker":"Healthy","en":"* Good idea, Anna. You must eat more vegetables … like celery!","ko":"* 좋은 아이디어, 안나. 당신은 더 많은 야채를 먹어야한다 ... 셀러리처럼!"},{"speaker":"Junky","en":"* Celery?! Do you know what the web says about celery?","ko":"* Celery?! 웹이 유명 인사에 대해 무엇을 알고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No, what?","ko":"아니, 무엇?"},{"speaker":"Junky","en":"“Celery is 95 percent water - 100 percent NOT ice cream.” I love the web! Healthy*: Anna, you mustn’t eat junk food. Junk food will kill you. Junky*: You are being silly.","ko":"\"Celery는 95 %의 물 - 100 %의 아이스크림이 아닙니다. 나는 웹을 좋아합니다! 건강한 * : Anna, 당신은 정크 음식을 먹지 않아야합니다. Junk 음식은 당신을 죽일 것입니다. Junky * : 실리입니다."},{"speaker":"Healthy","en":"No, you are!","ko":"아니, 당신은!"},{"speaker":"Junky","en":"No, you are.","ko":"아니, 당신은."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Will you two please be nice to each other? It is important to eat healthy foods. But, a little junk food will not kill me. Hmm, ice cream. Ice cream does sound good.","ko":"두 가지가 서로 좋을 것입니까? 건강한 음식을 먹는 것이 중요합니다. 그러나 작은 정크 음식은 나를 죽이지 않을 것입니다. Hmm, 아이스크림. 아이스크림은 소리가 좋습니다."},{"speaker":"Junky","en":"Take this cart to the frozen food aisle!","ko":"냉동 식품에 이 카트를 가져 가라!"},{"speaker":"Healthy","en":"No wait, go back! Go back! We forgot fruit. Go back!!","ko":"기다리지 말고 다시 가자! 우리는 과일을 잊었다. 다시 가자!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Okay, we are in the frozen food aisle!","ko":"잘, 우리는 냉동 식품 aisle에 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Junky","en":"Mmm, ice cream!","ko":"Mmm, 아이스크림!"},{"speaker":"Healthy","en":"Mmm, frozen peas!","ko":"Mmm, 언 페라!"},{"speaker":"Junky","en":"Nobody says, ‘Mmm, frozen peas. They say, ‘Mmm, ice cream!","ko":"Nobody 말한다, 'Mmm, 냉동 완두. 그들은 말한다, 'Mmm, 아이스크림!"},{"speaker":"Healthy","en":"Mmm, frozen peas!!","ko":"Mmm, 언 페라!!"},{"speaker":"Junky","en":"Mmm, ice cream!!","ko":"Mmm, 아이스크림!!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I am not going to tell you two again! Stop fighting!","ko":"나는 다시 당신에게 두 말을하지 않습니다! 싸움을 멈추십시오!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I smell fresh bread! I love the smells of a bakery!","ko":"나는 신선한 빵 냄새! 나는 베이커리의 냄새를 좋아합니다!"},{"speaker":"Healthy","en":"Oh, Anna, let’s buy a fresh loaf of whole wheat, organic bread!","ko":"오, 안나, 전체 밀, 유기 빵의 신선한 loaf를 살 수 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Junky","en":"You don’t have to buy bread. Buy some donuts, Anna!","ko":"빵을 살 필요가 없습니다. 몇 가지 도넛, 안나를 구입하십시오!"},{"speaker":"Healthy","en":"You mustn’t buy donuts. They are only fat and sugar.","ko":"당신은 도넛을 구입하지 않습니다. 그들은 단지 지방과 설탕입니다."},{"speaker":"Junky","en":"Exactly! You know, you are really no fun at all.","ko":"정확히! 당신은 알고, 당신은 정말 전혀 재미 없습니다. 영어 레슨을 배울하자 44 501"},{"speaker":"Healthy","en":"And you must think having high cholesterol is fun.","ko":"그리고 당신은 높은 콜레스테롤을 가지고 생각해야합니다."},{"speaker":"Junky","en":"Everyone likes donuts! That is why you don’t have friends!","ko":"모두가 donuts를 좋아한다! 그것은 당신이 친구를하지 않는 이유입니다!"},{"speaker":"Healthy","en":"And that is why your cholesterol is so high!","ko":"그리고 왜 당신의 콜레스테롤이 너무 높다!"},{"speaker":"Junky","en":"My cholesterol is none of your business!!","ko":"내 콜레스테롤은 당신의 사업의 아무도 없다!"},{"speaker":"Healthy","en":"And I have lots of friends!!","ko":"그리고 나는 친구를 많이 가지고!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Stop it! Stop it! Stop it! I am sick and tired of the both of you!!","ko":"중지! 그것을 중지! 중지! 나는 당신이 둘 다 아프고 피곤!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I know what you two need!","ko":"나는 당신이 두 가지 필요 알고!"},{"speaker":"Junky","en":"Anna! What are you doing?","ko":"Anna! 당신은 무엇을하고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Healthy","en":"Put me down!","ko":"나를 아래로 넣으십시오!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"You two need to cool off!","ko":"당신은 두 가지가 꺼져 있어야합니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I am going to go buy my healthy food and my junk food! Good bye!","ko":"나는 내 건강 한 음식과 내 정크 음식을 사려고! 좋은 bye!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Until next time … * Note: “Healthy” and “Junky” are Anna’s thoughts about what she should eat.","ko":"다음 시간까지 ... * 참고 : \"건강한\"및 \"준키\"는 Anna 's thoughts about what she should eat. 을 배울 수 있습니다 영어 레슨 44 502"}],"words":[{"en":"aisle","definition":"a passage where people walk through a store or market","ko":"통로"},{"en":"bakery","definition":"a place where bread, cakes, cookies, and other baked foods are made or sold","ko":"빵집"},{"en":"cart","definition":"(shopping cart) a metal basket on wheels used to hold groceries while you are shopping","ko":"수레"},{"en":"cholesterol","definition":"a substance that is found in the bodies of people and animals, a high percentage raises the risk of coronary heart disease","ko":"콜레스테롤"},{"en":"cool off","definition":"to become calm after a period of anger or conflict","ko":"식히다"},{"en":"fat","definition":"an oily solid or liquid substance in food","ko":"지방"},{"en":"freeze","definition":"to become a hard substance (such as ice) because of cold (past participle: frozen)","ko":"얼다"},{"en":"healthy","definition":"good for your health or healthful","ko":"건강한"},{"en":"junk food","definition":"food that is not good for your health because it contains high amounts of fat or sugar","ko":"정크푸드"},{"en":"kill","definition":"to cause the death of (a person, animal, or plant)","ko":"죽이다"},{"en":"must","definition":"verb. used to say that something is required or necessary","ko":"~해야 한다"},{"en":"organic","definition":"food that is grown or made without the use of artificial chemicals","ko":"유기농의"},{"en":"smell","definition":"the quality of a thing that you can sense with your nose","ko":"냄새 맡다"},{"en":"smell","definition":"to use your nose to sense smells","ko":"냄새"},{"en":"sugar","definition":"a sweet substance usually in the form of white or brown crystals or white powder that comes from plants and is used to make foods sweeter","ko":"설탕"},{"en":"whole wheat","definition":"made from wheat from which no part (such as the bran) has been removed","ko":"통밀"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 44 - Making Healthy Choices\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Anna say about the \ntimes she is hungry?\na.\t\nShe usually eats healthy foods.\nb.\t\nTwo sides of her tell her to eat healthy \nfood.\nc.\t\nShe never wants to eat junk food.\nd.\t\nTwo sides of her fight about what to \neat.\n4. What does Anna say to Junky and \nHealthy? \na.\t Healthy and junky foods are the same.\nb.\t It is important to eat healthy foods, but \nsome junk food is ok.\nc.\t Will you two be nice to me?\nd.\t I know that junk food will kill me, so I \nonly eat healthy food.\n2. What does Anna’s healthy side \nsay?\na.\t\nHealthy says “You mustn’t eat junk \nfood!”\nb.\t\nShe says that Anna doesn’t have to eat \ncelery.\nc.\t\nHealthy say that Anna should eat more \ncelery.\nd.\t\nShe says that there are many good \nvegetables.\n5. Why does Healthy want to go \nback? \na.\t\nHealthy wants Anna to buy ice cream.\nb.\t\nShe thinks Anna should look for peas.\nc.\t\nHealthy wants Anna to buy some fruit.\nd.\t\nShe wants Anna to buy more \nvegetables.\n3. What does Junky say about celery?\na.\t\nShe says that ice cream is better than \ncelery.\nb.\t\nJunky says that she learned to love \ncelery.\nc.\t\nShe says that people on the web like \ncelery.\nd.\t\nJunky says that it has 95% water and \nno ice cream.\n6. What statement means the same \nas “You mustn’t buy donuts”?  \na.\t\nYou really ought to buy donuts. \nb.\t\nIt is necessary to buy donuts. \nc.\t\nYou should not buy donuts. \nd.\t\nYou don’t have to buy donuts.","guide":{"id":44,"focus":"식생활과 건강한 선택을 이야기해요.","grammar":"must는 ‘반드시 ~해야 한다’, don’t have to는 ‘~할 필요 없다’예요.","mission":"건강에 좋은 음식 두 가지와 줄일 음식을 하나 말해 보세요.","example":"You must eat healthy food.","exampleKo":"건강한 음식을 먹어야 해요."}},{"id":45,"startPage":508,"endPage":520,"topics":"Talking about upcoming events​ Expressing desires to see sights or do activities on a trip","strategy":"Predict","goals":"Grammar: Future continuous verb tense Speaking and Pronunciation: Reduced form of “will” in future continuous tense","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"You know I love Washington, D.C. But I want to see more of the United States. My roommate Marsha and I will be on vacation at the same time. So, we are going on a road trip together! Hi, Marsha!","ko":"당신은 내가 사랑 워싱턴, D.C. 그러나 나는 미국의 더 많은 것을보고 싶어. 내 룸메이트 마샤와 나는 동시에 휴가에있을 것이다. 그래서, 우리는 함께 도로 여행에 가고있다! 안녕, 마샤!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Hi!","ko":"안녕하세요!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I packed my bags and I am ready to go!","ko":"나는 내 가방을 포장하고 나는 갈 준비가되어 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Did you make a list of all the places you want to see?","ko":"당신이보고 싶은 모든 장소의 목록을 만들었습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I did. I want to see New York City and the Statue of Liberty!","ko":"나는했다. 나는 뉴욕시와 자유의 동상을보고 싶다!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"And I want to see Mount Rushmore!","ko":"그리고 나는 산 Rushmore를보고 싶어!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"(Anna writes) Mount Rushmore.","ko":"(Anna 쓰기) 마운트 Rushmore."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"And don’t forget the Grand Canyon!","ko":"그리고 그랜드 캐년을 잊지 마세요!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"(Anna writes) Let’s not forget California’s redwood forest! There are so many places to see!","ko":"(Anna writes) 캘리포니아의 붉은 숲을 잊지 마세요! 볼 수있는 많은 장소가 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"We will be driving for a long time. So, we might get bored.","ko":"우리는 오랫동안 운전할 것입니다. 그래서, 우리는 지루하게 얻을 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Bored? No way! We can talk.","ko":"Bored? 아니 방법! 우리는 이야기 할 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Or not talk.","ko":"또는 얘기하지."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"We can play word games. We can sing! You know, our trip is like that famous American song. (sings) “This land is your land, This land is my land …”*","ko":"우리는 단어 게임을 할 수 있습니다. 우리는 노래 할 수 있습니다! 당신은 알고, 우리의 여행은 유명한 미국 노래와 같습니다. ( 노래) \"이 땅은 당신의 땅입니다, 이 땅은 내 땅입니다 ...\"*"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"(sings) “…from California to the New York island ...”","ko":"(sings) \"... 캘리포니아에서 뉴욕 섬에 ...\""},{"speaker":"BOTH","en":"“... to the redwood forest to the Gulf stream waters ... this land was made for you and me!”","ko":"“... 걸프 스트림 물에 레드 우드 숲에 ...이 땅은 당신과 나를 위해 만들어졌다!”"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Will we be stopping soon?","ko":"우리는 곧 멈추어질 것입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"We won’t be stopping soon.","ko":"우리는 곧 멈추지 않을 것입니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"I’m hungry.","ko":"나는 배고프다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Marsha, we just left D.C.! We’ll be eating lunch in about 2 hours. Can you wait?","ko":"Marsha, 우리는 그냥 D.C를 왼쪽! 우리는 약 2 시간에 점심 식사를 할 것입니다. 당신은 기다릴 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"I guess.","ko":"나는 추측한다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Here, have an apple. It’s organic! (Anna throws the apple. It goes out the window.)","ko":"여기, 사과가 있습니다. 그것은 유기입니다! (Anna는 사과를 던졌습니다. 그것은 창을 나옵니다.)"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Thanks.","ko":"감사합니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Okay, we will be arriving in New York City very soon!","ko":"괜찮아, 우리는 곧 뉴욕시에 도착합니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I can’t wait to see The Big Apple! Marsha, look! There she is!","ko":"나는 큰 애플을 볼 기다릴 수 없다! 마샤, 봐! 그녀는있다!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"The Statue of Liberty!","ko":"자유의 동상!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"She is awesome!","ko":"그녀는 훌륭합니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Marsha, in ten minutes, guess what we’ll be seeing?","ko":"Marsha, 10 분 안에, 우리가 무엇을 볼 것인가?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"What?","ko":"? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"The largest rocking chair in the world!","ko":"세계에서 가장 큰 로커!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"No, we won’t be seeing that.","ko":"아니, 우리는 그것을 본 적이 없습니다. 영어 수업을 배우자 45 512"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Marsha, it’s on my other list -- Best Roadside Sights. (Marsha grabs the paper and throws it out the window.)","ko":"Marsha, 그것은 내 다른 목록에 있습니다 -- 최고의 Roadside Sights. (Marsha는 종이를 잡고 창을 던져.)"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh no! We littered! And my list is gone. Don’t worry. I brought the book. (lifts up large book, starts reading) (Later)","ko":"Oh no! 우리는 멸망했습니다! 그리고 내 목록은 사라졌습니다. 걱정하지 마세요. 나는 책을 가져 왔습니다. (큰 책을 들고, 독서를 시작합니다) (레이터)"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"… and that is why I am so afraid of sheep.","ko":"... 그리고 나는 양을 두려워하는 이유입니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"(snores a little)","ko":"(작은 없습니다)"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Wow, I feel better. Marsha, you are a great listener.","ko":"와우, 나는 더 나은 느낌. 마샤, 당신은 훌륭한 청취자입니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"(waking up) Where are we?","ko":"(위로) 우리는 어디에 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"We will be entering North Dakota any minute now!","ko":"노스 다코타에 입장할 수 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"North Dakota! We are going in the wrong direction! We want to go to South Dakota!","ko":"북한 다코타! 우리는 잘못된 방향으로 가고 있습니다! 우리는 사우스 다코타에 가고 싶습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No problem. I will just exit the highway. We will be going south … in just a minute. There. Done! We’re going south! Okay, we will be stopping for gas and a bathroom break in about an hour.","ko":"아무 문제도 없습니다. 난 그냥 고속도로를 종료합니다. 우리는 남쪽으로 갈 것입니다 ... 단지 분. 거기. 끝난! 우리는 남쪽으로 가고 있습니다! 괜찮아, 우리는 가스를 멈추고 욕실은 약 시간에 휴식합니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Then we will be very near to Mount Rushmore!","ko":"그럼 우리는 Mount Rushmore에 매우 가까이있을 것입니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yay! Dead presidents’ heads on the side of a mountain!","ko":"Yay! 죽은 대통령의 산의 측면에 머리!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"We did it, Marsha! We made it to California! It’s beautiful!","ko":"우리는 그것을했다, 마샤! 우리는 캘리포니아에 그것을했다! 그것은 아름답다!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"And we saw everything on the list!","ko":"그리고 우리는 목록에서 모든 것을 보았습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well, we saw everything on page 1 of the list.","ko":"글쎄, 우리는 목록의 1 페이지에 모든 것을 보았습니다."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"What do you mean “page 1?”","ko":"당신은 무엇을 의미합니까 “페이지 1?”"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh. Here are pages 2, 3 and 4! We’ll be very busy driving back to Washington, D.C. Until next time … ! * This Land is Your Land was written by American folk singer Woody Guthrie. See below for the lyrics.","ko":"오. 여기에 페이지 2, 3 및 4입니다! 우리는 워싱턴, D.C. 다음 시간까지 매우 바쁜 운전이 될 것입니다 ... ! * 이 땅은 미국 민속 가수 Woody Guthrie에 의해 작성되었습니다. lyrics에 대한 아래를 참조하십시오. 영어 수업을 배우십시오 45 513"}],"words":[{"en":"break","definition":"a brief period of time during which someone stops an activity","ko":"휴식·깨지다"},{"en":"direction","definition":"the course or path on which something is moving or pointing","ko":"방향"},{"en":"enter","definition":"to go or come into (something)","ko":"들어가다"},{"en":"exit","definition":"to go out of a place or situation","ko":"나가다"},{"en":"highway","definition":"a main road that connects cities and towns","ko":"고속도로"},{"en":"land","definition":"the solid part of the surface of the Earth","ko":"땅"},{"en":"litter","definition":"to throw or leave trash on the ground in a public place","ko":"쓰레기를 버리다"},{"en":"pack","definition":"to put (something) into a bag or suitcase so that you can take it with you","ko":"짐을 싸다"},{"en":"place","definition":"a specific area or region of the world","ko":"장소"},{"en":"ready","definition":"prepared to do something","ko":"준비된"},{"en":"road trip","definition":"a long trip in a car or truck, etc","ko":"자동차 여행"},{"en":"rocking chair","definition":"chair that moves back and forth on rockers that are attached to its legs PLACE NAMES: California Grand Canyon Gulf Stream New York City North Dakota Mount Rushmore Redwood Forest South Dakota Statue of Liberty","ko":"흔들의자"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 45 - This Land is Your Land\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. Why are Marsha and Anna going on a \nroad trip together?\na.\t\nThey came from different parts of the ‘\ncountry.\nb.\t\nThey want to see Washington, D.C. on \nvacation.\nc.\t\nThey have vacation at the same time.\nd.\t\nThey stopped working at the same \nplace.\n4. What happened while Anna was \ntelling a story?\na.\t  Anna got angry with Marsha for falling \nasleep.\nb.\t Marsha fell asleep and Anna went in the \nwrong direction.\nc.\t Anna drove the car toward South \nDakota.\nd.\t Marsha looked at the book and chose \nsome sights.\n2. What does Anna explain to Marsha?\na.\t\nThey left DC only a short time ago, so \nthey will drive for two hours.\nb.\t Anna suggests that Marsha could have \na snack\nc.\t\nAnna says that Marsha should wait for \nlunch.\nd.\t Anna explains all of these things to \nMarsha.\n5. What strategy is Anna using when \nshe says, “We’ll be very busy driving \nback to Washington, D.C.”?\na.\t\nCooperating\nb.\t\nPersonalizing\nc.\t\nUsing a graphic image\nd.\t\nPredicting\n3. For what reason does Anna say, \n“Oh, no! We littered”?\na.\t Anna and Marsha do not agree on \nwhere to go.\nb.\t Marsha threw the paper out of the \nwindow.\nc.\t Anna forgot to tell Marsha about the \nsights.\nd.\t Marsha doesn’t want to see the rocking \nchair.\nThis Land Is Your Land\nWords and Music by Woody Guthrie\nChorus:\nThis land is your land This land is my land\nFrom California to the New York island;\nFrom the red wood forest to the Gulf Stream waters\nThis land was made for you and Me.\nAs I was walking that ribbon of highway,\nI saw above me that endless skyway:\nI saw below me that golden valley:\nThis land was made for you and me.\nI’ve roamed and rambled and I followed my footsteps\nTo the sparkling sands of her diamond deserts;\nAnd all around me a voice was sounding:\nThis land was made for you and me.\nWhen the sun came shining, and I was strolling,\nAnd the wheat fields waving and the dust clouds rolling,\nAs the fog was lifting a voice was chanting:\nThis land was made for you and me.\nAs I went walking I saw a sign there\nAnd on the sign it said “No Trespassing.”\nBut on the other side it didn’t say nothing,\nThat side was made for you and me.\nIn the shadow of the steeple I saw my people,\nBy the relief office I seen my people;\nAs they stood there hungry, I stood there asking\nIs this land made for you and me?\nNobody living can ever","guide":{"id":45,"focus":"여행 일정을 미리 설명해요.","grammar":"will be + 동사-ing는 ‘미래의 어느 때 ~하고 있을 것’이라는 뜻이에요.","mission":"여행 중 내일 이 시간에 무엇을 할지 말해 보세요.","example":"We’ll be driving tomorrow.","exampleKo":"내일 우리는 운전해서 이동하고 있을 거예요."}},{"id":46,"startPage":521,"endPage":531,"topics":"Asking for permission","strategy":"Act It Out","goals":"Grammar: Verb structures with lend, borrow, and loan Speaking: Asking for permission, borrowing things Pronunciation: Words ending with “r”","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Have a nice day at work Marsha!","ko":"일 마샤에 좋은 날이 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"You too, Anna. Oh, wait. Do you have pen and paper I can borrow?","ko":"당신은 너무, 안나. 오, 기다립니다. 펜과 종이를 가지고 나는 빌릴 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Of course.","ko":"물론."},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"We are meeting at this restaurant tonight.","ko":"우리는이 레스토랑의 밤새 회의입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What is happening tonight?","ko":"오늘 밤 무슨 일이 일어나고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Today is my birthday. We are celebrating at 7pm tonight. Did you forget?","ko":"오늘 내 생일입니다. 우리는 밤 7시에서 축하하고 있습니다. 잊었습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sorry, Marsha! I gotta go! See you later!","ko":"죄송합니다, 마샤! 나가 가자! 나중에 보자!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Don’t forget! Tonight … 7pm!","ko":"잊지 마세요! 오늘 밤 ... 오후 7시!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I forgot Marsha’s birthday! And I don’t get my paycheck until next week. I know. I’ll make her a gift. I’ll just have to borrow a couple of things.","ko":"나는 Marsha의 생일을 잊었다! 그리고 나는 다음 주까지 나의 paycheck를 얻지 않는다. 나는 알고있다. 나는 그녀의 선물을 만들 것입니다. 나는 단지 몇 가지를 빌릴 필요가있다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Amelia, may I borrow your stapler?","ko":"Amelia, 나는 stapler를 빌릴 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"Sure. I can lend you my stapler, Anna. But please return it. It’s my favorite stapler.","ko":"물론. 나는 내 stapler, Anna를 빌릴 수 있습니다. 그러나 그것을 돌려주세요. 그것은 내 마음에 드는 stapler입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"You can trust me. I understand. One time, I loaned my stapler to the wrong person.","ko":"당신은 나를 신뢰 할 수 있습니다. 나는 이해한다. 한 번, 나는 잘못된 사람에게 내 stapler를 빌려."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thanks, Amelia.","ko":"감사합니다, Amelia."},{"speaker":"Amelia","en":"Don’t mention it. Bye, stapler!","ko":"그것을 언급하지 마십시오. Bye, stapler!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Jonathan! Can I borrow your scissors?","ko":"Jonathan! 나는 가위를 빌릴 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Oh! Hi, Anna! What’re you doing?","ko":"오! 안녕, 안나! 당신은 무엇을하고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Can I borrow your scissors? Sorry to bother you.","ko":"가위를 빌릴 수 있습니까? 너에게 미안 해요."},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Yes, I can lend them to you, but you must return them. These scissors -- they are the sharpest scissors in the office. Watch.","ko":"예, 나는 그들에게 말씀 할 수 있습니다, 그러나 당신은 그들을 돌려해야합니다. 이 가위 -- 그들은 사무실에서 가장 날카로운 가위입니다. 시계."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Wow, those are sharp. I will be very careful.","ko":"와우, 그 날카로운. 나는 매우 조심한다."},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Okay.","ko":"이름 *"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"And I’ll bring them back tomorrow.","ko":"그리고 나는 내일을 다시 데려 갈 것이다."},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"Good.","ko":"좋은."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thank you.","ko":"고마워요."},{"speaker":"Jonathan","en":"You’re welcome.","ko":"천만에요."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Happy Birthday, Marsha! (gives Marsha a gift)","ko":"생일, 마샤! (가을 마샤 선물)"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Thanks, Anna! I love birthday gifts! Anna, it is … interesting. What is it?","ko":"감사합니다, 안나! 나는 생일 선물을 사랑한다! 안나, 그것은 ... 재미있다. 그것은 무엇입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well, I know you love hats. And you need office supplies. So, this is your own office supply hat!","ko":"잘, 나는 당신이 모자를 사랑한다는 것을 알고 있습니다. 그리고 당신은 사무실 공급을 필요로 합니다. 따라서, 이것은 당신의 자신의 사무실 공급 모자입니다!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"Wow! That is a lot of office supplies!","ko":"와우! 그것은 많은 사무실 용품입니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Many people loaned or shared their supplies with me. Some people really love their office supplies. It has paper, pens, tape, erasers, rubber bands, ] binder clips, paper clips, and a light!","ko":"많은 사람들이 대출 또는 저와 함께 공급을 공유합니다. 일부 사람들은 사무실 용품을 정말 좋아합니다. 그것은 종이, 펜, 테이프, 지우개, 고무 밴드, ] 바인더 클립, 종이 클립 및 빛이 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Marsha","en":"What is the balloon for?","ko":"풍선은 무엇입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"The balloon will help your friends find you. Let’s try it! You get a seat in the  restaurant - I will find you!","ko":"풍선은 친구가 당신을 찾을 수 있도록 도와줍니다. 시도하자! 당신은 하자의 영어 레슨에서 자리를 얻을 46 525 레스토랑 - 나는 당신을 찾을 것입니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Sometimes all the money in the world can’t buy the perfect gift. Until next time!","ko":"때로는 세계에서 모든 돈은 완벽한 선물을 살 수 없습니다. 다음 시간까지!"}],"words":[{"en":"borrow","definition":"to take and use (something that belongs to someone else) for a period of time before returning it","ko":"빌리다"},{"en":"bring back","definition":"to return with (something or someone)","ko":"가져와서 돌려주다"},{"en":"celebrate","definition":"to do something special or enjoyable for an important event, occasion or holiday","ko":"축하하다"},{"en":"gift","definition":"something that is given to another person","ko":"선물"},{"en":"lend","definition":"to give (something) to (someone) to be used for a period of time and then returned","ko":"빌려주다"},{"en":"loan","definition":"to give (something) to (someone) for a period of time","ko":"대출·빌려주기"},{"en":"mention","definition":"to talk or write about something or someone in a brief way don’t mention it - expression. used to answer someone who has just thanked you for something","ko":"언급하다"},{"en":"paycheck","definition":"the money that you regularly earn","ko":"급여 수표"},{"en":"sharp","definition":"having a thin edge that is able to cut things","ko":"날카로운"},{"en":"supplies","definition":"[plural] : things (such as food, equipment, fuel, and so on) that are needed for a particular purpose","ko":"용품"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 46 - May I Borrow That?\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Marsha want?\na.\t\nTo lend Anna something\nb.\t\nTo borrow some paper and a pen\nc.\t\nTo buy a birthday gift\nd.\t\nTo write a story\n4. What does Jonathan say about his \nscissors?\na.\t\nThey are the only scissors he has.\nb.\t\nThey are the most expensive scissors \nhe has.\nc.\t\nHe is doing something with the \nscissors now.\nd.\t\nAnna must return them if he lends them \nto her.\n2. Why does Anna want to make \nsomething?\na.\t\nAnna does not have money to buy a \ngift.\nb.\t\nShe has too many office supplies.\nc.\t\nAnna knows Marsha likes handmade \ngifts.\nd.\t\nShe gave Marsha all of her paycheck\n5. What do the friends say about the \nhat? \na.\t\nAnna says “I am loaning the hat to you.”\nb.\t\nMarsha says “The hat looks funny.”\nc.\t\nAnna says “I borrowed supplies to \nmake it.”\nd.\t\nMarsha says, “I borrowed Anna’s hat.”\n3. What is the main idea of this conver­\nsation?\n1.\t Amelia wants to borrow a stapler from \nAnna.\n2.\t Anna is giving someone a new stapler as \na gift.\n3.\t Amelia can lend her favorite stapler to \nAnna.\n4.\t Anna wants to lend Amelia a stapler.","guide":{"id":46,"focus":"물건을 빌리고 돌려주는 표현을 익혀요.","grammar":"borrow는 ‘빌려 오다’, lend는 ‘빌려주다’예요. 주고받는 방향이 달라요.","mission":"친구에게 연필을 빌리고 돌려주기로 약속해 보세요.","example":"May I borrow that?","exampleKo":"저것을 빌려도 될까요?"}},{"id":47,"startPage":532,"endPage":545,"topics":"Describing problems Offering and accepting help","strategy":"Find Out","goals":"Grammar: Past and present continuous tenses; reflexive pronouns (reviews) Speaking: Offering and accepting help Pronunciation: Reduced form of “I will” to talk about the future.","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi, Pete. What are you doing?","ko":"안녕, Pete. 당신은 무엇을하고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Oh! Hi, Anna. Right now, I am fixing my car.","ko":"오! 안녕, 안나. 지금, 나는 내 차를 해결하고 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"How’s it going?","ko":"어떻게 가고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"It’s going … not so good.","ko":"그것은 ... 그렇게 좋지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Okay so the one we’re looking for someone to tell for one week","ko":"1 주일 간 누군가를 찾고 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Anna, I can fix it myself. But thanks.","ko":"Anna, 나는 그것을 스스로 수정 할 수 있습니다. 그러나 감사."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Pete, I think I found your problem. These are spark plugs. (holds them up)","ko":"Pete, 나는 내가 당신의 문제를 발견 생각한다. 이들은 스파크 플러그입니다. (그들을 보라)"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"They start the engine.","ko":"그들은 엔진을 시작합니다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"I know that, Anna. But there were too many spark plugs … in there. So I took out the extra ones.","ko":"나는 그, 안나. 그러나 거기에 너무 많은 불꽃 플러그가 있었다 .... 그래서 나는 여분의 것을했다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"There are no extras, Pete. You need all of them. Pete, can you fix a car yourself?","ko":"추가는 없습니다, Pete. 당신은 그들 모두를 필요로합니다. Pete, 당신은 차를 직접 고칠 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Well, Anna, last night I was watching the online video course, “You CAN Fix a Car Yourself!”","ko":"글쎄, 안나, 지난 밤 나는 온라인 비디오 코스를보고했다, \"당신은 차를 직접 해결할 수 있습니다!\""},{"speaker":"Dan","en":"Yes, you CAN fix your car yourself!","ko":"그렇습니다, 당신은 당신의 차를 직접 고칠 수 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"And I watched the first 10 lessons. So, I think I know what I’m doing.","ko":"그리고 나는 첫 번째 10 레슨을 보았다. 그래서, 나는 내가 무슨 일을 알고 생각합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"How many lessons are there?","ko":"몇 가지 수업이 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Four hundred and fifty.","ko":"4 백과 치매."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"450! That’ll take too long! If I fix your car, I’ll have it running in 10 to 15 minutes.","ko":"450! 그것은 너무 오래 걸릴 것입니다! 나는 차를 수정하면, 나는 10에서 15 분으로 실행해야합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Where’re your tools?","ko":"도구는 어디에 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"I have this. (puts a useless tool in her hand). And this. (hands her another useless tool)","ko":"나는이. (자신에 쓸모없는 도구를 입력). 그리고이. (자신의 다른 쓸모없는 도구를 손으로)"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Great. Um, I’ll get my tools. I’ll be back in a flash!","ko":"그레이트. 우우, 나는 내 도구를 얻을 것이다. 나는 플래시에 다시거야!"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"But, Anna, I don’t need your ... (She goes and quickly comes back with tools.)","ko":"하지만, Anna, 나는 당신의 필요하지 않습니다 ... (그가 간다 신속 도구로 다시 온다.)"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"… help.","ko":"... 도움."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Pete, when I was a teenager, I was fixing cars -- myself. I learned from a master.","ko":"애완 동물, 내가 십대 때, 나는 차를 고정했다 -- 나 자신. 나는 마스터에서 배웠다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"You can trust me.","ko":"나를 신뢰 할 수 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Okay.","ko":"이름 *"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Great! But we need teamwork. You sit in the car. When I say “go,” you start the engine.","ko":"훌륭한! 그러나 우리는 팀웍을 필요로합니다. 당신은 차에 앉습니다. 나는 \"고,\"라고 말할 때 당신은 엔진을 시작합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Okay, go! ​","ko":"견적 요청"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Stop!","ko":"뚱 베어"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Okay, go! Huh.","ko":", 가자! ."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"It’s not starting! It’s not starting!","ko":"시작하지 않습니다! 그것은 시작하지 않습니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What’s wrong?","ko":"무엇이 잘못되었습니까?"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"This car is stupid … stupid, stupid!","ko":"이 차는 어 ... 어류, 어류!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Pete, kicking the tires will not help.","ko":"Pete, 타이어를 킥은 도움이되지 않습니다. 영어 수업을 배우자 47 536"},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"Well, you did not help, Anna. You did not help!!","ko":"잘, 당신은 도움이되지 않았다, Anna. 당신은 도움이되지 않았다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Pete, Pete! Pull yourself together, man. Give me the keys. I must feel the key in the ignition and turn it myself.","ko":"Pete, Pete! 함께 잡아, 남자. 나를 키하십시오. 나는 점화에 열쇠를 느끼고 자신을 돌려야합니다."},{"speaker":"Master","en":"Use the key, Anna. Turn the key, Anna. What are you forgetting, Anna?","ko":"키, 안나를 사용합니다. 키, 안나를 켭니다. 잊을 수 없는 것, 안나?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Pete. Pete.","ko":"펫. 페페."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"What?","ko":"? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ? ?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"You are out of gas.","ko":"당신은 가스 밖으로."},{"speaker":"Pete","en":"I can’t be out of gas. (looks at gauge) I’m out of gas. Sorry, Anna. I’ll go get some.","ko":"나는 가스를 밖으로 할 수 없습니다. (게이지에서 전망) 나는 가스 밖으로있다. 미안, 안나. 나는 몇 가지를 얻을 것이다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Pete. You relax. Clean your face. You can watch the rest of your online video course. It’ll be faster if I go … in a flash. Until next time … Dan (in the online video course): “Lesson 11. Always make sure you have a full tank of gas!”","ko":"Pete. 당신은 휴식을. 얼굴을 청소. 당신은 당신의 온라인 비디오 코스의 나머지를 볼 수 있습니다. 그것은 내가 갈 때 빠릅니다 ... 플래시에서. 다음 시간까지 ... Dan (온라인 비디오 코스에서) : \"Lesson 11. 항상 당신이 가스의 전체 탱크를 가지고 있는지 확인하십시오!\" 영어 수업 47 537"}],"words":[{"en":"break","definition":"a brief period of time during which someone stops an activity","ko":"고장 나다"},{"en":"course","definition":"a series of classes about a particular subject in a school","ko":"과정"},{"en":"engine","definition":"a machine that changes energy (such as heat from burning fuel) into mechanical motion","ko":"엔진"},{"en":"face","definition":"the front part of the head that has the eyes, nose, and mouth on it","ko":"얼굴"},{"en":"fix","definition":"to make (something) whole or able to work properly again or to repair (something)","ko":"고치다"},{"en":"flash","definition":"a sudden appearance or occurrence of something","ko":"번쩍이다"},{"en":"ignition","definition":"the electrical system in an engine that causes the fuel to burn so that the engine begins working","ko":"점화 장치"},{"en":"key","definition":"a device that is used to open a lock or start an automobile","ko":"열쇠"},{"en":"kick","definition":"to hit (someone or something) with your foot","ko":"차다"},{"en":"master","definition":"a person who has become very skilled at doing something","ko":"숙달하다"},{"en":"spark plug","definition":"a part of an engine that produces a spark that makes the fuel burn","ko":"점화 플러그"},{"en":"stupid","definition":"informal. used to refer to something in an angry or irritated way","ko":"바보 같은"},{"en":"tank","definition":"a container for holding a liquid or gas","ko":"연료 탱크"},{"en":"tire","definition":"a rubber ring that usually contains air and wheel of a car, or bicycle","ko":"타이어"},{"en":"tool","definition":"something (such as a hammer, saw, shovel, and so on) that you hold in your hand and use for a particular task","ko":"도구"},{"en":"video","definition":"a movie, television show or event that has been recorded so that it can be watched on a television or computer","ko":"동영상"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 47 - How Can I Help?\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Anna want to do?\na.\t\nGo on a trip in Pete’s car\nb.\t\nBorrow Pete’s car to visit friends\nc.\t\nHelp Pete fix his car\nd.\t\nTake Pete to visit some of her friends\n4. Why is Pete yelling?\na.\t Pete is angry because Anna is helping.\nb.\t He is angry because the spark plugs do \nnot work.\nc.\t Pete is angry because the car will not \nstart.\nd.\t He is angry because the car is stupid.\n2. Why does Pete take out the spark \nplugs?\na.\t\nPete is cleaning the spark plugs.\nb.\t\nHe is putting new spark plugs in the \nengine.\nc.\t\nPete thinks they did not work.\nd.\t\nHe thinks there were too many in the \nengine.\n5. What did Pete forget to do?\na.\t\nFill the tank with gas\nb.\t\nTurn the key in the ignition\nc.\t\nWatch the video course\na.\t\nAsk the Master for advice\n3. Where did Pete learn how to fix his \ncar?\na.\t Pete learned from a teenager.\nb.\t He watched videos online.\nc.\t Pete studied at a local garage.\nd.\t He took lessons from Anna.\nWords for Lesson 47","guide":{"id":47,"focus":"누군가에게 도움을 제안해요.","grammar":"Can I help you?는 ‘도와드릴까요?’라는 표현이에요. fix는 ‘고치다’예요.","mission":"고장 난 물건을 도와줄 때 쓸 말을 연습해 보세요.","example":"How can I help?","exampleKo":"어떻게 도와드릴까요?"}},{"id":48,"startPage":546,"endPage":557,"topics":"Review of making recommendations Talking about things to do and see","strategy":"Focus Attention","goals":"Grammar: Present perfect verb tense Speaking: Using the present perfect verb tense. Pronunciation: Reduced forms of has/have with the present perfect verb tense","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello! I have lived in Washington, D.C. for a long time now. And I have done a lot. I feel that I know this city pretty well. (walks off and comes back) That’s the wrong way. Where is it again?","ko":"안녕하세요! 나는 워싱턴에서 살았다, D.C. 오랫동안 지금. 그리고 나는 많은 일을했습니다. 나는이 도시를 꽤 잘 알고 있다고 생각합니다. (돌아서 다시 온다) 잘못된 방법입니다. 그것은 어디에 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"(sees a tourist at a sign) Excuse me, can I help you? Have we met before?","ko":"(신속에 관광을 참조) 내가 도와 줄 수 있습니까? 우리가 전에 만난 적이 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Jean","en":"I don’t think so. I’ve just flown in from Boston. My name is Jean.","ko":"나는 그렇게 생각하지 않습니다. 보스턴에서 그냥 흐르는거야. 내 이름은 Jean입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hi, Jean! I’m Anna. I really feel like we’ve met before. Anyway, how can I help?","ko":"안녕, Jean! 나는 Anna입니다. 나는 우리가 전에 만난 것처럼 정말 느낍니다. 어쨌든, 나는 어떻게 도울 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Jean","en":"I want to see an interesting museum but I don’t know which one.","ko":"나는 흥미로운 박물관을보고 싶어하지만 나는 어느 것을 알지 못한다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I can help with that. I’ve lived in Washington, D.C. a long time. I think I’ve seen all the museums.","ko":"나는 그와 함께 도움이 될 수 있습니다. 나는 워싱턴, D.C.에서 살았다. 나는 모든 박물관을 본 생각."},{"speaker":"Jean","en":"Wow, thanks. So, tell me, which museums are good?","ko":"와우, 감사. 그래서, 저에게 말해, 박물관은 좋은?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well, they are all good. But they’re all different. There are science museums and history museums and art and culture museums.","ko":"글쎄, 그들은 모두 좋다. 그러나 그들은 모두 다릅니다. 과학 박물관과 역사 박물관과 예술과 문화 박물관이 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Jean","en":"I want to see an unusual museum.","ko":"특별한 박물관을보고 싶습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I like the Sculpture Garden. Have you ever seen sculptures in a garden? It is really artistic!","ko":"나는 조각 정원을 좋아합니다. 정원에서 조각품을 본 적이 있습니까? 그것은 정말 예술적입니다!"},{"speaker":"Jean","en":"I have never seen a garden of sculptures! I’ll write that on my list!","ko":"나는 조각품의 정원을 본 적이 없다! 나는 내 목록에 그것을 쓸거야!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Have you been to the Museum of the American Indian? I’ve visited that museum many times. It is very peaceful.","ko":"미국 인디언 박물관에 왔습니까? 나는 박물관이 많은 시간을 방문했습니다. 그것은 매우 평화롭습니다."},{"speaker":"Jean","en":"I have always liked American Indian culture.","ko":"나는 항상 미국 인디언 문화를 좋아했다."},{"speaker":"Jean","en":"I’ll put that on my list. (writes on list) Do you have any other suggestions?","ko":"나는 내 목록에 그것을 넣어. (목록에 쓰기) 당신은 다른 제안이 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well, if you like plants, you can visit the U.S. Botanic Gardens. It’s very organic.","ko":"식물을 좋아한다면 미국 식물원을 방문 할 수 있습니다. 그것은 매우 유기적입니다."},{"speaker":"Jean","en":"I have always loved plants. I’ll write that on my list, too! Wow, you know so much about D.C.’s museums.","ko":"나는 항상 사랑한 식물을 가지고 있습니다. 나는 내 목록에 그것을 쓸 것입니다. 와우, 당신은 D.C.의 박물관에 대해 너무 많이 알고 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well, I have lived here for over a year.","ko":"잘, 나는 1 년 이상에 대해 여기에 살았다."},{"speaker":"Jean","en":"You’re so lucky to live in such a beautiful city filled with so many museums and a zoo!","ko":"너무 많은 박물관과 동물원에 가득한 아름다운 도시에 살고있는 운이 좋다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What? D.C. has a zoo?","ko":"D.C.에는 동물원이 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Jean","en":"Yes, and it’s beautiful. You’ve lived here for so long and you haven’t been to the zoo?","ko":"예, 그리고 그것은 아름답다. 당신은 너무 오래 살았고 당신은 동물원에 없었다?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I’ve never been to D.C.’s zoo. I’ve never been to any zoos!","ko":"나는 D.C.의 동물원에 결코 없었습니다. 나는 어떤 동물원에 결코 없었습니다!"},{"speaker":"Jean","en":"You have never seen zoo animals?","ko":"당신은 동물원 동물을 본 적이 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I grew up on a farm, Jean. I’ve known farm animals my whole life.","ko":"나는 농장에서 자랐다, Jean. 나는 내 전체 생활에서 알려진 농장 동물."},{"speaker":"Jean","en":"But the zoo has lions (makes sound of lion roaring) and elephants (makes sound of elephant trumpeting) and zebras (makes no sound)! If you have never seen a real, live elephant, you must. They are so majestic.","ko":"그러나 동물원에는 리온이 있습니다 (사자 roaring의 소리를 만드십시오) 코끼리와 코끼리 ( 코끼리 트럼펫의 소리를 만드십시오) zebras (소리를 만드십시오)! 당신이 진짜를 본 적이 있다면, 코끼리, 당신은해야합니다. 그들은 너무 majestic입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I will. I will! (writes list) There. I’ve written my own must-see zoo animal list!","ko":"나는. 나는! (쓰기 목록) 거기. 나는 내 자신의 겨우 동물원 동물 목록을 작성했습니다!"},{"speaker":"Jean","en":"Have fun at the zoo and thanks, Anna!","ko":"동물원과 감사에 재미있어, Anna!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Have fun at the museums, Jean! And thank YOU!","ko":"박물관, 장에서 재미있게! 그리고 감사합니다! 영어 수업을 배우자 48 552"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"This has been awesome! And I have seen every animal on my list! Jean, the tourist, helped me see more of my city. But where have I seen her before? Oh well. Until next time …","ko":"이 멋진! 그리고 나는 내 목록에 모든 동물을 본! 청바지, 관광, 내 도시의 더 많은 것을 볼 수. 그러나 내가 전에 본 곳? Oh 잘. 다음 시간까지 ..."}],"words":[{"en":"American Indian","definition":"a member of any of the first groups of people living in North America or South America. The members of these nations are also called Native Americans or by the name of their tribal nation, as in “a member of the Navajo tribe.”","ko":"아메리카 원주민"},{"en":"animal","definition":"a living thing that is not a human being or plant","ko":"동물"},{"en":"U.S. Botanic Garden","definition":"a large public garden in Washington, D.C. where plants are grown in order to be studied","ko":"미국 식물원"},{"en":"elephant","definition":"a very large gray animal that has a long, flexible nose and two long tusks","ko":"코끼리"},{"en":"lion","definition":"a large wild cat that has golden brown fur and that lives mainly in Africa","ko":"사자"},{"en":"majestic","definition":"large and impressively beautiful","ko":"웅장한"},{"en":"own","definition":"to have (something) as property or to legally possess (something)","ko":"자신의"},{"en":"plant","definition":"a living thing that grows in the ground, usually has leaves or flowers, and needs sun and water to survive","ko":"식물"},{"en":"science","definition":"knowledge about or study of the natural world based on facts learned through experiments and observation","ko":"과학"},{"en":"sculpture","definition":"a piece of art that is made by carving or molding clay, stone, wood or metal","ko":"조각"},{"en":"suggestion","definition":"an idea about what someone should do or how someone should behave","ko":"제안"},{"en":"zebra","definition":"an African animal that looks like a horse and has black and white stripes covering its body","ko":"얼룩말"},{"en":"zoo","definition":"a place where many kinds of animals are kept so that people can see them​","ko":"동물원"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 48 \nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does the tourist want Anna to \ndo?\na.\t\nShe wants Anna to go to a museum \nwith her.\nb.\t\nThe tourist wants to know how to get to \nBoston.\nc.\t\nShe wants Anna to tell her about \ninteresting museums.\nd.\t\nThe tourist wants to tell Anna about a \nmuseum.\n4. What surprises Jean?\na.\t\nAnna does not think the zoo is \nbeautiful.\nb.\t\nAnna often goes to the zoo in D.C.\nc.\t\nAnna has never been to a zoo.\nd.\t\nAnna does not like zoo animals.\n2. Jean wants to see an unusual \nmuseum. What does Anna \nrecommend?\na.\t\nA history museum\nb.\t\nThe sculpture garden\nc.\t\nThe science museum\nd.\t\nAll of the museums\n5. What does Jean recommend to \nAnna?\na.\t She recommends that Anna see an \nelephant.\nb.\t Jean recommends that Anna see some \nfarm animals.\nc.\t Jean tells Anna to make a list of animals.\nd.\t She says that Anna should come with \nher to the zoo.\n3. Why is Jean writing a list?\na.\t\nJean is writing her suggestions for \nAnna.\nb.\t\nJean is making a list of plants she \nwants to see.\nc.\t\nShe is writing about American Indian \nculture.\nd.\t\nShe is focusing her attention on \nlearning about museums.","guide":{"id":48,"focus":"지금까지의 경험을 물어요.","grammar":"Have you ever + 과거분사?는 ‘~해 본 적 있어요?’예요.","mission":"여행이나 특별한 경험을 서로 묻고 답해 보세요.","example":"Have you ever been there?","exampleKo":"거기에 가 본 적 있어요?"}},{"id":49,"startPage":558,"endPage":568,"topics":"Verb tenses Reacting to information","strategy":"Find Practice Opportunities","goals":"Grammar: Compare the present perfect verb tense with the past and present tenses Speaking: Present perfect, present, and past verb tenses Pronunciation: Reduced forms of “has” and “have” in the present perfect verb tense","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"It is no secret that Washington, D.C. has spies. Well, it should be a secret because spying is secret. But it’s not a secret. There’s even a spy museum! The International Spy Museum has created an amazing collection of spy things! And today, we will see them! My boss, Ms. Weaver, has sent me here … on a mission! Ms. Weaver: Hello, Anna, are you there?","ko":"그것은 워싱턴, D.C.는 스파이가 비밀이기 때문에 비밀이 없습니다. 그러나 비밀이 아닙니다. 스파이 박물관도 있습니다! 국제 스파이 박물관은 스파이 것들의 놀라운 컬렉션을 만들었습니다! 그리고 오늘, 우리는 그들을 볼 것입니다! 내 보스, Ms. 웨버, 여기 나를 보냈습니다 ... 임무에! Ms. Weaver: 안녕하세요, Anna, 거기에 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"That’s her. Yes, Agent Peacock. This is Agent Flamingo, reporting for duty. Ms. Weaver: Agent what? Look, Anna … I mean, Agent Flamingo, I want you to learn all you can about spying.","ko":"그건 그녀의. 예, 에이전트 공작. 이것은 에이전트 Flamingo, 의무에 대한보고입니다. Ms. Weaver: 에이전트 무엇? 보기, Anna ... 나는 의미, 에이전트 Flamingo, 나는 당신이 스파이에 대해 배울 것을 원합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"You mean, collect intelligence? Ms. Weaver: Yeah, it’s for our new show -- “D.C. Secrets.”","ko":"당신은 의미, 지능을 수집? Ms. 웨버: 그래, 그것은 우리의 새로운 쇼에 대한 -- \"D.C. 비밀.\""},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"You’ve got it, Agent Peacock. The mission is safe with me. Ms. Weaver: Oh, okay, great. Just be back by noon.","ko":"당신은 그것을 가지고있다, 에이전트 공작. 임무는 나를 안전. Ms. 웨버: 오, 괜찮아, 큰. 그냥 노온에 의해 다시."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Agent Peacock, I’m at an air duct! Ms. Weaver: Yes, spies sometimes sneak down air ducts.","ko":"Agent Peacock, 나는 공 덕트에있어! Ms. Weaver : 예, spies는 때때로 공 덕트를 운동합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I have never snuck down an air duct. It’s dark and small. I’m afraid of dark, small places. Ms. Weaver: You can do it, Agent Flamingo. You know, spies aren’t afraid of a little darkness.","ko":"나는 공기 덕트를 결코 멈춘 적이 없습니다. 그것은 어둠과 작은입니다. 나는 어두운, 작은 장소의 두려움입니다. 웨버 : 당신은 그것을 할 수 있습니다, 에이전트 플라밍고. 당신은 알고, spies는 약간 어둠을 두려워하지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Right. It’s just an air duct -- a dark, small air duct. Okay. I’m doing it, Agent Peacock! I am sneaking down a long, dark, small air duct. I’m having a little trouble breathing. Ms. Weaver: Just keep going, Agent Flamingo. Think of the team!","ko":"오른쪽. 그것은 단지 공기 덕트 -- 어두운, 작은 공기 덕트입니다. 괜찮아. 나는 그것을하고있어, Agent Peacock! 나는 긴, 어두운, 작은 공기 덕트를 운동하고 있습니다. 나는 작은 문제가 호흡하는거야. Ms. Weaver : 그냥 계속, 에이전트 Flamingo. 팀의 생각!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Okay, I will think of the team. I’m thinking of the team, Agent Peacock! I did it! I did it! I sneaked down an air duct. That was a little uncomfortable. Ms. Weaver: Good!","ko":"그래, 나는 팀의 생각한다. 나는 팀, 에이전트 공작의 생각이다! 나는 그것을했다! 나는 그것을했다! 나는 공기 덕트 아래로 운동했다. 그것은 약간 불편했다. Ms. Weaver : 좋은!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What’s the next mission? Ms. Weaver: Umm … have you ever cracked a code?","ko":"다음 임무는 무엇입니까? Ms. Weaver : Umm ... 코드를 부수 한 적이 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No. Ms. Weaver: Well, go learn. Spies use their brains.","ko":"No. Ms. Weaver: 글쎄, 배울 수 있습니다. 스파이는 뇌를 사용합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Got it! I’ve never cracked a code before. Let’s try, Agent Flamingo! This is really hard. I’m still trying to crack the code. I’ve cracked the code! I’ve cracked the code, Agent Peacock! My brain really hurts. Ms. Weaver: Great. Umm, Agent Flamingo, now answer this question: Do spies have to be in good shape?","ko":"그것을! 나는 전에 코드를 부수지 않았습니다. 시도하자, 에이전트 플라밍고! 이것은 정말 어렵다. 나는 여전히 코드를 부수려고 노력하고 있습니다. 나는 코드를 부수었다! 나는 코드, Agent Peacock을 부수했습니다! 내 두뇌는 정말 상처를 입었다. Weaver : Great. Umm, Agent Flamingo, 이제이 질문에 대답하십시오 : 두 spies는 좋은 모양에있을 수 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"“Yes,” Agent Peacock! Spies have to be in really good shape! Can you hear me? Ms. Weaver: You’re breaking up, Flamingo.","ko":"“예,” Agent Peacock! 스파이 정말 좋은 모양에 있어야! 당신은 나를들을 수? Ms. Weaver: 당신은 깨어난, Flamingo. Let’s Learn English Lesson 49 562"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"The International Spy Museum is awesome! Agent Peacock, I completed the mission! Ms. Weaver: Great. Great. Now, I have another very important mission for you.","ko":"국제 스파이 박물관은 굉장합니다! 에이전트 공작, 나는 임무를 완료! Ms. 웨버: 그레이트. 그레이트. 지금, 나는 당신을 위해 또 다른 중요한 임무가 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Got it. See you back at H.Q.! Ms. Weaver: Yummy! You brought my lunch! Thanks, Agent Flamingo!","ko":"그것을. H.Q에서 다시 보자! Ms. Weaver : Yummy! 당신은 내 점심을 가져! 감사합니다, 에이전트 Flamingo!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Mission completed. Agent Peacock! (Amelia makes a face.) Ms. Weaver: Don’t ask. Special thanks go out to the International Spy Museum for letting us film in the museum!","ko":"미션 완료. Agent Peacock! (아메리아는 얼굴을 만든다.) Ms. 웨버: 묻지 말라. 특별 감사는 우리 박물관에서 영화를 드리기 위해 국제 스파이 박물관에 간다! 의 Learn English Lesson 49 563"}],"words":[{"en":"agent","definition":"a person who tries to get secret information about another country or government","ko":"요원"},{"en":"air duct","definition":"a duct or pipe for air to flow through to the rooms of a building","ko":"환기 덕트"},{"en":"brain","definition":"the organ of the body in the head that controls functions, movements, sensations, and thoughts","ko":"뇌"},{"en":"breathe","definition":"to move air into and out of your lungs","ko":"숨 쉬다"},{"en":"code","definition":"a set of letters, numbers or symbols that is used to secretly send messages to someone","ko":"암호"},{"en":"collection","definition":"a group of interesting or beautiful objects brought together in order to show or study them","ko":"수집품"},{"en":"complete","definition":"to finish making or doing (something)","ko":"완성하다"},{"en":"crack","definition":"to find an answer or solution to (something)","ko":"갈라진 틈"},{"en":"duty","definition":"something that is done as part of a job","ko":"임무"},{"en":"flamingo","definition":"a tall wading bird with mainly pink or scarlet plumage and long legs and neck","ko":"홍학"},{"en":"H.Q. - abbrev. headquarters","definition":"a place from which something (such as a business or a military action) is controlled or directed","ko":"본부"},{"en":"intelligence","definition":"secret information that a government collects about an enemy or possible enemy","ko":"정보"},{"en":"mission","definition":"a task or job that someone is given to do","ko":"임무"},{"en":"operation","definition":"a set of planned actions for a particular purpose","ko":"작전"},{"en":"peacock","definition":"a male peafowl, which has very long tail feathers that it can spread like a fan","ko":"공작새"},{"en":"secret","definition":"a fact or piece of information that is kept hidden from other people","ko":"비밀"},{"en":"shape","definition":"a physically strong and healthy condition","ko":"모양"},{"en":"sneak","definition":"to move quietly and secretly in order to avoid being noticed","ko":"몰래 움직이다"},{"en":"spy","definition":"a person who tries secretly to get information about a country or organization for another country or organization","ko":"스파이"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 49 - Operation Spy!  \nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Ms. Weaver want?\na.\t\nShe wants to go on a mission.\nb.\t\nMs. Weaver wants Anna to learn about \nspying.\nc.\t\nShe wants to find a flamingo.\nd.\t\nMs. Weaver wants to tell Anna secrets \nabout D.C.\n4. What does Anna tell Ms. Weaver?\na.\t\nShe cannot hear what Ms. Weaver said.\nb.\t\nSpies must be in good shape.\nc.\t\nShe broke her spy phone.\nd.\t\nMs. Weaver should be in good shape.\n2. Why is Anna afraid?\na.\t\nAnna is afraid someone will catch her.\nb.\t\nShe doesn’t think Ms. Weaver will find \nher.\nc.\t\nAnna has never been in an air duct.\nd.\t\nShe doesn’t want to be a spy.\n5. What did Ms. Weaver want Anna to \ndo? \na.\t\nWhat did Ms. Weaver want Anna to do?\nb.\t\nWrite about the Spy Museum.\nc.\t\nReturn to the Spy Museum.\nd.\t\nGo to lunch with Amelia.\n3. What is Anna’s mission?\na.\t\nTo think like Agent Peacock\nb.\t\nTo learn to follow orders\nc.\t\nTo pretend to be someone else\nd.\t\nTo solve a secret code","guide":{"id":49,"focus":"임무 수행 경험과 시점을 구분해요.","grammar":"have + 과거분사는 경험·결과를 말하고, 단순 과거형은 언제 있었는지에 집중해요.","mission":"최근에 해낸 일을 한 가지 이야기해 보세요.","example":"I have finished the mission.","exampleKo":"저는 임무를 끝냈어요."}},{"id":50,"startPage":569,"endPage":579,"topics":"Duration of activity","strategy":"Monitor","goals":"Grammar: Present perfect continuous verb tense Speaking: Present perfect continuous verb tense Pronunciation: Pronouncing the word “for” quickly in sentences using the present perfect continuous and a time phrase","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello, and welcome to Georgetown University in Washington, D.C.! I am going back to school! Georgetown is the oldest Catholic and Jesuit university in the United States. The Jesuits are a religious order known worldwide for their many colleges and universities. Students have been studying here since 1792!","ko":"안녕하세요, 워싱턴에있는 조지타운 대학에 오신 것을 환영합니다, D.C.! 나는 학교로 돌아갑니다! 조지타운은 미국에서 가장 오래된 가톨릭과 Jesuit 대학입니다. Jesuits는 많은 대학과 대학을 위해 전 세계적으로 알려진 종교적 순서입니다. 학생들은 1792 년부터 여기에 공부하고 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Hey, are you finished with your report?","ko":"안녕, 당신은 당신의 보고서로 끝났습니까?"},{"speaker":"Taylor","en":"Almost. I have been writing and re-writing since last night! The subject is really interesting to me.","ko":"거의. 나는 지난 밤 이후 쓰고 재 쓰기하고있다! 주제는 정말 저에 흥미."},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"Me too! I have been studying this topic* for a long time.","ko":"나를 너무! 나는 오랫동안이 화제 *을 공부하고있다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Am I late?","ko":"나는 늦게?"},{"speaker":"Sarah","en":"You’re a little late. But don’t worry. The professor isn’t here yet.","ko":"조금 늦습니다. 그러나 걱정하지 마세요. 교수는 아직 없습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"How long has the class been waiting?","ko":"수업은 얼마나 기다리고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Taylor","en":"We’ve only been waiting for about 10 minutes.","ko":"약 10분만 기다리겠습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh good. Oh, no! I forgot my pencil sharpener. Excuse me, do you have a pencil sharpener I can borrow?","ko":"Oh good. Oh, no! 나는 연필 깎이를 잊어 버렸다. 나를 변태, 내가 빌릴 수있는 연필 깎이가 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Taylor","en":"No, sorry.","ko":"아니요, 죄송합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh wait. I found my extra one! Whew, that was close.","ko":"오 기다립니다. 나는 내 여분의 것을 발견! Whew, 그것은 닫혔다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"So, how long have you been studying at Georgetown?","ko":"그래서, 조지타운에서 얼마나 공부 했습니까?"},{"speaker":"Andrew","en":"I’ve been studying here since 2015.","ko":"2015년부터 공부하고 있습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Awesome. You know, I’ve been wanting to go back to school for a long time. So, here I am!","ko":"굉장. 알고, 나는 오랫동안 학교로 돌아가고 싶어. 그래서, 여기 나는!"},{"speaker":"Andrew","en":"Well, you picked a great school. I’ve been really happy here.","ko":"글쎄, 당신은 훌륭한 학교를 선택했습니다. 나는 여기에 정말 행복했습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Awesome. See, I’ve been working for several years now. So, going back to school makes me a little nervous.","ko":"굉장. 보고, 나는 몇 년 동안 일하고있다. 그래서, 학교로 돌아 가기 조금 긴장."},{"speaker":"Randall","en":"Don’t be nervous. Just pay attention and do your best!","ko":"신경이 없습니다. 관심을 지불하고 최선을 다하십시오!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"That is great advice. You know, I have been paying attention. But sometimes I still feel like I don’t understand. Like last week …","ko":"그건 좋은 조언입니다. 당신은 알고, 나는 관심을 지불하고있다. 그러나 때때로 나는 아직도 내가 이해하지 않는 것처럼 느낍니다. 지난 주처럼 ..."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What’s that?","ko":"그게 뭐니?"},{"speaker":"Jada","en":"This is my draft.","ko":"이것은 내 초안입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What draft?","ko":"어떤 초안?"},{"speaker":"Jada","en":"The professor told us to bring our drafts.","ko":"교수는 우리에게 우리의 초안을 가져 왔습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I think she said “giraffe.”","ko":"나는 그녀가 말했다 “giraffe.”"},{"speaker":"Jada","en":"No. She didn’t.","ko":"아니. 그녀는하지 않았다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Here comes the professor. Dr. Jones: Hello class! Sorry I’m late, but the snow storm made getting here really difficult. I see you’ve been waiting very patiently. So, let’s get started! Who wants to give their talk first?","ko":"여기 교수가 온다. 존스 : 헬로 클래스! 미안 해요 나는 늦게,하지만 눈 폭풍은 여기에 정말 어렵게했다. 나는 당신을 기다리고있어 매우 참을성있었습니다. 그래서, 시작하자! 누가 자신의 이야기를주고 싶습니까? 영어 수업을 배울하자 50 572"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Oh! Oh! Please, please pick me. Dr. Jones: Anna?","ko":"오! 오! 제발, 나를 선택하시기 바랍니다. 존스: 안나?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Who me? Sure. Thanks.","ko":"누가? 물론. 감사합니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Here is my report on “Violins in the City.”","ko":"여기에 내 보고서는 \"도시의 Violins\"입니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"People have been looking for a solution to the problem of violins in the city. I say stop! Stop! They are not the problem! In fact, violins are part of the solution!","ko":"사람들은 도시의 바이올린의 문제에 대한 해결책을 찾고있다. 나는 멈추지 않는다! 정지! 그들은 문제가되지 않습니다! 사실, 바이올린은 솔루션의 일부입니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Violins create beautiful music that can fill a city with hope. Dr. Jones: Anna …","ko":"Violins는 희망으로 도시를 채울 수있는 아름다운 음악을 만듭니다. Dr. Jones : Anna ..."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"If we put a violin in the hands of every child … Dr. Jones: Anna! The topic is “Violence in the city.” Violence. Not violins.","ko":"우리는 모든 아이의 손에 바이올린을 넣으면 ... 존스 : 안나! 주제는 \"도시의 활력.\" Violence입니다. 바이올린이 아닙니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Until next time …Like I was saying, many people are saying that violence in the city is a problem. A very big problem. * topic = subject","ko":"다음 시간까지 ...라고 말하기 때문에 많은 사람들이 도시에 폭력이 문제가 있다고합니다. 매우 큰 문제가 있습니다. * 주제 = 주제는 영어 수업을 배울 수 있습니다 50 573"}],"words":[{"en":"Catholic","definition":"of or relating to the Roman Catholic Church","ko":"가톨릭의"},{"en":"class","definition":"a group of students who meet regularly to be taught a subject or activity","ko":"수업"},{"en":"draft","definition":"a version of something (such as a report) that you make before you make the final version","ko":"초안"},{"en":"confused","definition":"unable to understand or think clearly","ko":"혼란스러운"},{"en":"giraffe","definition":"a very tall African animal that has an extremely long neck and legs","ko":"기린"},{"en":"Jesuit","definition":"a man who is a member of a religious group called the Roman Catholic Society of Jesus","ko":"예수회 회원"},{"en":"order","definition":"a religious organization whose members usually live together and promise to follow special rules and traditions","ko":"명령"},{"en":"patient","definition":"able to remain calm and not become annoyed when waiting for a long time","ko":"참을성 있는"},{"en":"pay attention","definition":"to listen to, watch, or consider something or someone very carefully","ko":"주의를 기울이다"},{"en":"pencil","definition":"an instrument used for writing and drawing that has a hard outer part and a black or colored center part","ko":"연필"},{"en":"professor","definition":"a teacher especially of the highest rank at a college or university","ko":"교수"},{"en":"religious","definition":"believing in a god or a group of gods and following the rules of a religion","ko":"종교적인"},{"en":"report","definition":"a written or spoken description of a situation or event","ko":"보고서"},{"en":"sharpener","definition":"a tool or machine that makes something sharp","ko":"연필깎이"},{"en":"since","definition":"in the time after (a specified time or event in the past) or from (a point in the past) until the present time","ko":"~이후로"},{"en":"solution","definition":"something that is used or done to deal with and end a problem","ko":"해결책"},{"en":"study","definition":"to learn about something by reading, memorizing facts or attending school","ko":"공부하다"},{"en":"understand","definition":"to know the meaning of something","ko":"이해하다"},{"en":"violence","definition":"the use of physical force to harm someone or to damage property","ko":"폭력"},{"en":"violin","definition":"a musical instrument that has four strings and that you play with a bow","ko":"바이올린"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 50 - Back to School\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Taylor say about her \nreport?\na.\t\nWhat does Taylor say about her report?\nb.\t\nTaylor says the topic is boring to her.\nc.\t\nShe has been writing and changing it \nsince last night.\nd.\t\nTaylor says she has finished her report.\n4. Why is Anna nervous?\na.\t\nAnna does not always understand the \nother students.\nb.\t\nShe does not always pay attention.\nc.\t\nAnna always forgets to do her work.\nd.\t\nShe has been working and now is going \nback to school.\n2. What does Anna ask the students?\na.\t\nShe asks what time it is.\nb.\t\nWhere the professor is today\nc.\t\nShe asks why the professor is late.\nd.\t\nHow long the class has been waiting\n5. What mistake did Anna make in \nher report?\na.\t\nShe does not talk loud enough.\nb.\t\nHer professor gave her a different \nsubject.\nc.\t\nShe does not understand the other \nstudents.\nd.\t\nHer professor does not like violins.\n3. What does Andrew say about \nGeorgetown?\na.\t\nHe tells Anna he was unhappy there in \n2015.\nb.\t\nAndrew tells Anna it is a good school.\nc.\t\nHe says he has not been there for a \nlong time.\nd.\t\nAndrew says he started studying in \n2016.","guide":{"id":50,"focus":"학교생활과 계속해 온 일을 말해요.","grammar":"have been + 동사-ing는 과거부터 지금까지 계속해 온 행동을 말해요.","mission":"최근 계속 공부하고 있는 내용을 설명해 보세요.","example":"I have been studying English.","exampleKo":"저는 계속 영어를 공부해 왔어요."}},{"id":51,"startPage":580,"endPage":588,"topics":"Habits Expressing appreciation Expressing dislike","strategy":"Set a Goal","goals":"Grammar: Review of present perfect and present perfect continuous; gerunds; infinitives (to + verb) Speaking: Gerunds and infinitives Pronunciation: Reduced form of “to” in sentences with infinitives","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"D.C. is a popular city for marathons! A marathon is a long race. Many marathons raise money for charity, you know - good works. A marathon is a good fitness goal too. I want to challenge myself in a marathon and maybe win a medal! Hey, there’s Ashley. Ashley! Wait for me! It’s Anna!","ko":"D.C.는 마라톤을위한 인기있는 도시입니다! 마라톤은 긴 경주입니다. 많은 마라톤은 자선을 위해 돈을 올리고 있습니다. 좋은 작품. 마라톤은 좋은 피트니스 목표입니다. 나는 마라톤에서 자신을 도전하고 아마 메달을 이길 원합니다! Hey, there's Ashley. Ashley! 대기! 그것은 안나입니다!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Ash … ley. Ash … ley.","ko":"Ash ... ley. 재 ... ley."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Are you okay, Anna?","ko":"안나, 괜찮습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I just ran … from over there.","ko":"나는 단지 ran ... 거기에서."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Do you want to sit down, Anna? Do you want some water? (Anna takes the bottle and tries to return it.) No thanks. You keep it.","ko":"앉고 싶습니까, Anna? 물을 원하십니까? (Anna는 병을 가지고 돌아갑니다.) 감사합니다. 유지하십시오."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thanks. I didn’t know you like to run.","ko":"감사합니다. 실행하고 싶습니다."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"I love running. In fact, this weekend, I will run in my first marathon.","ko":"나는 달리기를 좋아합니다. 사실, 이번 주말, 나는 나의 첫 번째 마라톤에서 실행됩니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Me … too.","ko":"나 ... 너무."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Really? You are running in a marathon?","ko":"정말? 당신은 마라톤에서 실행됩니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yeah. In a couple of days. Why do you ask … like that?","ko":"그래. 몇 일 안에. 왜 당신이 요구합니까?"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"What do you know about running in a marathon?","ko":"marathon에서 실행하는 것에 대해 무엇을 알고 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I know that there’s a lot of running and sometimes you can win a medal.","ko":"나는 달리기와 때때로 당신은 메달을 이길 수 있다는 것을 알고있다."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"How long have you been training?","ko":"훈련은 얼마입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I started today. I’ve been training for an hour … no, an hour and seven minutes!","ko":"오늘부터 시작되었습니다. 1 시간 동안 훈련되었습니다 ... 아니, 시간 및 7 분!"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Anna, training a little every day is a good habit to get into. Not all at once!","ko":"Anna, 매일 훈련은 좋은 습관입니다. 한 번에하지 마십시오!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thanks for the advice, Ashley. But I’m running in a special race.","ko":"조언 주셔서 감사합니다, 애슐리. 그러나 나는 특별한 경주에서 실행됩니다."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"What marathon is it?","ko":"어떤 마라톤은?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I don’t remember the name. But the website said everyone gets a medal.","ko":"나는 이름을 기억하지 않습니다. 그러나 웹 사이트는 모두가 메달을 얻고 있다고 말했다."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Okay, well, good luck, Anna!","ko":"괜찮아, 잘, 행운, 안나!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thanks, Ashley. Good luck to you, too.","ko":"감사합니다, 애슐리. 당신에게 행운을 빌어 요, 너무."},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Thank you.","ko":"고마워요."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Bye!","ko":"이름 *"},{"speaker":"Ashley","en":"Bye, Anna!","ko":"으로, 안나!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"See you! (At the race: an announcer calls out race information)","ko":"당신을 참조하십시오! (경쟁이 : 레이더는 경주 정보를 호출)"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello. I am here to enter the race!","ko":"안녕하세요. 나는 여기에 레이스를 입력합니다!"},{"speaker":"Woman","en":"But ma’am you can’t enter the race.","ko":"그러나 ma’am 당신은 경주를 입력 할 수 없습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"What? How am I going to meet my goal?","ko":"무엇? 나는 어떻게 나의 목표를 만나려고?"},{"speaker":"Woman","en":"Ma’am, this race is for children. You can’t run with the children.","ko":"Ma’am,이 레이스는 아이들을위한 것입니다. 당신은 아이들과 함께 실행할 수 없습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Children? Children. That’s perfect. I just might win!","ko":"아이들? 아이들. 그게 완벽합니다. 난 그냥 승리 할 수 있습니다!"},{"speaker":"Woman","en":"No, ma’am. You really can’t run with the children.","ko":"아니, ma'am. 당신은 정말 아이들과 함께 실행할 수 없습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I’m sorry. Of course. I was only thinking of my goal.","ko":"나는 미안 해요. 물론. 나는 단지 내 목표의 생각이었다."},{"speaker":"Woman","en":"Well, you can help us with our goal, which is to raise money for sick children.  Would you like to help us?","ko":"영어 회화를 단기간에 완성하세요. 800 페이지가 넘는 레슨과 8000 개 이상의 오디오 클립을 다운로드 하시고, 자신을 영어 환경에 항상 노출 시키세요. 인터넷이나 컴퓨터에 상관없이 MP3 플레이어를 통해 언제나 영어를 듣고 따라할 수 있습니다. 영어회화 다운로드 페이지로 이동하시면 좀 더 자세한 내용을 알려드립니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"I’ve just found my new goal. And I get to wear a medal. (to child who finished race) Good job!","ko":"나는 그냥 내 새로운 목표를 발견했다. 그리고 나는 메달을 착용한다. (아직을 끝내는 아이) 좋은 일!"}],"words":[{"en":"challenge","definition":"to test the ability, skill, or strength of (someone or something)","ko":"도전"},{"en":"charity","definition":"a organization that helps people in need","ko":"자선단체"},{"en":"fitness","definition":"the condition of being physically fit and healthy","ko":"체력"},{"en":"goal","definition":"something that you are trying to do or achieve","ko":"목표"},{"en":"habit","definition":"something that a person does often in a regular and repeated way","ko":"습관"},{"en":"marathon","definition":"a running race that is about 26 miles (42 kilometers) long","ko":"마라톤"},{"en":"medal","definition":"a piece of metal often in the form of a coin with designs and words in honor of a special event, a person, or an achievement","ko":"메달"},{"en":"race","definition":"a competition between people, animals or vehicles to see which one is fastest","ko":"경주"},{"en":"special","definition":"different from what is normal or usual","ko":"특별한"},{"en":"train","definition":"to try to make yourself stronger, faster, or better at doing something before competing in an event or competition","ko":"훈련하다"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 51 - A Good Habit\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Anna say about \nmarathons?\na.\t\nMarathons are too long and are too \nchallenging for her.\nb.\t\nThat marathons cost money for many \ncharities.\nc.\t\nMarathons help people stay fit and \nraise money for charities.\nd.\t\nThat they are hard work for people in \nWashington, D.C.\n3. What does Ashley tell Anna about \ntraining?\na.\t\nAnna needs to train many hours every \nday.\nb.\t\nShe should start training today for this \nweekend.\nc.\t\nAnna has been training with her for a \nlong time.\nd.\t\nIt is good to train a little every day.\n2. What are Ashley and Anna talking \nabout?\na.\t\nThey are both running in a marathon.\nb.\t\nThey both do not like to run.\nc.\t\nThey are making plans to run together.\nd.\t\nThey have been running for a couple of \ndays.\n4. What does the woman say to Anna?\na.\t\nShe can pay money to run with \nchildren.\nb.\t\nAnna can help to raise money for the \nchildren.\nc.\t\nShe does not have a goal.\nd.\t\nAnna is not as fast as the children.","guide":{"id":51,"focus":"좋은 습관과 목표를 세워요.","grammar":"enjoy + 동사-ing와 want to + 동사원형처럼 동사 뒤의 형태가 달라요.","mission":"앞으로 만들고 싶은 습관을 한 문장으로 쓰세요.","example":"I want to build a good habit.","exampleKo":"좋은 습관을 만들고 싶어요."}},{"id":52,"startPage":589,"endPage":601,"topics":"Taking risks Discussing feelings Describing accomplishments","strategy":"Evaluate","goals":"Grammar: Review verb tenses; Phrasal verbs Speaking: Phrasal verbs Pronunciation: Pronounce the blended form of “sit down”","conversation":[{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Hello, it’s Anna! I did it - Washington, D.C. is my home. Looking back over the past year, I’ve done so many amazing things! I have met people from all over the world. I’ve made many good friends. And I have a great job! And I’ve taken a lot of chances. And now I have some really big news! Wait for it… and 3, 2, 1…","ko":"안녕하세요, 그것은 안나입니다! 나는 그것을했다 - 워싱턴, D.C. 내 집입니다. 지난 해에 다시보고, 나는 너무 많은 놀라운 일을했습니다! 나는 전 세계의 사람들을 만났다. 나는 많은 좋은 친구를 만들었습니다. 그리고 나는 큰 일을 가지고! 그리고 나는 많은 기회를 가지고있다. 그리고 지금 나는 정말 큰 소식을 가지고 있습니다! 그것을 기다리고 ... 그리고 3, 2, 1 ..."},{"speaker":"Kelly","en":"Hello and welcome to “Around the Corner and Across the Street from the Actor’s Studio!” Many people dream of becoming actors. But very often, those dreams don’t come true.","ko":"안녕하세요. “ 코너 중 하나이며 Actor’s Studio에서 거리 건너!” 많은 사람들이 배우가되는 꿈. 그러나 매우 자주, 그 꿈은 진실하지 않습니다."},{"speaker":"Kelly","en":"Well, today we will meet a woman and -- her acting career has really taken off. In fact, she acted in my play, “The Woods Are Alive!” Oh. She really brought the part of Tree Number 15 to life! Let’s give a warm welcome to Anna Matteo!","ko":"글쎄, 오늘 우리는 여성을 만나고 -- 그녀의 행동 경력을 쌓았습니다. 사실, 그녀는 내 연극에서 행동, \"나무는 살아있다!\" Oh. 그녀는 정말 트리 번호의 일부를 가져 왔습니다 15 생활! Anna Matteo에 따뜻한 환영을주십시오!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thank you. Thank you so much for having me here.","ko":"감사합니다. 여기에 나를 위해 대단히 감사합니다."},{"speaker":"Kelly","en":"Please, please, sit down. Here, here, let me help you.","ko":"제발, 앉아. 여기, 여기, 나를 도와주세요."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Thanks. Thanks. Wow, it is great to see you again, Director Kelly!","ko":"감사합니다. 감사합니다. 와우, 그것은 당신을 다시 볼 수있는 좋은, 감독 켈리!"},{"speaker":"Kelly","en":"It’s great to see you too, Anna. I see you are still wearing your tree costume. Does this have anything to do with your big news?","ko":"나나도 볼 수 있습니다. 나는 여전히 나무 의상을 입은 것을 볼 수 있습니다. 이것은 당신의 큰 소식과 함께 할 수있는 것은 아무것도 있습니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes. Yes, it does.","ko":"예. 예, 그것은."},{"speaker":"Kelly","en":"Well, Anna, please share that news with us.","ko":"글쎄, 안나, 우리와 함께 소식을 공유하십시오."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Kelly, I will be acting in three movies.","ko":"Kelly, 나는 세 영화에서 행동한다."},{"speaker":"Kelly","en":"That is amazing! Anna, tell us more.","ko":"그건 놀랍습니다! Anna, 우리에게 더 많은 것을 알려줍니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Well, the first is a science fiction movie. The second is a romantic comedy. And the third is an action movie.","ko":"글쎄, 첫 번째 과학 소설 영화입니다. 두 번째는 로맨틱 코미디입니다. 그리고 세 번째는 액션 영화입니다."},{"speaker":"Kelly","en":"That is so great! Let me guess -- you’re playing a tree in all of them!","ko":"그건 너무 훌륭합니다! 나를 추측하자 -- 당신은 그들 모두에서 나무를 연주!"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes! This is what happened. To prepare for your play, I had to find out what it was like to BE a tree in the world. I had to find out where to eat, where to shop, where to meet people and how to get around the city.","ko":"예! 이것은 무슨 일이 일어 났습니다. 당신의 플레이를 준비하기 위해, 나는 세계에서 나무가되기를 좋아하는 것을 발견했다. 나는 먹을 곳을 발견했다, 어디 가게, 사람들을 만나고 도시 주변을 얻는 방법."},{"speaker":"Kelly","en":"Amazing. I think big things are going to happen for you, Anna. So, tell me, will you be moving to Hollywood for a career in movies?","ko":"놀랍습니다. 나는 큰 것들이 당신을 위해 일어나고 있다고 생각합니다, Anna. 그래서, 말해, 당신은 영화에서 경력을 위해 할리우드로 이동할 것입니까?"},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"No. I’ll make the movies and then come back. Washington, D.C. is my home.","ko":"아니. 나는 영화를 만들 것입니다 그리고 그 후. 워싱턴, D.C. 내 집입니다."},{"speaker":"Kelly","en":"I’m sure your family is very proud.","ko":"가족이 매우 자랑스럽습니다."},{"speaker":"Anna","en":"Yes, they are. You know, Kelly, not too long ago, I didn’t feel very good about my life. I had to make a change. So, I took some chances. Sometimes I succeeded. Sometimes I failed. But I will never stop trying.","ko":"예, 그들은. 당신은 알고, 켈리, 너무 오래 전에, 나는 내 인생에 대해 아주 좋은 느낌하지 않았다. 나는 변경을 만들기 위해했다. 그래서, 나는 약간의 기회를했다. 때때로 나는 성공했다. 때때로 나는 실패. 그러나 나는 시도하지 않을 것이다."},{"speaker":"Kelly","en":"Well, thank you for sharing your news and so much more with us, Anna.","ko":"잘, 당신의 뉴스를 공유하고 매우 더 많은 것을 저희, Anna."},{"speaker":"Kelly","en":"Until next time …","ko":"다음 시간까지 ... 영어 수업을 배우자 52 593"}],"words":[{"en":"action movie","definition":"a movie with events that happen quickly and that cause feelings of danger and excitement ​","ko":"액션 영화"},{"en":"bring to life","definition":"make or become active, lively, or interesting","ko":"생기를 불어넣다"},{"en":"career","definition":"a job or profession that someone does for a long time","ko":"직업·경력"},{"en":"come back","definition":"to return to a place","ko":"돌아오다"},{"en":"fail","definition":"to not succeed or to end without success","ko":"실패하다"},{"en":"find out","definition":"to learn (something) by making an effort","ko":"알아내다"},{"en":"get around","definition":"to go, walk, or travel to different places","ko":"여기저기 다니다"},{"en":"prepare","definition":"to make yourself ready for something that you will be doing or something that you expect to happen","ko":"준비하다"},{"en":"proud","definition":"very happy and pleased because of something you have done, something you own, or someone you know or are related to","ko":"자랑스러운"},{"en":"romantic comedy","definition":"a movie or play that deals with love in a light, humorous way","ko":"로맨틱 코미디"},{"en":"science fiction","definition":"a kind of story about how people and societies are affected by imaginary scientific developments in the future","ko":"공상 과학"},{"en":"share","definition":"to tell someone about (your feelings, opinions, or thoughts)","ko":"나누다"},{"en":"take chances","definition":"to do things even though there could be good or bad results","ko":"도전하다"},{"en":"take off","definition":"make great progress","ko":"이륙하다·벗다"}],"quiz":"Quiz - Level 1, Lesson 52 - Taking Chances\nListen. Circle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What does Kelly tell us about Anna?\na.\t\nAnna wrote a play called, “The Woods \nAre Alive!”\nb.\t\nShe played a tree and her career is \nmaking good progress.\nc.\t\nAnna’s dream of a career as an actor \ndid not come true.\nd.\t\nShe is taking off some time from work.\n3. Where will Anna make her movies?\na.\t\nShe will make her movies at home in \nWashington, D.C.\nb.\t\nShe will make her movies and then \nreturn to Washington, D.C.\nc.\t\nShe will go to Hollywood to live and \nmake her movies.\nd.\t\nShe will not leave her home to make \nher movies.\n2. What does Anna say about movies?\na.\t\nShe is playing a tree in three movies.\nb.\t\nAnna saw an action movie yesterday.\nc.\t\nShe is interested in science fiction \nmovies.\nd.\t\nAnna loves romantic comedies.\n4. What strategy is Anna using in this \nvideo?\na.\t\nAct it out\nb.\t\nMonitor\nc.\t\nEvaluate\nd.\t\nPredict\nLet’s Learn English\nAdditional Resources\n596\nLevel 1\nAdditional \nResources\nOther VOA Learning English Courses\nLet’s Teach English\nThe Let’s Teach English video series offers free online training for English language \neducators worldwide.\nLet’s Learn English - Level 2\nThe Level 2 course of Let’s Learn English has 30 lessons.\nOn the VOA Learning English Website\nVOA English Challenge Test\nThe EF Standard English Test is a free standardized English test developed by EF \nEducation First. The test gives a CEFR score from A1 - C2. Let’s Learn English Level 1 is \ngood for learners from level A2 to B1. Let’s Learn English Level 2 is good for learners from \nlevel B2 to C1.\nLearning English Word Book\nA 1500-word dictionary is available on our website in the form of a downloadable book. \nCongratulations! You have now finished Let’s Learn English Level 1\nPrint the certificate on the next page to show your achievement.\nLEARNING ENGLISH \nCertificate of Achievement \nThis certificate is presented to: \nFor successful completion of \nLet's Learn English \nLevel 1 \nA self-directed 52-lesson program to develop \nlistening, speaking, vocabulary and writing skills \nin American English. \nAwarded this day of \nYolanda Lopez \nActing Director, Voice of America. \nI \nI \nChief, VOA Learning English\nLet’s Learn English\nAdditional Resources\n598","guide":{"id":52,"focus":"도전과 성취를 되돌아봐요.","grammar":"come back, find out 같은 동사+전치사 표현(구동사)을 익혀요.","mission":"1년 동안 새롭게 시도한 일을 떠올리고 영어로 말해 보세요.","example":"I’ve taken a lot of chances.","exampleKo":"저는 여러 번 새로운 도전을 했어요."}}];
